INSERT INTO `evidence_item` VALUES (1,1,'OV01','overview',1,'Overview paragraph 1','This unit bridges the gap between theory and practice by integrating the knowledge and key skills developed across the Digital Business or Business Information Systems specialisation. It provides students with a practical teamwork experience to identify, analyse, and solve contemporary problems by exploring the socio-technical ecosystem in which a digital business operates. This experiential learning opportunity enhances students’ career-readiness by consolidating their professional skills and ability to apply the Business Information Systems knowledge in authentic situations.','this unit bridges the gap between theory and practice by integrating the knowledge and key skills developed across the digital business or business information systems specialisation. it provides students with a practical teamwork experience to identify, analyse, and solve contemporary problems by exploring the socio-technical ecosystem in which a digital business operates. this experiential learning opportunity enhances students\' career-readiness by consolidating their professional skills and ability to apply the business information systems knowledge in authentic situations.','overview:OV01'),(2,1,'LO01','learning_outcome',2,'Learning outcome 1','LO1. Apply advanced principles and theories related to digital business and information systems in the context of an actual business organisation','lo1. apply advanced principles and theories related to digital business and information systems in the context of an actual business organisation','learning_outcome:LO01'),(3,1,'LO02','learning_outcome',3,'Learning outcome 2','LO2. Analyse open-ended business scenarios and evaluate the implications of digital technologies for business','lo2. analyse open-ended business scenarios and evaluate the implications of digital technologies for business','learning_outcome:LO02'),(4,1,'LO03','learning_outcome',4,'Learning outcome 3','LO3. Apply techniques for organisational and business process analyses to resolve an actual business problem','lo3. apply techniques for organisational and business process analyses to resolve an actual business problem','learning_outcome:LO03'),(5,1,'LO04','learning_outcome',5,'Learning outcome 4','LO4. Communicate in a professional and confident manner, both orally and in writing, with actual business professionals','lo4. communicate in a professional and confident manner, both orally and in writing, with actual business professionals','learning_outcome:LO04'),(6,1,'LO05','learning_outcome',6,'Learning outcome 5','LO5. Apply team management concepts and theories to effectively work in, and manage, cross-functional teams','lo5. apply team management concepts and theories to effectively work in, and manage, cross-functional teams','learning_outcome:LO05'),(7,1,'LO06','learning_outcome',7,'Learning outcome 6','LO6. Analyse and reflect critically on the ethical and social implications of digital business','lo6. analyse and reflect critically on the ethical and social implications of digital business','learning_outcome:LO06'),(8,1,'AS01','assessment',8,'Leadership and Professional Development: Goals Achievement Overall assessment of the goals achievement','Type: Written exam. Description: Leadership and Professional Development: Goals Achievement Overall assessment of the goals achievement','type: written exam. description: leadership and professional development: goals achievement overall assessment of the goals achievement','assessment:AS01'),(9,1,'AS02','assessment',9,'Project Progress Q&A QA&A post project progress presentation','Type: Q&A following presentation, submission or placement. Description: Project Progress Q&A QA&A post project progress presentation','type: q&a following presentation, submission or placement. description: project progress q&a qa&a post project progress presentation','assessment:AS02'),(10,1,'AS03','assessment',10,'Project Progress Infographic submission Project progress updates presentation','Type: Presentation. Description: Project Progress Infographic submission Project progress updates presentation','type: presentation. description: project progress infographic submission project progress updates presentation','assessment:AS03'),(11,1,'AS04','assessment',11,'Groupwork Accountability Survey Peer review to assess members contribution and determine their group marks','Type: Evaluation. Description: Groupwork Accountability Survey Peer review to assess members contribution and determine their group marks','type: evaluation. description: groupwork accountability survey peer review to assess members contribution and determine their group marks','assessment:AS04'),(12,1,'AS05','assessment',12,'Group Charter Each group must establish roles and norms.','Type: Written work. Description: Group Charter Each group must establish roles and norms.','type: written work. description: group charter each group must establish roles and norms.','assessment:AS05'),(13,1,'AS06','assessment',13,'Business Models Submission of partner\'s business, operating models, and IS architecture','Type: Case studies. Description: Business Models Submission of partner\'s business, operating models, and IS architecture','type: case studies. description: business models submission of partner\'s business, operating models, and is architecture','assessment:AS06'),(14,1,'AS07','assessment',14,'Leadership and Professional Development: Personal Goals Personal goals development plan','Type: Practical skill. Description: Leadership and Professional Development: Personal Goals Personal goals development plan','type: practical skill. description: leadership and professional development: personal goals personal goals development plan','assessment:AS07'),(15,1,'AS08','assessment',15,'Pitch to Partner Slides submission before class Delivered during class time','Type: Presentation. Description: Pitch to Partner Slides submission before class Delivered during class time','type: presentation. description: pitch to partner slides submission before class delivered during class time','assessment:AS08'),(16,1,'AS09','assessment',16,'Innovation Review Submission of Innovation Scorecard and infographic of solution idea','Type: Creative work. Description: Innovation Review Submission of Innovation Scorecard and infographic of solution idea','type: creative work. description: innovation review submission of innovation scorecard and infographic of solution idea','assessment:AS09'),(17,1,'AS10','assessment',17,'Boardroom Presentation Slides submission before class Live presentation','Type: Presentation. Description: Boardroom Presentation Slides submission before class Live presentation','type: presentation. description: boardroom presentation slides submission before class live presentation','assessment:AS10'),(18,1,'AS11','assessment',18,'Boardroom Presentation Q&A Q&A post boardroom presentation','Type: Q&A following presentation, submission or placement. Description: Boardroom Presentation Q&A Q&A post boardroom presentation','type: q&a following presentation, submission or placement. description: boardroom presentation q&a q&a post boardroom presentation','assessment:AS11'),(19,1,'AS12','assessment',19,'Group Report Written report','Type: Case studies. Description: Group Report Written report','type: case studies. description: group report written report','assessment:AS12'),(20,1,'WK01','weekly_schedule',20,'Week 01: Unit Introduction & Project Immersion','Unit Introduction & Project Immersion. Learning activity: Seminar (3 hr)','unit introduction & project immersion. learning activity: seminar (3 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK01'),(21,1,'WK02','weekly_schedule',21,'Week 02: Partner Briefing & Group Collaboration','Partner Briefing & Group Collaboration. Learning activity: Seminar (3 hr)','partner briefing & group collaboration. learning activity: seminar (3 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK02'),(22,1,'WK03','weekly_schedule',22,'Week 03: Problem & Opportunity Scoping','Problem & Opportunity Scoping. Learning activity: Seminar (3 hr)','problem & opportunity scoping. learning activity: seminar (3 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK03'),(23,1,'WK04','weekly_schedule',23,'Week 04: Project Planning','Project Planning. Learning activity: Seminar (3 hr)','project planning. learning activity: seminar (3 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK04'),(24,1,'WK05','weekly_schedule',24,'Week 05: Pitch to Partner','Pitch to Partner. Learning activity: Seminar (3 hr)','pitch to partner. learning activity: seminar (3 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK05'),(25,1,'WK06','weekly_schedule',25,'Week 06: Research & Analysis','Research & Analysis. Learning activity: Seminar (3 hr)','research & analysis. learning activity: seminar (3 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK06'),(26,1,'WK07','weekly_schedule',26,'Week 07: Ideation','Ideation. Learning activity: Seminar (3 hr)','ideation. learning activity: seminar (3 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK07'),(27,1,'WK08','weekly_schedule',27,'Week 08: Prototyping','Prototyping. Learning activity: Seminar (3 hr)','prototyping. learning activity: seminar (3 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK08'),(28,1,'WK09','weekly_schedule',28,'Week 09: Prototype Validation','Prototype Validation. Learning activity: Seminar (3 hr)','prototype validation. learning activity: seminar (3 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK09'),(29,1,'WK10','weekly_schedule',29,'Week 10: Implementation Planning','Implementation Planning. Learning activity: Seminar (3 hr)','implementation planning. learning activity: seminar (3 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK10'),(30,1,'WK11','weekly_schedule',30,'Week 11: Presentation Planning','Presentation Planning. Learning activity: Seminar (3 hr)','presentation planning. learning activity: seminar (3 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK11'),(31,1,'WK12','weekly_schedule',31,'Week 12: Boardroom Presentation','Boardroom Presentation. Learning activity: Seminar (3 hr)','boardroom presentation. learning activity: seminar (3 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK12'),(32,1,'WK13','weekly_schedule',32,'Week 13: Review & Closure','Review & Closure. Learning activity: Seminar (3 hr)','review & closure. learning activity: seminar (3 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK13'),(33,2,'OV01','overview',1,'Overview paragraph 1','The Digital Economy, with its focus on information as a key business resource, has changed the way Business Information Systems (BIS) is viewed in organisations. BIS are now seen as enablers of innovation in which people, supported by powerful technology, are considered to be the most important component. This is because problem-solving, innovation and critical thinking skills cannot be outsourced or easily acquired by competitors. This unit is designed to develop your understanding of how businesses operate. It shows how information systems support business operations and management through integration of people, business processes and systems. You will be provided with an introduction to state-of-the-art business analysis techniques, frameworks and models to assist in understanding the nature and contribution of BIS in a range of business contexts. With its emphasis on business rather than IT, this unit does not require prior IT-related experience. In this unit, you will learn about the increasingly important role of IT in business and acquire valuable business analysis and problem-solving skills.','the digital economy, with its focus on information as a key business resource, has changed the way business information systems (bis) is viewed in organisations. bis are now seen as enablers of innovation in which people, supported by powerful technology, are considered to be the most important component. this is because problem-solving, innovation and critical thinking skills cannot be outsourced or easily acquired by competitors. this unit is designed to develop your understanding of how businesses operate. it shows how information systems support business operations and management through integration of people, business processes and systems. you will be provided with an introduction to state-of-the-art business analysis techniques, frameworks and models to assist in understanding the nature and contribution of bis in a range of business contexts. with its emphasis on business rather than it, this unit does not require prior it-related experience. in this unit, you will learn about the increasingly important role of it in business and acquire valuable business analysis and problem-solving skills.','overview:OV01'),(34,2,'LO01','learning_outcome',2,'Learning outcome 1','LO1. make judgments about ways in which Information Technology can enable innovation and improvement in business','lo1. make judgments about ways in which information technology can enable innovation and improvement in business','learning_outcome:LO01'),(35,2,'LO02','learning_outcome',3,'Learning outcome 2','LO2. demonstrate basic business analysis skills, such as strategic analysis, data modelling, and business process modelling','lo2. demonstrate basic business analysis skills, such as strategic analysis, data modelling, and business process modelling','learning_outcome:LO02'),(36,2,'LO03','learning_outcome',4,'Learning outcome 3','LO3. create and understand visual representations of business processes using BPMN notation, as well as basic data models as the basis for information systems design','lo3. create and understand visual representations of business processes using bpmn notation, as well as basic data models as the basis for information systems design','learning_outcome:LO03'),(37,2,'LO04','learning_outcome',5,'Learning outcome 4','LO4. create databases in MS Access software','lo4. create databases in ms access software','learning_outcome:LO04'),(38,2,'LO05','learning_outcome',6,'Learning outcome 5','LO5. understand and address basic issues pertaining to information ethics','lo5. understand and address basic issues pertaining to information ethics','learning_outcome:LO05'),(39,2,'LO06','learning_outcome',7,'Learning outcome 6','LO6. work as an effective team in a problem-solving environment','lo6. work as an effective team in a problem-solving environment','learning_outcome:LO06'),(40,2,'LO07','learning_outcome',8,'Learning outcome 7','LO7. display an understanding of business design in an end-to-end manner from business idea to business execution.','lo7. display an understanding of business design in an end-to-end manner from business idea to business execution.','learning_outcome:LO07'),(41,2,'AS01','assessment',9,'Final exam Written exam','Type: Written exam. Description: Final exam Written exam','type: written exam. description: final exam written exam','assessment:AS01'),(42,2,'AS02','assessment',10,'Weekly Homework Practical task','Type: Practical skill. Description: Weekly Homework Practical task','type: practical skill. description: weekly homework practical task','assessment:AS02'),(43,2,'AS03','assessment',11,'Early Feedback Task #EarlyFeedbackTask','Type: Out-of-class quiz. Description: Early Feedback Task #EarlyFeedbackTask','type: out-of-class quiz. description: early feedback task #earlyfeedbacktask','assessment:AS03'),(44,2,'AS04','assessment',12,'Mid-semester exam Written exam','Type: Written test. Description: Mid-semester exam Written exam','type: written test. description: mid-semester exam written exam','assessment:AS04'),(45,2,'AS05','assessment',13,'Group project Project report','Type: Written work. Description: Group project Project report','type: written work. description: group project project report','assessment:AS05'),(46,2,'AD01','assessment_description',14,'Assessment description 1','Group work: Team-based learning (TBL) is a set of group-based activities designed to help students to acquire higher-level learning skills in this context, including creativity, lateral and reflective thinking, problem-solving and critical analysis as well as the applied and experiential BIS knowledge. This assessment component will consider group homework preparation for the TBL sessions as well as their work and participation in, and outcomes of collaborative in-class activities in finalising their homework submissions. The TBL activity sheets will be uploaded on Canvas.','group work: team-based learning (tbl) is a set of group-based activities designed to help students to acquire higher-level learning skills in this context, including creativity, lateral and reflective thinking, problem-solving and critical analysis as well as the applied and experiential bis knowledge. this assessment component will consider group homework preparation for the tbl sessions as well as their work and participation in, and outcomes of collaborative in-class activities in finalising their homework submissions. the tbl activity sheets will be uploaded on canvas.','assessment_description:AD01'),(47,2,'AD02','assessment_description',15,'Assessment description 2','Early Feedback Task: The objective of this task is to focus on the fundamental concepts, and applied knowledge acquired in sessions 1-3. This task will be in the form of a Canvas Quiz with multiple choice questions.','early feedback task: the objective of this task is to focus on the fundamental concepts, and applied knowledge acquired in sessions 1-3. this task will be in the form of a canvas quiz with multiple choice questions.','assessment_description:AD02'),(48,2,'AD03','assessment_description',16,'Assessment description 3','Group project report: The objective of this task is to use the knowledge and practical skills acquired in this unit of study to investigate and solve a real-life business problem. Students are expected to create and describe their own business idea for a pre-defined scenario, which they will receive through Canvas.','group project report: the objective of this task is to use the knowledge and practical skills acquired in this unit of study to investigate and solve a real-life business problem. students are expected to create and describe their own business idea for a pre-defined scenario, which they will receive through canvas.','assessment_description:AD03'),(49,2,'AD04','assessment_description',17,'Assessment description 4','Mid-semester exam: This exam will focus on the fundamental concepts, and applied and experiential knowledge acquired in weeks 1-6 of the unit. Note: This assessment will take the form of a supervised exam. It is a closed-book exam with no materials allowed.','mid-semester exam: this exam will focus on the fundamental concepts, and applied and experiential knowledge acquired in weeks 1-6 of the unit. note: this assessment will take the form of a supervised exam. it is a closed-book exam with no materials allowed.','assessment_description:AD04'),(50,2,'AD05','assessment_description',18,'Assessment description 5','Final exam: This exam will focus on the fundamental concepts, and applied and experiential knowledge acquired in weeks 1-12, including the practical assignment. Note: This assessment will take the form of a supervised exam. It is a closed-book exam with no materials allowed.','final exam: this exam will focus on the fundamental concepts, and applied and experiential knowledge acquired in weeks 1-12, including the practical assignment. note: this assessment will take the form of a supervised exam. it is a closed-book exam with no materials allowed.','assessment_description:AD05'),(51,2,'AD06','assessment_description',19,'Assessment description 6','Detailed information for each assessment can be found on Canvas.','detailed information for each assessment can be found on canvas.','assessment_description:AD06'),(52,2,'WK01','weekly_schedule',20,'Week 01: Unit overview and introduction to information systems','Unit overview and introduction to information systems. Learning activity: Seminar (2 hr)','unit overview and introduction to information systems. learning activity: seminar (2 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK01'),(53,2,'WK02','weekly_schedule',21,'Week 02: Introduction to business processes','Introduction to business processes. Learning activity: Seminar (2 hr)','introduction to business processes. learning activity: seminar (2 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK02'),(54,2,'WK03','weekly_schedule',22,'Week 02: Introduction to business processes','Introduction to business processes. Learning activity: Tutorial (1 hr)','introduction to business processes. learning activity: tutorial (1 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK03'),(55,2,'WK04','weekly_schedule',23,'Week 03: Strategy and competitive advantage','Strategy and competitive advantage. Learning activity: Seminar (2 hr)','strategy and competitive advantage. learning activity: seminar (2 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK04'),(56,2,'WK05','weekly_schedule',24,'Week 03: Strategy and competitive advantage','Strategy and competitive advantage. Learning activity: Tutorial (1 hr)','strategy and competitive advantage. learning activity: tutorial (1 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK05'),(57,2,'WK06','weekly_schedule',25,'Week 04: Databases and information design','Databases and information design. Learning activity: Seminar (2 hr)','databases and information design. learning activity: seminar (2 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK06'),(58,2,'WK07','weekly_schedule',26,'Week 04: Databases and information design','Databases and information design. Learning activity: Tutorial (1 hr)','databases and information design. learning activity: tutorial (1 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK07'),(59,2,'WK08','weekly_schedule',27,'Week 05: Data modelling','Data modelling. Learning activity: Seminar (2 hr)','data modelling. learning activity: seminar (2 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK08'),(60,2,'WK09','weekly_schedule',28,'Week 05: Data modelling','Data modelling. Learning activity: Tutorial (1 hr)','data modelling. learning activity: tutorial (1 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK09'),(61,2,'WK10','weekly_schedule',29,'Week 06: Business information systems ethics','Business information systems ethics. Learning activity: Seminar (2 hr)','business information systems ethics. learning activity: seminar (2 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK10'),(62,2,'WK11','weekly_schedule',30,'Week 06: Business information systems ethics','Business information systems ethics. Learning activity: Tutorial (1 hr)','business information systems ethics. learning activity: tutorial (1 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK11'),(63,2,'WK12','weekly_schedule',31,'Week 07: Business process management','Business process management. Learning activity: Seminar (2 hr)','business process management. learning activity: seminar (2 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK12'),(64,2,'WK13','weekly_schedule',32,'Week 07: Business process management','Business process management. Learning activity: Tutorial (1 hr)','business process management. learning activity: tutorial (1 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK13'),(65,2,'WK14','weekly_schedule',33,'Week 08: Business process modelling (BPMN)','Business process modelling (BPMN). Learning activity: Seminar (2 hr)','business process modelling (bpmn). learning activity: seminar (2 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK14'),(66,2,'WK15','weekly_schedule',34,'Week 08: Business process modelling (BPMN)','Business process modelling (BPMN). Learning activity: Tutorial (1 hr)','business process modelling (bpmn). learning activity: tutorial (1 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK15'),(67,2,'WK16','weekly_schedule',35,'Week 09: Project consultation','Project consultation. Learning activity: Tutorial (1 hr)','project consultation. learning activity: tutorial (1 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK16'),(68,2,'WK17','weekly_schedule',36,'Week 10: Business process analysis and improvement','Business process analysis and improvement. Learning activity: Seminar (2 hr)','business process analysis and improvement. learning activity: seminar (2 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK17'),(69,2,'WK18','weekly_schedule',37,'Week 10: Business process analysis and improvement','Business process analysis and improvement. Learning activity: Tutorial (1 hr)','business process analysis and improvement. learning activity: tutorial (1 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK18'),(70,2,'WK19','weekly_schedule',38,'Week 11: Cybersecurity','Cybersecurity. Learning activity: Seminar (2 hr)','cybersecurity. learning activity: seminar (2 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK19'),(71,2,'WK20','weekly_schedule',39,'Week 11: Cybersecurity','Cybersecurity. Learning activity: Tutorial (1 hr)','cybersecurity. learning activity: tutorial (1 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK20'),(72,2,'WK21','weekly_schedule',40,'Week 12: Business intelligence systems','Business intelligence systems. Learning activity: Seminar (2 hr)','business intelligence systems. learning activity: seminar (2 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK21'),(73,2,'WK22','weekly_schedule',41,'Week 12: Business intelligence systems','Business intelligence systems. Learning activity: Tutorial (1 hr)','business intelligence systems. learning activity: tutorial (1 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK22'),(74,2,'WK23','weekly_schedule',42,'Week 13: Exam briefing and unit review','Exam briefing and unit review. Learning activity: Seminar (2 hr)','exam briefing and unit review. learning activity: seminar (2 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK23'),(75,3,'OV01','overview',1,'Overview paragraph 1','Digital ecosystems (such as social media, blockchain, technology platforms, artificial intelligence, big data, people analytics, and cybersecurity) fundamentally change the way we collect and present ideas, communicate, and work together. In this unit, students are introduced to various digital ecosystems and their implications for how work is done. Students learn about how employers recruit graduates online, what it is like to join and work in a modern, digital workplace, and the tensions that arise when traditional, structured workplaces are transformed through digital, flexible, and networked ways of working. Students engage in hands-on activities to acquire skills for how to present themselves effectively and professionally online (personal branding), how to communicate in digital channels in an organisational context (professional communication), how to effectively search for and work with digital information (data literacy), and how to digitally coordinate work in teams.','digital ecosystems (such as social media, blockchain, technology platforms, artificial intelligence, big data, people analytics, and cybersecurity) fundamentally change the way we collect and present ideas, communicate, and work together. in this unit, students are introduced to various digital ecosystems and their implications for how work is done. students learn about how employers recruit graduates online, what it is like to join and work in a modern, digital workplace, and the tensions that arise when traditional, structured workplaces are transformed through digital, flexible, and networked ways of working. students engage in hands-on activities to acquire skills for how to present themselves effectively and professionally online (personal branding), how to communicate in digital channels in an organisational context (professional communication), how to effectively search for and work with digital information (data literacy), and how to digitally coordinate work in teams.','overview:OV01'),(76,3,'LO01','learning_outcome',2,'Learning outcome 1','LO1. understand how digital technology changes work environments and how work is organised','lo1. understand how digital technology changes work environments and how work is organised','learning_outcome:LO01'),(77,3,'LO02','learning_outcome',3,'Learning outcome 2','LO2. demonstrate critical discernment of popular claims about the future of work and the role of technology in this transformation process','lo2. demonstrate critical discernment of popular claims about the future of work and the role of technology in this transformation process','learning_outcome:LO02'),(78,3,'LO03','learning_outcome',4,'Learning outcome 3','LO3. communicate ideas effectively using digital online technology and audiovisual elements','lo3. communicate ideas effectively using digital online technology and audiovisual elements','learning_outcome:LO03'),(79,3,'LO04','learni