ficial Intelligence','Digital organising 1 - Fundamentals of Artificial Intelligence. Learning activity: Tutorial (1.5 hr)','digital organising 1 - fundamentals of artificial intelligence. learning activity: tutorial (1.5 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK16'),(106,3,'WK17','weekly_schedule',32,'Week 09: Digital organizing 2 - Agentic AI and Business Applications','Digital organizing 2 - Agentic AI and Business Applications. Learning activity: Lecture (1.5 hr)','digital organizing 2 - agentic ai and business applications. learning activity: lecture (1.5 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK17'),(107,3,'WK18','weekly_schedule',33,'Week 09: Digital organizing 2 - Agentic AI and Business Applications','Digital organizing 2 - Agentic AI and Business Applications. Learning activity: Tutorial (1.5 hr)','digital organizing 2 - agentic ai and business applications. learning activity: tutorial (1.5 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK18'),(108,3,'WK19','weekly_schedule',34,'Week 10: Digital Platforms 1 - Blockchain Foundations','Digital Platforms 1 - Blockchain Foundations. Learning activity: Lecture (1.5 hr)','digital platforms 1 - blockchain foundations. learning activity: lecture (1.5 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK19'),(109,3,'WK20','weekly_schedule',35,'Week 10: Digital Platforms 1 - Blockchain Foundations','Digital Platforms 1 - Blockchain Foundations. Learning activity: Tutorial (1.5 hr)','digital platforms 1 - blockchain foundations. learning activity: tutorial (1.5 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK20'),(110,3,'WK21','weekly_schedule',36,'Week 11: Digital Platforms 2 - Blockchain Implications for Business and Society','Digital Platforms 2 - Blockchain Implications for Business and Society. Learning activity: Lecture (1.5 hr)','digital platforms 2 - blockchain implications for business and society. learning activity: lecture (1.5 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK21'),(111,3,'WK22','weekly_schedule',37,'Week 11: Digital Platforms 2 - Blockchain Implications for Business and Society','Digital Platforms 2 - Blockchain Implications for Business and Society. Learning activity: Tutorial (1.5 hr)','digital platforms 2 - blockchain implications for business and society. learning activity: tutorial (1.5 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK22'),(112,3,'WK23','weekly_schedule',38,'Week 12: Digital Ecosystems','Digital Ecosystems. Learning activity: Lecture (1.5 hr)','digital ecosystems. learning activity: lecture (1.5 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK23'),(113,3,'WK24','weekly_schedule',39,'Week 12: Digital Ecosystems','Digital Ecosystems. Learning activity: Tutorial (1.5 hr)','digital ecosystems. learning activity: tutorial (1.5 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK24'),(114,3,'WK25','weekly_schedule',40,'Week 13: Unit review and exam preparation','Unit review and exam preparation. Learning activity: Lecture (1.5 hr)','unit review and exam preparation. learning activity: lecture (1.5 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK25'),(115,3,'WK26','weekly_schedule',41,'Week 13: Unit review and exam preparation','Unit review and exam preparation. Learning activity: Tutorial (1.5 hr)','unit review and exam preparation. learning activity: tutorial (1.5 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK26'),(116,4,'OV01','overview',1,'Overview paragraph 1','The rapid evolution and widespread adoption of digital technologies are transforming societies, economies, and the environment. These transformations bring significant benefits but also pose serious risks of harm, particularly for vulnerable and marginalised stakeholders, requiring a balanced approach that genuinely serves the common good. This unit unpacks the ethical dilemmas of sociotechnical change, exploring how digital technologies like artificial intelligence, blockchain, and social media impact privacy, equity, democracy, dignity, business, the environment, and more. Guided by compassion as a foundational principle, students will critically examine the ambiguous and pluralistic nature of digital innovations, developing the skills to manage ethical dilemmas and promote responsible digital innovation for the common good. The course integrates ethical theories with recent practical case studies, equipping students to address contemporary ethical dilemmas in today\'s digital world.','the rapid evolution and widespread adoption of digital technologies are transforming societies, economies, and the environment. these transformations bring significant benefits but also pose serious risks of harm, particularly for vulnerable and marginalised stakeholders, requiring a balanced approach that genuinely serves the common good. this unit unpacks the ethical dilemmas of sociotechnical change, exploring how digital technologies like artificial intelligence, blockchain, and social media impact privacy, equity, democracy, dignity, business, the environment, and more. guided by compassion as a foundational principle, students will critically examine the ambiguous and pluralistic nature of digital innovations, developing the skills to manage ethical dilemmas and promote responsible digital innovation for the common good. the course integrates ethical theories with recent practical case studies, equipping students to address contemporary ethical dilemmas in today\'s digital world.','overview:OV01'),(117,4,'LO01','learning_outcome',2,'Learning outcome 1','LO1. Analyse the ethical challenges and paradoxes associated with digital innovations.','lo1. analyse the ethical challenges and paradoxes associated with digital innovations.','learning_outcome:LO01'),(118,4,'LO02','learning_outcome',3,'Learning outcome 2','LO2. Critically evaluate the societal, economic, and environmental impacts of digital technologies, considering both benefits and harms.','lo2. critically evaluate the societal, economic, and environmental impacts of digital technologies, considering both benefits and harms.','learning_outcome:LO02'),(119,4,'LO03','learning_outcome',4,'Learning outcome 3','LO3. Apply ethical frameworks and theories to navigate and resolve ethical dilemmas in digital innovation.','lo3. apply ethical frameworks and theories to navigate and resolve ethical dilemmas in digital innovation.','learning_outcome:LO03'),(120,4,'LO04','learning_outcome',5,'Learning outcome 4','LO4. Communicate and collaborate effectively on ethical issues in diverse professional contexts.','lo4. communicate and collaborate effectively on ethical issues in diverse professional contexts.','learning_outcome:LO04'),(121,4,'LO05','learning_outcome',6,'Learning outcome 5','LO5. Make informed decisions that balance technological progress with societal well-being and ethical integrity.','lo5. make informed decisions that balance technological progress with societal well-being and ethical integrity.','learning_outcome:LO05'),(122,4,'AS01','assessment',7,'GenAI Strategy Plan and critically reflect on using GenAI and how it affects learning.','Type: Written work. Description: GenAI Strategy Plan and critically reflect on using GenAI and how it affects learning.','type: written work. description: genai strategy plan and critically reflect on using genai and how it affects learning.','assessment:AS01'),(123,4,'AS02','assessment',8,'Individual assignment Written report','Type: Written work. Description: Individual assignment Written report','type: written work. description: individual assignment written report','assessment:AS02'),(124,4,'AS03','assessment',9,'Group Assignment / Business Presentation Slides and Oral presentation','Type: Interactive oral. Description: Group Assignment / Business Presentation Slides and Oral presentation','type: interactive oral. description: group assignment / business presentation slides and oral presentation','assessment:AS03'),(125,4,'AS04','assessment',10,'Reflective Journal Individual reflective learning journal, stimulated by prompts.','Type: Portfolio or journal. Description: Reflective Journal Individual reflective learning journal, stimulated by prompts.','type: portfolio or journal. description: reflective journal individual reflective learning journal, stimulated by prompts.','assessment:AS04'),(126,4,'AS05','assessment',11,'Group Assignment / Business Report Written report','Type: Written work. Description: Group Assignment / Business Report Written report','type: written work. description: group assignment / business report written report','assessment:AS05'),(127,4,'AD01','assessment_description',12,'Assessment description 1','Individual assignment: This assignment aims to assist students’ development as an independent learner of the knowledge and skills acquired in this unit. Students are to select, analyse and submit a brief business report on a news item for a specific company relevant to this unit.','individual assignment: this assignment aims to assist students\' development as an independent learner of the knowledge and skills acquired in this unit. students are to select, analyse and submit a brief business report on a news item for a specific company relevant to this unit.','assessment_description:AD01'),(128,4,'AD02','assessment_description',13,'Assessment description 2','Group project report: The group project is an applied project aimed at assessing the knowledge acquired in this unit of study. Students will be required to demonstrate their critical thinking and analytical skills to analyse and recommend improvements to real-world businesses.','group project report: the group project is an applied project aimed at assessing the knowledge acquired in this unit of study. students will be required to demonstrate their critical thinking and analytical skills to analyse and recommend improvements to real-world businesses.','assessment_description:AD02'),(129,4,'AD03','assessment_description',14,'Assessment description 3','Group project presentation: The group project presentations are aimed at assessing the level of knowledge acquired in this unit of study. All group members must actively participate in the presentation.','group project presentation: the group project presentations are aimed at assessing the level of knowledge acquired in this unit of study. all group members must actively participate in the presentation.','assessment_description:AD03'),(130,4,'AD04','assessment_description',15,'Assessment description 4','Reflective journal: Individual continuous, reflective journal about the student’s authentic learning experience gleaned from the group project and the in-class activities. While the submission is due in W13, students are encouraged to reflect on weekly prompts by the teaching team, and can discuss their reflections in the weekly consultations. The final deliverable is a written reflective journal of 1500 words (± 10%).','reflective journal: individual continuous, reflective journal about the student\'s authentic learning experience gleaned from the group project and the in-class activities. while the submission is due in w13, students are encouraged to reflect on weekly prompts by the teaching team, and can discuss their reflections in the weekly consultations. the final deliverable is a written reflective journal of 1500 words (± 10%).','assessment_description:AD04'),(131,4,'AD05','assessment_description',16,'Assessment description 5','Generative AI Strategy: By developing a clear strategy for using GenAI tools in assignment work, students will enhance their ability to leverage GenAI for tasks such as identifying literature, structuring ideas, refining text, and fact-checking while ensuring ethical and effective practices. The goal is not just to ensure academic integrity but also to reflect on how GenAI tools shape analytical and critical thinking skills. The deliverable is a 600 word (± 10%) document.','generative ai strategy: by developing a clear strategy for using genai tools in assignment work, students will enhance their ability to leverage genai for tasks such as identifying literature, structuring ideas, refining text, and fact-checking while ensuring ethical and effective practices. the goal is not just to ensure academic integrity but also to reflect on how genai tools shape analytical and critical thinking skills. the deliverable is a 600 word (± 10%) document.','assessment_description:AD05'),(132,4,'AD06','assessment_description',17,'Assessment description 6','Detailed information for each assessment can be found on Canvas.','detailed information for each assessment can be found on canvas.','assessment_description:AD06'),(133,4,'WK01','weekly_schedule',18,'Week 01: Unit introduction','Unit introduction. Learning activity: Lecture (1.5 hr)','unit introduction. learning activity: lecture (1.5 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK01'),(134,4,'WK02','weekly_schedule',19,'Week 01: Warm-Up & Individual Assignment Prep','Warm-Up & Individual Assignment Prep. Learning activity: Tutorial (1.5 hr)','warm-up & individual assignment prep. learning activity: tutorial (1.5 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK02'),(135,4,'WK03','weekly_schedule',20,'Week 02: The Big Picture: Compassionate Digital Innovation','The Big Picture: Compassionate Digital Innovation. Learning activity: Lecture (1.5 hr)','the big picture: compassionate digital innovation. learning activity: lecture (1.5 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK03'),(136,4,'WK04','weekly_schedule',21,'Week 02: Selecting Evidence','Selecting Evidence. Learning activity: Tutorial (1.5 hr)','selecting evidence. learning activity: tutorial (1.5 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK04'),(137,4,'WK05','weekly_schedule',22,'Week 03: Digital Harm Analysis','Digital Harm Analysis. Learning activity: Lecture (1.5 hr)','digital harm analysis. learning activity: lecture (1.5 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK05'),(138,4,'WK06','weekly_schedule',23,'Week 03: Analysing Evidence','Analysing Evidence. Learning activity: Tutorial (1.5 hr)','analysing evidence. learning activity: tutorial (1.5 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK06'),(139,4,'WK07','weekly_schedule',24,'Week 04: Ambivalent Affordances of Digital Technologies','Ambivalent Affordances of Digital Technologies. Learning activity: Lecture (1.5 hr)','ambivalent affordances of digital technologies. learning a