ty: lecture (1.5 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK25'),(275,7,'WK26','weekly_schedule',46,'Week 13: Data Governance Evaluation and Application','Data Governance Evaluation and Application. Learning activity: Tutorial (1.5 hr)','data governance evaluation and application. learning activity: tutorial (1.5 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK26'),(276,8,'OV01','overview',1,'Overview paragraph 1','This unit provides students with an in-depth understanding of the way in which implementation and use of large scale integrated Enterprise Systems change the nature of organisational capabilities, processes, and roles. Students will gain an understanding of the strategic role of Enterprise Systems in providing a platform for improved business operations and designing information infrastructures. In this unit, students will gain considerable hands-on experience with an enterprise-wide system, such as SAP, concentrating on the way in which such systems support integrated business processes. Through a combination of discussion and practical work, students will gain a strong knowledge in both the organisational and technical aspects of Enterprise Systems. Students will also explore the emergence and implications of cloud-based Enterprise Systems and the implementation process. Assumed knowledge for this unit is INFS1000 or equivalent.','this unit provides students with an in-depth understanding of the way in which implementation and use of large scale integrated enterprise systems change the nature of organisational capabilities, processes, and roles. students will gain an understanding of the strategic role of enterprise systems in providing a platform for improved business operations and designing information infrastructures. in this unit, students will gain considerable hands-on experience with an enterprise-wide system, such as sap, concentrating on the way in which such systems support integrated business processes. through a combination of discussion and practical work, students will gain a strong knowledge in both the organisational and technical aspects of enterprise systems. students will also explore the emergence and implications of cloud-based enterprise systems and the implementation process. assumed knowledge for this unit is infs1000 or equivalent.','overview:OV01'),(277,8,'LO01','learning_outcome',2,'Learning outcome 1','LO1. demonstrate your understanding of the integrated nature of Enterprise Systems and their strategic role in providing a platform for improved business operations','lo1. demonstrate your understanding of the integrated nature of enterprise systems and their strategic role in providing a platform for improved business operations','learning_outcome:LO01'),(278,8,'LO02','learning_outcome',3,'Learning outcome 2','LO2. demonstrate your understanding of the role of Enterprise Systems in information infrastructures and evaluate the organisational effects of increasing integration and standardisation','lo2. demonstrate your understanding of the role of enterprise systems in information infrastructures and evaluate the organisational effects of increasing integration and standardisation','learning_outcome:LO02'),(279,8,'LO03','learning_outcome',4,'Learning outcome 3','LO3. demonstrate your understanding of the issues associated with implementing and supporting Enterprise Systems.','lo3. demonstrate your understanding of the issues associated with implementing and supporting enterprise systems.','learning_outcome:LO03'),(280,8,'LO04','learning_outcome',5,'Learning outcome 4','LO4. demonstrate your understanding of the change undergone in organisations during the implementation and use of Enterprise Systems','lo4. demonstrate your understanding of the change undergone in organisations during the implementation and use of enterprise systems','learning_outcome:LO04'),(281,8,'LO05','learning_outcome',6,'Learning outcome 5','LO5. demonstrate your theoretical understanding of the organisational structures, master data and processes within SAP','lo5. demonstrate your theoretical understanding of the organisational structures, master data and processes within sap','learning_outcome:LO05'),(282,8,'LO06','learning_outcome',7,'Learning outcome 6','LO6. demonstrate your hands-on experience in executing transactions and analysing information using SAP','lo6. demonstrate your hands-on experience in executing transactions and analysing information using sap','learning_outcome:LO06'),(283,8,'LO07','learning_outcome',8,'Learning outcome 7','LO7. work both independently and as a responsible member of a diverse team, collaborate and communicate in a professional manner with people from diverse backgrounds.','lo7. work both independently and as a responsible member of a diverse team, collaborate and communicate in a professional manner with people from diverse backgrounds.','learning_outcome:LO07'),(284,8,'AS01','assessment',9,'Final Exam n/a','Type: Written exam. Description: Final Exam n/a','type: written exam. description: final exam n/a','assessment:AS01'),(285,8,'AS02','assessment',10,'Individual assignment n/a','Type: Written work. Description: Individual assignment n/a','type: written work. description: individual assignment n/a','assessment:AS02'),(286,8,'AS03','assessment',11,'Group project n/a','Type: Written work. Description: Group project n/a','type: written work. description: group project n/a','assessment:AS03'),(287,8,'AD01','assessment_description',12,'Assessment description 1','Individual assignment: Based upon a business case and your own independent research, you are required to complete hands-on exercises in SAP and design an SAP organisational structure for an implementation project.','individual assignment: based upon a business case and your own independent research, you are required to complete hands-on exercises in sap and design an sap organisational structure for an implementation project.','assessment_description:AD01'),(288,8,'AD02','assessment_description',13,'Assessment description 2','Group project: Based upon a business case and the group\'s independent research, students are required to analyse an information infrastructure and identify requirements for an Enterprise Systems solution.','group project: based upon a business case and the group\'s independent research, students are required to analyse an information infrastructure and identify requirements for an enterprise systems solution.','assessment_description:AD02'),(289,8,'AD03','assessment_description',14,'Assessment description 3','Final exam: This is a closed book exam. Students will need to demonstrate their understanding of all material covered in the unit of study.','final exam: this is a closed book exam. students will need to demonstrate their understanding of all material covered in the unit of study.','assessment_description:AD03'),(290,8,'AD04','assessment_description',15,'Assessment description 4','Detailed information for each assessment can be found on Canvas.','detailed information for each assessment can be found on canvas.','assessment_description:AD04'),(291,8,'WK01','weekly_schedule',16,'Week 01: Introduction to Business Processes and Enterprise Systems','Introduction to Business Processes and Enterprise Systems. Learning activity: Seminar (3 hr)','introduction to business processes and enterprise systems. learning activity: seminar (3 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK01'),(292,8,'WK02','weekly_schedule',17,'Week 02: Financial accounting 1','Financial accounting 1. Learning activity: Seminar (3 hr)','financial accounting 1. learning activity: seminar (3 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK02'),(293,8,'WK03','weekly_schedule',18,'Week 03: Financial accounting 2','Financial accounting 2. Learning activity: Seminar (3 hr)','financial accounting 2. learning activity: seminar (3 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK03'),(294,8,'WK04','weekly_schedule',19,'Week 04: Procurement 1','Procurement 1. Learning activity: Seminar (3 hr)','procurement 1. learning activity: seminar (3 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK04'),(295,8,'WK05','weekly_schedule',20,'Week 05: Procurement 2','Procurement 2. Learning activity: Seminar (3 hr)','procurement 2. learning activity: seminar (3 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK05'),(296,8,'WK06','weekly_schedule',21,'Week 06: CATWOE 1 & Enterprise Systems and Information Infrastructures','CATWOE 1 & Enterprise Systems and Information Infrastructures. Learning activity: Seminar (3 hr)','catwoe 1 & enterprise systems and information infrastructures. learning activity: seminar (3 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK06'),(297,8,'WK07','weekly_schedule',22,'Week 07: CATWOE 2 & Software Vendor Evaluation','CATWOE 2 & Software Vendor Evaluation. Learning activity: Seminar (3 hr)','catwoe 2 & software vendor evaluation. learning activity: seminar (3 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK07'),(298,8,'WK08','weekly_schedule',23,'Week 08: ES Trends – Cloud Applications','ES Trends – Cloud Applications. Learning activity: Seminar (3 hr)','es trends - cloud applications. learning activity: seminar (3 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK08'),(299,8,'WK09','weekly_schedule',24,'Week 09: Managing ES – Risks and Controls','Managing ES – Risks and Controls. Learning activity: Seminar (3 hr)','managing es - risks and controls. learning activity: seminar (3 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK09'),(300,8,'WK10','weekly_schedule',25,'Week 10: Managing ES Projects','Managing ES Projects. Learning activity: Seminar (3 hr)','managing es projects. learning activity: seminar (3 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK10'),(301,8,'WK11','weekly_schedule',26,'Week 11: Group Assignment Work and Consultations','Group Assignment Work and Consultations. Learning activity: Seminar (3 hr)','group assignment work and consultations. learning activity: seminar (3 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK11'),(302,8,'WK12','weekly_schedule',27,'Week 12: Group Presentations','Group Presentations. Learning activity: Seminar (3 hr)','group presentations. learning activity: seminar (3 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK12'),(303,8,'WK13','weekly_schedule',28,'Week 13: Review and Preparation for the Final Exam','Review and Preparation for the Final Exam. Learning activity: Seminar (3 hr)','review and preparation for the final exam. learning activity: seminar (3 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK13'),(304,9,'OV01','overview',1,'Overview paragraph 1','To gain or maintain their competitive edge, more than ever before, organisations need to rely on high-quality information to support decision making processes at all organisational levels. Business Intelligence (BI) is now being recognised as one of the top business priorities world-wide. While in the past, the term BI was used to describe a very broad range of software applications, the latest thinking in this field emphasises IS support for human intelligence, in the context of business decision making. In this unit, students learn how BI helps information discovery and how to analyse multidimensional data. Students gain hands-on experience in using a commercial BI platform. These practical skills, combined with in-depth analytical skills enable students to assist any organization (regardless of its size and industry domain) to derive more intelligence from its data, improve its performance and ultimately, compete on analytics. Issues are explored from the business rather than the technology perspective. This unit does not require prior programming experience.','to gain or maintain their competitive edge, more than ever before, organisations need to rely on high-quality information to support decision making processes at all organisational levels. business intelligence (bi) is now being recognised as one of the top business priorities world-wide. while in the past, the term bi was used to describe a very broad range of software applications, the latest thinking in this field emphasises is support for human intelligence, in the context of business decision making. in this unit, students learn how bi helps information discovery and how to analyse multidimensional data. students gain hands-on experience in using a commercial bi platform. these practical skills, combined with in-depth analytical skills enable students to assist any organization (regardless of its size and industry domain) to derive more intelligence from its data, improve its performance and ultimately, compete on analytics. issues are explored from the business rather than the technology perspective. this unit does not require prior programming experience.','overview:OV01'),(305,9,'LO01','learning_outcome',2,'Learning outcome 1','LO1. use appropriate conceptual frameworks to analyse the role of different business intelligence applications in supporting day to day business and improving organisational and competitive advantage','lo1. use appropriate conceptual frameworks to analyse the role of different business intelligence applications in supporting day to day business and improving organisational and competitive advantage','learning_outcome:LO01'),(306,9,'LO02','learning_outcome',3,'Learning outcome 2','LO2. describe the organisational issues related to a business intelligence based management approach and propose solutions to overcome the issues','lo2. describe the organisational issues related to a business intelligence based management approach and propose solutions to overcome the issues','learning_outcome:LO02'),(307,9,'LO03','learning_outcome',4,'Learning outcome 3','LO3. design a business intelligence solution to address a business problem using a commercial business intelligence platform','lo3. design a business intelligence solution to address a business problem using a commercial business intelligence platform','learning_outcome:LO03'),(308,9,'LO04','learning_outcome',5,'Learning outcome 4','LO4. relate business intelligence to business performance management, business process management and information management in an enterprise','lo4. relate business intelligence to business performance management, business process management and information management in an enterprise','learning_outcome:LO04'),(309,9,'LO05','learning_outcome',6,'Learning outcome 5','LO5. demonstrate an awareness of the current and emerging trends in business intelligence.','lo5. demonstrate an awareness of the current and emerging trends in business intelligence.','learning_outcome:LO05'),(310,9,'AS01','assessment',7,'Final exam BringYourOwnDevice exam on campus','Type: Written exam. Description: Final exam BringYourOwnDevice exam on campus','type: written exam. description: final exam bringyourowndevice exam on campus','assessment:AS01'),(311,9,'AS02','assessment',8,'Tutorial work 1 Tableau tutorial 1 - multiple due dates','Type: Data analysis. Description: Tutorial work 1 Tableau tutorial 1 - multiple due dates','type: data analysis. description: tutorial work 1 tableau tutorial 1 - multiple due dates','assessment:AS02'),(312,9,'AS03','assessment',9,'Tutorial work 2 Tableau tutorial 2 - multiple due dates','Type: Data analysis. Description: Tutorial work 2 Tableau tutorial 2 - multiple due dates','type: data analysis. description: tutorial work 2 tableau tutorial 2 - multiple due dates','assessment:AS03'),(313,9,'AS04','assessment',10,'Mid-semester exam BringYourOwnDevice exam on campus','Type: Written test. Description: Mid-semester exam BringYourOwnDevice exam on campus','type: written test. description: mid-semester exam bringyourowndevice exam on campus','assessment:AS04'),(314,9,'AS05','assessment',11,'Practical Assignment - Data Visualisation Solution and Reflection Analysing the BI process and data visualisation using Tableau','Type: Data analysis. Description: Practical Assignment - Data Visualisation Solution and Reflection Analysing the BI process and data visualisation using Tableau','type: data analysis. description: practical assignment - data visualisation solution and reflection analysing the bi process and data visualisation using tableau','assessment:AS05'),(315,9,'AS06','assessment',12,'Practical Assignment - Presentation Analysing the BI process and data visualisation using Tableau','Type: Presentation. Description: Practical Assignment - Presentation Analysing the BI process and data visualisation using Tableau','type: presentation. description: practical assignment - presentation analysing the bi process and data visualisation using tableau','assessment:AS06'),(316,9,'AD01','assessment_description',13,'Assessment description 1','Tutorial work 1 and 2: Students are expected to demonstrate the understanding of the basics of using Tableau and designing a visualisation solution. The tutorials are done during normal class time and must be submitted by the end of the class time.','tutorial work 1 and 2: students are expected to demonstrate the understanding of the basics of using tableau and designing a visualisation solution. the tutorials are done during normal class time and must be submitted by the end of the class time.','assessment_description:AD01'),(317,9,'AD02','assessment_description',14,'Assessment description 2','Mid-semester exam: This exam tests the understanding of the foundational business intelligence concepts.','mid-semester exam: this exam tests the understanding of the foundational business intelligence concepts.','assessment_description:AD02'),(318,9,'AD03','assessment_description',15,'Assessment description 3','Practical assignment: Students are required to develop a data visualisation solution to address a business problem using Tableau. A data set will be provided to students. Each group will present their results in the Campus sessions on week 12.','practical assignment: students are required to develop a data visualisation solution to address a business problem using tableau. a data set will be provided to students. each group will present their results in the campus sessions on week 12.','assessment_description:AD03'),(319,9,'AD04','assessment_description',16,'Assessment description 4','Final exam: The final exam tests the understanding of business intelligence concepts and frameworks in an organisational context. This exam covers all the unit materials. Students will be assessed in a Bring Your Own Device (BYOD) exam taken on campus with supervision. Further information about the delivery of the exams will be provided closer to the test exam.','final exam: the final exam tests the understanding of business intelligence concepts and frameworks in an organisational context. this exam covers all the unit materials. students will be assessed in a bring your own device (byod) exam taken on campus with supervision. further information about the delivery of the exams will be provided closer to the test exam.','assessment_description:AD04'),(320,9,'AD05','assessment_description',17,'Assessment description 5','Detailed information for each assessment can be found on Canvas.','detailed information for each assessment can be found on canvas.','assessment_description:AD05'),(321,9,'WK01','weekly_schedule',18,'Week 01: Introduction to unit of study','Introduction to unit of study. Learning activity: Seminar (3 hr)','introduction to unit of study. learning activity: seminar (3 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK01'),(322,9,'WK02','weekly_schedule',19,'Week 02: Foundations for understanding business intelligence','Foundations for understanding business intelligence. Learning activity: Seminar (3 hr)','foundations for understanding business intelligence. learning activity: seminar (3 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK02'),(323,9,'WK03','weekly_schedule',20,'Week 03: Data Warehousing: the business perspective','Data Warehousing: the business perspective. Learning activity: Seminar (3 hr)','data warehousing: the business perspective. learning activity: seminar (3 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK03'),(324,9,'WK04','weekly_schedule',21,'Week 04: Data quality and value of information','Data quality and value of information. Learning activity: Seminar (3 hr)','data quality and value of information. learning activity: seminar (3 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK04'),(325,9,'WK05','weekly_schedule',22,'Week 05: Information discovery and decision making','Information discovery and decision making. Learning activity: Seminar (3 hr)','information discovery and decision making. learning activity: seminar (3 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK05'),(326,9,'WK06','weekly_schedule',23,'Week 06: Designing business intelligence solutions','Designing business intelligence solutions. Learning activity: Seminar (3 hr)','designing business intelligence solutions. learning activity: seminar (3 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK06'),(327,9,'WK07','weekly_schedule',24,'Week 07: Preparation for the mid semester exam and comprehensive case discussion','Preparation for the mid semester exam and comprehensive case discussion. Learning activity: Seminar (3 hr)','preparation for the mid semester exam and comprehensive case discussion. learning activity: seminar (3 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK07'),(328,9,'WK08','weekly_schedule',25,'Week 08: Mid-semester exam','Mid-semester exam. Learning activity: Seminar (1 hr)','mid-semester exam. learning activity: seminar (1 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK08'),(329,9,'WK09','weekly_schedule',26,'Week 09: Multi-dimensional modeling, OLAP and ethics','Multi-dimensional modeling, OLAP and ethics. Learning activity: Seminar (3 hr)','multi-dimensional modeling, olap and ethics. learning activity: seminar (3 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK09'),(330,9,'WK10','weekly_schedule',27,'Week 10: Business performance management: the role of business intelligence and data visualisation. AI Support for Decision Making.','Business performance management: the role of business intelligence and data visualisation. AI Support for Decision Making.. Learning activity: Seminar (3 hr)','business performance management: the role of business intelligence and data visualisation. ai support for decision making.. learning activity: seminar (3 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK10'),(331,9,'WK11','weekly_schedule',28,'Week 11: Group project work and consultations','Group project work and consultations. Learning activity: Seminar (3 hr)','group project work and consultations. learning activity: seminar (3 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK11'),(332,9,'WK12','weekly_schedule',29,'Week 12: Group presentations','Group presentations. Learning activity: Seminar (3 hr)','group presentations. learning activity: seminar (3 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK12'),(333,9,'WK13','weekly_schedule',30,'Week 13: Preparation for the final exam','Preparation for the final exam. Learning activity: Seminar (3 hr)','preparation for the final exam. learning activity: seminar (3 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK13'),(334,10,'OV01','overview',1,'Overview paragraph 1','This unit provides an in-depth understanding of the role of business processes in effectively and efficiently managing business operations. Students gain essential skills of the entire Business Process Management (BPM) lifecycle, from process identification and design to process monitoring, including process modelling, analysis, redesign, and automation required to achieve high performance and deliver the strategy in a service-oriented environment. Students also gain highly sought after practical skills of using BPM tools to recommend improvements by documenting and simulating current and new processes.','this unit provides an in-depth understanding of the role of business processes in effectively and efficiently managing business operations. students gain essential skills of the entire business process management (bpm) lifecycle, from process identification and design to process monitoring, including process modelling, analysis, redesign, and automation required to achieve high performance and deliver the strategy in a service-oriented environment. students also gain highly sought after practical skills of using bpm tools to recommend improvements by documenting and simulating current and new processes.','overview:OV01'),(335,10,'LO01','learning_outcome',2,'Learning outcome 1','LO1. Discuss the role of Business Process Management (BPM) in a business environment and how BPM initiatives contribute to improving the overall business performance','lo1. discuss the role of business process management (bpm) in a business environment and how bpm initiatives contribute to improving the overall business performance','learning_outcome:LO01'),(336,10,'LO02','learning_outcome',3,'Learning outcome 2','LO2. Apply the BPM principles, concepts, and frameworks to business problems and practice as captured in the BPM lifecycle','lo2. apply the bpm principles, concepts, and frameworks to business problems and practice as captured in the bpm lifecycle','learning_outcome:LO02'),(337,10,'LO03','learning_outcome',4,'Learning outcome 3','LO3. Address the issues and challenges associated with process improvement initiatives in organisations','lo3. address the issues and challenges associated with process improvement initiatives in organisations','learning_outcome:LO03'),(338,10,'LO04','learning_outcome',5,'Learning outcome 4','LO4. Evaluate the impact of process design and redesign decisions on stakeholders and the role of change management in addressing the risks associated with such changes in organisations','lo4. evaluate the impact of process design and redesign decisions on stakeholders and the role of change management in addressing the risks associated with such changes in organisations','learning_outcome:LO04'),(339,10,'LO05','learning_outcome',6,'Learning outcome 5','LO5. Use BPM tools to model, document, and analyse processes during the BPM lifecycle stages','lo5. use bpm tools to model, document, and analyse processes during the bpm lifecycle stages','learning_outcome:LO05'),(340,10,'LO06','learning_outcome',7,'Learning outcome 6','LO6. Work independently, collaborate, and communicate in a professional manner with people from diverse backgrounds within a team work environment','lo6. work independently, collaborate, and communicate in a professional manner with people from diverse backgrounds within a team work environment','learning_outcome:LO06'),(341,10,'AS01','assessment',8,'Final Exam Written exam','Type: Written exam. Description: Final Exam Written exam','type: written exam. description: final exam written exam','assessment:AS01'),(342,10,'AS02','assessment',9,'Individual Assignment Written submission','Type: Case studies. Description: Individual Assignment Written submission','type: case studies. description: individual assignment written submission','assessment:AS02'),(343,10,'AS03','assessment',10,'Group Plan Pitch (5 min) Presentation & Submission','Type: Case studies. Description: Group Plan Pitch (5 min) Presentation & Submission','type: case studies. description: group plan pitch (5 min) presentation & submission','assessment:AS03'),(344,10,'AS04','assessment',11,'Group Project Group Report Written Submission','Type: Case studies. Description: Group Project Group Report Written Submission','type: case studies. description: group project group report written submission','assessment:AS04'),(345,10,'AD01','assessment_description',12,'Assessment description 1','Individual assignment: In this assignment students will take the role of the process analyst and engage in process discovery and analysis within a given business case context.','individual assignment: in this assignment students will take the role of the process analyst and engage in process discovery and analysis within a given business case context.','assessment_description:AD01'),(346,10,'AD02','assessment_description',13,'Assessment description 2','Group Plan assignment: In this assignment students will analyse the market and identify new services to be executed via new and modified business processes. Students will also develop a project plan to guide the project execution. Students will present and make a written submission.','group plan assignment: in this assignment students will analyse the market and identify new services to be executed via new and modified business processes. students will also develop a project plan to guide the project execution. students will present and make a written submission.','assessment_description:AD02'),(347,10,'AD03','assessment_description',14,'Assessment description 3','Group Report assignment: In this assignment students will design new processes following the services proposed in the Group Plan assignment. Students will assess the feasibility of the new processes, the resources required, and the challenges encountered during process implementation. Students will use Signavio (BPM tool) to document, simulate and analyse the new business processes. Students will present a summary of the findings and recommendations.','group report assignment: in this assignment students will design new processes following the services proposed in the group plan assignment. students will assess the feasibility of the new processes, the resources required, and the challenges encountered during process implementation. students will use signavio (bpm tool) to document, simulate and analyse the new business processes. students will present a summary of the findings and recommendations.','assessment_description:AD03'),(348,10,'AD04','assessment_description',15,'Assessment description 4','Final exam: A supervised exam that will test students theoretical understanding, critical thinking, and ability to apply and evaluate BPM concepts and principles in practice.','final exam: a supervised exam that will test students theoretical understanding, critical thinking, and ability to apply and evaluate bpm concepts and principles in practice.','assessment_description:AD04'),(349,10,'AD05','assessment_description',16,'Assessment description 5','Detailed information for each assessment will be released as appropiate on Canvas.','detailed information for each assessment will be released as appropiate on canvas.','assessment_description:AD05'),(350,10,'WK01','weekly_schedule',17,'Week 01: Introduction to the Unit and Business Process Management (BPM)','Introduction to the Unit and Business Process Management (BPM). Learning activity: Seminar (3 hr)','introduction to the unit and business process management (bpm). learning activity: seminar (3 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK01'),(351,10,'WK02','weekly_schedule',18,'Week 02: Process identification','Process identification. Learning activity: Seminar (3 hr)','process identification. learning activity: seminar (3 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK02'),(352,10,'WK03','weekly_schedule',19,'Week 03: Process discovery','Process discovery. Learning activity: Seminar (3 hr)','process discovery. learning activity: seminar (3 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK03'),(353,10,'WK04','weekly_schedule',20,'Week 04: Process modelling (1) - BPMN Notation','Process modelling (1) - BPMN Notation. Learning activity: Seminar (3 hr)','process modelling (1) - bpmn notation. learning activity: seminar (3 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK04'),(354,10,'WK05','weekly_schedule',21,'Week 05: Process modelling (2) - As-Is Modelling using BPMN and Signavio','Process modelling (2) - As-Is Modelling using BPMN and Signavio. Learning activity: Seminar (3 hr)','process modelling (2) - as-is modelling using bpmn and signavio. learning activity: seminar (3 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK05'),(355,10,'WK06','weekly_schedule',22,'Week 06: Process analysis (1) (qualitative)','Process analysis (1) (qualitative). Learning activity: Seminar (3 hr)','process analysis (1) (qualitative). learning activity: seminar (3 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK06'),(356,10,'WK07','weekly_schedule',23,'Week 07: Process analysis (2) (quantitative): As-Is Simulation using Signavio','Process analysis (2) (quantitative): As-Is Simulation using Signavio. Learning activity: Seminar (3 hr)','process analysis (2) (quantitative): as-is simulation using signavio. learning activity: seminar (3 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK07'),(357,10,'WK08','weekly_schedule',24,'Week 08: Process improvement (1) - Redesign heuristics','Process improvement (1) - Redesign heuristics. Learning activity: Seminar (3 hr)','process improvement (1) - redesign heuristics. learning activity: seminar (3 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK08'),(358,10,'WK09','weekly_schedule',25,'Week 09: Group plan presentations - Feedback collection','Group plan presentations - Feedback collection. Learning activity: Seminar (3 hr)','group plan presentations - feedback collection. learning activity: seminar (3 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK09'),(359,10,'WK10','weekly_schedule',26,'Week 10: Process improvement (2) - To-Be Simulation using Signavio','Process improvement (2) - To-Be Simulation using Signavio. Learning activity: Seminar (3 hr)','process improvement (2) - to-be simulation using signavio. learning activity: seminar (3 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK10'),(360,10,'WK11','weekly_schedule',27,'Week 11: Process implementation, monitoring and mining','Process implementation, monitoring and mining. Learning activity: Seminar (3 hr)','process implementation, monitoring and mining. learning activity: seminar (3 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK11'),(361,10,'WK12','weekly_schedule',28,'Week 12: Emerging topics in BPM; Group project consultation','Emerging topics in BPM; Group project consultation. Learning activity: Seminar (3 hr)','emerging topics in bpm; group project consultation. learning activity: seminar (3 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK12'),(362,10,'WK13','weekly_schedule',29,'Week 13: Unit Review and Final Exam Practice','Unit Review and Final Exam Practice. Learning activity: Seminar (3 hr)','unit review and final exam practice. learning activity: seminar (3 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK13'),(363,11,'OV01','overview',1,'Overview paragraph 1','This unit provides students with the opportunity to address complex problems identified by industry, community, and government organisations. With mentorship from a major industry partner and an academic lead, students integrate their academic skills and knowledge by working in diverse teams across disciplinary boundaries. Students research, analyse and present solutions to a real-world problem, and build on their interpersonal and transferable skills by engaging with and learning from experts in the field. See the ICPU website for further information here: https://www.sydney.edu.au/students/industry-and-community-projects.html.','this unit provides students with the opportunity to address complex problems identified by industry, community, and government organisations. with mentorship from a major industry partner and an academic lead, students integrate their academic skills and knowledge by working in diverse teams across disciplinary boundaries. students research, analyse and present solutions to a real-world problem, and build on their interpersonal and transferable skills by engaging with and learning from experts in the field. see the icpu website for further information here: https://www.sydney.edu.au/students/industry-and-community-projects.html.','overview:OV01'),(364,11,'LO01','learning_outcome',2,'Learning outcome 1','LO1. Demonstrate critical awareness of, and apply, disciplinary knowledge, skills and personal attributes to address complex real-world problems','lo1. demonstrate critical awareness of, and apply, disciplinary knowledge, skills and personal attributes to address complex real-world problems','learning_outcome:LO01'),(365,11,'LO02','learning_outcome',3,'Learning outcome 2','LO2. Assess and integrate diverse stakeholder perspectives to generate innovative insights into complex problems','lo2. assess and integrate diverse stakeholder perspectives to generate innovative insights into complex problems','learning_outcome:LO02'),(366,11,'LO03','learning_outcome',4,'Learning outcome 3','LO3. Purposefully select and apply complex problem-solving approaches and methods','lo3. purposefully select and apply complex problem-solving approaches and methods','learning_outcome:LO03'),(367,11,'LO04','learning_outcome',5,'Learning outcome 4','LO4. Communicate novel ideas effectively and persuasively in professional settings using relevant media','lo4. communicate novel ideas effectively and persuasively in professional settings using relevant media','learning_outcome:LO04'),(368,11,'LO05','learning_outcome',6,'Learning outcome 5','LO5. Demonstrate professionalism (proficiency, adaptivity, and proactivity) in collaborative project work','lo5. demonstrate professionalism (proficiency, adaptivity, and proactivity) in collaborative project work','learning_outcome:LO05'),(369,11,'AS01','assessment',7,'Participation Compulsory 90% class participation','Type: Contribution. Description: Participation Compulsory 90% class participation','type: contribution. description: participation compulsory 90% class participation','assessment:AS01'),(370,11,'AS02','assessment',8,'Individual Statement Instalment 1 Written task','Type: Portfolio or journal. Description: Individual Statement Instalment 1 Written task','type: portfolio or journal. description: individual statement instalment 1 written task','assessment:AS02'),(371,11,'AS03','assessment',9,'Group Plan Research plan','Type: Written work. Description: Group Plan Research plan','type: written work. description: group plan research plan','assessment:AS03'),(372,11,'AS04','assessment',10,'Individual Statement Instalment 2 Written task','Type: Portfolio or journal. Description: Individual Statement Instalment 2 Written task','type: portfolio or journal. description: individual statement instalment 2 written task','assessment:AS04'),(373,11,'AS05','assessment',11,'Group Presentation Oral presentation inclusive of 300-word or equivalent Executive summary','Type: Presentation. Description: Group Presentation Oral presentation inclusive of 300-word or equivalent Executive summary','type: presentation. description: group presentation oral presentation inclusive of 300-word or equivalent executive summary','assessment:AS05'),(374,11,'AS06','assessment',12,'Group Project Report Report','Type: Written work. Description: Group Project Report Report','type: written work. description: group project report report','assessment:AS06'),(375,11,'AS07','assessment',13,'Group Work Survey Questionnaire','Type: Evaluation. Description: Group Work Survey Questionnaire','type: evaluation. description: group work survey questionnaire','assessment:AS07'),(376,11,'AD01','assessment_description',14,'Assessment description 1','Individual Statements aims to analyse and reflect on students’ own and other members’ ways of contributing to their work on this project.','individual statements aims to analyse and reflect on students\' own and other members\' ways of contributing to their work on this project.','assessment_description:AD01'),(377,11,'AD02','assessment_description',15,'Assessment description 2','Group Plan aims to articulate the issues the group will address and develop a project plan.','group plan aims to articulate the issues the group will address and develop a project plan.','assessment_description:AD02'),(378,11,'AD03','assessment_description',16,'Assessment description 3','Group Presentation including Executive Summary aims to present students’ work and findings to the project partner.','group presentation including executive summary aims to present students\' work and findings to the project partner.','assessment_description:AD03'),(379,11,'AD04','assessment_description',17,'Assessment description 4','Group Project Report aims to conduct in depth analysis/es and research, discuss the results, and provide recommendations or solutions to the issues outlined in the group plan.','group project report aims to conduct in depth analysis/es and research, discuss the results, and provide recommendations or solutions to the issues outlined in the group plan.','assessment_description:AD04'),(380,11,'AD05','assessment_description',18,'Assessment description 5','Group Work Survey aims to evaluate student’s contributions relative to the contributions of other team members.','group work survey aims to evaluate student\'s contributions relative to the contributions of other team members.','assessment_description:AD05'),(381,11,'AD06','assessment_description',19,'Assessment description 6','Participation aims to ensure active participation by all team members for the project work.','participation aims to ensure active participation by all team members for the project work.','assessment_description:AD06'),(382,11,'AD07','assessment_description',20,'Assessment description 7','Detailed information for each assessment can be found on Canvas.','detailed information for each assessment can be found on canvas.','assessment_description:AD07'),(383,11,'AD08','assessment_description',21,'Assessment description 8','Individual contributions to group assessments may adjust the final grade that a student receives, through what is known as a Relative Performance Factor. Please see Canvas Assignment page for more details.','individual contributions to group assessments may adjust the final grade that a student receives, through what is known as a relative performance factor. please see canvas assignment page for more details.','assessment_description:AD08'),(384,11,'AD09','assessment_description',22,'Assessment description 9','Using AI in ICPU','using ai in icpu','assessment_description:AD09'),(385,11,'AD10','assessment_description',23,'Assessment description 10','The Use of Generative AI across multiple sectors of work is increasing exponentially. While use of these tools brings new opportunities such as increased productivity, there are also many potential limitations such as inhibiting the development of analytical and creative thinking skills. Importantly, in ICPU where 80% of assessments are group-based, your use of AI tools must also be negotiated collegially and adhere to the Student Charter 2020, including upholding honesty, ethics, professionalism, and academic integrity (please ensure you are familiar with the updated Academic Integrity 2022 policy).','the use of generative ai across multiple sectors of work is increasing exponentially. while use of these tools brings new opportunities such as increased productivity, there are also many potential limitations such as inhibiting the development of analytical and creative thinking skills. importantly, in icpu where 80% of assessments are group-based, your use of ai tools must also be negotiated collegially and adhere to the student charter 2020, including upholding honesty, ethics, professionalism, and academic integrity (please ensure you are familiar with the updated academic integrity 2022 policy).','assessment_description:AD10'),(386,11,'AD11','assessment_description',24,'Assessment description 11','AI tools permitted','ai tools permitted','assessment_description:AD11'),(387,11,'AD12','assessment_description',25,'Assessment description 12','You are permitted to use automated writing tools and generative artificial intelligence (AI) to facilitate your learning and completion of this assignment in individual and group project work. Please adhere to the following guidelines:','you are permitted to use automated writing tools and generative artificial intelligence (ai) to facilitate your learning and completion of this assignment in individual and group project work. please adhere to the following guidelines:','assessment_description:AD12'),(388,11,'AD13','assessment_description',26,'Assessment description 13','Do not enter confidential, personal, copyrighted or otherwise sensitive information into any AI tool, including but not limited to materials shared by industry and/or community partners (noting also the confidentiality clauses that apply in the Student Deed Poll)','do not enter confidential, personal, copyrighted or otherwise sensitive information into any ai tool, including but not limited to materials shared by industry and/or community partners (noting also the confidentiality clauses that apply in the student deed poll)','assessment_description:AD13'),(389,11,'AD14','assessment_description',27,'Assessment description 14','If you use these tools, you must be aware of their limitations, biases, and propensity for fabrication','if you use these tools, you must be aware of their limitations, biases, and propensity for fabrication','assessment_description:AD14'),(390,11,'AD15','assessment_description',28,'Assessment description 15','Do not rely on the accuracy of outputs. You remain responsible for your work. This means you must independently verify and edit AI-generated content to ensure the integrity, accuracy, and suitability of the output','do not rely on the accuracy of outputs. you remain responsible for your work. this means you must independently verify and edit ai-generated content to ensure the integrity, accuracy, and suitability of the output','assessment_description:AD15'),(391,11,'AD16','assessment_description',29,'Assessment description 16','While there are many AI tools available, both free and paid, we strongly recommend the use of tools endorsed by the University such as Microsoft Copilot, Cogniti and Adobe Firefly. For a list of AI tools and their uses, see the Different Generative AI Tools page on the AI in Education Canvas site.','while there are many ai tools available, both free and paid, we strongly recommend the use of tools endorsed by the university such as microsoft copilot, cogniti and adobe firefly. for a list of ai tools and their uses, see the different generative ai tools page on the ai in education canvas site.','assessment_description:AD16'),(392,11,'AD17','assessment_description',30,'Assessment description 17','Where AI is used, you are advised to keep copies of the prompts you provided and AI outputs as evidence of your research and writing process. This allows you to produce an accurate acknowledgement of AI use when you submit your work, see guidance below. This can be requested by the unit coordinator if there is any uncertainty about the originality of your work.','where ai is used, you are advised to keep copies of the prompts you provided and ai outputs as evidence of your research and writing process. this allows you to produce an accurate acknowledgement of ai use when you submit your work, see guidance below. this can be requested by the unit coordinator if there is any uncertainty about the originality of your work.','assessment_description:AD17'),(393,11,'AD18','assessment_description',31,'Assessment description 18','Acknowledging the use of AI','acknowledging the use of ai','assessment_description:AD18'),(394,11,'AD19','assessment_description',32,'Assessment description 19','It is not appropriate to copy-paste AI-generated responses directly as part of your own writing since the work you submit should reflect the understanding you have acquired, your critical engagement with the material and your process of continuous revision and improvement.','it is not appropriate to copy-paste ai-generated responses directly as part of your own writing since the work you submit should reflect the understanding you have acquired, your critical engagement with the material and your process of continuous revision and improvement.','assessment_description:AD19'),(395,11,'AD20','assessment_description',33,'Assessment description 20','Where AI is used, you are advised to keep copies of the prompts you provided and AI outputs as evidence of your research and writing process. This allows you to produce an accurate acknowledgement of AI use when you submit your work, see wording below. This can be requested by the unit coordinator if there is any uncertainty about the originality of your work.','where ai is used, you are advised to keep copies of the prompts you provided and ai outputs as evidence of your research and writing process. this allows you to produce an accurate acknowledgement of ai use when you submit your work, see wording below. this can be requested by the unit coordinator if there is any uncertainty about the originality of your work.','assessment_description:AD20'),(396,11,'AD21','assessment_description',34,'Assessment description 21','You must acknowledge any uses of AI by inserting a note at the end of your submission where you need to describe the tool(s) that you used, what prompt(s) you provided, how the output of the artificial intelligence was used or adapted by you, and how you verified sources or information if applicable. This additional description does not add to your word count. An example of such an acknowledgement that you may provide might look like:','you must acknowledge any uses of ai by inserting a note at the end of your submission where you need to describe the tool(s) that you used, what prompt(s) you provided, how the output of the artificial intelligence was used or adapted by you, and how you verified sources or information if applicable. this additional description does not add to your word count. an example of such an acknowledgement that you may provide might look like:','assessment_description:AD21'),(397,11,'AD22','assessment_description',35,'Assessment description 22','I acknowledge the use of ChatGPT (https://chat.openai.com/) to refine the academic language of my own work. On date I submitted my entire essay (link to original document here) with the prompt to <“Improve the academic tone and accuracy of language, including grammatical structures, punctuation and vocabulary”>. The output (link here) was then modified further to better represent my own tone and style of writing. One of the limitations I noted was insert limitation and I revised my assessment to address this limitation by insert response.','i acknowledge the use of chatgpt (https://chat.openai.com/) to refine the academic language of my own work. on date i submitted my entire essay (link to original document here) with the prompt to <“improve the academic tone and accuracy of language, including grammatical structures, punctuation and vocabulary”>. the output (link here) was then modified further to better represent my own tone and style of writing. one of the limitations i noted was insert limitation and i revised my assessment to address this limitation by insert response.','assessment_description:AD22'),(398,11,'AD23','assessment_description',36,'Assessment description 23','Please note, your project supervisor may require you to provide a written statement if you would like to use AI heavily in your work, (i.e. for multiple approved uses above or heavy use within any individual use categories), a different approach may be needed including clearly stating the percentage of work attributed to AI for each assessment. If you are unsure or have any concerns, please discuss these with your Project Supervisor in advance. In all cases, individual group members must be transparent with their group members about intended use of generative AI in groupwork.','please note, your project supervisor may require you to provide a written statement if you would like to use ai heavily in your work, (i.e. for multiple approved uses above or heavy use within any individual use categories), a different approach may be needed including clearly stating the percentage of work attributed to ai for each assessment. if you are unsure or have any concerns, please discuss these with your project supervisor in advance. in all cases, individual group members must be transparent with their group members about intended use of generative ai in groupwork.','assessment_description:AD23'),(399,11,'WK01','weekly_schedule',37,'Weekly: See Canvas site for detailed project schedule','See Canvas site for detailed project schedule. Learning activity: Lecture (1 hr)','see canvas site for detailed project schedule. learning activity: lecture (1 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK01'),(400,11,'WK02','weekly_schedule',38,'Weekly: See Canvas site for detailed project schedule','See Canvas site for detailed project schedule. Learning activity: Tutorial (2 hr)','see canvas site for detailed project schedule. learning activity: tutorial (2 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK02'),(401,12,'OV01','overview',1,'Overview paragraph 1','This capstone unit bridges the gap between theory and practice by integrating knowledge and consolidating key skills developed across the Business Information Systems major. It aims to provide students with practical experience in identifying, analysing, and solving contemporary business problems. Much of this unit is dedicated to a problem-solving, experiential approach to learning. Students ensure their career-readiness by demonstrating their ability to apply concepts, theories, frameworks, methodologies, and skills to authentic problems and challenges faced in the field of information systems.','this capstone unit bridges the gap between theory and practice by integrating knowledge and consolidating key skills developed across the business information systems major. it aims to provide students with practical experience in identifying, analysing, and solving contemporary business problems. much of this unit is dedicated to a problem-solving, experiential approach to learning. students ensure their career-readiness by demonstrating their ability to apply concepts, theories, frameworks, methodologies, and skills to authentic problems and challenges faced in the field of information systems.','overview:OV01'),(402,12,'LO01','learning_outcome',2,'Learning outcome 1','LO1. apply and relate information systems theories and concepts in the context of an actual business problem with societal relevance','lo1. apply and relate information systems theories and concepts in the context of an actual business problem with societal relevance','learning_outcome:LO01'),(403,12,'LO02','learning_outcome',3,'Learning outcome 2','LO2. analyse open-ended business scenarios and evaluate the implications of information systems decisions','lo2. analyse open-ended business scenarios and evaluate the implications of information systems decisions','learning_outcome:LO02'),(404,12,'LO03','learning_outcome',4,'Learning outcome 3','LO3. apply techniques for organisational and business process analyses to resolve an actual business problem','lo3. apply techniques for organisational and business process analyses to resolve an actual business problem','learning_outcome:LO03'),(405,12,'LO04','learning_outcome',5,'Learning outcome 4','LO4. communicate in a professional and confident manner, both orally and in writing, with actual business professionals','lo4. communicate in a professional and confident manner, both orally and in writing, with actual business professionals','learning_outcome:LO04'),(406,12,'LO05','learning_outcome',6,'Learning outcome 5','LO5. apply team management concepts and theories to effectively work in, and manage, cross-functional teams','lo5. apply team management concepts and theories to effectively work in, and manage, cross-functional teams','learning_outcome:LO05'),(407,12,'LO06','learning_outcome',7,'Learning outcome 6','LO6. analyse and reflect critically on the ethical and social implications of information systems.','lo6. analyse and reflect critically on the ethical and social implications of information systems.','learning_outcome:LO06'),(408,12,'AS01','assessment',8,'Generative AI Strategy Plan and critically reflect on using GenAI and how it affects learning.','Type: Written work. Description: Generative AI Strategy Plan and critically reflect on using GenAI and how it affects learning.','type: written work. description: generative ai strategy plan and critically reflect on using genai and how it affects learning.','assessment:AS01'),(409,12,'AS02','assessment',9,'Individual progress report and viva Students submit an individual role-based progress report, assessed through a supervised in-class viva where verified students explain and defend their work. Consultation schedules are on Canvas; the submission deadline is Week 13.','Type: In-person written or creative task. Description: Individual progress report and viva Students submit an individual role-based progress report, assessed through a supervised in-class viva where verified students explain and defend their work. Consultation schedules are on Canvas; the submission deadline is Week 13.','type: in-person written or creative task. description: individual progress report and viva students submit an individual role-based progress report, assessed through a supervised in-class viva where verified students explain and defend their work. consultation schedules are on canvas; the submission deadline is week 13.','assessment:AS02'),(410,12,'AS03','assessment',10,'Group project presentation Students deliver a prepared presentation, followed by a supervised in-class Q&A. During the Q&A, verified students respond to teaching staff questions under supervision and without unapproved external assistance.','Type: Q&A following presentation, submission or placement. Description: Group project presentation Students deliver a prepared presentation, followed by a supervised in-class Q&A. During the Q&A, verified students respond to teaching staff questions under supervision and without unapproved external assistance.','type: q&a following presentation, submission or placement. description: group project presentation students deliver a prepared presentation, followed by a supervised in-class q&a. during the q&a, verified students respond to teaching staff questions under supervision and without unapproved external assistance.','assessment:AS03'),(411,12,'AS04','assessment',11,'Reflective Journal Individual, continuous, reflective learning journal, stimulated by prompts.','Type: Portfolio or journal. Description: Reflective Journal Individual, continuous, reflective learning journal, stimulated by prompts.','type: portfolio or journal. description: reflective journal individual, continuous, reflective learning journal, stimulated by prompts.','assessment:AS04'),(412,12,'AS05','assessment',12,'Group assignment Written report','Type: Written work. Description: Group assignment Written report','type: written work. description: group assignment written report','assessment:AS05'),(413,12,'AD01','assessment_description',13,'Assessment description 1','Individual assignment: This assignment is in the form of an individual progress report that corresponds to a specific section of the group project. The content of this report will vary depending on the student\'s designated role within the project team. The report comprises 1500 (± 10%) words and associated discussions during the group consultation sessions.','individual assignment: this assignment is in the form of an individual progress report that corresponds to a specific section of the group project. the content of this report will vary depending on the student\'s designated role within the project team. the report comprises 1500 (± 10%) words and associated discussions during the group consultation sessions.','assessment_description:AD01'),(414,12,'AD02','assessment_description',14,'Assessment description 2','Group assignment: This assessment item requires students to work within their project groups to analyse and provide recommendations for resolving a business problem of an actual client. Each project group will be expected to look for and acquire their own client, and design a technology-enabled solution that will improve a substantive business process of the client. The deliverables of the project include a 15 minute presentation and a project report of 6000 (± 10%) words.','group assignment: this assessment item requires students to work within their project groups to analyse and provide recommendations for resolving a business problem of an actual client. each project group will be expected to look for and acquire their own client, and design a technology-enabled solution that will improve a substantive business process of the client. the deliverables of the project include a 15 minute presentation and a project report of 6000 (± 10%) words.','assessment_description:AD02'),(415,12,'AD03','assessment_description',15,'Assessment description 3','Reflective journal: Individual, continuous, reflective journal about the student’s authentic learning experience gleaned from the group project and the in-class activities. The student will draft the reflective journal continuously in Canvas and the teaching team will ask them 4-5 ‘provocative’ questions to prompt their critical reflection throughout the semester. The final deliverable is a written reflective journal of 1500 words (± 10%).','reflective journal: individual, continuous, reflective journal about the student\'s authentic learning experience gleaned from the group project and the in-class activities. the student will draft the reflective journal continuously in canvas and the teaching team will ask them 4-5 \'provocative\' questions to prompt their critical reflection throughout the semester. the final deliverable is a written reflective journal of 1500 words (± 10%).','assessment_description:AD03'),(416,12,'AD04','assessment_description',16,'Assessment description 4','Generative AI Strategy: By developing a clear strategy for using GenAI tools in assignment work, students will enhance their ability to leverage GenAI for tasks such as identifying literature, structuring ideas, refining text, and fact-checking while ensuring ethical and effective practices. The goal is not just to ensure academic integrity but also to reflect on how GenAI tools shape analytical and critical thinking skills. The deliverable is a 600 word (± 10%) document.','generative ai strategy: by developing a clear strategy for using genai tools in assignment work, students will enhance their ability to leverage genai for tasks such as identifying literature, structuring ideas, refining text, and fact-checking while ensuring ethical and effective practices. the goal is not just to ensure academic integrity but also to reflect on how genai tools shape analytical and critical thinking skills. the deliverable is a 600 word (± 10%) document.','assessment_description:AD04'),(417,12,'AD05','assessment_description',17,'Assessment description 5','Detailed information for each assessment can be found on Canvas.','detailed information for each assessment can be found on canvas.','assessment_description:AD05'),(418,12,'WK01','weekly_schedule',18,'Week 01: Unit Introduction','Unit Introduction. Learning activity: Seminar (3 hr)','unit introduction. learning activity: seminar (3 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK01'),(419,12,'WK02','weekly_schedule',19,'Week 02: Case Study Research Methods','Case Study Research Methods. Learning activity: Seminar (3 hr)','case study research methods. learning activity: seminar (3 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK02'),(420,12,'WK03','weekly_schedule',20,'Week 03: Business Problem Identification','Business Problem Identification. Learning activity: Seminar (3 hr)','business problem identification. learning activity: seminar (3 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK03'),(421,12,'WK04','weekly_schedule',21,'Week 04: Design Science Research Methods','Design Science Research Methods. Learning activity: Seminar (3 hr)','design science research methods. learning activity: seminar (3 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK04'),(422,12,'WK05','weekly_schedule',22,'Week 05: Solution Objective','Solution Objective. Learning activity: Seminar (3 hr)','solution objective. learning activity: seminar (3 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK05'),(423,12,'WK06','weekly_schedule',23,'Week 06: Prototyping and Storytelling','Prototyping and Storytelling. Learning activity: Seminar (3 hr)','prototyping and storytelling. learning activity: seminar (3 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK06'),(424,12,'WK07','weekly_schedule',24,'Week 07: Outsourcing and Automation','Outsourcing and Automation. Learning activity: Seminar (3 hr)','outsourcing and automation. learning activity: seminar (3 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK07'),(425,12,'WK08','weekly_schedule',25,'Week 08: IT Project Management','IT Project Management. Learning activity: Seminar (3 hr)','it project management. learning activity: seminar (3 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK08'),(426,12,'WK09','weekly_schedule',26,'Week 09: Usability Engineering','Usability Engineering. Learning activity: Seminar (3 hr)','usability engineering. learning activity: seminar (3 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK09'),(427,12,'WK10','weekly_schedule',27,'Week 10: Design Ethics','Design Ethics. Learning activity: Seminar (3 hr)','design ethics. learning activity: seminar (3 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK10'),(428,12,'WK11','weekly_schedule',28,'Week 11: Scientific Writing','Scientific Writing. Learning activity: Seminar (3 hr)','scientific writing. learning activity: seminar (3 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK11'),(429,12,'WK12','weekly_schedule',29,'Week 12: Unit Review and Debriefing','Unit Review and Debriefing. Learning activity: Seminar (3 hr)','unit review and debriefing. learning activity: seminar (3 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK12'),(430,12,'WK13','weekly_schedule',30,'Week 13: Project presentations','Project presentations. Learning activity: Seminar (3 hr)','project presentations. learning activity: seminar (3 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK13'),(431,13,'OV01','overview',1,'Overview paragraph 1','This unit introduces students to the foundations of business information systems and the emerging strategic role of information and communication technologies (ICT) in transforming organisations. Students develop an understanding of how ICT come to matter to organisations as they disrupt, change and transform organisations and organisational processes. The unit covers systems issues, information literacy and use, and how various digital technologies work together to create an infrastructure for digital business and how technologies (such as social media) are disrupting \'business as usual\'. The role of information systems in capturing and distributing organisational knowledge and in enhancing decision-making is explored. Students gain an understanding of socio-technical networks, how information systems function, and how processes in organisations can be leveraged to create digital innovation and business transformation.','this unit introduces students to the foundations of business information systems and the emerging strategic role of information and communication technologies (ict) in transforming organisations. students develop an understanding of how ict come to matter to organisations as they disrupt, change and transform organisations and organisational processes. the unit covers systems issues, information literacy and use, and how various digital technologies work together to create an infrastructure for digital business and how technologies (such as social media) are disrupting \'business as usual\'. the role of information systems in capturing and distributing organisational knowledge and in enhancing decision-making is explored. students gain an understanding of socio-technical networks, how information systems function, and how processes in organisations can be leveraged to create digital innovation and business transformation.','overview:OV01'),(432,13,'LO01','learning_outcome',2,'Learning outcome 1','LO1. Interpret, analyze, model and visualize representations of business processes, organisational structures and data.','lo1. interpret, analyze, model and visualize representations of business processes, organisational structures and data.','learning_outcome:LO01'),(433,13,'LO02','learning_outcome',3,'Learning outcome 2','LO2. Appraise and critically assess the use of digital technology in business, society and individual workplace contexts.','lo2. appraise and critically assess the use of digital technology in business, society and individual workplace contexts.','learning_outcome:LO02'),(434,13,'LO03','learning_outcome',4,'Learning outcome 3','LO3. Effectively communicate and collaborate with different personalities, individually and in group settings, incomplex digital work environments to achieve positive and sustainable change outcomes.','lo3. effectively communicate and collaborate with different personalities, individually and in group settings, incomplex digital work environments to achieve positive and sustainable change outcomes.','learning_outcome:LO03'),(435,13,'LO04','learning_outcome',5,'Learning outcome 4','LO4. Evaluate the operations of a business and suggest and design solutions and improvements enabled by digital technology.','lo4. evaluate the operations of a business and suggest and design solutions and improvements enabled by digital technology.','learning_outcome:LO04'),(436,13,'LO05','learning_outcome',6,'Learning outcome 5','LO5. Identify current trends in business information systems and ability to assess their implications for managers, organisations, employees and other stakeholders.','lo5. identify current trends in business information systems and ability to assess their implications for managers, organisations, employees and other stakeholders.','learning_outcome:LO05'),(437,13,'LO06','learning_outcome',7,'Learning outcome 6','LO6. Appraise and Examine the problem space within which technology is used with the aim to argue for the design of a specific solution','lo6. appraise and examine the problem space within which technology is used with the aim to argue for the design of a specific solution','learning_outcome:LO06'),(438,13,'AS01','assessment',8,'End of Semester Reflective Essay An end of semester reflection on the unit learning. For details see Canvas.','Type: Written work. Description: End of Semester Reflective Essay An end of semester reflection on the unit learning. For details see Canvas.','type: written work. description: end of semester reflective essay an end of semester reflection on the unit learning. for details see canvas.','assessment:AS01'),(439,13,'AS02','assessment',9,'Participation Individual, see canvas for details','Type: Contribution. Description: Participation Individual, see canvas for details','type: contribution. description: participation individual, see canvas for details','assessment:AS02'),(440,13,'AS03','assessment',10,'Reflection on Group Work Provide and respond to feedback on the performance of team members.','Type: Evaluation. Description: Reflection on Group Work Provide and respond to feedback on the performance of team members.','type: evaluation. description: reflection on group work provide and respond to feedback on the performance of team members.','assessment:AS03'),(441,13,'AS04','assessment',11,'Group Project Design proposal for system, with weekly formative submissions, see Canvas.','Type: Portfolio or journal. Description: Group Project Design proposal for system, with weekly formative submissions, see Canvas.','type: portfolio or journal. description: group project design proposal for system, with weekly formative submissions, see canvas.','assessment:AS04'),(442,13,'AS05','assessment',12,'Group project Presentation Each team should offer a 3-minute proposal presentation followed by a 5-minute Q&A. see Canvas.','Type: Presentation. Description: Group project Presentation Each team should offer a 3-minute proposal presentation followed by a 5-minute Q&A. see Canvas.','type: presentation. description: group project presentation each team should offer a 3-minute proposal presentation followed by a 5-minute q&a. see canvas.','assessment:AS05'),(443,13,'AD01','assessment_description',13,'Assessment description 1','For details on assessments please see the assessment section and details provided on the Unit’s Canvas site.','for details on assessments please see the assessment section and details provided on the unit\'s canvas site.','assessment_description:AD01'),(444,13,'WK01','weekly_schedule',14,'Week 01: Introduction to Foundation in Digital Business; BIS as Technology','Introduction to Foundation in Digital Business; BIS as Technology. Learning activity: Seminar (3 hr)','introduction to foundation in digital business; bis as technology. learning activity: seminar (3 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK01'),(445,13,'WK02','weekly_schedule',15,'Week 02: BIS as Disruption; BIS as Transformation; BIS as Project','BIS as Disruption; BIS as Transformation; BIS as Project. Learning activity: Seminar (3 hr)','bis as disruption; bis as transformation; bis as project. learning activity: seminar (3 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK02'),(446,13,'WK03','weekly_schedule',16,'Week 03: BIS as Tool; BIS as Information; Workshop - Information Searching','BIS as Tool; BIS as Information; Workshop - Information Searching. Learning activity: Seminar (3 hr)','bis as tool; bis as information; workshop - information searching. learning activity: seminar (3 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK03'),(447,13,'WK04','weekly_schedule',17,'Week 04: Workshop - Design Thinking','Workshop - Design Thinking. Learning activity: Seminar (3 hr)','workshop - design thinking. learning activity: seminar (3 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK04'),(448,13,'WK05','weekly_schedule',18,'Week 05: BIS as System; BIS as System Dynamic','BIS as System; BIS as System Dynamic. Learning activity: Seminar (3 hr)','bis as system; bis as system dynamic. learning activity: seminar (3 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK05'),(449,13,'WK06','weekly_schedule',19,'Week 06: BIS as System Thinking; BIS as Designed','BIS as System Thinking; BIS as Designed. Learning activity: Seminar (3 hr)','bis as system thinking; bis as designed. learning activity: seminar (3 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK06'),(450,13,'WK07','weekly_schedule',20,'Week 07: BIS and IT; BIS as Data; Workshop - Data Flow Diagrams','BIS and IT; BIS as Data; Workshop - Data Flow Diagrams. Learning activity: Seminar (3 hr)','bis and it; bis as data; workshop - data flow diagrams. learning activity: seminar (3 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK07'),(451,13,'WK08','weekly_schedule',21,'Week 08: Self-directed study and consultation','Self-directed study and consultation. Learning activity: Seminar (3 hr)','self-directed study and consultation. learning activity: seminar (3 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK08'),(452,13,'WK09','weekly_schedule',22,'Week 09: BIS as Workflow; Workshop - Introduction to BPMN; BIS as tool for efficiency','BIS as Workflow; Workshop - Introduction to BPMN; BIS as tool for efficiency. Learning activity: Seminar (3 hr)','bis as workflow; workshop - introduction to bpmn; bis as tool for efficiency. learning activity: seminar (3 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK09'),(453,13,'WK10','weekly_schedule',23,'Week 10: BIS as Decision; BIS as Insight','BIS as Decision; BIS as Insight. Learning activity: Seminar (3 hr)','bis as decision; bis as insight. learning activity: seminar (3 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK10'),(454,13,'WK11','weekly_schedule',24,'Week 11: BIS and Ethics; BIS as Developed','BIS and Ethics; BIS as Developed. Learning activity: Seminar (3 hr)','bis and ethics; bis as developed. learning activity: seminar (3 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK11'),(455,13,'WK12','weekly_schedule',25,'Week 12: BIS and Sustainability; Summary and Farewell','BIS and Sustainability; Summary and Farewell. Learning activity: Seminar (3 hr)','bis and sustainability; summary and farewell. learning activity: seminar (3 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK12'),(456,13,'WK13','weekly_schedule',26,'Week 13: Group Project pitch/presentation to clients.','Group Project pitch/presentation to clients.. Learning activity: Seminar (3 hr)','group project pitch/presentation to clients.. learning activity: seminar (3 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK13'),(457,14,'OV01','overview',1,'Overview paragraph 1','Strategic Information Systems Sourcing has at its core the cost-effective sourcing and delivery of IS solutions with the aim of supporting and enabling business strategy. It covers the procurement of in-house systems, outsourcing strategies and third-party IS sourcing (for example from \'the cloud\'). The focus of this unit is on managerial decisions in relation to the design, implementation and delivery of an IS sourcing strategy, and the governance of IS sourcing solutions. Students develop knowledge of the concepts, tools and methodologies used in the negotiation and development of an IS sourcing strategy.','strategic information systems sourcing has at its core the cost-effective sourcing and delivery of is solutions with the aim of supporting and enabling business strategy. it covers the procurement of in-house systems, outsourcing strategies and third-party is sourcing (for example from \'the cloud\'). the focus of this unit is on managerial decisions in relation to the design, implementation and delivery of an is sourcing strategy, and the governance of is sourcing solutions. students develop knowledge of the concepts, tools and methodologies used in the negotiation and development of an is sourcing strategy.','overview:OV01'),(458,14,'LO01','learning_outcome',2,'Learning outcome 1','LO1. Evaluate opportunities for outsourcing IT services within a range of business settings.','lo1. evaluate opportunities for outsourcing it services within a range of business settings.','learning_outcome:LO01'),(459,14,'LO02','learning_outcome',3,'Learning outcome 2','LO2. Demonstrate your understanding of the range of available outsourced IT services by selecting suitable services for a set of provided business scenarios.','lo2. demonstrate your understanding of the range of available outsourced it services by selecting suitable services for a set of provided business scenarios.','learning_outcome:LO02'),(460,14,'LO03','learning_outcome',4,'Learning outcome 3','LO3. Demonstrate understanding of the theories related to outsourcing by applying them to evaluate various outsourcing scenarios.','lo3. demonstrate understanding of the theories related to outsourcing by applying them to evaluate various outsourcing scenarios.','learning_outcome:LO03'),(461,14,'LO04','learning_outcome',5,'Learning outcome 4','LO4. Evaluate strategic information systems sourcing decisions in a business setting.','lo4. evaluate strategic information systems sourcing decisions in a business setting.','learning_outcome:LO04'),(462,14,'LO05','learning_outcome',6,'Learning outcome 5','LO5. Identify risks associated with outsourcing and describe the risk mitigation strategies that are commonly applied and suggest recommendations on suitable controls.','lo5. identify risks associated with outsourcing and describe the risk mitigation strategies that are commonly applied and suggest recommendations on suitable controls.','learning_outcome:LO05'),(463,14,'LO06','learning_outcome',7,'Learning outcome 6','LO6. Demonstrate understanding of the sourcing process from a vendor perspective.','lo6. demonstrate understanding of the sourcing process from a vendor perspective.','learning_outcome:LO06'),(464,14,'AS01','assessment',8,'Individual assignment II Reflective essay on in-class activities','Type: Written work. Description: Individual assignment II Reflective essay on in-class activities','type: written work. description: individual assignment ii reflective essay on in-class activities','assessment:AS01'),(465,14,'AS02','assessment',9,'Case Study Presentation on a chosen case article','Type: Presentation. Description: Case Study Presentation on a chosen case article','type: presentation. description: case study presentation on a chosen case article','assessment:AS02'),(466,14,'AS03','assessment',10,'Case study on IT Sourcing Decision Worksheet Presentation Complete in class','Type: Case studies. Description: Case study on IT Sourcing Decision Worksheet Presentation Complete in class','type: case studies. description: case study on it sourcing decision worksheet presentation complete in class','assessment:AS03'),(467,14,'AS04','assessment',11,'Individual assignment I Develop an information systems sourcing plan','Type: Written work. Description: Individual assignment I Develop an information systems sourcing plan','type: written work. description: individual assignment i develop an information systems sourcing plan','assessment:AS04'),(468,14,'AS05','assessment',12,'Group Report IS pitching plan as a vendor','Type: Written work. Description: Group Report IS pitching plan as a vendor','type: written work. description: group report is pitching plan as a vendor','assessment:AS05'),(469,14,'AS06','assessment',13,'Video creation Marketing video for a chosen information system','Type: Creative work. Description: Video creation Marketing video for a chosen information system','type: creative work. description: video creation marketing video for a chosen information system','assessment:AS06'),(470,14,'AD01','assessment_description',14,'Assessment description 1','Individual Assessments','individual assessments','assessment_description:AD01'),(471,14,'AD02','assessment_description',15,'Assessment description 2','Individual Assignment I: Develop an information systems sourcing plan','individual assignment i: develop an information systems sourcing plan','assessment_description:AD02'),(472,14,'AD03','assessment_description',16,'Assessment description 3','Individual Assignment II: An reflective essay on in-class activities; consist of multiple components.','individual assignment ii: an reflective essay on in-class activities; consist of multiple components.','assessment_description:AD03'),(473,14,'AD04','assessment_description',17,'Assessment description 4','Group Assessments:','group assessments:','assessment_description:AD04'),(474,14,'AD05','assessment_description',18,'Assessment description 5','Case Study Discussion: Every group presents one case study in class. The order is to be determined in class.','case study discussion: every group presents one case study in class. the order is to be determined in class.','assessment_description:AD05'),(475,14,'AD06','assessment_description',19,'Assessment description 6','In-class Assessment: Work as a group to solve a sourcing decision making case study in class. Including worksheet and presentation.','in-class assessment: work as a group to solve a sourcing decision making case study in class. including worksheet and presentation.','assessment_description:AD06'),(476,14,'AD07','assessment_description',20,'Assessment description 7','Group Project Report: Develop an IS pitching proposal as a vendor','group project report: develop an is pitching proposal as a vendor','assessment_description:AD07'),(477,14,'AD08','assessment_description',21,'Assessment description 8','Group Project Video: Marketing/Pitching video for a chosen information systems.','group project video: marketing/pitching video for a chosen information systems.','assessment_description:AD08'),(478,14,'AD09','assessment_description',22,'Assessment description 9','Detailed information for each assessment can be found on Canvas.','detailed information for each assessment can be found on canvas.','assessment_description:AD09'),(479,14,'WK01','weekly_schedule',23,'Week 01: Introduction to IS sourcing','Introduction to IS sourcing. Learning activity: Seminar (3 hr)','introduction to is sourcing. learning activity: seminar (3 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK01'),(480,14,'WK02','weekly_schedule',24,'Week 02: Strategic Management and Information Systems','Strategic Management and Information Systems. Learning activity: Seminar (3 hr)','strategic management and information systems. learning activity: seminar (3 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK02'),(481,14,'WK03','weekly_schedule',25,'Week 03: IS Outsourcing Foundations','IS Outsourcing Foundations. Learning activity: Seminar (3 hr)','is outsourcing foundations. learning activity: seminar (3 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK03'),(482,14,'WK04','weekly_schedule',26,'Week 04: Business Process Analysis in IS Sourcing: BAM and CATWOE','Business Process Analysis in IS Sourcing: BAM and CATWOE. Learning activity: Seminar (3 hr)','business process analysis in is sourcing: bam and catwoe. learning activity: seminar (3 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK04'),(483,14,'WK05','weekly_schedule',27,'Week 05: Going to Market','Going to Market. Learning activity: Seminar (3 hr)','going to market. learning activity: seminar (3 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK05'),(484,14,'WK06','weekly_schedule',28,'Week 06: Evaluating Sourcing Options and Vendors','Evaluating Sourcing Options and Vendors. Learning activity: Seminar (3 hr)','evaluating sourcing options and vendors. learning activity: seminar (3 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK06'),(485,14,'WK07','weekly_schedule',29,'Week 07: Integrated Discussion of Sourcing Decision Making','Integrated Discussion of Sourcing Decision Making. Learning activity: Seminar (3 hr)','integrated discussion of sourcing decision making. learning activity: seminar (3 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK07'),(486,14,'WK08','weekly_schedule',30,'Week 08: Vendors\' perspectives','Vendors\' perspectives. Learning activity: Seminar (3 hr)','vendors\' perspectives. learning activity: seminar (3 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK08'),(487,14,'WK09','weekly_schedule',31,'Week 09: Vendors\' perspectives','Vendors\' perspectives. Learning activity: Seminar (3 hr)','vendors\' perspectives. learning activity: seminar (3 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK09'),(488,14,'WK10','weekly_schedule',32,'Week 10: FinOps: Financial Operations for Cloud Cost Optimization','FinOps: Financial Operations for Cloud Cost Optimization. Learning activity: Seminar (3 hr)','finops: financial operations for cloud cost optimization. learning activity: seminar (3 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK10'),(489,14,'WK11','weekly_schedule',33,'Week 11: Sourcing Risks and Control Strategies','Sourcing Risks and Control Strategies. Learning activity: Seminar (3 hr)','sourcing risks and control strategies. learning activity: seminar (3 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK11'),(490,14,'WK12','weekly_schedule',34,'Week 12: Managing Transition and Post-Sourcing Operations','Managing Transition and Post-Sourcing Operations. Learning activity: Seminar (3 hr)','managing transition and post-sourcing operations. learning activity: seminar (3 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK12'),(491,14,'WK13','weekly_schedule',35,'Week 13: Revision','Revision. Learning activity: Seminar (3 hr)','revision. learning activity: seminar (3 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK13'),(492,15,'OV01','overview',1,'Overview paragraph 1','The disruptive forces of digital technologies require businesses to be in a constant state of change to stay competitive in turbulent markets. However, as companies need to maintain their current revenue streams, they need to progress through a series of digital transformation projects. In this unit students learn how to analyse an organisation within a local and global context and develop knowledge of techniques required for managing digital business transformation initiatives. Topics covered include: the drivers of digital business transformation, managing digital transformation as a process, understand the power of disruptive technologies, technological impacts on new forms of organizational arrangements.','the disruptive forces of digital technologies require businesses to be in a constant state of change to stay competitive in turbulent markets. however, as companies need to maintain their current revenue streams, they need to progress through a series of digital transformation projects. in this unit students learn how to analyse an organisation within a local and global context and develop knowledge of techniques required for managing digital business transformation initiatives. topics covered include: the drivers of digital business transformation, managing digital transformation as a process, understand the power of disruptive technologies, technological impacts on new forms of organizational arrangements.','overview:OV01'),(493,15,'LO01','learning_outcome',2,'Learning outcome 1','LO1. Identify and describe the drivers and enablers of digital transformation in business settings.','lo1. identify and describe the drivers and enablers of digital transformation in business settings.','learning_outcome:LO01'),(494,15,'LO02','learning_outcome',3,'Learning outcome 2','LO2. Critically analyse business problems that necessitate digital transformation and change in an organisation.','lo2. critically analyse business problems that necessitate digital transformation and change in an organisation.','learning_outcome:LO02'),(495,15,'LO03','learning_outcome',4,'Learning outcome 3','LO3. Critically and creatively analyse and propose business innovations to address identified business problems.','lo3. critically and creatively analyse and propose business innovations to address identified business problems.','learning_outcome:LO03'),(496,15,'LO04','learning_outcome',5,'Learning outcome 4','LO4. Critically analyse the challenges for businesses in the face of innovation and technological advancements.','lo4. critically analyse the challenges for businesses in the face of innovation and technological advancements.','learning_outcome:LO04'),(497,15,'LO05','learning_outcome',6,'Learning outcome 5','LO5. Critically and creatively analyse various strategies to overcome challenges in digital transformation.','lo5. critically and creatively analyse various strategies to overcome challenges in digital transformation.','learning_outcome:LO05'),(498,15,'LO06','learning_outcome',7,'Learning outcome 6','LO6. Critically synthesise and apply methods, models and frameworks with business analysis, communication and research skills in digital transformation projects.','lo6. critically synthesise and apply methods, models and frameworks with business analysis, communication and research skills in digital transformation projects.','learning_outcome:LO06'),(499,15,'LO07','learning_outcome',8,'Learning outcome 7','LO7. Collaborate and communicate in a professional manner with people from diverse backgrounds.','lo7. collaborate and communicate in a professional manner with people from diverse backgrounds.','learning_outcome:LO07'),(500,15,'LO08','learning_outcome',9,'Learning outcome 8','LO8. Contribute effectively as a responsible member of a diverse team for group assessments.','lo8. contribute effectively as a responsible member of a diverse team for group assessments.','learning_outcome:LO08'),(501,15,'AS01','assessment',10,'Final Exam Written Exam','Type: Written exam. Description: Final Exam Written Exam','type: written exam. description: final exam written exam','assessment:AS01'),(502,15,'AS02','assessment',11,'Assignment 1 Individual in-class presentation in week 5/6. This is a 90-second pitch accompanied by a one-page poster.','Type: Presentation. Description: Assignment 1 Individual in-class presentation in week 5/6. This is a 90-second pitch accompanied by a one-page poster.','type: presentation. description: assignment 1 individual in-class presentation in week 5/6. this is a 90-second pitch accompanied by a one-page poster.','assessment:AS02'),(503,15,'AS03','assessment',12,'Assignment 2c Group presentation (In-class presentation Week 12/13)','Type: Presentation. Description: Assignment 2c Group presentation (In-class presentation Week 12/13)','type: presentation. description: assignment 2c group presentation (in-class presentation week 12/13)','assessment:AS03'),(504,15,'AS04','assessment',13,'Assignment 2a Group report outline','Type: Case studies. Description: Assignment 2a Group report outline','type: case studies. description: assignment 2a group report outline','assessment:AS04'),(505,15,'AS05','assessment',14,'Assignment 2b Business report and presentation slides','Type: Case studies. Description: Assignment 2b Business report and presentation slides','type: case studies. description: assignment 2b business report and presentation slides','assessment:AS05'),(506,15,'AD01','assessment_description',15,'Assessment description 1','• Assignment 1 (Executive Pitch and Q&A): Students will select a company that has undergone digital transformation and analyse recent news articles about the company. They will synthesise the key insights and evaluate the likely transformative impact of these developments, and communicate their analysis through a one-page poster and a 90-second executive pitch. Students will be encouraged to focus on an industry and company aligned with their future career interests. • Assignment 2a (Group Report Outline): Students will work in groups as a team of consultants to submit a structured outline for their Digital Transformation Management Plan for a selected company. The outline will present the company background and context, diagnose the need for digital transformation, and propose and briefly evaluate potential digital solutions. This submission is designed to support formative feedback from the teaching team, which groups should use to strengthen their final report and presentation.','• assignment 1 (executive pitch and q&a): students will select a company that has undergone digital transformation and analyse recent news articles about the company. they will synthesise the key insights and evaluate the likely transformative impact of these developments, and communicate their analysis through a one-page poster and a 90-second executive pitch. students will be encouraged to focus on an industry and company aligned with their future career interests. • assignment 2a (group report outline): students will work in groups as a team of consultants to submit a structured outline for their digital transformation management plan for a selected company. the outline will present the company background and context, diagnose the need for digital transformation, and propose and briefly evaluate potential digital solutions. this submission is designed to support formative feedback from the teaching team, which groups should use to strengthen their final report and presentation.','assessment_description:AD01'),(507,15,'AD02','assessment_description',16,'Assessment description 2','• Assignment 2b (Group Report & Presentation Slides): Students will work in groups to develop a professional business report that proposes a digital transformation solution for a selected organisation. Building on feedback from the proposal outline, the report should describe the solution in sufficient detail to show how it addresses the organisation’s challenges, and apply current change management frameworks to analyse the organisation and develop a transformative change management plan aligned with the solution and project requirements.','• assignment 2b (group report & presentation slides): students will work in groups to develop a professional business report that proposes a digital transformation solution for a selected organisation. building on feedback from the proposal outline, the report should describe the solution in sufficient detail to show how it addresses the organisation\'s challenges, and apply current change management frameworks to analyse the organisation and develop a transformative change management plan aligned with the solution and project requirements.','assessment_description:AD02'),(508,15,'AD03','assessment_description',17,'Assessment description 3','• Assignment 2c (In-class presentation): All students in each team to design, develop, and present the critical details from Assignment 2b (group report).','• assignment 2c (in-class presentation): all students in each team to design, develop, and present the critical details from assignment 2b (group report).','assessment_description:AD03'),(509,15,'AD04','assessment_description',18,'Assessment description 4','• Final Exam: This exam will focus on the fundamental concepts and applied and experiential knowledge acquired across the semester. Note: This assessment will take the form of a supervised exam. It is a closed- book exam; no materials are allowed.','• final exam: this exam will focus on the fundamental concepts and applied and experiential knowledge acquired across the semester. note: this assessment will take the form of a supervised exam. it is a closed- book exam; no materials are allowed.','assessment_description:AD04'),(510,15,'AD05','assessment_description',19,'Assessment description 5','Detailed information for each assessment can be found on Canvas.','detailed information for each assessment can be found on canvas.','assessment_description:AD05'),(511,15,'WK01','weekly_schedule',20,'Week 01: Introduction and Overview','Introduction and Overview. Learning activity: Lecture (2 hr)','introduction and overview. learning activity: lecture (2 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK01'),(512,15,'WK02','weekly_schedule',21,'Week 02: Understanding Disruption','Understanding Disruption. Learning activity: Lecture (2 hr)','understanding disruption. learning activity: lecture (2 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK02'),(513,15,'WK03','weekly_schedule',22,'Week 02: Understanding Disruption','Understanding Disruption. Learning activity: Tutorial (1 hr)','understanding disruption. learning activity: tutorial (1 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK03'),(514,15,'WK04','weekly_schedule',23,'Week 03: The Drivers and Enablers of Digital Transformation','The Drivers and Enablers of Digital Transformation. Learning activity: Lecture (2 hr)','the drivers and enablers of digital transformation. learning activity: lecture (2 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK04'),(515,15,'WK05','weekly_schedule',24,'Week 03: The Drivers and Enablers of Digital Transformation','The Drivers and Enablers of Digital Transformation. Learning activity: Tutorial (1 hr)','the drivers and enablers of digital transformation. learning activity: tutorial (1 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK05'),(516,15,'WK06','weekly_schedule',25,'Week 04: Manage Change and Transformation-1','Manage Change and Transformation-1. Learning activity: Lecture (2 hr)','manage change and transformation-1. learning activity: lecture (2 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK06'),(517,15,'WK07','weekly_schedule',26,'Week 04: Manage Change and Transformation-1','Manage Change and Transformation-1. Learning activity: Tutorial (1 hr)','manage change and transformation-1. learning activity: tutorial (1 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK07'),(518,15,'WK08','weekly_schedule',27,'Week 05: Manage Change and Transformation-2','Manage Change and Transformation-2. Learning activity: Lecture (2 hr)','manage change and transformation-2. learning activity: lecture (2 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK08'),(519,15,'WK09','weekly_schedule',28,'Week 05: Manage Change and Transformation-2','Manage Change and Transformation-2. Learning activity: Tutorial (1 hr)','manage change and transformation-2. learning activity: tutorial (1 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK09'),(520,15,'WK10','weekly_schedule',29,'Week 06: Overcome Challenges of Digital Transformation','Overcome Challenges of Digital Transformation. Learning activity: Lecture (2 hr)','overcome challenges of digital transformation. learning activity: lecture (2 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK10'),(521,15,'WK11','weekly_schedule',30,'Week 06: Overcome Challenges of Digital Transformation','Overcome Challenges of Digital Transformation. Learning activity: Tutorial (1 hr)','overcome challenges of digital transformation. learning activity: tutorial (1 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK11'),(522,15,'WK12','weekly_schedule',31,'Week 07: Digital Transformation of Consumption','Digital Transformation of Consumption. Learning activity: Lecture (2 hr)','digital transformation of consumption. learning activity: lecture (2 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK12'),(523,15,'WK13','weekly_schedule',32,'Week 07: Digital Transformation of Consumption','Digital Transformation of Consumption. Learning activity: Tutorial (1 hr)','digital transformation of consumption. learning activity: tutorial (1 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK13'),(524,15,'WK14','weekly_schedule',33,'Week 08: Digital Transformation of Communication','Digital Transformation of Communication. Learning activity: Lecture (2 hr)','digital transformation of communication. learning activity: lecture (2 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK14'),(525,15,'WK15','weekly_schedule',34,'Week 08: Digital Transformation of Communication','Digital Transformation of Communication. Learning activity: Tutorial (1 hr)','digital transformation of communication. learning activity: tutorial (1 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK15'),(526,15,'WK16','weekly_schedule',35,'Week 09: Digital Transformation of Traditional Industries','Digital Transformation of Traditional Industries. Learning activity: Lecture (2 hr)','digital transformation of traditional industries. learning activity: lecture (2 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK16'),(527,15,'WK17','weekly_schedule',36,'Week 09: Digital Transformation of Traditional Industries','Digital Transformation of Traditional Industries. Learning activity: Tutorial (1 hr)','digital transformation of traditional industries. learning activity: tutorial (1 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK17'),(528,15,'WK18','weekly_schedule',37,'Week 10: Group assignment consultation and self-directed learning','Group assignment consultation and self-directed learning. Learning activity: Lecture (2 hr)','group assignment consultation and self-directed learning. learning activity: lecture (2 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK18'),(529,15,'WK19','weekly_schedule',38,'Week 10: Group assignment consultation and self-directed learning','Group assignment consultation and self-directed learning. Learning activity: Tutorial (1 hr)','group assignment consultation and self-directed learning. learning activity: tutorial (1 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK19'),(530,15,'WK20','weekly_schedule',39,'Week 11: Review and Synthesis','Review and Synthesis. Learning activity: Lecture (2 hr)','review and synthesis. learning activity: lecture (2 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK20'),(531,15,'WK21','weekly_schedule',40,'Week 12: Group Presentations','Group Presentations. Learning activity: Lecture (2 hr)','group presentations. learning activity: lecture (2 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK21'),(532,15,'WK22','weekly_schedule',41,'Week 13: Group Presentations','Group Presentations. Learning activity: Lecture (3 hr)','group presentations. learning activity: lecture (3 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK22'),(533,16,'OV01','overview',1,'Overview paragraph 1','The unit provides an overall introduction to the different components of digital information infrastructures in organisational contexts. This includes organisational enterprise systems architecture, legacy systems, enterprise systems, cloud infrastructure and enabling technologies such as blockchain, internet of things, or web services. Strategic managerial issues that arise from the implementation, use, and security management of information infrastructures and enterprise systems are also covered. The unit utilises a combination of practical sessions with Enterprise Systems, such as SAP, and case study analyses to build a deep understanding of relevant topics.','the unit provides an overall introduction to the different components of digital information infrastructures in organisational contexts. this includes organisational enterprise systems architecture, legacy systems, enterprise systems, cloud infrastructure and enabling technologies such as blockchain, internet of things, or web services. strategic managerial issues that arise from the implementation, use, and security management of information infrastructures and enterprise systems are also covered. the unit utilises a combination of practical sessions with enterprise systems, such as sap, and case study analyses to build a deep understanding of relevant topics.','overview:OV01'),(534,16,'LO01','learning_outcome',2,'Learning outcome 1','LO1. explore the strategic managerial issues that arise from the implementation and use of enterprise systems as a means of integrating data and standardising processes','lo1. explore the strategic managerial issues that arise from the implementation and use of enterprise systems as a means of integrating data and standardising processes','learning_outcome:LO01'),(535,16,'LO02','learning_outcome',3,'Learning outcome 2','LO2. use an example enterprise system to gain hands-on competency in supporting key business processes','lo2. use an example enterprise system to gain hands-on competency in supporting key business processes','learning_outcome:LO02'),(536,16,'LO03','learning_outcome',4,'Learning outcome 3','LO3. provide an overview of an enterprise system implementation solution which addresses key processes, data and organisational structures, and explain the reasons behind the solution','lo3. provide an overview of an enterprise system implementation solution which addresses key processes, data and organisational structures, and explain the reasons behind the solution','learning_outcome:LO03'),(537,16,'LO04','learning_outcome',5,'Learning outcome 4','LO4. evaluate the place of enterprise systems in broader digital information infrastructure.','lo4. evaluate the place of enterprise systems in broader digital information infrastructure.','learning_outcome:LO04'),(538,16,'LO05','learning_outcome',6,'Learning outcome 5','LO5. evaluate in a critical manner the technical trends which may impact on future enterprise systems use','lo5. evaluate in a critical manner the technical trends which may impact on future enterprise systems use','learning_outcome:LO05'),(539,16,'LO06','learning_outcome',7,'Learning outcome 6','LO6. present ideas and arguments effectively, deliver a comprehensive and integrated enterprise information infrastructure that reflects a collective effort from a professional project team','lo6. present ideas and arguments effectively, deliver a comprehensive and integrated enterprise information infrastructure that reflects a collective effort from a professional project team','learning_outcome:LO06'),(540,16,'LO07','learning_outcome',8,'Learning outcome 7','LO7. apply the principles of IT resources management to effectively solve real-world problems.','lo7. apply the principles of it resources management to effectively solve real-world problems.','learning_outcome:LO07'),(541,16,'AS01','assessment',9,'Final Exam Closed book exam','Type: Written exam. Description: Final Exam Closed book exam','type: written exam. description: final exam closed book exam','assessment:AS01'),(542,16,'AS02','assessment',10,'Case Presentation Presentation on Case Study Articles','Type: Presentation. Description: Case Presentation Presentation on Case Study Articles','type: presentation. description: case presentation presentation on case study articles','assessment:AS02'),(543,16,'AS03','assessment',11,'Individual Assignment Written report with specified questions','Type: Practical skill. Description: Individual Assignment Written report with specified questions','type: practical skill. description: individual assignment written report with specified questions','assessment:AS03'),(544,16,'AS04','assessment',12,'Group project report Report','Type: Written work. Description: Group project report Report','type: written work. description: group project report report','assessment:AS04'),(545,16,'AS05','assessment',13,'Group project presentation Report','Type: Presentation. Description: Group project presentation Report','type: presentation. description: group project presentation report','assessment:AS05'),(546,16,'AD01','assessment_description',14,'Assessment description 1','Individual assignment: The individual assignment consists of multiple components that may include the completion of tasks with SAP and a written report.','individual assignment: the individual assignment consists of multiple components that may include the completion of tasks with sap and a written report.','assessment_description:AD01'),(547,16,'AD02','assessment_description',15,'Assessment description 2','Group project: You must demonstrate an information infrastructure which explains the role of enterprise systems within that infrastructure, discusses organisational and change management issues, and examines the effect of new technological trends.','group project: you must demonstrate an information infrastructure which explains the role of enterprise systems within that infrastructure, discusses organisational and change management issues, and examines the effect of new technological trends.','assessment_description:AD02'),(548,16,'AD03','assessment_description',16,'Assessment description 3','Case presentation: Each group is scheduled for a 10-minute case presentation during different weeks. The goal of these presentations is to help the class better understand the case background.','case presentation: each group is scheduled for a 10-minute case presentation during different weeks. the goal of these presentations is to help the class better understand the case background.','assessment_description:AD03'),(549,16,'AD04','assessment_description',17,'Assessment description 4','Final exam: This is a closed-book exam and will assess your ability to demonstrate your understanding of all material covered in the unit of study.','final exam: this is a closed-book exam and will assess your ability to demonstrate your understanding of all material covered in the unit of study.','assessment_description:AD04'),(550,16,'AD05','assessment_description',18,'Assessment description 5','Detailed information for each assessment can be found on Canvas.','detailed information for each assessment can be found on canvas.','assessment_description:AD05'),(551,16,'WK01','weekly_schedule',19,'Week 01: Introduction','Introduction. Learning activity: Seminar (3 hr)','introduction. learning activity: seminar (3 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK01'),(552,16,'WK02','weekly_schedule',20,'Week 02: Business Process and Enterprise Systems','Business Process and Enterprise Systems. Learning activity: Seminar (3 hr)','business process and enterprise systems. learning activity: seminar (3 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK02'),(553,16,'WK03','weekly_schedule',21,'Week 03: Enterprise Systems and Accounting Process I','Enterprise Systems and Accounting Process I. Learning activity: Seminar (3 hr)','enterprise systems and accounting process i. learning activity: seminar (3 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK03'),(554,16,'WK04','weekly_schedule',22,'Week 04: Enterprise Systems and Procurement Process I','Enterprise Systems and Procurement Process I. Learning activity: Seminar (3 hr)','enterprise systems and procurement process i. learning activity: seminar (3 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK04'),(555,16,'WK05','weekly_schedule',23,'Week 05: Enterprise Systems and Procurement Process II','Enterprise Systems and Procurement Process II. Learning activity: Seminar (3 hr)','enterprise systems and procurement process ii. learning activity: seminar (3 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK05'),(556,16,'WK06','weekly_schedule',24,'Week 06: Enterprise Systems and Lead to Cash Process','Enterprise Systems and Lead to Cash Process. Learning activity: Seminar (3 hr)','enterprise systems and lead to cash process. learning activity: seminar (3 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK06'),(557,16,'WK07','weekly_schedule',25,'Week 07: Integrated Discussion on Enterprise Systems','Integrated Discussion on Enterprise Systems. Learning activity: Seminar (3 hr)','integrated discussion on enterprise systems. learning activity: seminar (3 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK07'),(558,16,'WK08','weekly_schedule',26,'Week 08: Guest Lecture (TBC)','Guest Lecture (TBC). Learning activity: Seminar (3 hr)','guest lecture (tbc). learning activity: seminar (3 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK08'),(559,16,'WK09','weekly_schedule',27,'Week 09: Cloud Computing and Enterprise Systems','Cloud Computing and Enterprise Systems. Learning activity: Seminar (3 hr)','cloud computing and enterprise systems. learning activity: seminar (3 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK09'),(560,16,'WK10','weekly_schedule',28,'Week 10: Blockchain and IoT','Blockchain and IoT. Learning activity: Seminar (3 hr)','blockchain and iot. learning activity: seminar (3 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK10'),(561,16,'WK11','weekly_schedule',29,'Week 11: Managing Digital Information Infrastructure I','Managing Digital Information Infrastructure I. Learning activity: Seminar (3 hr)','managing digital information infrastructure i. learning activity: seminar (3 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK11'),(562,16,'WK12','weekly_schedule',30,'Week 12: Managing Digital Information Infrastructure II','Managing Digital Information Infrastructure II. Learning activity: Seminar (3 hr)','managing digital information infrastructure ii. learning activity: seminar (3 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK12'),(563,16,'WK13','weekly_schedule',31,'Week 13: Course Revision','Course Revision. Learning activity: Seminar (3 hr)','course revision. learning activity: seminar (3 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK13'),(564,17,'OV01','overview',1,'Overview paragraph 1','This unit highlights the key concepts of business process management (BPM) and their importance to organisations in supporting the business operations and providing opportunities for competitive advantage and innovation. It provides a detailed understanding of the concepts, strategies, tools and technologies required throughout the BPM lifecycle. This unit takes both the strategic and change management perspectives in designing process architecture and governance, as well as analysing, designing, and measuring performance of processes across value chains and aligned to industry standards. The unit also develops practical skills in modelling and simulating processes using business process management tools.','this unit highlights the key concepts of business process management (bpm) and their importance to organisations in supporting the business operations and providing opportunities for competitive advantage and innovation. it provides a detailed understanding of the concepts, strategies, tools and technologies required throughout the bpm lifecycle. this unit takes both the strategic and change management perspectives in designing process architecture and governance, as well as analysing, designing, and measuring performance of processes across value chains and aligned to industry standards. the unit also develops practical skills in modelling and simulating processes using business process management tools.','overview:OV01'),(565,17,'LO01','learning_outcome',2,'Learning outcome 1','LO1. Discuss the holistic role of Business Process Management (BPM) in a business environment to improve performance and align to overall strategy.','lo1. discuss the holistic role of business process management (bpm) in a business environment to improve performance and align to overall strategy.','learning_outcome:LO01'),(566,17,'LO02','learning_outcome',3,'Learning outcome 2','LO2. Apply BPM methodologies, concepts, and principles to business problems and practice following the BPM lifecycle.','lo2. apply bpm methodologies, concepts, and principles to business problems and practice following the bpm lifecycle.','learning_outcome:LO02'),(567,17,'LO03','learning_outcome',4,'Learning outcome 3','LO3. Address the issues and challenges associated with process change initiatives in organisations.','lo3. address the issues and challenges associated with process change initiatives in organisations.','learning_outcome:LO03'),(568,17,'LO04','learning_outcome',5,'Learning outcome 4','LO4. Evaluate the impact of process change projects on stakeholders and the role of change management in mitigating risks in such projects.','lo4. evaluate the impact of process change projects on stakeholders and the role of change management in mitigating risks in such projects.','learning_outcome:LO04'),(569,17,'LO05','learning_outcome',6,'Learning outcome 5','LO5. Use BPM tools to model, document, and analyse processes during the BPM lifecycle.','lo5. use bpm tools to model, document, and analyse processes during the bpm lifecycle.','learning_outcome:LO05'),(570,17,'LO06','learning_outcome',7,'Learning outcome 6','LO6. Work independently in a professional and ethical manner','lo6. work independently in a professional and ethical manner','learning_outcome:LO06'),(571,17,'LO07','learning_outcome',8,'Learning outcome 7','LO7. Work as a responsible member of a diverse team, collaborate and communicate in a professional manner with people from diverse backgrounds.','lo7. work as a responsible member of a diverse team, collaborate and communicate in a professional manner with people from diverse backgrounds.','learning_outcome:LO07'),(572,17,'AS01','assessment',9,'Final exam Written exam','Type: Written exam. Description: Final exam Written exam','type: written exam. description: final exam written exam','assessment:AS01'),(573,17,'AS02','assessment',10,'Individual assignment Written submission','Type: Case studies. Description: Individual assignment Written submission','type: case studies. description: individual assignment written submission','assessment:AS02'),(574,17,'AS03','assessment',11,'Business Proposal Business idea and execution plan proposal','Type: Creative work. Description: Business Proposal Business idea and execution plan proposal','type: creative work. description: business proposal business idea and execution plan proposal','assessment:AS03'),(575,17,'AS04','assessment',12,'Business Report Group Report Submission','Type: Case studies. Description: Business Report Group Report Submission','type: case studies. description: business report group report submission','assessment:AS04'),(576,17,'AD01','assessment_description',13,'Assessment description 1','Individual assignment: In this assignment students will take the role of the process analyst and engage in process discovery and analysis within a given business case context.','individual assignment: in this assignment students will take the role of the process analyst and engage in process discovery and analysis within a given business case context.','assessment_description:AD01'),(577,17,'AD02','assessment_description',14,'Assessment description 2','Business Proposal assignment: In this asignment students will analyse the market and identify new services for a business case seeking to expand. Students will propose a new service and a plan to guide the execution of the project.','business proposal assignment: in this asignment students will analyse the market and identify new services for a business case seeking to expand. students will propose a new service and a plan to guide the execution of the project.','assessment_description:AD02'),(578,17,'AD03','assessment_description',15,'Assessment description 3','Business Report assignment: In this assignment students will desing new processes following the service proposed in their Business Proposal pitch. Students will assess the feasibility of new processes, the resources required, and the challenges encountered during process implementation. Students will use Signavio (BPM tool) to document, simulate and analyse the new business processes.','business report assignment: in this assignment students will desing new processes following the service proposed in their business proposal pitch. students will assess the feasibility of new processes, the resources required, and the challenges encountered during process implementation. students will use signavio (bpm tool) to document, simulate and analyse the new business processes.','assessment_description:AD03'),(579,17,'AD04','assessment_description',16,'Assessment description 4','Final exam: A supervised exam that will test students’ theoretical understanding, critical thinking, and ability to apply and evaluate BPM concepts and principles in practice.','final exam: a supervised exam that will test students\' theoretical understanding, critical thinking, and ability to apply and evaluate bpm concepts and principles in practice.','assessment_description:AD04'),(580,17,'AD05','assessment_description',17,'Assessment description 5','Detailed information for each assessment can be found on Canvas.','detailed information for each assessment can be found on canvas.','assessment_description:AD05'),(581,17,'WK01','weekly_schedule',18,'Week 01: Overview of Business Process Management (BPM)','Overview of Business Process Management (BPM). Learning activity: Seminar (3 hr)','overview of business process management (bpm). learning activity: seminar (3 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK01'),(582,17,'WK02','weekly_schedule',19,'Week 02: Process identification','Process identification. Learning activity: Seminar (3 hr)','process identification. learning activity: seminar (3 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK02'),(583,17,'WK03','weekly_schedule',20,'Week 03: Process gove