WK05','weekly_schedule',20,'Week 05: Business model in the digital era-1','Business model in the digital era-1. Learning activity: Seminar (3 hr)','business model in the digital era-1. learning activity: seminar (3 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK05'),(614,18,'WK06','weekly_schedule',21,'Week 06: Business model in the digital era-2','Business model in the digital era-2. Learning activity: Seminar (3 hr)','business model in the digital era-2. learning activity: seminar (3 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK06'),(615,18,'WK07','weekly_schedule',22,'Week 07: Group project activity','Group project activity. Learning activity: Seminar (3 hr)','group project activity. learning activity: seminar (3 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK07'),(616,18,'WK08','weekly_schedule',23,'Week 08: Group project activity','Group project activity. Learning activity: Seminar (3 hr)','group project activity. learning activity: seminar (3 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK08'),(617,18,'WK09','weekly_schedule',24,'Week 09: Self-directed learning & Group assignment consultation','Self-directed learning & Group assignment consultation. Learning activity: Seminar (3 hr)','self-directed learning & group assignment consultation. learning activity: seminar (3 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK09'),(618,18,'WK10','weekly_schedule',25,'Week 10: Digital business model- industry-specific development','Digital business model- industry-specific development. Learning activity: Seminar (3 hr)','digital business model- industry-specific development. learning activity: seminar (3 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK10'),(619,18,'WK11','weekly_schedule',26,'Week 11: Digital business model- industry-specific development','Digital business model- industry-specific development. Learning activity: Seminar (3 hr)','digital business model- industry-specific development. learning activity: seminar (3 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK11'),(620,18,'WK12','weekly_schedule',27,'Week 12: Review and synthesis','Review and synthesis. Learning activity: Seminar (3 hr)','review and synthesis. learning activity: seminar (3 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK12'),(621,18,'WK13','weekly_schedule',28,'Week 13: Group Presentation','Group Presentation. Learning activity: Seminar (3 hr)','group presentation. learning activity: seminar (3 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK13'),(622,19,'OV01','overview',1,'Overview paragraph 1','Business analytics and the ability to interpret and respond to related outputs, is a major source of competitive advantage in the information age and is therefore a leading business priority globally. In recent times, this field has evolved from a technology topic to a management priority, creating an unprecedented demand for new competencies in managing with data. Taking a business rather than technology perspective, this unit covers the enterprise ecosystem in the context of strategic and operational analytics and decision making. Topics include innovation through advanced analytics, data driven performance management, strategic business improvement and management of complex BI projects. The unit offers hands-on experience in using a commercial platform, combined with in-depth analytical skills, and enables students completing the unit to help any organization to derive more value from data and information and compete on analytics.','business analytics and the ability to interpret and respond to related outputs, is a major source of competitive advantage in the information age and is therefore a leading business priority globally. in recent times, this field has evolved from a technology topic to a management priority, creating an unprecedented demand for new competencies in managing with data. taking a business rather than technology perspective, this unit covers the enterprise ecosystem in the context of strategic and operational analytics and decision making. topics include innovation through advanced analytics, data driven performance management, strategic business improvement and management of complex bi projects. the unit offers hands-on experience in using a commercial platform, combined with in-depth analytical skills, and enables students completing the unit to help any organization to derive more value from data and information and compete on analytics.','overview:OV01'),(623,19,'LO01','learning_outcome',2,'Learning outcome 1','LO1. Apply the fundamental concepts and practice of managing through data challenges in differentiated organisational settings.','lo1. apply the fundamental concepts and practice of managing through data challenges in differentiated organisational settings.','learning_outcome:LO01'),(624,19,'LO02','learning_outcome',3,'Learning outcome 2','LO2. Identify and analyse issues, challenges and solutions in managing through data/business analytics systems from the business rather thantechnical perspective.','lo2. identify and analyse issues, challenges and solutions in managing through data/business analytics systems from the business rather thantechnical perspective.','learning_outcome:LO02'),(625,19,'LO03','learning_outcome',4,'Learning outcome 3','LO3. Critically examine the intra and inter organisational and societal issues involved in implementing various types of analytical systems.','lo3. critically examine the intra and inter organisational and societal issues involved in implementing various types of analytical systems.','learning_outcome:LO03'),(626,19,'LO04','learning_outcome',5,'Learning outcome 4','LO4. Design and implement a small-scale data analysis project in an organisational setting.','lo4. design and implement a small-scale data analysis project in an organisational setting.','learning_outcome:LO04'),(627,19,'LO05','learning_outcome',6,'Learning outcome 5','LO5. Evaluate different analytical outputs and their ethical impacts.','lo5. evaluate different analytical outputs and their ethical impacts.','learning_outcome:LO05'),(628,19,'LO06','learning_outcome',7,'Learning outcome 6','LO6. Apply advanced principles and techniques related to strategy, organizational change and information governance to help organisations effectively maximise value from their data, information assets and technology investments.','lo6. apply advanced principles and techniques related to strategy, organizational change and information governance to help organisations effectively maximise value from their data, information assets and technology investments.','learning_outcome:LO06'),(629,19,'AS01','assessment',8,'Reflective Essay Written essay on core learnings','Type: Portfolio or journal. Description: Reflective Essay Written essay on core learnings','type: portfolio or journal. description: reflective essay written essay on core learnings','assessment:AS01'),(630,19,'AS02','assessment',9,'Mid-semester test Mid-semester test will assess core learnings from weeks 1-5','Type: Written test. Description: Mid-semester test Mid-semester test will assess core learnings from weeks 1-5','type: written test. description: mid-semester test mid-semester test will assess core learnings from weeks 1-5','assessment:AS02'),(631,19,'AS03','assessment',10,'Project report Written report','Type: Data analysis. Description: Project report Written report','type: data analysis. description: project report written report','assessment:AS03'),(632,19,'AS04','assessment',11,'Group project presentation Group presentation of written report and related analysis','Type: Presentation. Description: Group project presentation Group presentation of written report and related analysis','type: presentation. description: group project presentation group presentation of written report and related analysis','assessment:AS04'),(633,19,'AD01','assessment_description',12,'Assessment description 1','Mid-semester test to be held in Week 7 on core concepts delivered in weeks 1-5.','mid-semester test to be held in week 7 on core concepts delivered in weeks 1-5.','assessment_description:AD01'),(634,19,'AD02','assessment_description',13,'Assessment description 2','Group project and report: In groups, students will use Tableau to explore a real-world data set and consider the implications for distinct personas. Students will prepare a report outlining this analysis. Students will be orally examined in groups on the contents of this report.','group project and report: in groups, students will use tableau to explore a real-world data set and consider the implications for distinct personas. students will prepare a report outlining this analysis. students will be orally examined in groups on the contents of this report.','assessment_description:AD02'),(635,19,'AD03','assessment_description',14,'Assessment description 3','Reflective essay: Students will utilise a reflective framework to critically evaluate managerial practices','reflective essay: students will utilise a reflective framework to critically evaluate managerial practices','assessment_description:AD03'),(636,19,'WK01','weekly_schedule',15,'Week 01: Foundational and historical concepts','Foundational and historical concepts. Learning activity: Seminar (3 hr)','foundational and historical concepts. learning activity: seminar (3 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK01'),(637,19,'WK02','weekly_schedule',16,'Week 02: Decision making for managers','Decision making for managers. Learning activity: Seminar (3 hr)','decision making for managers. learning activity: seminar (3 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK02'),(638,19,'WK03','weekly_schedule',17,'Week 03: Data quality','Data quality. Learning activity: Seminar (3 hr)','data quality. learning activity: seminar (3 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK03'),(639,19,'WK04','weekly_schedule',18,'Week 04: Strategies & business models for valuecreation','Strategies & business models for valuecreation. Learning activity: Seminar (3 hr)','strategies & business models for valuecreation. learning activity: seminar (3 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK04'),(640,19,'WK05','weekly_schedule',19,'Week 05: Strategic alignment and IT governance','Strategic alignment and IT governance. Learning activity: Seminar (3 hr)','strategic alignment and it governance. learning activity: seminar (3 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK05'),(641,19,'WK06','weekly_schedule',20,'Week 06: Exam preparation','Exam preparation. Learning activity: Seminar (3 hr)','exam preparation. learning activity: seminar (3 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK06'),(642,19,'WK07','weekly_schedule',21,'Week 07: Mid-semester Test','Mid-semester Test. Learning activity: Seminar (3 hr)','mid-semester test. learning activity: seminar (3 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK07'),(643,19,'WK08','weekly_schedule',22,'Week 08: Analytics, people and culture','Analytics, people and culture. Learning activity: Seminar (3 hr)','analytics, people and culture. learning activity: seminar (3 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK08'),(644,19,'WK09','weekly_schedule',23,'Week 09: Ethics for business intelligence','Ethics for business intelligence. Learning activity: Seminar (3 hr)','ethics for business intelligence. learning activity: seminar (3 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK09'),(645,19,'WK10','weekly_schedule',24,'Week 10: Managing the change process and stakeholders','Managing the change process and stakeholders. Learning activity: Seminar (3 hr)','managing the change process and stakeholders. learning activity: seminar (3 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK10'),(646,19,'WK11','weekly_schedule',25,'Week 11: Guest Lecture','Guest Lecture. Learning activity: Seminar (3 hr)','guest lecture. learning activity: seminar (3 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK11'),(647,19,'WK12','weekly_schedule',26,'Week 12: Managing emerging technologies: Blockchain and AI','Managing emerging technologies: Blockchain and AI. Learning activity: Seminar (3 hr)','managing emerging technologies: blockchain and ai. learning activity: seminar (3 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK12'),(648,19,'WK13','weekly_schedule',27,'Week 13: Managing the cloud','Managing the cloud. Learning activity: Seminar (3 hr)','managing the cloud. learning activity: seminar (3 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK13'),(649,20,'OV01','overview',1,'Overview paragraph 1','Data visualisation, storytelling, and scenario development are prominent analytical practices that are increasingly used by professionals seeking to use data for decision making. This unit aims to equip students with necessary knowledge and data visualisation skills, acquired through real-world projects and applications inspired by leading industry practices. Students develop a holistic view of data visualisation and acquire knowledge of related tools to deal with organisational and societal challenges. This unit focuses on business/organisational decision makers and their use of data visualisation. As such this unit does not require any prior IT, computer science or data science experience.','data visualisation, storytelling, and scenario development are prominent analytical practices that are increasingly used by professionals seeking to use data for decision making. this unit aims to equip students with necessary knowledge and data visualisation skills, acquired through real-world projects and applications inspired by leading industry practices. students develop a holistic view of data visualisation and acquire knowledge of related tools to deal with organisational and societal challenges. this unit focuses on business/organisational decision makers and their use of data visualisation. as such this unit does not require any prior it, computer science or data science experience.','overview:OV01'),(650,20,'LO01','learning_outcome',2,'Learning outcome 1','LO1. Apply fundamental concepts of data visualisation to analyse and present data-related challenges in organisational and societal settings.','lo1. apply fundamental concepts of data visualisation to analyse and present data-related challenges in organisational and societal settings.','learning_outcome:LO01'),(651,20,'LO02','learning_outcome',3,'Learning outcome 2','LO2. Identify and analyse multi-disciplinary issues and ethical challenges associated with the use of data visualisation techniques.','lo2. identify and analyse multi-disciplinary issues and ethical challenges associated with the use of data visualisation techniques.','learning_outcome:LO02'),(652,20,'LO03','learning_outcome',4,'Learning outcome 3','LO3. Explain principles and best practices of data visualisation as it applies to current and emerging industry trends.','lo3. explain principles and best practices of data visualisation as it applies to current and emerging industry trends.','learning_outcome:LO03'),(653,20,'LO04','learning_outcome',5,'Learning outcome 4','LO4. Design and develop data visualisations based on real world datasets.','lo4. design and develop data visualisations based on real world datasets.','learning_outcome:LO04'),(654,20,'LO05','learning_outcome',6,'Learning outcome 5','LO5. Recommend and evaluate data visualisation solutions and present outcomes orally and verbally.','lo5. recommend and evaluate data visualisation solutions and present outcomes orally and verbally.','learning_outcome:LO05'),(655,20,'AS01','assessment',7,'Skills-based assessment Self-paced workshop','Type: Practical skill. Description: Skills-based assessment Self-paced workshop','type: practical skill. description: skills-based assessment self-paced workshop','assessment:AS01'),(656,20,'AS02','assessment',8,'Case study discussion Presentation','Type: Case studies. Description: Case study discussion Presentation','type: case studies. description: case study discussion presentation','assessment:AS02'),(657,20,'AS03','assessment',9,'In-class assessment Case study discussion','Type: Conversation. Description: In-class assessment Case study discussion','type: conversation. description: in-class assessment case study discussion','assessment:AS03'),(658,20,'AS04','assessment',10,'Individual assignment Written report','Type: Written work. Description: Individual assignment Written report','type: written work. description: individual assignment written report','assessment:AS04'),(659,20,'AS05','assessment',11,'Group project report Written report','Type: Written work. Description: Group project report Written report','type: written work. description: group project report written report','assessment:AS05'),(660,20,'AS06','assessment',12,'Group project presentation Presentation','Type: Presentation. Description: Group project presentation Presentation','type: presentation. description: group project presentation presentation','assessment:AS06'),(661,20,'AD01','assessment_description',13,'Assessment description 1','Case Study Discussion: The purpose of this assignment is for students to apply data visualisation concepts to real-world business cases and datasets. Case studies will be assigned on a weekly basis and discussed in class.','case study discussion: the purpose of this assignment is for students to apply data visualisation concepts to real-world business cases and datasets. case studies will be assigned on a weekly basis and discussed in class.','assessment_description:AD01'),(662,20,'AD02','assessment_description',14,'Assessment description 2','In-class Assessment: The purpose of this assignment is for students to evaluate and discuss data visualsation solutions as they are being applied to real-world business cases and datasets. Case studies will be assigned on a weekly basis and discussed in class.','in-class assessment: the purpose of this assignment is for students to evaluate and discuss data visualsation solutions as they are being applied to real-world business cases and datasets. case studies will be assigned on a weekly basis and discussed in class.','assessment_description:AD02'),(663,20,'AD03','assessment_description',15,'Assessment description 3','Individual Assignment: The purpose of this assignment is for students to use data visualisation techniques to address a business problem within a particular business case context.','individual assignment: the purpose of this assignment is for students to use data visualisation techniques to address a business problem within a particular business case context.','assessment_description:AD03'),(664,20,'AD04','assessment_description',16,'Assessment description 4','Group Project Report: The purpose of this assignment is to enable students to explain principles and best practices of data visualisation as it applies to a business or societal context, conduct research, stimulate broader thinking through collaborative teamwork and present their findings in written format.','group project report: the purpose of this assignment is to enable students to explain principles and best practices of data visualisation as it applies to a business or societal context, conduct research, stimulate broader thinking through collaborative teamwork and present their findings in written format.','assessment_description:AD04'),(665,20,'AD05','assessment_description',17,'Assessment description 5','Group Project Presentation: The purpose of this assignment is for students to evaluate and recommend data visualisation solutions in a manner relevant to decision makers. The assignment will assess students on their ability to utilize essential business communication skills and correspond with an audience in oral and interactive forms.','group project presentation: the purpose of this assignment is for students to evaluate and recommend data visualisation solutions in a manner relevant to decision makers. the assignment will assess students on their ability to utilize essential business communication skills and correspond with an audience in oral and interactive forms.','assessment_description:AD05'),(666,20,'AD06','assessment_description',18,'Assessment description 6','Skills-based Assessment: The purpose of this assignment is for students to develop the skills to design and develop data visualisation solutions. This are self-paced skill development exercises that have to be completed throughout the semester.','skills-based assessment: the purpose of this assignment is for students to develop the skills to design and develop data visualisation solutions. this are self-paced skill development exercises that have to be completed throughout the semester.','assessment_description:AD06'),(667,20,'AD07','assessment_description',19,'Assessment description 7','Detailed information for each assessment can be found on Canvas.','detailed information for each assessment can be found on canvas.','assessment_description:AD07'),(668,20,'WK01','weekly_schedule',20,'Week 01: Introduction to Data Visualisation','Introduction to Data Visualisation. Learning activity: Seminar (3 hr)','introduction to data visualisation. learning activity: seminar (3 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK01'),(669,20,'WK02','weekly_schedule',21,'Week 02: Conceptual Foundations of Data Visualisation','Conceptual Foundations of Data Visualisation. Learning activity: Seminar (3 hr)','conceptual foundations of data visualisation. learning activity: seminar (3 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK02'),(670,20,'WK03','weekly_schedule',22,'Week 03: Designing Effective Visualisations','Designing Effective Visualisations. Learning activity: Seminar (3 hr)','designing effective visualisations. learning activity: seminar (3 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK03'),(671,20,'WK04','weekly_schedule',23,'Week 04: Knowledge Discovery via Data Analytics','Knowledge Discovery via Data Analytics. Learning activity: Seminar (3 hr)','knowledge discovery via data analytics. learning activity: seminar (3 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK04'),(672,20,'WK05','weekly_schedule',24,'Week 05: Data Quality','Data Quality. Learning activity: Seminar (3 hr)','data quality. learning activity: seminar (3 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK05'),(673,20,'WK06','weekly_schedule',25,'Week 06: Comprehensive Case Discussion','Comprehensive Case Discussion. Learning activity: Seminar (3 hr)','comprehensive case discussion. learning activity: seminar (3 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK06'),(674,20,'WK07','weekly_schedule',26,'Week 07: Ethics of Data Visualisation','Ethics of Data Visualisation. Learning activity: Seminar (3 hr)','ethics of data visualisation. learning activity: seminar (3 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK07'),(675,20,'WK08','weekly_schedule',27,'Week 08: Infographics','Infographics. Learning activity: Seminar (3 hr)','infographics. learning activity: seminar (3 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK08'),(676,20,'WK09','weekly_schedule',28,'Week 09: Visual Storytelling','Visual Storytelling. Learning activity: Seminar (3 hr)','visual storytelling. learning activity: seminar (3 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK09'),(677,20,'WK10','weekly_schedule',29,'Week 10: Visualisation Principles and DV Lifecycle','Visualisation Principles and DV Lifecycle. Learning activity: Seminar (3 hr)','visualisation principles and dv lifecycle. learning activity: seminar (3 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK10'),(678,20,'WK11','weekly_schedule',30,'Week 11: Guided Project Work','Guided Project Work. Learning activity: Seminar (3 hr)','guided project work. learning activity: seminar (3 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK11'),(679,20,'WK12','weekly_schedule',31,'Week 12: Group Presentations','Group Presentations. Learning activity: Seminar (3 hr)','group presentations. learning activity: seminar (3 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK12'),(680,20,'WK13','weekly_schedule',32,'Week 13: Group Presentations','Group Presentations. Learning activity: Seminar (3 hr)','group presentations. learning activity: seminar (3 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK13'),(681,21,'OV01','overview',1,'Overview paragraph 1','As the amount of data generated continues to grow dramatically, managing data at scale presents a set of challenges for which organizations have to be uniquely prepared. This unit provides students with what they need to know about generating, collecting, processing, storing, managing, analysing and interpreting data. The unit provides an understanding of the importance of data strategies, data governance and data quality, challenges associated with data protection, privacy and security, data management practices, and modern platforms and architecture to streamline data operations within an organisation. Students learn the importance of confidentiality, integrity, and availability of data in mitigating information risks and emergent issues around data ethics.','as the amount of data generated continues to grow dramatically, managing data at scale presents a set of challenges for which organizations have to be uniquely prepared. this unit provides students with what they need to know about generating, collecting, processing, storing, managing, analysing and interpreting data. the unit provides an understanding of the importance of data strategies, data governance and data quality, challenges associated with data protection, privacy and security, data management practices, and modern platforms and architecture to streamline data operations within an organisation. students learn the importance of confidentiality, integrity, and availability of data in mitigating information risks and emergent issues around data ethics.','overview:OV01'),(682,21,'LO01','learning_outcome',2,'Learning outcome 1','LO1. Analyse, identify, and define organisational data management challenges based on theory and practice','lo1. analyse, identify, and define organisational data management challenges based on theory and practice','learning_outcome:LO01'),(683,21,'LO02','learning_outcome',3,'Learning outcome 2','LO2. Propose and justify data management strategies for real-world organisational scenarios','lo2. propose and justify data management strategies for real-world organisational scenarios','learning_outcome:LO02'),(684,21,'LO03','learning_outcome',4,'Learning outcome 3','LO3. Evaluate data-related systems, processes, components, and outcomes by applying theoretical concepts and knowledge of best practices','lo3. evaluate data-related systems, processes, components, and outcomes by applying theoretical concepts and knowledge of best practices','learning_outcome:LO03'),(685,21,'LO04','learning_outcome',5,'Learning outcome 4','LO4. Explain principles of data protection, privacy, securi