','assessment:AS06'),(694,21,'AD01','assessment_description',14,'Assessment description 1','In-class assessment: Case studies will be assigned on a weekly basis and discussed in class.','in-class assessment: case studies will be assigned on a weekly basis and discussed in class.','assessment_description:AD01'),(695,21,'AD02','assessment_description',15,'Assessment description 2','Case Studies: Case studies will be assigned on a weekly basis and discussed in class.','case studies: case studies will be assigned on a weekly basis and discussed in class.','assessment_description:AD02'),(696,21,'AD03','assessment_description',16,'Assessment description 3','Individual Assignment: Topic for this assignment will be provided by the lecturer and discussed in class.','individual assignment: topic for this assignment will be provided by the lecturer and discussed in class.','assessment_description:AD03'),(697,21,'AD04','assessment_description',17,'Assessment description 4','Group Report: The group report is part of the final project and will assess knowledge gained in all parts of the unit.','group report: the group report is part of the final project and will assess knowledge gained in all parts of the unit.','assessment_description:AD04'),(698,21,'AD05','assessment_description',18,'Assessment description 5','Group Presentation: The group report is part of the final project and will assess abilities to communicate findings in oral and visual forms.','group presentation: the group report is part of the final project and will assess abilities to communicate findings in oral and visual forms.','assessment_description:AD05'),(699,21,'AD06','assessment_description',19,'Assessment description 6','Skills-based Assessment: Self-paced skill development exercises to be completed.','skills-based assessment: self-paced skill development exercises to be completed.','assessment_description:AD06'),(700,21,'WK01','weekly_schedule',20,'Week 01: Introduction and Importance of Managing Data at Scale','Introduction and Importance of Managing Data at Scale. Learning activity: Seminar (3 hr)','introduction and importance of managing data at scale. learning activity: seminar (3 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK01'),(701,21,'WK02','weekly_schedule',21,'Week 02: Planning and Design in Data Lifecycle Management','Planning and Design in Data Lifecycle Management. Learning activity: Seminar (3 hr)','planning and design in data lifecycle management. learning activity: seminar (3 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK02'),(702,21,'WK03','weekly_schedule',22,'Week 03: Enabling and Maintaining Data: Part 1','Enabling and Maintaining Data: Part 1. Learning activity: Seminar (3 hr)','enabling and maintaining data: part 1. learning activity: seminar (3 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK03'),(703,21,'WK04','weekly_schedule',23,'Week 04: Enabling and Maintaining Data: Part 2','Enabling and Maintaining Data: Part 2. Learning activity: Seminar (3 hr)','enabling and maintaining data: part 2. learning activity: seminar (3 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK04'),(704,21,'WK05','weekly_schedule',24,'Week 05: Using and Enhancing Data','Using and Enhancing Data. Learning activity: Seminar (3 hr)','using and enhancing data. learning activity: seminar (3 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK05'),(705,21,'WK06','weekly_schedule',25,'Week 06: Workshop','Workshop. Learning activity: Seminar (3 hr)','workshop. learning activity: seminar (3 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK06'),(706,21,'WK07','weekly_schedule',26,'Week 07: Data Quality Management','Data Quality Management. Learning activity: Seminar (3 hr)','data quality management. learning activity: seminar (3 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK07'),(707,21,'WK08','weekly_schedule',27,'Week 08: Data Ethics','Data Ethics. Learning activity: Seminar (3 hr)','data ethics. learning activity: seminar (3 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK08'),(708,21,'WK09','weekly_schedule',28,'Week 09: Data Protection, Privacy, Security and Risks','Data Protection, Privacy, Security and Risks. Learning activity: Seminar (3 hr)','data protection, privacy, security and risks. learning activity: seminar (3 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK09'),(709,21,'WK10','weekly_schedule',29,'Week 10: Data Governance and Maturity Assessment','Data Governance and Maturity Assessment. Learning activity: Seminar (3 hr)','data governance and maturity assessment. learning activity: seminar (3 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK10'),(710,21,'WK11','weekly_schedule',30,'Week 11: Group Project Workshop','Group Project Workshop. Learning activity: Seminar (3 hr)','group project workshop. learning activity: seminar (3 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK11'),(711,21,'WK12','weekly_schedule',31,'Week 12: Group Presentations','Group Presentations. Learning activity: Seminar (3 hr)','group presentations. learning activity: seminar (3 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK12'),(712,21,'WK13','weekly_schedule',32,'Week 13: Group Presentations','Group Presentations. Learning activity: Seminar (3 hr)','group presentations. learning activity: seminar (3 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK13'),(713,22,'OV01','overview',1,'Overview paragraph 1','This unit provides an in-depth understanding of cybersecurity management, essential to organisations in protecting their data and information assets against threats and attacks. Students are exposed to concepts, methodologies, and strategies that will equip them with key skills needed to prevent, detect, and mitigate security risks, while addressing ethical and privacy concerns. This unit covers a range of topics of cybersecurity risk management, including awareness of emerging technologies, information security policy, governance frameworks, and incident response planning in response to social engineering and ransomware attacks. Students also learn how to respond to and mitigate incidents and manage employees, while developing security education with focus on effective training and awareness programs.','this unit provides an in-depth understanding of cybersecurity management, essential to organisations in protecting their data and information assets against threats and attacks. students are exposed to concepts, methodologies, and strategies that will equip them with key skills needed to prevent, detect, and mitigate security risks, while addressing ethical and privacy concerns. this unit covers a range of topics of cybersecurity risk management, including awareness of emerging technologies, information security policy, governance frameworks, and incident response planning in response to social engineering and ransomware attacks. students also learn how to respond to and mitigate incidents and manage employees, while developing security education with focus on effective training and awareness programs.','overview:OV01'),(714,22,'LO01','learning_outcome',2,'Learning outcome 1','LO1. Discuss the role of information assets and governance management frameworks in protecting such assets in organisations','lo1. discuss the role of information assets and governance management frameworks in protecting such assets in organisations','learning_outcome:LO01'),(715,22,'LO02','learning_outcome',3,'Learning outcome 2','LO2. Evaluate the risks associated with information assets and their impact on organisation','lo2. evaluate the risks associated with information assets and their impact on organisation','learning_outcome:LO02'),(716,22,'LO03','learning_outcome',4,'Learning outcome 3','LO3. Apply cybersecurity concepts and methodologies to design and implement effective security management strategies and practices','lo3. apply cybersecurity concepts and methodologies to design and implement effective security management strategies and practices','learning_outcome:LO03'),(717,22,'LO04','learning_outcome',5,'Learning outcome 4','LO4. Evaluate managerial approaches for addressing cybersecurity threats and attacks using real-world scenarios','lo4. evaluate managerial approaches for addressing cybersecurity threats and attacks using real-world scenarios','learning_outcome:LO04'),(718,22,'LO05','learning_outcome',6,'Learning outcome 5','LO5. Address the impact of employee behaviours in mitigating security risks and ensuring a secure work environment','lo5. address the impact of employee behaviours in mitigating security risks and ensuring a secure work environment','learning_outcome:LO05'),(719,22,'LO06','learning_outcome',7,'Learning outcome 6','LO6. Communicate cybersecurity issues, and collaborate towards solutions in a professional manner with people from diverse backgrounds','lo6. communicate cybersecurity issues, and collaborate towards solutions in a professional manner with people from diverse backgrounds','learning_outcome:LO06'),(720,22,'AS01','assessment',8,'Class contribution Weekly workshop contribution','Type: Contribution. Description: Class contribution Weekly workshop contribution','type: contribution. description: class contribution weekly workshop contribution','assessment:AS01'),(721,22,'AS02','assessment',9,'Early-Feedback Task Multiple-Choice Quiz','Type: Out-of-class quiz. Description: Early-Feedback Task Multiple-Choice Quiz','type: out-of-class quiz. description: early-feedback task multiple-choice quiz','assessment:AS02'),(722,22,'AS03','assessment',10,'Reflective Report Reflective Report','Type: Portfolio or journal. Description: Reflective Report Reflective Report','type: portfolio or journal. description: reflective report reflective report','assessment:AS03'),(723,22,'AS04','assessment',11,'Video briefing Video briefing','Type: Portfolio or journal. Description: Video briefing Video briefing','type: portfolio or journal. description: video briefing video briefing','assessment:AS04'),(724,22,'AS05','assessment',12,'Individual Report Individual Report','Type: Case studies. Description: Individual Report Individual Report','type: case studies. description: individual report individual report','assessment:AS05'),(725,22,'AS06','assessment',13,'Group project report Group Assignment','Type: Written work. Description: Group project report Group Assignment','type: written work. description: group project report group assignment','assessment:AS06'),(726,22,'AS07','assessment',14,'Group presentation Group presentation','Type: Presentation. Description: Group presentation Group presentation','type: presentation. description: group presentation group presentation','assessment:AS07'),(727,22,'AD01','assessment_description',15,'Assessment description 1','Detailed information for each assessment can be found on Canvas.','detailed information for each assessment can be found on canvas.','assessment_description:AD01'),(728,22,'WK01','weekly_schedule',16,'Week 01: Cybersecurity Foundations','Cybersecurity Foundations. Learning activity: Seminar (3 hr)','cybersecurity foundations. learning activity: seminar (3 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK01'),(729,22,'WK02','weekly_schedule',17,'Week 02: Cybersecurity Architecture (A)','Cybersecurity Architecture (A). Learning activity: Seminar (3 hr)','cybersecurity architecture (a). learning activity: seminar (3 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK02'),(730,22,'WK03','weekly_schedule',18,'Week 03: Cybersecurity Architecture (B)','Cybersecurity Architecture (B). Learning activity: Seminar (3 hr)','cybersecurity architecture (b). learning activity: seminar (3 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK03'),(731,22,'WK04','weekly_schedule',19,'Week 04: Incident Response','Incident Response. Learning activity: Seminar (3 hr)','incident response. learning activity: seminar (3 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK04'),(732,22,'WK05','weekly_schedule',20,'Week 05: Risk Management','Risk Management. Learning activity: Seminar (3 hr)','risk management. learning activity: seminar (3 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK05'),(733,22,'WK06','weekly_schedule',21,'Week 06: Assurance','Assurance. Learning activity: Seminar (3 hr)','assurance. learning activity: seminar (3 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK06'),(734,22,'WK07','weekly_schedule',22,'Week 07: Governance, Strategy, and Privacy','Governance, Strategy, and Privacy. Learning activity: Seminar (3 hr)','governance, strategy, and privacy. learning activity: seminar (3 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK07'),(735,22,'WK08','weekly_schedule',23,'Week 08: AI in Cyber Attacks and Defense','AI in Cyber Attacks and Defense. Learning activity: Seminar (3 hr)','ai in cyber attacks and defense. learning activity: seminar (3 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK08'),(736,22,'WK09','weekly_schedule',24,'Week 09: Group Project','Group Project. Learning activity: Seminar (3 hr)','group project. learning activity: seminar (3 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK09'),(737,22,'WK10','weekly_schedule',25,'Week 10: Group Project','Group Project. Learning activity: Seminar (3 hr)','group project. learning activity: seminar (3 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK10'),(738,22,'WK11','weekly_schedule',26,'Week 11: Industry Clinics for Group Project','Industry Clinics for Group Project. Learning activity: Seminar (3 hr)','industry clinics for group project. learning activity: seminar (3 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK11'),(739,22,'WK12','weekly_schedule',27,'Week 12: Incident Response (Advanced) and the Aftermath of Attacks','Incident Response (Advanced) and the Aftermath of Attacks. Learning activity: Seminar (3 hr)','incident response (advanced) and the aftermath of attacks. learning activity: seminar (3 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK12'),(740,22,'WK13','weekly_schedule',28,'Week 13: Final Group Project Presentations','Final Group Project Presentations. Learning activity: Seminar (3 hr)','final group project presentations. learning activity: seminar (3 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK13'),(741,23,'OV01','overview',1,'Overview paragraph 1','Traditional approaches to project management and design work well under stable conditions, when intended outcomes are well understood. Yet, under conditional of market disruption, in innovation projects, new product development or for start-up businesses, traditional methods are often restrictive and inflexible. Agile Project Management and Design Thinking offer alternative approaches that value continuous change, flexibility, time-to-market, interactive learning and self-organisation over rigorous planning and design processes. In this unit, students will learn the ethos, principles, and methods of agile project management and design thinking. Students will experience hands-on techniques such as design thinking, learn management and Scrum as applied in practice. Learning will revolve around practical activities, insights from experienced guest speakers and case studies representing various industries.','traditional approaches to project management and design work well under stable conditions, when intended outcomes are well understood. yet, under conditional of market disruption, in innovation projects, new product development or for start-up businesses, traditional methods are often restrictive and inflexible. agile project management and design thinking offer alternative approaches that value continuous change, flexibility, time-to-market, interactive learning and self-organisation over rigorous planning and design processes. in this unit, students will learn the ethos, principles, and methods of agile project management and design thinking. students will experience hands-on techniques such as design thinking, learn management and scrum as applied in practice. learning will revolve around practical activities, insights from experienced guest speakers and case studies representing various industries.','overview:OV01'),(742,23,'LO01','learning_outcome',2,'Learning outcome 1','LO1. demonstrate knowledge of the key principles of agile projects and their differences to traditional project management values','lo1. demonstrate knowledge of the key principles of agile projects and their differences to traditional project management values','learning_outcome:LO01'),(743,23,'LO02','learning_outcome',3,'Learning outcome 2','LO2. describe and apply foundational agile project management practices','lo2. describe and apply foundational agile project management practices','learning_outcome:LO02'),(744,23,'LO03','learning_outcome',4,'Learning outcome 3','LO3. describe and apply foundational design thinking practices','lo3. describe and apply foundational design thinking practices','learning_outcome:LO03'),(745,23,'LO04','learning_outcome',5,'Learning outcome 4','LO4. reflect critically about key issues in agile project management and design thinking and communicate your reflections effectively','lo4. reflect critically about key issues in agile project management and design thinking and communicate your reflections effectively','learning_outcome:LO04'),(746,23,'LO05','learning_outcome',6,'Learning outcome 5','LO5. engage effectively in team-based agile project management and design thinking practices','lo5. engage effectively in team-based agile project management and design thinking practices','learning_outcome:LO05'),(747,23,'LO06','learning_outcome',7,'Learning outcome 6','LO6. communicate effectively in group work situations in accordance with agile project management and design thinking practices','lo6. communicate effectively in group work situations in accordance with agile project management and design thinking practices','learning_outcome:LO06'),(748,23,'LO07','learning_outcome',8,'Learning outcome 7','LO7. understand the principles of people-centric design and project work practices.','lo7. understand the principles of people-centric design and project work practices.','learning_outcome:LO07'),(749,23,'AS01','assessment',9,'Essay Written essay','Type: Written work. Description: Essay Written essay','type: written work. description: essay written essay','assessment:AS01'),(750,23,'AS02','assessment',10,'Learning journals Written journal','Type: Portfolio or journal. Description: Learning journals Written journal','type: portfolio or journal. description: learning journals written journal','assessment:AS02'),(751,23,'AS03','assessment',11,'Agile activities Participation','Type: Contribution. Description: Agile activities Participation','type: contribution. description: agile activities participation','assessment:AS03'),(752,23,'AS04','assessment',12,'Product owner meetings Discussion','Type: Conversation. Description: Product owner meetings Discussion','type: conversation. description: product owner meetings discussion','assessment:AS04'),(753,23,'AS05','assessment',13,'Agile project delivery Project delivery','Type: Portfolio or journal. Description: Agile project delivery Project delivery','type: portfolio or journal. description: agile project delivery project delivery','assessment:AS05'),(754,23,'AD01','assessment_description',14,'Assessment description 1','Learning journals: The purpose of the journal is to help students keep up to date with the required work and provide students and the unit coordinators with timely feedback on student learning progress. The journal is an integral part of the agile delivery of the core part of this unit. You will reflect on each week\'s topic utilising a set of brief instructions provided via Canvas for each of the learning journal submissions. Assessment of the weekly learning journal submissions will consider both grasps of the week\'s topic, but more importantly the degree of self-reflection and engagement with the topic.','learning journals: the purpose of the journal is to help students keep up to date with the required work and provide students and the unit coordinators with timely feedback on student learning progress. the journal is an integral part of the agile delivery of the core part of this unit. you will reflect on each week\'s topic utilising a set of brief instructions provided via canvas for each of the learning journal submissions. assessment of the weekly learning journal submissions will consider both grasps of the week\'s topic, but more importantly the degree of self-reflection and engagement with the topic.','assessment_description:AD01'),(755,23,'AD02','assessment_description',15,'Assessment description 2','Agile activities: The agile learning sessions are built around hands-on activities whose learning outcomes depend on the active participation of each student. It is paramount that students pay attention to the purpose of each activity and show initiative in applying themselves to the task at hand. In-class activities involve the development of artefacts across agile sprints through iterative work, enabling multiple forms of engagement and active participation and allowing students to contribute in a variety of ways.','agile activities: the agile learning sessions are built around hands-on activities whose learning outcomes depend on the active participation of each student. it is paramount that students pay attention to the purpose of each activity and show initiative in applying themselves to the task at hand. in-class activities involve the development of artefacts across agile sprints through iterative work, enabling multiple forms of engagement and active participation and allowing students to contribute in a variety of ways.','assessment_description:AD02'),(756,23,'AD03','assessment_description',16,'Assessment description 3','Product owner meetings: The purpose of PO meetings is for students to engage in time-boxed discussions with a designated product owner from the teaching team to review each sprint’s MVP. Teams use targeted feedback on personas, design thinking, and concept development to refine their work and guide priorities for the next sprint, with an emphasis on learning and iteration rather than polished outcomes.','product owner meetings: the purpose of po meetings is for students to engage in time-boxed discussions with a designated product owner from the teaching team to review each sprint\'s mvp. teams use targeted feedback on personas, design thinking, and concept development to refine their work and guide priorities for the next sprint, with an emphasis on learning and iteration rather than polished outcomes.','assessment_description:AD03'),(757,23,'AD04','assessment_description',17,'Assessment description 4','Agile project delivery: The objective of the agile project is to use the knowledge and practical skills in agile projects and design thinking acquired in this unit of study to apply to a real-world problem. The focus of this project is in applying appropriate techniques and practices in creating the desired project outcome represented in diagrams, video and textual elements. While the outcome as such is not unimportant, the focus of this assignment and its assessment is on the application of the agile project management and design thinking techniques.','agile project delivery: the objective of the agile project is to use the knowledge and practical skills in agile projects and design thinking acquired in this unit of study to apply to a real-world problem. the focus of this project is in applying appropriate techniques and practices in creating the desired project outcome represented in diagrams, video and textual elements. while the outcome as such is not unimportant, the focus of this assignment and its assessment is on the application of the agile project management and design thinking techniques.','assessment_description:AD04'),(758,23,'AD05','assessment_description',18,'Assessment description 5','Essay: The purpose of the essay is to demonstrate grasp of the agile philosophy and principles, as well as the agile project management and design thinking practices and techniques. The focus of the essay will lie in synthesising the learnings derived from the unit of study.','essay: the purpose of the essay is to demonstrate grasp of the agile philosophy and principles, as well as the agile project management and design thinking practices and techniques. the focus of the essay will lie in synthesising the learnings derived from the unit of study.','assessment_description:AD05'),(759,23,'AD06','assessment_description',19,'Assessment description 6','Detailed information for each assessment can be found on Canvas.','detailed information for each assessment can be found on canvas.','assessment_description:AD06'),(760,23,'WK01','weekly_schedule',20,'Week 01: Introduction and overview','Introduction and overview. Learning activity: Seminar (3 hr)','introduction and overview. learning activity: seminar (3 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK01'),(761,23,'WK02','weekly_schedule',21,'Week 02: Practices, principles and philosophy of agile project delivery','Practices, principles and philosophy of agile project delivery. Learning activity: Seminar (3 hr)','practices, principles and philosophy of agile project delivery. learning activity: seminar (3 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK02'),(762,23,'WK03','weekly_schedule',22,'Week 03: Practices, principles and philosophy of design thinking','Practices, principles and philosophy of design thinking. Learning activity: Seminar (3 hr)','practices, principles and philosophy of design thinking. learning activity: seminar (3 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK03'),(763,23,'WK04','weekly_schedule',23,'Week 04: Agile learning session 1','Agile learning session 1. Learning activity: Seminar (3 hr)','agile learning session 1. learning activity: seminar (3 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK04'),(764,23,'WK05','weekly_schedule',24,'Week 05: Agile learning session 2','Agile learning session 2. Learning activity: Seminar (3 hr)','agile learning session 2. learning activity: seminar (3 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK05'),(765,23,'WK06','weekly_schedule',25,'Week 06: Agile learning session 3','Agile learning session 3. Learning activity: Seminar (3 hr)','agile learning session 3. learning activity: seminar (3 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK06'),(766,23,'WK07','weekly_schedule',26,'Week 07: Agile learning session 4','Agile learning session 4. Learning activity: Seminar (3 hr)','agile learning session 4. learning activity: seminar (3 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK07'),(767,23,'WK08','weekly_schedule',27,'Week 08: Agile learning session 5','Agile learning session 5. Learning activity: Seminar (3 hr)','agile learning session 5. learning activity: seminar (3 hr)','weekly_schedule:W