of technology in business and society. it problematizes the hype surrounding new technological developments (gadgets), the deification of technology as a solution to problems of all kinds (gods), and the, often unintended, consequences of technology applications (godzilla). the unit utilises current technological developments as examples for discussion and examines technology and its design and application in the context of social networks, power relations, and current business trends.','overview:OV01'),(774,24,'LO01','learning_outcome',2,'Learning outcome 1','LO1. Make and defend evaluations of socio-technical systems.','lo1. make and defend evaluations of socio-technical systems.','learning_outcome:LO01'),(775,24,'LO02','learning_outcome',3,'Learning outcome 2','LO2. Construct arguments regarding the benefits and consequences of technologies in organizational and societal setting.','lo2. construct arguments regarding the benefits and consequences of technologies in organizational and societal setting.','learning_outcome:LO02'),(776,24,'LO03','learning_outcome',4,'Learning outcome 3','LO3. Categorize perspectives based on alternative ethical stances.','lo3. categorize perspectives based on alternative ethical stances.','learning_outcome:LO03'),(777,24,'LO04','learning_outcome',5,'Learning outcome 4','LO4. Create and assess alternative scenario prototypes of socio-technical systems at individual, organizational and societal levels.','lo4. create and assess alternative scenario prototypes of socio-technical systems at individual, organizational and societal levels.','learning_outcome:LO04'),(778,24,'AS01','assessment',6,'Reflection Journal The purpose of the reflection journal is to reflect on the weeks learning.','Type: Portfolio or journal. Description: Reflection Journal The purpose of the reflection journal is to reflect on the weeks learning.','type: portfolio or journal. description: reflection journal the purpose of the reflection journal is to reflect on the weeks learning.','assessment:AS01'),(779,24,'AS02','assessment',7,'Reflection Journal The purpose of the reflection journal is to reflect on the weeks learning.','Type: Portfolio or journal. Description: Reflection Journal The purpose of the reflection journal is to reflect on the weeks learning.','type: portfolio or journal. description: reflection journal the purpose of the reflection journal is to reflect on the weeks learning.','assessment:AS02'),(780,24,'AS03','assessment',8,'Reflection Journal The purpose of the reflection journal is to reflect on the weeks learning.','Type: Portfolio or journal. Description: Reflection Journal The purpose of the reflection journal is to reflect on the weeks learning.','type: portfolio or journal. description: reflection journal the purpose of the reflection journal is to reflect on the weeks learning.','assessment:AS03'),(781,24,'AS04','assessment',9,'Group Project Students will work in groups applying methods introduced during class.','Type: Creative work. Description: Group Project Students will work in groups applying methods introduced during class.','type: creative work. description: group project students will work in groups applying methods introduced during class.','assessment:AS04'),(782,24,'AS05','assessment',10,'Final Essay The final report/essay will provide opportunity to synthesize learning.','Type: Written work. Description: Final Essay The final report/essay will provide opportunity to synthesize learning.','type: written work. description: final essay the final report/essay will provide opportunity to synthesize learning.','assessment:AS05'),(783,24,'AD01','assessment_description',11,'Assessment description 1','Video learning journals (working in pairs, (3 videos 2.5 minutes each; via Canvas)','video learning journals (working in pairs, (3 videos 2.5 minutes each; via canvas)','assessment_description:AD01'),(784,24,'AD02','assessment_description',12,'Assessment description 2','Group project presentations/demonstrations in class (10 minutes exhibition including Q&A during week 8. 750 word writeup due same day.)','group project presentations/demonstrations in class (10 minutes exhibition including q&a during week 8. 750 word writeup due same day.)','assessment_description:AD02'),(785,24,'AD03','assessment_description',13,'Assessment description 3','Final essay (1000 words) submitted via Canvas','final essay (1000 words) submitted via canvas','assessment_description:AD03'),(786,24,'WK01','weekly_schedule',14,'Week 01: Futures, Megatrends and Metaphors','Futures, Megatrends and Metaphors. Learning activity: Lecture (5 hr)','futures, megatrends and metaphors. learning activity: lecture (5 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK01'),(787,24,'WK02','weekly_schedule',15,'Week 02: Forecasting, Prediction; Gadgets on the Loose','Forecasting, Prediction; Gadgets on the Loose. Learning activity: Lecture (5 hr)','forecasting, prediction; gadgets on the loose. learning activity: lecture (5 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK02'),(788,24,'WK03','weekly_schedule',16,'Week 03: Scenario thinking, scenario analysis; Modern Gods','Scenario thinking, scenario analysis; Modern Gods. Learning activity: Lecture (5 hr)','scenario thinking, scenario analysis; modern gods. learning activity: lecture (5 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK03'),(789,24,'WK04','weekly_schedule',17,'Week 04: Foresight, speculative futures ; Monsters in the Classroom','Foresight, speculative futures ; Monsters in the Classroom. Learning activity: Lecture (5 hr)','foresight, speculative futures ; monsters in the classroom. learning activity: lecture (5 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK04'),(790,24,'WK05','weekly_schedule',18,'Week 05: Digital Geographies; Speculation','Digital Geographies; Speculation. Learning activity: Lecture (5 hr)','digital geographies; speculation. learning activity: lecture (5 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK05'),(791,24,'WK06','weekly_schedule',19,'Week 06: AI Fluency Sprint','AI Fluency Sprint. Learning activity: Lecture (5 hr)','ai fluency sprint. learning activity: lecture (5 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK06'),(792,24,'WK07','weekly_schedule',20,'Week 07: Technological Imaginaries','Technological Imaginaries. Learning activity: Lecture (5 hr)','technological imaginaries. learning activity: lecture (5 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK07'),(793,24,'WK08','weekly_schedule',21,'Week 08: In-class work and Presentations; Attendance Mandatory','In-class work and Presentations; Attendance Mandatory. Learning activity: Lecture (5 hr)','in-class work and presentations; attendance mandatory. learning activity: lecture (5 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK08'),(794,25,'OV01','overview',1,'Overview paragraph 1','This unit introduces students to the foundations of project management in business contexts. It provides an overview and practical understanding of different project management approaches, ranging from structured frameworks such as the Project Management Body of Knowledge (PMBOK) to light-weight techniques such as Agile or Lean Management. Students learn how to select appropriate projects based on their alignment with an organisation\'s strategy and then how to manage those projects successfully from initiation through execution to completion. The unit explores both the technical and behavioural aspects of project management and students gain experience in critically analysing the application of techniques in specific business contexts. As organisations increasingly structure their activities on a project basis, the unit is of value to a range of discipline specialisations.','this unit introduces students to the foundations of project management in business contexts. it provides an overview and practical understanding of different project management approaches, ranging from structured frameworks such as the project management body of knowledge (pmbok) to light-weight techniques such as agile or lean management. students learn how to select appropriate projects based on their alignment with an organisation\'s strategy and then how to manage those projects successfully from initiation through execution to completion. the unit explores both the technical and behavioural aspects of project management and students gain experience in critically analysing the application of techniques in specific business contexts. as organisations increasingly structure their activities on a project basis, the unit is of value to a range of discipline specialisations.','overview:OV01'),(795,25,'LO01','learning_outcome',2,'Learning outcome 1','LO1. Apply and analyse project management methodologies, frameworks and knowledge areas for planning across the project lifecycle.','lo1. apply and analyse project management methodologies, frameworks and knowledge areas for planning across the project lifecycle.','learning_outcome:LO01'),(796,25,'LO02','learning_outcome',3,'Learning outcome 2','LO2. Evaluate formal and adaptive project management practices, considering their guiding principles and processes.','lo2. evaluate formal and adaptive project management practices, considering their guiding principles and processes.','learning_outcome:LO02'),(797,25,'LO03','learning_outcome',4,'Learning outcome 3','LO3. Evaluate and critically analyse the factors affecting various project stakeholders and team processes.','lo3. evaluate and critically analyse the factors affecting various project stakeholders and team processes.','learning_outcome:LO03'),(798,25,'LO04','learning_outcome',5,'Learning outcome 4','LO4. Create and critically reflect on project planning by applying relevant project management techniques.','lo4. create and critically reflect on project planning by applying relevant project management techniques.','learning_outcome:LO04'),(799,25,'LO05','learning_outcome',6,'Learning outcome 5','LO5. Identify and critically assess project challenges, success factors and the applicability of formal project management frameworks.','lo5. identify and critically assess project challenges, success factors and the applicability of formal project management frameworks.','learning_outcome:LO05'),(800,25,'AS01','assessment',7,'Individual assignment 2 Written task','Type: Written work. Description: Individual assignment 2 Written task','type: written work. description: individual assignment 2 written task','assessment:AS01'),(801,25,'AS02','assessment',8,'Individual assignment 1 Written tasks completed in tutorials','Type: In-person written or creative task. Description: Individual assignment 1 Written tasks completed in tutorials','type: in-person written or creative task. description: individual assignment 1 written tasks completed in tutorials','assessment:AS02'),(802,25,'AS03','assessment',9,'Class Quiz Online quiz','Type: Out-of-class quiz. Description: Class Quiz Online quiz','type: out-of-class quiz. description: class quiz online quiz','assessment:AS03'),(803,25,'AS04','assessment',10,'Group Project Assignment Written task','Type: Written work. Description: Group Project Assignment Written task','type: written work. description: group project assignment written task','assessment:AS04'),(804,25,'AD01','assessment_description',11,'Assessment description 1','Class Quiz: One (1) online quiz will be completed by Monday, Week 4 at 23:59. The quiz assesses students’ understanding of foundational project management concepts introduced in the first three weeks of the unit, including the project management landscape, project value and benefits, governance, ethics, professional practice, and contemporary project management frameworks. Questions may draw on lecture content, tutorial activities, prescribed readings, and other learning resources. The quiz will be administered through Canvas using a variety of question types. Students will be assessed on the accuracy and completeness of their responses.','class quiz: one (1) online quiz will be completed by monday, week 4 at 23:59. the quiz assesses students\' understanding of foundational project management concepts introduced in the first three weeks of the unit, including the project management landscape, project value and benefits, governance, ethics, professional practice, and contemporary project management frameworks. questions may draw on lecture content, tutorial activities, prescribed readings, and other learning resources. the quiz will be administered through canvas using a variety of question types. students will be assessed on the accuracy and completeness of their responses.','assessment_description:AD01'),(805,25,'AD02','assessment_description',12,'Assessment description 2','Individual Assignment 1: This secure written assessment is completed progressively during tutorials in Weeks 4, 5 and 6. Students will assume the role of a project team member who has been asked by a Project Manager to investigate a proposed project and provide professional advice to support project planning and decision-making.','individual assignment 1: this secure written assessment is completed progressively during tutorials in weeks 4, 5 and 6. students will assume the role of a project team member who has been asked by a project manager to investigate a proposed project and provide professional advice to support project planning and decision-making.','assessment_description:AD02'),(806,25,'AD03','assessment_description',13,'Assessment description 3','Working with a supplied project scenario, students will engage with project information and stakeholder perspectives to analyse the project’s context, complexity, uncertainty, and organisational environment. Students will evaluate the suitability of different project management approaches, identify project risks and challenges, and provide recommendations regarding project delivery, planning priorities, and success factors.','working with a supplied project scenario, students will engage with project information and stakeholder perspectives to analyse the project\'s context, complexity, uncertainty, and organisational environment. students will evaluate the suitability of different project management approaches, identify project risks and challenges, and provide recommendations regarding project delivery, planning priorities, and success factors.','assessment_description:AD03'),(807,25,'AD04','assessment_description',14,'Assessment description 4','This assessment is completed during scheduled tutorial classes. Work undertaken during each tutorial session will be recorded to maintain assessment integrity and combined into a final submission. Students will be assessed on their ability to critically analyse project contexts, evaluate project management frameworks and methodologies, identify project challenges, and provide well-supported recommendations for project planning and delivery.','this assessment is completed during scheduled tutorial classes. work undertaken during each tutorial session will be recorded to maintain assessment integrity and combined into a final submission. students will be assessed on their ability to critically analyse project contexts, evaluate project management frameworks and methodologies, identify project challenges, and provide well-supported recommendations for project planning and delivery.','assessment_description:AD04'),(808,25,'AD05','assessment_description',15,'Assessment description 5','Group Project Assignment: This assignment adopts a Project-Based Learning (PBL) approach, in which student teams act as a project planning team, developing a comprehensive project planning portfolio for a simulated, realistic organisational project.','group project assignment: this assignment adopts a project-based learning (pbl) approach, in which student teams act as a project planning team, developing a comprehensive project planning portfolio for a simulated, realistic organisational project.','assessment_description:AD05'),(809,25,'AD06','assessment_description',16,'Assessment description 6','Throughout the semester, teams will work within a simulated project environment supported by AI-enabled stakeholder personas. These stakeholder personas may represent, for example, project sponsors, clients, regulators, technical specialists, end users, operations managers, and other project stakeholders. Teams will be required to actively engage with these stakeholders to gather information, clarify requirements, resolve conflicts, manage emerging issues, and inform project planning decisions.','throughout the semester, teams will work within a simulated project environment supported by ai-enabled stakeholder personas. these stakeholder personas may represent, for example, project sponsors, clients, regulators, technical specialists, end users, operations managers, and other project stakeholders. teams will be required to actively engage with these stakeholders to gather information, clarify requirements, resolve conflicts, manage emerging issues, and inform project planning decisions.','assessment_description:AD06'),(810,25,'AD07','assessment_description',17,'Assessment description 7','As the project progresses, new information, stakeholder feedback, constraints, and project challenges may emerge, requiring teams to reassess assumptions and adapt their planning approaches. Students will apply project management concepts, methodologies, frameworks, and techniques to develop a professional project planning portfolio that may include governance structures, project scope, methodology selection and tailoring rationale, schedules, stakeholder and communication plans, resource and team plans, risk management artefacts, and approaches to measuring project success and benefits realisation.','as the project progresses, new information, stakeholder feedback, constraints, and project challenges may emerge, requiring teams to reassess assumptions and adapt their planning approaches. students will apply project management concepts, methodologies, frameworks, and techniques to develop a professional project planning portfolio that may include governance structures, project scope, methodology selection and tailoring rationale, schedules, stakeholder and communication plans, resource and team plans, risk management artefacts, and approaches to measuring project success and benefits realisation.','assessment_description:AD07'),(811,25,'AD08','assessment_description',18,'Assessment description 8','Students will be expected to justify their project management decisions and demonstrate how project context, complexity, uncertainty, stakeholder needs, and organisational objectives have influenced their chosen approach. Students will be assessed on the quality and integration of their planning artefacts, continued and professional engagement with project stakeholders, application of project management theory to practice, and the strength of their supporting rationale.','students will be expected to justify their project management decisions and demonstrate how project context, complexity, uncertainty, stakeholder needs, and organisational objectives have influenced their chosen approach. students will be assessed on the quality and integration of their planning artefacts, continued and professional engagement with project stakeholders, application of project management theory to practice, and the strength of their supporting rationale.','assessment_description:AD08'),(812,25,'AD09','assessment_description',19,'Assessment description 9','Individual Assignment 2: This individual assessment requires students to critically evaluate project management decisions made throughout the group project and reflect on their professional learning and development. Drawing on unit concepts, contemporary project management literature, experiences gained through the project simulation, and interactions with project stakeholders, students will prepare a concise analytical report examining the suitability and application of project management approaches in complex organisational environments.','individual assignment 2: this individual assessment requires students to critically evaluate project management decisions made throughout the group project and reflect on their professional learning and development. drawing on unit concepts, contemporary project management literature, experiences gained through the project simulation, and interactions with project stakeholders, students will prepare a concise analytical report examining the suitability and application of project management approaches in complex organisational environments.','assessment_description:AD09'),(813,25,'AD10','assessment_description',20,'Assessment description 10','Students will critically analyse project challenges, stakeholder dynamics, team processes, planning decisions, and the selection and tailoring of project management methodologies and frameworks. Students will also reflect on lessons learned from the project, considering how project complexity, uncertainty, stakeholder engagement, and emerging technologies influenced project outcomes and decision-making.','students will critically analyse project challenges, stakeholder dynamics, team processes, planning decisions, and the selection and tailoring of project management methodologies and frameworks. students will also reflect on lessons learned from the project, considering how project complexity, uncertainty, stakeholder engagement, and emerging technologies influenced project outcomes and decision-making.','assessment_description:AD10'),(814,25,'AD11','assessment_description',21,'Assessment description 11','Students will be assessed on the quality of their critical analysis, the integration of relevant literature, the depth of their reflection, their ability to evaluate project management approaches, and their capacity to justify recommendations for future practice.','students will be assessed on the quality of their critical analysis, the integration of relevant literature, the depth of their reflection, their ability to evaluate project management approaches, and their capacity to justify recommendations for future practice.','assessment_description:AD11'),(815,25,'AD12','assessment_description',22,'Assessment description 12','Detailed instructions, marking criteria, project briefs, stakeholder interaction requirements, and submission guidelines for all assessments will be provided on Canvas.','detailed instructions, marking criteria, project briefs, stakeholder interaction requirements, and submission guidelines for all assessments will be provided on canvas.','assessment_description:AD12'),(816,25,'WK01','weekly_schedule',23,'Week 01: The Project Management Landscape [online recorded lecture + on-campus tutorial]','The Project Management Landscape [online recorded lecture + on-campus tutorial]. Learning activity: Lecture (1.5 hr)','the project management landscape [online recorded lecture + on-campus tutorial]. learning activity: lecture (1.5 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK01'),(817,25,'WK02','weekly_schedule',24,'Week 01: The Project Management Landscape [online recorded lecture + on-campus tutorial]','The Project Management Landscape [online recorded lecture + on-campus tutorial]. Learning activity: Tutorial (1.5 hr)','the project management landscape [online recorded lecture + on-campus tutorial]. learning activity: tutorial (1.5 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK02'),(818,25,'WK03','weekly_schedule',25,'Week 02: Value, Strategy and Benefits Realisation [online recorded lecture + on-campus tutorial]','Value, Strategy and Benefits Realisation [online recorded lecture + on-campus tutorial]. Learning activity: Lecture (1.5 hr)','value, strategy and benefits realisation [online recorded lecture + on-campus tutorial]. learning activity: lecture (1.5 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK03'),(819,25,'WK04','weekly_schedule',26,'Week 02: Value, Strategy and Benefits Realisation [online recorded lecture + on-campus tutorial]','Value, Strategy and Benefits Realisation [online recorded lecture + on-campus tutorial]. Learning activity: Tutorial (1.5 hr)','value, strategy and benefits realisation [online recorded lecture