 tutorial]. Learning activity: Tutorial (1.5 hr)','risk, uncertainty and project challenges [online recorded lecture + on-campus tutorial]. learning activity: tutorial (1.5 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK14'),(830,25,'WK15','weekly_schedule',37,'Week 08: Communication and Stakeholder Engagement [online recorded lecture + on-campus tutorial]','Communication and Stakeholder Engagement [online recorded lecture + on-campus tutorial]. Learning activity: Lecture (1.5 hr)','communication and stakeholder engagement [online recorded lecture + on-campus tutorial]. learning activity: lecture (1.5 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK15'),(831,25,'WK16','weekly_schedule',38,'Week 08: Communication and Stakeholder Engagement [online recorded lecture + on-campus tutorial]','Communication and Stakeholder Engagement [online recorded lecture + on-campus tutorial]. Learning activity: Tutorial (1.5 hr)','communication and stakeholder engagement [online recorded lecture + on-campus tutorial]. learning activity: tutorial (1.5 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK16'),(832,25,'WK17','weekly_schedule',39,'Week 09: Resources, Teams and Leadership [online recorded lecture + on-campus tutorial]','Resources, Teams and Leadership [online recorded lecture + on-campus tutorial]. Learning activity: Lecture (1.5 hr)','resources, teams and leadership [online recorded lecture + on-campus tutorial]. learning activity: lecture (1.5 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK17'),(833,25,'WK18','weekly_schedule',40,'Week 09: Resources, Teams and Leadership [online recorded lecture + on-campus tutorial]','Resources, Teams and Leadership [online recorded lecture + on-campus tutorial]. Learning activity: Tutorial (1.5 hr)','resources, teams and leadership [online recorded lecture + on-campus tutorial]. learning activity: tutorial (1.5 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK18'),(834,25,'WK19','weekly_schedule',41,'Week 10: Performance, Finance and Benefits Realisation [online recorded lecture + on-campus tutorial]','Performance, Finance and Benefits Realisation [online recorded lecture + on-campus tutorial]. Learning activity: Lecture (1.5 hr)','performance, finance and benefits realisation [online recorded lecture + on-campus tutorial]. learning activity: lecture (1.5 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK19'),(835,25,'WK20','weekly_schedule',42,'Week 10: Performance, Finance and Benefits Realisation [online recorded lecture + on-campus tutorial]','Performance, Finance and Benefits Realisation [online recorded lecture + on-campus tutorial]. Learning activity: Tutorial (1.5 hr)','performance, finance and benefits realisation [online recorded lecture + on-campus tutorial]. learning activity: tutorial (1.5 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK20'),(836,25,'WK21','weekly_schedule',43,'Week 11: Sustainability, Responsibility and Emerging Challenges [online recorded lecture + on-campus tutorial]','Sustainability, Responsibility and Emerging Challenges [online recorded lecture + on-campus tutorial]. Learning activity: Lecture (1.5 hr)','sustainability, responsibility and emerging challenges [online recorded lecture + on-campus tutorial]. learning activity: lecture (1.5 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK21'),(837,25,'WK22','weekly_schedule',44,'Week 11: Sustainability, Responsibility and Emerging Challenges [online recorded lecture + on-campus tutorial]','Sustainability, Responsibility and Emerging Challenges [online recorded lecture + on-campus tutorial]. Learning activity: Tutorial (1.5 hr)','sustainability, responsibility and emerging challenges [online recorded lecture + on-campus tutorial]. learning activity: tutorial (1.5 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK22'),(838,25,'WK23','weekly_schedule',45,'Week 12: Tailoring, Adaptive and Hybrid Project Management [online recorded lecture + on-campus tutorial]','Tailoring, Adaptive and Hybrid Project Management [online recorded lecture + on-campus tutorial]. Learning activity: Lecture (1.5 hr)','tailoring, adaptive and hybrid project management [online recorded lecture + on-campus tutorial]. learning activity: lecture (1.5 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK23'),(839,25,'WK24','weekly_schedule',46,'Week 12: Tailoring, Adaptive and Hybrid Project Management [online recorded lecture + on-campus tutorial]','Tailoring, Adaptive and Hybrid Project Management [online recorded lecture + on-campus tutorial]. Learning activity: Tutorial (1.5 hr)','tailoring, adaptive and hybrid project management [online recorded lecture + on-campus tutorial]. learning activity: tutorial (1.5 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK24'),(840,25,'WK25','weekly_schedule',47,'Week 13: AI, PM Maturity and Professional Identity [online recorded lecture + on-campus tutorial]','AI, PM Maturity and Professional Identity [online recorded lecture + on-campus tutorial]. Learning activity: Lecture (1.5 hr)','ai, pm maturity and professional identity [online recorded lecture + on-campus tutorial]. learning activity: lecture (1.5 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK25'),(841,25,'WK26','weekly_schedule',48,'Week 13: AI, PM Maturity and Professional Identity [online recorded lecture + on-campus tutorial]','AI, PM Maturity and Professional Identity [online recorded lecture + on-campus tutorial]. Learning activity: Tutorial (1.5 hr)','ai, pm maturity and professional identity [online recorded lecture + on-campus tutorial]. learning activity: tutorial (1.5 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK26'),(842,26,'OV01','overview',1,'Overview paragraph 1','Despite the widely acknowledged importance of data as a strategic resource, organisations continue to struggle with appropriately managing their data assets. This unit highlights the crucial importance of data governance in the administration, protection, and optimisation of data. It provides an exploration into the core principles of data governance, discusses the influence of emerging technologies, such as artificial intelligence, and examines the broader societal and ethical implications surrounding data. Through interactive case studies and hands-on assessments, students learn about the complex issues surrounding data governance and formulate and persuasively communicate practical data governance approaches to empower organisations to navigate their data landscape.','despite the widely acknowledged importance of data as a strategic resource, organisations continue to struggle with appropriately managing their data assets. this unit highlights the crucial importance of data governance in the administration, protection, and optimisation of data. it provides an exploration into the core principles of data governance, discusses the influence of emerging technologies, such as artificial intelligence, and examines the broader societal and ethical implications surrounding data. through interactive case studies and hands-on assessments, students learn about the complex issues surrounding data governance and formulate and persuasively communicate practical data governance approaches to empower organisations to navigate their data landscape.','overview:OV01'),(843,26,'LO01','learning_outcome',2,'Learning outcome 1','LO1. Discuss and apply the foundational principles and concepts of data governance, including stewardship, data quality, security, metadata, and lifecycle management','lo1. discuss and apply the foundational principles and concepts of data governance, including stewardship, data quality, security, metadata, and lifecycle management','learning_outcome:LO01'),(844,26,'LO02','learning_outcome',3,'Learning outcome 2','LO2. Reflect critically on the implications of emerging technologies, such as artificial intelligence, blockchain, and internet of things, on data governance practices','lo2. reflect critically on the implications of emerging technologies, such as artificial intelligence, blockchain, and internet of things, on data governance practices','learning_outcome:LO02'),(845,26,'LO03','learning_outcome',4,'Learning outcome 3','LO3. Analyze case studies of data governance practices in various (inter)organizational contexts to identify stakeholders, key success factors, challenges, and opportunities','lo3. analyze case studies of data governance practices in various (inter)organizational contexts to identify stakeholders, key success factors, challenges, and opportunities','learning_outcome:LO03'),(846,26,'LO04','learning_outcome',5,'Learning outcome 4','LO4. Evaluate the broader societal and ethical implications surrounding data governance, including privacy and transparency, and propose and discuss the effectiveness of ethical guidelines','lo4. evaluate the broader societal and ethical implications surrounding data governance, including privacy and transparency, and propose and discuss the effectiveness of ethical guidelines','learning_outcome:LO04'),(847,26,'LO05','learning_outcome',6,'Learning outcome 5','LO5. Assess how organizations can leverage digital data and become more data-driven to enhance decision-making processes','lo5. assess how organizations can leverage digital data and become more data-driven to enhance decision-making processes','learning_outcome:LO05'),(848,26,'LO06','learning_outcome',7,'Learning outcome 6','LO6. Develop and present a comprehensive data governance strategy tailored to a specific case organization, integrating lecture materials, and ensuring alignment with the organizational context','lo6. develop and present a comprehensive data governance strategy tailored to a specific case organization, integrating lecture materials, and ensuring alignment with the organizational context','learning_outcome:LO06'),(849,26,'AS01','assessment',8,'Individual Report A Please see detailed Individual Assignment requirements in Canvas.','Type: Written work. Description: Individual Report A Please see detailed Individual Assignment requirements in Canvas.','type: written work. description: individual report a please see detailed individual assignment requirements in canvas.','assessment:AS01'),(850,26,'AS02','assessment',9,'Individual report B Part I Report B part I (750 words); marked for completeness. Failure to submit will affect the mark for Report B part II.','Type: Case studies. Description: Individual report B Part I Report B part I (750 words); marked for completeness. Failure to submit will affect the mark for Report B part II.','type: case studies. description: individual report b part i report b part i (750 words); marked for completeness. failure to submit will affect the mark for report b part ii.','assessment:AS02'),(851,26,'AS03','assessment',10,'Individual Report B Part II Full report after a mandatory in-class assignment in week 9. Failure to attend in class in week 9 will prohibit the student from being able to submit this report. Further assignment requirements in Canvas.','Type: Case studies. Description: Individual Report B Part II Full report after a mandatory in-class assignment in week 9. Failure to attend in class in week 9 will prohibit the student from being able to submit this report. Further assignment requirements in Canvas.','type: case studies. description: individual report b part ii full report after a mandatory in-class assignment in week 9. failure to attend in class in week 9 will prohibit the student from being able to submit this report. further assignment requirements in canvas.','assessment:AS03'),(852,26,'AS04','assessment',11,'Group project pitch Pitch of data strategy','Type: Presentation. Description: Group project pitch Pitch of data strategy','type: presentation. description: group project pitch pitch of data strategy','assessment:AS04'),(853,26,'AS05','assessment',12,'Group project report Full report with formative submissions throughout the semester. See Canvas for full details.','Type: Written work. Description: Group project report Full report with formative submissions throughout the semester. See Canvas for full details.','type: written work. description: group project report full report with formative submissions throughout the semester. see canvas for full details.','assessment:AS05'),(854,26,'AD01','assessment_description',13,'Assessment description 1','Group project report and pitch: The group project is an applied assignment that requires the team\'s development of a data strategy.','group project report and pitch: the group project is an applied assignment that requires the team\'s development of a data strategy.','assessment_description:AD01'),(855,26,'AD02','assessment_description',14,'Assessment description 2','Individual Assignment A: The report will assess the implications of generative AI for data governance.','individual assignment a: the report will assess the implications of generative ai for data governance.','assessment_description:AD02'),(856,26,'AD03','assessment_description',15,'Assessment description 3','Individual Assignment B: The report will explore decision-making with data in complex organizational settings.','individual assignment b: the report will explore decision-making with data in complex organizational settings.','assessment_description:AD03'),(857,26,'WK01','weekly_schedule',16,'Week 01: Introduction and overview','Introduction and overview. Learning activity: Seminar (3 hr)','introduction and overview. learning activity: seminar (3 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK01'),(858,26,'WK02','weekly_schedule',17,'Week 02: Introduction to data governance','Introduction to data governance. Learning activity: Seminar (3 hr)','introduction to data governance. learning activity: seminar (3 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK02'),(859,26,'WK03','weekly_schedule',18,'Week 03: Strategies, programs, and frameworks','Strategies, programs, and frameworks. Learning activity: Seminar (3 hr)','strategies, programs, and frameworks. learning activity: seminar (3 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK03'),(860,26,'WK04','weekly_schedule',19,'Week 04: Data quality','Data quality. Learning activity: Seminar (3 hr)','data quality. learning activity: seminar (3 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK04'),(861,26,'WK05','weekly_schedule',20,'Week 05: The impact of emerging technologies','The impact of emerging technologies. Learning activity: Seminar (3 hr)','the impact of emerging technologies. learning activity: seminar (3 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK05'),(862,26,'WK06','weekly_schedule',21,'Week 06: Leveraging digital data for decision-making','Leveraging digital data for decision-making. Learning activity: Seminar (3 hr)','leveraging digital data for decision-making. learning activity: seminar (3 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK06'),(863,26,'WK07','weekly_schedule',22,'Week 07: Societal and ethical considerations','Societal and ethical considerations. Learning activity: Seminar (3 hr)','societal and ethical considerations. learning activity: seminar (3 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK07'),(864,26,'WK08','weekly_schedule',23,'Week 08: Securing and protecting data','Securing and protecting data. Learning activity: Seminar (3 hr)','securing and protecting data. learning activity: seminar (3 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK08'),(865,26,'WK09','weekly_schedule',24,'Week 09: Collective data governance','Collective data governance. Learning activity: Seminar (3 hr)','collective data governance. learning activity: seminar (3 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK09'),(866,26,'WK10','weekly_schedule',25,'Week 10: Power and politics','Power and politics. Learning activity: Seminar (3 hr)','power and politics. learning activity: seminar (3 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK10'),(867,26,'WK11','weekly_schedule',26,'Week 11: Managing and sustaining change','Managing and sustaining change. Learning activity: Seminar (3 hr)','managing and sustaining change. learning activity: seminar (3 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK11'),(868,26,'WK12','weekly_schedule',27,'Week 12: Guest lecture, review and synthesis','Guest lecture, review and synthesis. Learning activity: Seminar (3 hr)','guest lecture, review and synthesis. learning activity: seminar (3 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK12'),(869,26,'WK13','weekly_schedule',28,'Week 13: Group pitches','Group pitches. Learning activity: Seminar (3 hr)','group pitches. learning activity: seminar (3 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK13'),(870,27,'OV01','overview',1,'Overview paragraph 1','This unit bridges the gap between theory and practice by integrating the knowledge and key skills developed across the Digital Business or Business Information Systems specialisation. It provides students with a practical teamwork experience to identify, analyse, and solve contemporary problems by exploring the socio-technical ecosystem in which a digital business operates. This experiential learning opportunity enhances students’ career-readiness by consolidating their professional skills and ability to apply the Business Information Systems knowledge in authentic situations.','this unit bridges the gap between theory and practice by integrating the knowledge and key skills developed across the digital business or business information systems specialisation. it provides students with a practical teamwork experience to identify, analyse, and solve contemporary problems by exploring the socio-technical ecosystem in which a digital business operates. this experiential learning opportunity enhances students\' career-readiness by consolidating their professional skills and ability to apply the business information systems knowledge in authentic situations.','overview:OV01'),(871,27,'LO01','learning_outcome',2,'Learning outcome 1','LO1. Apply advanced principles and theories related to digital business and information systems in the context of an actual business organisation','lo1. apply advanced principles and theories related to digital business and information systems in the context of an actual business organisation','learning_outcome:LO01'),(872,27,'LO02','learning_outcome',3,'Learning outcome 2','LO2. Analyse open-ended business scenarios and evaluate the implications of digital technologies for business','lo2. analyse open-ended business scenarios and evaluate the implications of digital technologies for business','learning_outcome:LO02'),(873,27,'LO03','learning_outcome',4,'Learning outcome 3','LO3. Apply techniques for organisational and business process analyses to resolve an actual business problem','lo3. apply techniques for organisational and business process analyses to resolve an actual business problem','learning_outcome:LO03'),(874,27,'LO04','learning_outcome',5,'Learning outcome 4','LO4. Communicate in a professional and confident manner, both orally and in writing, with actual business professionals','lo4. communicate in a professional and confident manner, both orally and in writing, with actual business professionals','learning_outcome:LO04'),(875,27,'LO05','learning_outcome',6,'Learning outcome 5','LO5. Apply team management concepts and theories to effectively work in, and manage, cross-functional teams','lo5. apply team management concepts and theories to effectively work in, and manage, cross-functional teams','learning_outcome:LO05'),(876,27,'LO06','learning_outcome',7,'Learning outcome 6','LO6. Analyse and reflect critically on the ethical and social implications of digital business','lo6. analyse and reflect critically on the ethical and social implications of digital business','learning_outcome:LO06'),(877,27,'AS01','assessment',8,'Leadership and Professional Development: Goals Achievement Overall assessment of the goals achievement','Type: Written exam. Description: Leadership and Professional Development: Goals Achievement Overall assessment of the goals achievement','type: written exam. description: leadership and professional development: goals achievement overall assessment of the goals achievement','assessment:AS01'),(878,27,'AS02','assessment',9,'Project Progress Q&A QA&A post project progress presentation','Type: Q&A following presentation, submission or placement. Description: Project Progress Q&A QA&A post project progress presentation','type: q&a following presentation, submission or placement. description: project progress q&a qa&a post project progress presentation','assessment:AS02'),(879,27,'AS03','assessment',10,'Project Progress Infographic submission Project progress updates presentation','Type: Presentation. Description: Project Progress Infographic submission Project progress updates presentation','type: presentation. description: project progress infographic submission project progress updates presentation','assessment:AS03'),(880,27,'AS04','assessment',11,'Groupwork Accountability Survey Peer review to assess members contribution and determine their group marks','Type: Evaluation. Description: Groupwork Accountability Survey Peer review to assess members contribution and determine their group marks','type: evaluation. description: groupwork accountability survey peer review to assess members contribution and determine their group marks','assessment:AS04'),(881,27,'AS05','assessment',12,'Group Charter Each group must establish roles and norms.','Type: Written work. Description: Group Charter Each group must establish roles and norms.','type: written work. description: group charter each group must establish roles and norms.','assessment:AS05'),(882,27,'AS06','assessment',13,'Business Models Submission of partner\'s business, operating models, and IS architecture','Type: Case studies. Description: Business Models Submission of partner\'s business, operating models, and IS architecture','type: case studies. description: business models submission of partner\'s business, operating models, and is architecture','assessment:AS06'),(883,27,'AS07','assessment',14,'Leadership and Professional Development: Personal Goals Personal goals development plan','Type: Practical skill. Description: Leadership and Professional Development: Personal Goals Personal goals development plan','type: practical skill. description: leadership and professional development: personal goals personal goals development plan','assessment:AS07'),(884,27,'AS08','assessment',15,'Pitch to Partner Slides submission before class Delivered during class time','Type: Presentation. Description: Pitch to Partner Slides submission before class Delivered during class time','type: presentation. description: pitch to partner slides submission before class delivered during class time','assessment:AS08'),(885,27,'AS09','assessment',16,'Innovation Review Submission of Innovation Scorecard and infographic of solution idea','Type: Creative work. Description: Innovation Review Submission of Innovation Scorecard and infographic of solution idea','type: creative work. description: innovation review submission of innovation scorecard and infographic of solution idea','assessment:AS09'),(886,27,'AS10','assessment',17,'Boardroom Presentation Slides submission before class Live presentation','Type: Presentation. Description: Boardroom Presentation Slides submission before class Live presentation','type: presentation. description: boardroom presentation slides submission before class live presentation','assessment:AS10'),(887,27,'AS11','assessment',18,'Boardroom Presentation Q&A Q&A post boardroom presentation','Type: Q&A following presentation, submission or placement. Description: Boardroom Presentation Q&A Q&A post boardroom presentation','type: q&a following presentation, submission or placement. description: boardroom presentation q&a q&a post boardroom presentation','assessment:AS11'),(888,27,'AS12','assessment',19,'Group Report Written report','Type: Case studies. Description: Group Report Written report','type: case studies. description: group report written report','assessment:AS12'),(889,27,'AD01','assessment_description',20,'Assessment description 1','Group Charter - submisison of a group project charter including group roles and norms.','group charter - submisison of a group project charter including group roles and norms.','assessment_description:AD01'),(890,27,'AD02','assessment_description',21,'Assessment description 2','Business Models - submission of partner\'s business business and operating models, and IS architecture.','business models - submission of partner\'s business business and operating models, and is architecture.','assessment_description:AD02'),(891,27,'AD03','assessment_description',22,'Assessment description 3','Pitch to Partner - presentation of a compelling case for problem/ opportunity and a project plan.Collection of feedback from partner, academics, and peers.','pitch to partner - presentation of a compelling case for problem/ opportunity and a project plan.collection of feedback from partner, academics, and peers.','assessment_description:AD03'),(892,27,'AD04','assessment_description',23,'Assessment description 4','Innovation Review - submission of Innovation scorecard (template) and infographic of solution idea, to ensure innovative and creative thinking is embedded in the final solution.','innovation review - submission of innovation scorecard (template) and infographic of solution idea, to ensure innovative and creative thinking is embedded in the final solution.','assessment_description:AD04'),(893,27,'AD05','assessment_description',24,'Assessment description 5','Project Progress and Q&A – individual presentation followed by Q&A by each member of the team on the project progress as well as insights and lessons learned on professional skills.','project progress and q&a - individual presentation followed by q&a by each member of the team on the project progress as well as insights and lessons learned on professional skills.','assessment_description:AD05'),(894,27,'AD06','assessment_description',25,'Assessment description 6','Group Report – detailed report clearly communicating the project background, approach, analyses,solution recommendation and implementation.','group report - detailed report clearly communicating the project background, approach, analyses,solution recommendation and implementation.','assessment_description:AD06'),(895,27,'AD07','assessment_description',26,'Assessment description 7','Boardroom Presentation and Q&A - presentation of the project work with focus on solution recommendation followed by Q&A.','boardroom presentation and q&a - presentation of the project work with focus on solution recommendation followed by q&a.','assessment_description:AD07'),(896,27,'AD08','assessment_description',27,'Assessment description 8','Leadership and Professional Development – exploration, development, and reflection on leadership and professional skills through the development of a portfolio for job applications, career development, and workplace success (professional identity). Two assessments: 1) Personal Goals development plan, and 2) Goals Achievement final exam, which is a hurdle task - students must pass it in order to pass the unit. Failing the hurdle task results in a capped fail mark of 49 in the unit.','leadership and professional development - exploration, development, and reflection on leadership and professional skills through the development of a portfolio for job applications, career development, and workplace success (professional identity). two assessments: 1) personal goals development plan, and 2) goals achievement final exam, which is a hurdle task - students must pass it in order to pass the unit. failing the hurdle task results in a capped fail mark of 49 in the unit.','assessment_description:AD08'),(897,27,'WK01','weekly_schedule',28,'Week 01: Unit Introduction & Project Immersion','Unit Introduction & Project Immersion. Learning activity: Seminar (3 hr)','unit introduction & project immersion. learning activity: seminar (3 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK01'),(898,27,'WK02','weekly_schedule',29,'Week 02: Partner Briefing & Group Collaboration','Partner Briefing & Group Collaboration. Learning activity: Seminar (3 hr)','partner briefing & group collaboration. learning activity: seminar (3 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK02'),(899,27,'WK03','weekly_schedule',30,'Week 03: Problem & Opportunity Scoping','Problem & Opportunity Scoping. Learning activity: Seminar (3 hr)','problem & opportunity scoping. learning activity: seminar (3 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK03'),(900,27,'WK04','weekly_schedule',31,'Week 04: Project Planning','Project Planning. Learning activity: Seminar (3 hr)','project planning. learning activity: seminar (3 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK04'),(901,27,'WK05','weekly_schedule',32,'Week 05: Pitch to Partner','Pitch to Partner. Learning activity: Seminar (3 hr)','pitch to partner. learning activity: seminar (3 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK05'),(902,27,'WK06','weekly_schedule',33,'Week 06: Research & Analysis','Research & Analysis. Learning activity: Seminar (3 hr)','research & analysis. learning activity: seminar (3 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK06'),(903,27,'WK07','weekly_schedule',34,'Week 07: Ideation','Ideation. Learning activity: Seminar (3 hr)','ideation. learning activity: seminar (3 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK07'),(904,27,'WK08','weekly_schedule',35,'Week 08: Prototyping','Prototyping. Learning activity: Seminar (3 hr)','prototyping. learning activity: seminar (3 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK08'),(905,27,'WK09','weekly_schedule',36,'Week 09: Prototype Validation','Prototype Validation. Learning activity: Seminar (3 hr)','prototype validation. learning activity: seminar (3 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK09'),(906,27,'WK10','weekly_schedule',37,'Week 10: Implementation Planning','Implementation Planning. Learning activity: Seminar (3 hr)','implementation planning. learning activity: seminar (3 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK10'),(907,27,'WK11','weekly_schedule',38,'Week 11: Presentation Planning','Presentation Planning. Learning activity: Seminar (3 hr)','presentation planning. learning activity: seminar (3 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK11'),(908,27,'WK12','weekly_schedule',39,'Week 12: Boardroom Presentation','Boardroom Presentation. Learning activity: Seminar (3 hr)','boardroom presentation. learning activity: seminar (3 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK12'),(909,27,'WK13','weekly_schedule',40,'Week 13: Review & Closure','Review & Closure. Learning activity: Seminar (3 hr)','review & closure. learning activity: seminar (3 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK13'),(910,28,'OV01','overview',1,'Overview paragraph 1','The Digital Economy, with its focus on information as a key business resource, has changed the way Business Information Systems (BIS) is viewed in organisations. BIS are now seen as enablers of innovation in which people, supported by powerful technology, are considered to be the most important component. This is because problem-solving, innovation and critical thinking skills cannot be outsourced or easily acquired by competitors. This unit is designed to develop your understanding of how businesses operate. It shows how information systems support business operations and management through integration of people, business processes and systems. You will be provided with an introduction to state-of-the-art business analysis techniques, frameworks and models to assist in understanding the nature and contribution of BIS in a range of business contexts. With its emphasis on business rather than IT, this unit does not require prior IT-related experience. In this unit, you will learn about the increasingly important role of IT in business and acquire valuable business analysis and problem-solving skills.','the digital economy, with its focus on information as a key business resource, has changed the way business information systems (bis) is viewed in organisations. bis are now seen as enablers of innovation in which people, supported by powerful technology, are considered to be the most important component. this is because problem-solving, innovation and critical thinking skills cannot be outsourced or easily acquired by competitors. this unit is designed to develop your understanding of how businesses operate. it shows how information systems support business operations and management through integration of people, business processes and systems. you will be provided with an introduction to state-of-the-art business analysis techniques, frameworks and models to assist in understanding the nature and contribution of bis in a range of business contexts. with its emphasis on business rather than it, this unit does not require prior it-related experience. in this unit, you will learn about the increasingly important role of it in business and acquire valuable business analysis and problem-solving skills.','overview:OV01'),(911,28,'LO01','learning_outcome',2,'Learning outcome 1','LO1. make judgments about ways in which Information Technology can enable innovation and improvement in business','lo1. make judgments about ways in which information technology can enable innovation and improvement in business','learning_outcome:LO01'),(912,28,'LO02','learning_outcome',3,'Learning outcome 2','LO2. demonstrate basic business analysis skills, such as strategic analysis, data modelling, and business process modelling','lo2. demonstrate basic business analysis skills, such as strategic analysis, data modelling, and business process modelling','learning_outcome:LO02'),(913,28,'LO03','learning_outcome',4,'Learning outcome 3','LO3. create and understand visual representations of business processes using BPMN notation, as well as basic data models as the basis for information systems design','lo3. create and understand visual representations of business processes using bpmn notation, as well as basic data models as the basis for information systems design','learning_outcome:LO03'),(914,28,'LO04','learning_outcome',5,'Learning outcome 4','LO4. create databases in MS Access software','lo4. create databases in ms access software','learning_outcome:LO04'),(915,28,'LO05','learning_outcome',6,'Learning outcome 5','LO5. understand and address basic issues pertaining to information ethics','lo5. understand and address basic issues pertaining to information ethics','learning_outcome:LO05'),(916,28,'LO06','learning_outcome',7,'Learning outcome 6','LO6. work as an effective team in a problem-solving environment','lo6. work as an effective team in a problem-solving environment','learning_outcome:LO06'),(917,28,'LO07','learning_outcome',8,'Learning outcome 7','LO7. display an unders