),(995,30,'OV01','overview',1,'Overview paragraph 1','Digital ecosystems (such as social media, blockchain, technology platforms, artificial intelligence, big data, people analytics, and cybersecurity) fundamentally change the way we collect and present ideas, communicate, and work together. In this unit, students are introduced to various digital ecosystems and their implications for how work is done. Students learn about how employers recruit graduates online, what it is like to join and work in a modern, digital workplace, and the tensions that arise when traditional, structured workplaces are transformed through digital, flexible, and networked ways of working. Students engage in hands-on activities to acquire skills for how to present themselves effectively and professionally online (personal branding), how to communicate in digital channels in an organisational context (professional communication), how to effectively search for and work with digital information (data literacy), and how to digitally coordinate work in teams.','digital ecosystems (such as social media, blockchain, technology platforms, artificial intelligence, big data, people analytics, and cybersecurity) fundamentally change the way we collect and present ideas, communicate, and work together. in this unit, students are introduced to various digital ecosystems and their implications for how work is done. students learn about how employers recruit graduates online, what it is like to join and work in a modern, digital workplace, and the tensions that arise when traditional, structured workplaces are transformed through digital, flexible, and networked ways of working. students engage in hands-on activities to acquire skills for how to present themselves effectively and professionally online (personal branding), how to communicate in digital channels in an organisational context (professional communication), how to effectively search for and work with digital information (data literacy), and how to digitally coordinate work in teams.','overview:OV01'),(996,30,'LO01','learning_outcome',2,'Learning outcome 1','LO1. understand how digital technology changes work environments and how work is organised','lo1. understand how digital technology changes work environments and how work is organised','learning_outcome:LO01'),(997,30,'LO02','learning_outcome',3,'Learning outcome 2','LO2. demonstrate critical discernment of popular claims about the future of work and the role of technology in this transformation process','lo2. demonstrate critical discernment of popular claims about the future of work and the role of technology in this transformation process','learning_outcome:LO02'),(998,30,'LO03','learning_outcome',4,'Learning outcome 3','LO3. communicate ideas effectively using digital online technology and audiovisual elements','lo3. communicate ideas effectively using digital online technology and audiovisual elements','learning_outcome:LO03'),(999,30,'LO04','learning_outcome',5,'Learning outcome 4','LO4. make judgements about the effective use of digital technologies for purposes of self-presentation online','lo4. make judgements about the effective use of digital technologies for purposes of self-presentation online','learning_outcome:LO04'),(1000,30,'LO05','learning_outcome',6,'Learning outcome 5','LO5. appreciate the complexities of working with others effectively in a digital work environment.','lo5. appreciate the complexities of working with others effectively in a digital work environment.','learning_outcome:LO05'),(1001,30,'AS01','assessment',7,'Final exam Final exam','Type: Written exam. Description: Final exam Final exam','type: written exam. description: final exam final exam','assessment:AS01'),(1002,30,'AS02','assessment',8,'Individual Quiz Individual Quiz: Based on first three week topics','Type: Out-of-class quiz. Description: Individual Quiz Individual Quiz: Based on first three week topics','type: out-of-class quiz. description: individual quiz i