earning activity: Lecture (1.5 hr)','using ai in digital business. learning activity: lecture (1.5 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK13'),(1150,33,'WK14','weekly_schedule',31,'Week 07: Using AI in digital business','Using AI in digital business. Learning activity: Tutorial (1.5 hr)','using ai in digital business. learning activity: tutorial (1.5 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK14'),(1151,33,'WK15','weekly_schedule',32,'Week 08: AI ethics','AI ethics. Learning activity: Lecture (1.5 hr)','ai ethics. learning activity: lecture (1.5 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK15'),(1152,33,'WK16','weekly_schedule',33,'Week 08: AI ethics','AI ethics. Learning activity: Tutorial (1.5 hr)','ai ethics. learning activity: tutorial (1.5 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK16'),(1153,33,'WK17','weekly_schedule',34,'Week 09: Design of Digital Systems & Usability','Design of Digital Systems & Usability. Learning activity: Lecture (1.5 hr)','design of digital systems & usability. learning activity: lecture (1.5 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK17'),(1154,33,'WK18','weekly_schedule',35,'Week 09: Design of Digital Systems & Usability','Design of Digital Systems & Usability. Learning activity: Tutorial (1.5 hr)','design of digital systems & usability. learning activity: tutorial (1.5 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK18'),(1155,33,'WK19','weekly_schedule',36,'Week 10: Innovation and digital disruption','Innovation and digital disruption. Learning activity: Lecture (1.5 hr)','innovation and digital disruption. learning activity: lecture (1.5 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK19'),(1156,33,'WK20','weekly_schedule',37,'Week 10: Innovation and digital disruption','Innovation and digital disruption. Learning activity: Tutorial (1.5 hr)','innovation and digital disruption. learning activity: tutorial (1.5 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK20'),(1157,33,'WK21','weekly_schedule',38,'Week 11: Review','Review. Learning activity: Lecture (1.5 hr)','review. learning activity: lecture (1.5 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK21'),(1158,33,'WK22','weekly_schedule',39,'Week 11: Review','Review. Learning activity: Tutorial (1.5 hr)','review. learning activity: tutorial (1.5 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK22'),(1159,33,'WK23','weekly_schedule',40,'Week 12: Group assignment presentations','Group assignment presentations. Learning activity: Lecture (1.5 hr)','group assignment presentations. learning activity: lecture (1.5 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK23'),(1160,33,'WK24','weekly_schedule',41,'Week 12: Group assignment presentations','Group assignment presentations. Learning activity: Tutorial (1.5 hr)','group assignment presentations. learning activity: tutorial (1.5 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK24'),(1161,33,'WK25','weekly_schedule',42,'Week 13: Group assignment presentations','Group assignment presentations. Learning activity: Lecture (1.5 hr)','group assignment presentations. learning activity: lecture (1.5 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK25'),(1162,33,'WK26','weekly_schedule',43,'Week 13: Group assignment presentations','Group assignment presentations. Learning activity: Tutorial (1.5 hr)','group assignment presentations. learning activity: tutorial (1.5 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK26'),(1163,34,'OV01','overview',1,'Overview paragraph 1','Projects are a common way of managing organisational transformation and change, the development of new products and the implementation of Information Technology (IT) in business. Information Systems (IS) business analysts will work in projects and need an understanding of both project management and the project environment. This unit will introduce you to the end-to-end project management lifecycle as described in the Project Management Body of Knowledge (PMBOK). You will learn how to successfully manage projects from initiation through execution to completion. The focus of this unit will be on the management, execution, and coordination of project activities. To this end, you will learn hands-on project management techniques and gain first-hand experience with a modern online project management platform, including an introduction to agile project management methodologies.','projects are a common way of managing organisational transformation and change, the development of new products and the implementation of information technology (it) in business. information systems (is) business analysts will work in projects and need an understanding of both project management and the project environment. this unit will introduce you to the end-to-end project management lifecycle as described in the project management body of knowledge (pmbok). you will learn how to successfully manage projects from initiation through execution to completion. the focus of this unit will be on the management, execution, and coordination of project activities. to this end, you will learn hands-on project management techniques and gain first-hand experience with a modern online project management platform, including an introduction to agile project management methodologies.','overview:OV01'),(1164,34,'LO01','learning_outcome',2,'Learning outcome 1','LO1. describe the key phases of the project management life cycle including the tools and methods used in each of those phases','lo1. describe the key phases of the project management life cycle including the tools and methods used in each of those phases','learning_outcome:LO01'),(1165,34,'LO02','learning_outcome',3,'Learning outcome 2','LO2. describe and explain the need for project management in the context of information systems (IS)','lo2. describe and explain the need for project management in the context of information systems (is)','learning_outcome:LO02'),(1166,34,'LO03','learning_outcome',4,'Learning outcome 3','LO3. recognise the key attributes of alternative IS project management methodologies including Agile methods','lo3. recognise the key attributes of alternative is project management methodologies including agile methods','learning_outcome:LO03'),(1167,34,'LO04','learning_outcome',5,'Learning outcome 4','LO4. analyse critically past Information Systems projects, explaining and justifying key themes that contributed to the success or failure of those projects','lo4. analyse critically past information systems projects, explaining and justifying key themes that contributed to the success or failure of those projects','learning_outcome:LO04'),(1168,34,'LO05','learning_outcome',6,'Learning outcome 5','LO5. set up and manage a project using an online project management platform','lo5. set up and manage a project using an online project management platform','learning_outcome:LO05'),(1169,34,'LO06','learning_outcome',7,'Learning outcome 6','LO6. describe and explain contemporary IS trends and issues that impact IS project management','lo6. describe and explain contemporary is trends and issues that impact is project management','learning_outcome:LO06'),(1170,34,'LO07','learning_outcome',8,'Learning outcome 7','LO7. learn about design thinking and how to manage ideas in a team setting, both hard and soft skills.','lo7. learn about design thinking and how to manage ideas in a team setting, both hard and soft skills.','learning_outcome:LO07'),(1171,34,'AS01','assessment',9,'Final exam n/a','Type: Written exam. Description: Final exam n/a','type: written exam. description: final exam n/a','assessment:AS01'),(1172,34,'AS02','assessment',10,'Project Guide Early feedback','Type: Written work. Description: Project Guide Early feedback','type: written work. description: project guide early feedback','assessment:AS02'),(1173,34,'AS03','assessment',11,'Group assignment Group assignment around the case study and the team\'s approach','Type: Written work. Description: Group assignment Group assignment around the case study and the team\'s approach','type: written work. description: group assignment group assignment around the case study and the team\'s approach','assessment:AS03'),(1174,34,'AD01','assessment_description',12,'Assessment description 1','Group assignment: Utilising an online project management platform, groups are required to organise their work and develop a report relating to specific information systems (IS) project management issue or trend. Students will be provided a list of contemporary IS project management trends/issues in week 2. Each group must select one of these topics and submit their nominated topic for approval to the unit coordinator by week 4. No more than three groups may select the same issue/trend.','group assignment: utilising an online project management platform, groups are required to organise their work and develop a report relating to specific information systems (is) project management issue or trend. students will be provided a list of contemporary is project management trends/issues in week 2. each group must select one of these topics and submit their nominated topic for approval to the unit coordinator by week 4. no more than three groups may select the same issue/trend.','assessment_description:AD01'),(1175,34,'AD02','assessment_description',13,'Assessment description 2','Project Guide: Individual conceptualisation of the nature of projects both formation and execution as a written individual submission.','project guide: individual conceptualisation of the nature of projects both formation and execution as a written individual submission.','assessment_description:AD02'),(1176,34,'AD03','assessment_description',14,'Assessment description 3','Written exam. A final assessment that pulls together the concepts and implications of project development and management. This is focused on concepts as discussed in the lectures, not defintions. Importantly this builds on both lecture material and your group work.','written exam. a final assessment that pulls together the concepts and implications of project development and management. this is focused on concepts as discussed in the lectures, not defintions. importantly this builds on both lecture material and your group work.','assessment_description:AD03'),(1177,34,'AD04','assessment_description',15,'Assessment description 4','Detailed information for each assessment can be found on Canvas.','detailed information for each assessment can be found on canvas.','assessment_description:AD04'),(1178,34,'WK01','weekly_schedule',16,'Week 01: Introduction to project management and teams','Introduction to project management and teams. Learning activity: Seminar (3 hr)','introduction to project management and teams. learning activity: seminar (3 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK01'),(1179,34,'WK02','weekly_schedule',17,'Week 02: The project management lifecycles + CX -UX -UI: I have to do what exactly? Is this the right thing to even be doing?','The project management lifecycles + CX -UX -UI: I have to do what exactly? Is this the right thing to even be doing?. Learning activity: Seminar (3 hr)','the project management lifecycles + cx -ux -ui: i have to do what exactly? is this the right thing to even be doing?. learning activity: seminar (3 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK02'),(1180,34,'WK03','weekly_schedule',18,'Week 03: Agile and procedural management and the role of the project manager : So you want to run this thing?','Agile and procedural management and the role of the project manager : So you want to run this thing?. Learning activity: Seminar (3 hr)','agile and procedural management and the role of the project manager : so you want to run this thing?. learning activity: seminar (3 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK03'),(1181,34,'WK04','weekly_schedule',19,'Week 04: The triple constraint and scope management: we are doing what exactly?','The triple constraint and scope management: we are doing what exactly?. Learning activity: Seminar (3 hr)','the triple constraint and scope management: we are doing what exactly?. learning activity: seminar (3 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK04'),(1182,34,'WK05','weekly_schedule',20,'Week 05: Cost and resource management: how much is this going to be?','Cost and resource management: how much is this going to be?. Learning activity: Seminar (3 hr)','cost and resource management: how much is this going