th understanding of the way in which implementation and use of large scale integrated Enterprise Systems change the nature of organisational capabilities, processes, and roles. Students will gain an understanding of the strategic role of Enterprise Systems in providing a platform for improved business operations and designing information infrastructures. In this unit, students will gain considerable hands-on experience with an enterprise-wide system, such as SAP, concentrating on the way in which such systems support integrated business processes. Through a combination of discussion and practical work, students will gain a strong knowledge in both the organisational and technical aspects of Enterprise Systems. Students will also explore the emergence and implications of cloud-based Enterprise Systems and the implementation process. Assumed knowledge for this unit is INFS1000 or equivalent.','this unit provides students with an in-depth understanding of the way in which implementation and use of large scale integrated enterprise systems change the nature of organisational capabilities, processes, and roles. students will gain an understanding of the strategic role of enterprise systems in providing a platform for improved business operations and designing information infrastructures. in this unit, students will gain considerable hands-on experience with an enterprise-wide system, such as sap, concentrating on the way in which such systems support integrated business processes. through a combination of discussion and practical work, students will gain a strong knowledge in both the organisational and technical aspects of enterprise systems. students will also explore the emergence and implications of cloud-based enterprise systems and the implementation process. assumed knowledge for this unit is infs1000 or equivalent.','overview:OV01'),(1238,36,'LO01','learning_outcome',2,'Learning outcome 1','LO1. demonstrate your understanding of the integrated nature of Enterprise Systems and their strategic role in providing a platform for improved business operations','lo1. demonstrate your understanding of the integrated nature of enterprise systems and their strategic role in providing a platform for improved business operations','learning_outcome:LO01'),(1239,36,'LO02','learning_outcome',3,'Learning outcome 2','LO2. demonstrate your understanding of the role of Enterprise Systems in information infrastructures and evaluate the organisational effects of increasing integration and standardisation','lo2. demonstrate your understanding of the role of enterprise systems in information infrastructures and evaluate the organisational effects of increasing integration and standardisation','learning_outcome:LO02'),(1240,36,'LO03','learning_outcome',4,'Learning outcome 3','LO3. demonstrate your understanding of the issues associated with implementing and supporting Enterprise Systems.','lo3. demonstrate your understanding of the issues associated with implementing and supporting enterprise systems.','learning_outcome:LO03'),(1241,36,'LO04','learning_outcome',5,'Learning outcome 4','LO4. demonstrate your understanding of the change undergone in organisations during the implementation and use of Enterprise Systems','lo4. demonstrate your understanding of the change undergone in organisations during the implementation and use of enterprise systems','learning_outcome:LO04'),(1242,36,'LO05','learning_outcome',6,'Learning outcome 5','LO5. demonstrate your theoretical understanding of the organisational structures, master data and processes within SAP','lo5. demonstrate your theoretical understanding of the organisational structures, master data and processes within sap','learning_outcome:LO05'),(1243,36,'LO06','learning_outcome',7,'Learning outcome 6','LO6. demonstrate your hands-on experience in executing transactions and analysing information using SAP','lo6. demonstrate your hands-on experience in executing transactions and analysing information using sap','learning_outcome:LO06'),(1244,36,'LO07','learning_outcome',8,'Learning outcome 7','LO7. work both independently and as a responsible member of a diverse team, collaborate and communicate in a professional manner with people from diverse backgrounds.','lo7. work both independently and as a responsible member of a diverse team, collaborate and communicate in a professional manner with people from diverse backgrounds.','learning_outcome:LO07'),(1245,36,'AS01','assessment',9,'Final Exam n/a','Type: Written exam. Description: Final Exam n/a','type: written exam. description: final exam n/a','assessment:AS01'),(1246,36,'AS02','assessment',10,'Individual assignment n/a','Type: Written work. Description: Individual assignment n/a','type: written work. description: individual assignment n/a','assessment:AS02'),(1247,36,'AS03','assessment',11,'Group project n/a','Type: Written work. Description: Group project n/a','type: written work. description: group project n/a','assessment:AS03'),(1248,36,'AD01','assessment_description',12,'Assessment description 1','Individual assignment: Based upon a business case and your own independent research, you are required to complete hands-on exercises in SAP and design an SAP organisational structure for an implementation project.','individual assignment: based upon a business case and your own independent research, you are required to complete hands-on exercises in sap and design an sap organisational structure for an implementation project.','assessment_description:AD01'),(1249,36,'AD02','assessment_description',13,'Assessment description 2','Group project: Based upon a business case and the group\'s independent research, students are required to analyse an information infrastructure and identify requirements for an Enterprise Systems solution.','group project: based upon a business case and the group\'s independent research, students are required to analyse an information infrastructure and identify requirements for an enterprise systems solution.','assessment_description:AD02'),(1250,36,'AD03','assessment_description',14,'Assessment description 3','Final exam: This is a closed book exam. Students will need to demonstrate their understanding of all material covered in the unit of study.','final exam: this is a closed book exam. students will need to demonstrate their understanding of all material covered in the unit of study.','assessment_description:AD03'),(1251,36,'AD04','assessment_description',15,'Assessment description 4','Detailed information for each assessment can be found on Canvas.','detailed information for each assessment can be found on canvas.','assessment_description:AD04'),(1252,36,'WK01','weekly_schedule',16,'Week 01: Introduction to Business Processes and Enterprise Systems','Introduction to Business Processes and Enterprise Systems. Learning activity: Seminar (3 hr)','introduction to business processes and enterprise systems. learning activity: seminar (3 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK01'),(1253,36,'WK02','weekly_schedule',17,'Week 02: Financial accounting 1','Financial accounting 1. Learning activity: Seminar (3 hr)','financial accounting 1. learning activity: seminar (3 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK02'),(1254,36,'WK03','weekly_schedule',18,'Week 03: Financial accounting 2','Financial accounting 2. Learning activity: Seminar (3 hr)','financial accounting 2. learning activity: seminar (3 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK03'),(1255,36,'WK04','weekly_schedule',19,'Week 04: Procurement 1','Procurement 1. Learning activity: Seminar (3 hr)','procurement 1. learning activity: seminar (3 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK04'),(1256,36,'WK05','weekly_schedule',20,'Week 05: Procurement 2','Procurement 2. Learning activity: Seminar (3 hr)','procurement 2. learning activity: seminar (3 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK05'),(1257,36,'WK06','weekly_schedule',21,'Week 06: CATWOE 1 & Enterprise Systems and Information Infrastructures','CATWOE 1 & Enterprise Systems and Information Infrastructures. Learning activity: Seminar (3 hr)','catwoe 1 & enterprise systems and information infrastructures. learning activity: seminar (3 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK06'),(1258,36,'WK07','weekly_schedule',22,'Week 07: CATWOE 2 & Software Vendor Evaluation','CATWOE 2 & Software Vendor Evaluation. Learning activity: Seminar (3 hr)','catwoe 2 & software vendor evaluation. learning activity: seminar (3 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK07'),(1259,36,'WK08','weekly_schedule',23,'Week 08: ES Trends – Cloud Applications','ES Trends – Cloud Applications. Learning activity: Seminar (3 hr)','es trends - cloud applications. learning activity: seminar (3 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK08'),(1260,36,'WK09','weekly_schedule',24,'Week 09: Managing ES – Risks and Controls','Managing ES – Risks and Controls. Learning activity: Seminar (3 hr)','managing es - risks and controls. learning activity: seminar (3 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK09'),(1261,36,'WK10','weekly_schedule',25,'Week 10: Managing ES Projects','Managing ES Projects. Learning activity: Seminar (3 hr)','managing es projects. learning activity: seminar (3 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK10'),(1262,36,'WK11','weekly_schedule',26,'Week 11: Group Assignment Work and Consultations','Group Assignment Work and Consultations. Learning activity: Seminar (3 hr)','group assignment work and consultations. learning activity: seminar (3 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK11'),(1263,36,'WK12','weekly_schedule',27,'Week 12: Group Presentations','Group Presentations. Learning activity: Seminar (3 hr)','group presentations. learning activity: seminar (3 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK12'),(1264,36,'WK13','weekly_schedule',28,'Week 13: Review and Preparation for the Final Exam','Review and Preparation for the Final Exam. Learning activity: Seminar (3 hr)','review and preparation for the final exam. learning activity: seminar (3 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK13'),(1265,37,'OV01','overview',1,'Overview paragraph 1','To gain or maintain their competitive edge, more than ever before, organisations need to rely on high-quality information to support decision making processes at all organisational levels. Business Intelligence (BI) is now being recognised as one of the top business priorities world-wide. While in the past, the term BI was used to describe a very broad range of software applications, the latest thinking in this field emphasises IS support for human intelligence, in the context of business decision making. In this unit, students learn how BI helps information discovery and how to analyse multidimensional data. Students gain hands-on experience in using a commercial BI platform. These practical skills, combined with in-depth analytical skills enable students to assist any organization (regardless of its size and industry domain) to derive more intelligence from its data, improve its performance and ultimately, compete on analytics. Issues are explored from the business rather than the technology perspective. This unit does not require prior programming experience.','to gain or maintain their competitive edge, more than ever before, organisations need to rely on high-quality information to support decision making processes at all organisational levels. business intelligence (bi) is now being recognised as one of the top business priorities world-wide. while in the past, the term bi was used to describe a very broad range of software applications, the latest thinking in this field emphasises is support for human intelligence, in the context of business decision making. in this unit, students learn how bi helps information discovery and how to analyse multidimensional data. students gain hands-on experience in using a commercial bi platform. these practical skills, combined with in-depth analytical skills enable students to assist any organization (regardless of its size and industry domain) to derive more intelligence from its data, improve its performance and ultimately, compete on analytics. issues are explored from the business rather than the technology perspective. this unit does not require prior programming experience.','overview:OV01'),(1266,37,'LO01','learning_outcome',2,'Learning outcome 1','LO1. use appropriate conceptual frameworks to analyse the role of different business intelligence applications in supporting day to day business and improving organisational and competitive advantage','lo1. use appropriate conceptual frameworks to analyse the role of different business intelligence applications in supporting day to day business and improving organisational and competitive advantage','learning_outcome:LO01'),(1267,37,'LO02','learning_outcome',3,'Learning outcome 2','LO2. describe the organisational issues related to a business intelligence based management approach and propose solutions to overcome the issues','lo2. describe the organisational issues related to a business intelligence based management approach and propose solutions to overcome the issues','learning_outcome:LO02'),(1268,37,'LO03','learning_outcome',4,'Learning outcome 3','LO3. design a business intelligence solution to address a business problem using a commercial business intelligence platform','lo3. design a business intelligence solution to address a business problem using a commercial business intelligence platform','learning_outcome:LO03'),(1269,37,'LO04','learning_outcome',5,'Learning outcome 4','LO4. relate business intelligence to business performance management, business process management and information management in an enterprise','lo4. relate business intelligence to business performance management, business process management and information management in an enterprise','learning_outcome:LO04'),(1270,37,'LO05','learning_outcome',6,'Learning outcome 5','LO5. demonstrate an awareness of the current and emerging trends in business intelligence.','lo5. demonstrate an awareness of the current and emerging trends in business intelligence.','learning_outcome:LO05'),(1271,37,'AS01','assessment',7,'Final exam BringYourOwnDevice exam on campus','Type: Written exam. Description: Final exam BringYourOwnDevice exam on campus','type: written exam. description: final exam bringyourowndevice exam on campus','assessment:AS01'),(1272,37,'AS02','assessment',8,'Tutorial work 1 Tableau tutorial 1 - multiple due dates','Type: Data analysis. Description: Tutorial work 1 Tableau tutorial 1 - multiple due dates','type: data analysis. description: tutorial work 1 tableau tutorial 1 - multiple due dates','assessment:AS02'),(1273,37,'AS03','assessment',9,'Tutorial work 2 Tableau tutorial 2 - multiple due dates','Type: Data analysis. Description: Tutorial work 2 Tableau tutorial 2 - multiple due dates','type: data analysis. description: tutorial work 2 tableau tutorial 2 - multiple due dates','assessment:AS03'),(1274,37,'AS04','assessment',10,'Mid-semester exam BringYourOwnDevice exam on campus','Type: Written test. Description: Mid-semester exam BringYourOwnDevice exam on campus','type: written test. description: mid-semester exam bringyourowndevice exam on campus','assessment:AS04'),(1275,37,'AS05','assessment',11,'Practical Assignment - Data Visualisation Solution and Reflection Analysing the BI process and data visualisation using Tableau','Type: Data analysis. Description: Practical Assignment - Data Visualisation Solution and Reflection Analysing the BI process and data visualisation using Tableau','type: data analysis. description: practical assignment - data visualisation solution and reflection analysing the bi process and data visualisation using tableau','assessment:AS05'),(1276,37,'AS06','assessment',12,'Practical Assignment - Presentation Analysing the BI process and data visualisation using Tableau','Type: Presentation. Description: Practical Assignment - Presentation Analysing the BI process and data visualisation using Tableau','type: presentation. description: practical assignment - presentation analysing the bi process and data visualisation using tableau','assessment:AS06'),(1277,37,'AD01','assessment_description',13,'Assessment description 1','Tutorial work 1 and 2: Students are expected to demonstrate the understanding of the basics of using Tableau and designing a visualisation solution. The tutorials are done during normal class time and must be submitted by the end of the class time.','tutorial work 1 and 2: students are expected to demonstrate the understanding of the basics of using tableau and designing a visualisation solution. the tutorials are done during normal class time and must be submitted by the end of the class time.','assessment_description:AD01'),(1278,37,'AD02','assessment_description',14,'Assessment description 2','Mid-semester exam: This exam tests the understanding of the foundational business intelligence concepts.','mid-semester exam: this exam tests the understanding of the foundational business intelligence concepts.','assessment_description:AD02'),(1279,37,'AD03','assessment_description',15,'Assessment description 3','Practical assignment: Students are required to develop a data visualisation solution to address a business problem using Tableau. A data set will be provided to students. Each group will present their results in the Campus sessions on week 12.','practical assignment: students are required to develop a data visualisation solution to address a business problem using tableau. a data set will be provided to students. each group will present their results in the campus sessions on week 12.','assessment_description:AD03'),(1280,37,'AD04','assessment_description',16,'Assessment description 4','Final exam: The final exam tests the understanding of business intelligence concepts and frameworks in an organisational context. This exam covers all the unit materials. Students will be assessed in a Bring Your Own Device (BYOD) exam taken on campus with supervision. Further information about the delivery of the exams will be provided closer to the test exam.','final exam: the final exam tests the understanding of business intelligence concepts and frameworks in an organisational context. this exam covers all the unit materials. students will be assessed in a bring your own device (byod) exam taken on campus with supervision. further information about the delivery of the exams will be provided closer to the test exam.','assessment_description:AD04'),(1281,37,'AD05','assessment_description',17,'Assessment description 5','Detailed information for each assessment can be found on Canvas.','detailed information for each assessment can be found on canvas.','assessment_description:AD05'),(1282,37,'WK01','weekly_schedule',18,'Week 01: Introduction to unit of study','Introduction to unit of study. Learning activity: Seminar (3 hr)','introduction to unit of study. learning activity: seminar (3 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK01'),(1283,37,'WK02','weekly_schedule',19,'Week 02: Foundations for understanding business intelligence','Foundations for understanding business intelligence. Learning activity: Seminar (3 hr)','foundations for understanding business intelligence. learning activity: seminar (3 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK02'),(1284,37,'WK03','weekly_schedule',20,'Week 03: Data Warehousing: the business perspective','Data Warehousing: the business perspective. Learning activity: Seminar (3 hr)','data warehousing: the business perspective. learning activity: seminar (3 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK03'),(1285,37,'WK04','weekly_schedule',21,'Week 04: Data quality and value of information','Data quality and value of information. Learning activity: Seminar (3 hr)','data quality and value of information. learning activity: seminar (3 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK04'),(1286,37,'WK05','weekly_schedule',22,'Week 05: Information discovery and decision making','Information discovery and decision making. Learning activity: Seminar (3 hr)','information discovery and decision making. learning activity: seminar (3 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK05'),(1287,37,'WK06','weekly_schedule',23,'Week 06: Designing business intelligence solutions','Designing business intelligence solutions. Learning activity: Seminar (3 hr)','designing business intelligence solutions. learning activity: seminar (3 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK06'),(1288,37,'WK07','weekly_schedule',24,'Week 07: Preparation for the mid semester exam and comprehensive case discussion','Preparation for the mid semester exam and comprehensive case discussion. Learning activity: Seminar (3 hr)','preparation for the mid semester exam and comprehensive case discussion. learning activity: seminar (3 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK07'),(1289,37,'WK08','weekly_schedule',25,'Week 08: Mid-semester exam','Mid-semester exam. Learning activity: Seminar (1 hr)','mid-semester exam. learning activity: seminar (1 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK08'),(1290,37,'WK09','weekly_schedule',26,'Week 09: Multi-dimensional modeling, OLAP and ethics','Multi-dimensional modeling, OLAP and ethics. Learning activity: Seminar (3 hr)','multi-dimensional modeling, olap and ethics. learning activity: seminar (3 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK09'),(1291,37,'WK10','weekly_schedule',27,'Week 10: Business performance management: the role of business intelligence and data visualisation. AI Support for Decision Making.','Business performance management: the role of business intelligence and data visualisation. AI Support for Decision Making.. Learning activity: Seminar (3 hr)','business performance management: the role of business intelligence and data visualisation. ai support for decision making.. learning activity: seminar (3 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK10'),(1292,37,'WK11','weekly_schedule',28,'Week 11: Group project work and consultations','Group project work and consultations. Learning activity: Seminar (3 hr)','group project work and consultations. learning activity: seminar (3 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK11'),(1293,37,'WK12','weekly_schedule',29,'Week 12: Group presentations','Group presentations. Learning activity: Seminar (3 hr)','group presentations. learning activity: seminar (3 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK12'),(1294,37,'WK13','weekly_schedule',30,'Week 13: Preparation for the final exam','Preparation for the final exam. Learning activity: Seminar (3 hr)','preparation for the final exam. learning activity: seminar (3 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK13'),(1295,38,'OV01','overview',1,'Overview paragraph 1','This unit provides an in-depth understanding of the role of business processes in effectively and efficiently managing business operations. Students gain essential skills of the entire Business Process Management (BPM) lifecycle, from process identification and design to process monitoring, including process modelling, analysis, redesign, and automation required to achieve high performance and deliver the strategy in a service-oriented environment. Students also gain highly sought after practical skills of using BPM tools to recommend improvements by documenting and simulating current and new processes.','this unit provides an in-depth understanding of the role of business processes in effectively and efficiently managing business operations. students gain essential skills of the entire business process management (bpm) lifecycle, from process identification and design to process monitoring, including process modelling, analysis, redesign, and automation required to achieve high performance and deliver the strategy in a service-oriented environment. students also gain highly sought after practical skills of using bpm tools to recommend improvements by documenting and simulating current and new processes.','overview:OV01'),(1296,38,'LO01','learning_outcome',2,'Learning outcome 1','LO1. Discuss the role of Business Process Management (BPM) in a business environment and how BPM initiatives contribute to improving the overall business performance','lo1. discuss the role of business process management (bpm) in a business environment and how bpm initiatives contribute to improving the overall business performance','learning_outcome:LO01'),(1297,38,'LO02','learning_outcome',3,'Learning outcome 2','LO2. Apply the BPM principles, concepts, and frameworks to business problems and practice as captured in the BPM lifecycle','lo2. apply the bpm principles, concepts, and frameworks to business problems and practice as captured in the bpm lifecycle','learning_outcome:LO02'),(1298,38,'LO03','learning_outcome',4,'Learning outcome 3','LO3. Address the issues and challenges associated with process improvement initiatives in organisations','lo3. address the issues and challenges associated with process improvement initiatives in organisations','learning_outcome:LO03'),(1299,38,'LO04','learning_outcome',5,'Learning outcome 4','LO4. Evaluate the impact of process design and redesign decisions on stakeholders and the role of change management in addressing the risks associated with such changes in organisations','lo4. evaluate the impact of process design and redesign decisions on stakeholders and the role of change management in addressing the risks associated with such changes in organisations','learning_outcome:LO04'),(1300,38,'LO05','learning_outcome',6,'Learning outcome 5','LO5. Use BPM tools to model, document, and analyse processes during the BPM lifecycle stages','lo5. use bpm tools to model, document, and analyse processes during the bpm lifecycle stages','learning_outcome:LO05'),(1301,38,'LO06','learning_outcome',7,'Learning outcome 6','LO6. Work independently, collaborate, and communicate in a professional manner with people from diverse backgrounds within a team work environment','lo6. work independently, collaborate, and communicate in a professional manner with people from diverse backgrounds within a team work environment','learning_outcome:LO06'),(1302,38,'AS01','assessment',8,'Final Exam Written exam','Type: Written exam. Description: Final Exam Written exam','type: written exam. description: final exam written exam','assessment:AS01'),(1303,38,'AS02','assessment',9,'Individual Assignment Written submission','Type: Case studies. Description: Individual Assignment Written submission','type: case studies. description: individual assignment written submission','assessment:AS02'),(1304,38,'AS03','assessment',10,'Group Plan Pitch (5 min) Presentation & Submission','Type: Case studies. Description: Group Plan Pitch (5 min) Presentation & Submission','type: case studies. description: group plan pitch (5 min) presentation & submission','assessment:AS03'),(1305,38,'AS04','assessment',11,'Group Project Group Report Written Submission','Type: Case studies. Description: Group Project Group Report Written Submission','type: case studies. description: group project group report written submission','assessment:AS04'),(1306,38,'AD01','assessment_description',12,'Assessment description 1','Individual assignment: In this assignment students will take the role of the process analyst and engage in process discovery and analysis within a given business case context.','individual assignment: in this assignment students will take the role of the process analyst and engage in process discovery and analysis within a given business case context.','assessment_description:AD01'),(1307,38,'AD02','assessment_description',13,'Assessment description 2','Group Plan assignment: In this assignment students will analyse the market and identify new services to be executed via new and modified business processes. Students will also develop a project plan to guide the project execution. Students will present and make a written submission.','group plan assignment: in this assignment students will analyse the market and identify new services to be executed via new and modified business processes. students will also develop a project plan to guide the project execution. students will present and make a written submission.','assessment_description:AD02'),(1308,38,'AD03','assessment_description',14,'Assessment description 3','Group Report assignment: In this assignment students will design new processes following the services proposed in the Group Plan assignment. Students will assess the feasibility of the new processes, the resources required, and the challenges encountered during process implementation. Students will use Signavio (BPM tool) to document, simulate and analyse the new business processes. Students will present a summary of the findings and recommendations.','group report assignment: in this assignment students will design new processes following the services proposed in the group plan assignment. students will assess the feasibility of the new processes, the resources required, and the challenges encountered during process implementation. students will use signavio (bpm tool) to document, simulate and analyse the new business processes. students will present a summary of the findings and recommendations.','assessment_description:AD03'),(1309,38,'AD04','assessment_description',15,'Assessment description 4','Final exam: A supervised exam that will test students theoretical understanding, critical thinking, and ability to apply and evaluate BPM concepts and principles in practice.','final exam: a supervised exam that will test students theoretical understanding, critical thinking, and ability to apply and evaluate bpm concepts and principles in practice.','assessment_description:AD04'),(1310,38,'AD05','assessment_description',16,'Assessment description 5','Detailed information for each assessment will be released as appropiate on Canvas.','detailed information for each assessment will be released as appropiate on canvas.','assessment_description:AD05'),(1311,38,'WK01','weekly_schedule',17,'Week 01: Introduction to the Unit and Business Process Management (BPM)','Introduction to the Unit and Business Process Management (BPM). Learning activity: Seminar (3 hr)','introduction to the unit and business process management (bpm). learning activity: seminar (3 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK01'),(1312,38,'WK02','weekly_schedule',18,'Week 02: Process identification','Process identification. Learning activity: Seminar (3 hr)','process identification. learning activity: seminar (3 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK02'),(1313,38,'WK03','weekly_schedule',19,'Week 03: Process discovery','Process discovery. Learning activity: Seminar (3 hr)','process discovery. learning activity: seminar (3 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK03'),(1314,38,'WK04','weekly_schedule',20,'Week 04: Process modelling (1) - BPMN Notation','Process modelling (1) - BPMN Notation. Learning activity: Seminar (3 hr)','process modelling (1) - bpmn notation. learning activity: seminar (3 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK04'),(1315,38,'WK05','weekly_schedule',21,'Week 05: Process modelling (2) - As-Is Modelling using BPMN and Signavio','Process modelling (2) - As-Is Modelling using BPMN and Signavio. Learning activity: Seminar (3 hr)','process modelling (2) - as-is modelling using bpmn and signavio. learning activity: seminar (3 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK05'),(1316,38,'WK06','weekly_schedule',22,'Week 06: Process analysis (1) (qualitative)','Process analysis (1) (qualitative). Learning activity: Seminar (3 hr)','process analysis (1) (qualitative). learning activity: seminar (3 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK06'),(1317,38,'WK07','weekly_schedule',23,'Week 07: Process analysis (2) (quantitative): As-Is Simulation using Signavio','Process analysis (2) (quantitative): As-Is Simulation using Signavio. Learning activity: Seminar (3 hr)','process analysis (2) (quantitative): as-is simulation using signavio. learning activity: seminar (3 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK07'),(1318,38,'WK08','weekly_schedule',24,'Week 08: Process improvement (1) - Redesign heuristics','Process improvement (1) - Redesign heuristics. Learning activity: Seminar (3 hr)','process improvement (1) - redesign heuristics. learning activity: seminar (3 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK08'),(1319,38,'WK09','weekly_schedule',25,'Week 09: Group plan presentations - Feedback collection','Group plan presentations - Feedback collection. Learning activity: Seminar (3 hr)','group plan presentations - feedback collection. learning activity: seminar (3 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK09'),(1320,38,'WK10','weekly_schedule',26,'Week 10: Process improvement (2) - To-Be Simulation using Signavio','Process improvement (2) - To-Be Simulation using Signavio. Learning activity: Seminar (3 hr)','process improvement (2) - to-be simulation using signavio. learning activity: seminar (3 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK10'),(1321,38,'WK11','weekly_schedule',27,'Week 11: Process implementation, monitoring and mining','Process implementation, monitoring and mining. Learning activity: Seminar (3 hr)','process implementation, monitoring and mining. learning activity: seminar (3 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK11'),(1322,38,'WK12','weekly_schedule',28,'Week 12: Emerging topics in BPM; Group project consultation','Emerging topics in BPM; Group project consultation. Learning activity: Seminar (3 hr)','emerging topics in bpm; group project consultation. learning activity: seminar (3 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK12'),(1323,38,'WK13','weekly_schedule',29,'Week 13: Unit Review and Final Exam Practice','Unit Review and Final Exam Practice. Learning activity: Seminar (3 hr)','unit review and final exam practice. learning activity: seminar (3 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK13'),(1324,39,'OV01','overview',1,'Overview paragraph 1','This unit provides students with the opportunity to address complex problems identified by industry, community, and government organisations. With mentorship from a major industry partner and an academic lead, students integrate their academic skills and knowledge by working in diverse teams across disciplinary boundaries. Students research, analyse and present solutions to a real-world problem, and build on their interpersonal and transferable skills by engaging with and learning from experts in the field. See the ICPU website for further information here: https://www.sydney.edu.au/students/industry-and-community-projects.html.','this unit provides students with the opportunity to address complex problems identified by industry, community, and government organisations. with mentorship from a major industry partner and an academic lead, students integrate their academic skills and knowledge by working in diverse teams across disciplinary boundaries. students research, analyse and present solutions to a real-world problem, and build on their interpersonal and transferable skills by engaging with and learning from experts in the field. see the icpu website for further information here: https://www.sydney.edu.au/students/industry-and-community-projects.html.','overview:OV01'),(1325,39,'LO01','learning_outcome',2,'Learning outcome 1','LO1. Demonstrate critical awareness of, and apply, disciplinary knowledge, skills and personal attributes to address complex real-world problems','lo1. demonstrate critical awareness of, and apply, disciplinary knowledge, skills and personal attributes to address complex real-world problems','learning_outcome:LO01'),(1326,39,'LO02','learning_outcome',3,'Learning outcome 2','LO2. Assess and integrate diverse stakeholder perspectives to generate innovative insights into complex problems','lo2. assess and integrate diverse stakeholder perspectives to generate innovative insights into complex problems','learning_outcome:LO02'),(1327,39,'LO03','learning_outcome',4,'Learning outcome 3','LO3. Purposefully select and apply complex problem-solving approaches and methods','lo3. purposefully select and apply complex problem-solving approaches and methods','learning_outcome:LO03'),(1328,39,'LO04','learning_outcome',5,'Learning outcome 4','LO4. Communicate novel ideas effectively and persuasively in professional settings using relevant media','lo4. communicate novel ideas effectively and persuasively in professional settings using relevant media','learning_outcome:LO04'),(1329,39,'LO05','learning_outcome',6,'Learning outcome 5','LO5. Demonstrate professionalism (proficiency, adaptivity, and proactivity) in collaborative project work','lo5. demonstrate professionalism (proficiency, adaptivity, and proactivity) in collaborative project work','learning_outcome:LO05'),(1330,39,'AS01','assessment',7,'Participation Compulsory 90% class participation','Type: Contribution. Description: Participation Compulsory 90% class participation','type: contribution. description: participation compulsory 90% class participation','assessment:AS01'),(1331,39,'AS02','assessment',8,'Individual Statement Instalment 1 Written task','Type: Portfolio or journal. Description: Individual Statement Instalment 1 Written task','type: portfolio or journal. description: individual statement instalment 1 written task','assessment:AS02'),(1332,39,'AS03','assessment',9,'Group Plan Research plan','Type: Written work. Description: Group Plan Research plan','type: written work. description: group plan research plan','assessment:AS03'),(1333,39,'AS04','assessment',10,'Individual Statement Instalment 2 Written task','Type: Portfolio or journal. Description: Individual Statement Instalment 2 Written task','type: portfolio or journal. description: individual statement instalment 2 written task','assessment:AS04'),(1334,39,'AS05','assessment',11,'Group Presentation Oral presentation inclusive of 300-word or equivalent Executive summary','Type: Presentation. Description: Group Presentation Oral presentation inclusive of 300-word or equivalent Executive summary','type: presentation. description: group presentation oral presentation inclusive of 300-word or equivalent executive summary','assessment:AS05'),(1335,39,'AS06','assessment',12,'Group Project Report Report','Type: Written work. Description: Group Project Report Report','type: written work. description: group project report report','assessment:AS06'),(1336,39,'AS07','assessment',13,'Group Work Survey Questionnaire','Type: Evaluation. Description: Group Work Survey Questionnaire','type: evaluation. description: group work survey questionnaire','assessment:AS07'),(1337,39,'AD01','assessment_description',14,'Assessment description 1','Group plan aims to articulate the issues the group will address and develop a project plan.','group plan aims to articulate the issues the group will address and develop a project plan.','assessment_description:AD01'),(1338,39,'AD02','assessment_description',15,'Assessment description 2','Individual statement aims to analyse and reflect on students’ own and other members’ ways of contributing to their work on this project.','individual statement aims to analyse and reflect on students\' own and other members\' ways of contributing to their work on this project.','assessment_description:AD02'),(1339,39,'AD03','assessment_description',16,'Assessment description 3','Group report aims to conduct in depth analysis/es and research, discuss the results, and provide recommendations or solutions to the issues outlined in the group plan.','group report aims to conduct in depth analysis/es and research, discuss the results, and provide recommendations or solutions to the issues outlined in the group plan.','assessment_description:AD03'),(1340,39,'AD04','assessment_description',17,'Assessment description 4','Group presentation including Executive Summary aims to present students’ work and findings to the project partner.','group presentation including executive summary aims to present students\' work and findings to the project partner.','assessment_description:AD04'),(1341,39,'AD05','assessment_description',18,'Assessment description 5','Group work survey aims to evaluate student’s contributions relative to the contributions of other team members.','group work survey aims to evaluate student\'s contributions relative to the contributions of other team members.','assessment_description:AD05'),(1342,39,'AD06','assessment_description',19,'Assessment description 6','Attendance aims to ensure active participation by all team members for the project work.','attendance aims to ensure active participation by all team members for the project work.','assessment_description:AD06'),(1343,39,'AD07','assessment_description',20,'Assessment description 7','Detailed information for each assessment can be found on Canvas.','detailed information for each assessment can be found on canvas.','assessment_description:AD07'),(1344,39,'AD08','assessment_description',21,'Assessment description 8','Individual contributions to group assessments may adjust the final grade that a student receives, through what is known as a Relative Performance Factor. Please see Canvas Assignment page for more details.','individual contributions to group assessments may adjust the final grade that a student receives, through what is known as a relative performance factor. please see canvas assignment page for more details.','assessment_description:AD08'),(1345,39,'AD09','assessment_description',22,'Assessment description 9','Using AI in ICPU','using ai in icpu','assessment_description:AD09'),(1346,39,'AD10','assessment_description',23,'Assessment description 10','The Use of Generative AI across multiple sectors of work is increasing exponentially. While use of these tools brings new opportunities such as increased productivity, there are also many potential limitations such as inhibiting the development of analytical and creative thinking skills. Importantly, in ICPU where 80% of assessments are group-based, your use of AI tools must also be negotiated collegially and adhere to the Student Charter 2020, including upholding honesty, ethics, professionalism, and academic integrity (please ensure you are familiar with the updated Academic Integrity 2022 policy).','the use of generative ai across multiple sectors of work is increasing exponentially. while use of these tools brings new opportunities such as increased productivity, there are also many potential limitations such as inhibiting the development of analytical and creative thinking skills. importantly, in icpu where 80% of assessments are group-based, your use of ai tools must also be negotiated collegially and adhere to the student charter 2020, including upholding honesty, ethics, professionalism, and academic integrity (please ensure you are familiar with the updated academic integrity 2022 policy).','assessment_description:AD10'),(1347,39,'AD11','assessment_description',24,'Assessment description 11','AI tools permitted','ai tools permitted','assessment_description:AD11'),(1348,39,'AD12','assessment_description',25,'Assessment description 12','You are permitted to use automated writing tools and generative artificial intelligence (AI) to facilitate your learning and completion of this assignment in individual and group project work. Please adhere to the following guidelines:','you are permitted to use automated writing tools and generative artificial intelligence (ai) to facilitate your learning and completion of this assignment in individual and group project work. please adhere to the following guidelines:','assessment_description:AD12'),(1349,39,'AD13','assessment_description',26,'Assessment description 13','Do not enter confidential, personal, copyrighted or otherwise sensitive information into any AI tool, including but not limited to materials shared by industry and/or community partners (noting also the confidentiality clauses that apply in the Student Deed Poll)','do not enter confidential, personal, copyrighted or otherwise sensitive information into any ai tool, including but not limited to materials shared by industry and/or community partners (noting also the confidentiality clauses that apply in the student deed poll)','assessment_description:AD13'),(1350,39,'AD14','assessment_description',27,'Assessment description 14','If you use these tools, you must be aware of their limitations, biases, and propensity for fabrication','if you use these tools, you must be aware of their limitations, biases, and propensity for fabrication','assessment_description:AD14'),(1351,39,'AD15','assessment_description',28,'Assessment description 15','Do not rely on the accuracy of outputs. You remain responsible for your work. This means you must independently verify and edit AI-generated content to ensure the integrity, accuracy, and suitability of the output','do not rely on the accuracy of outputs. you remain responsible for your work. this means you must independently verify and edit ai-generated content to ensure the integrity, accuracy, and suitability of the output','assessment_description:AD15'),(1352,39,'AD16','assessment_description',29,'Assessment description 16','While there are many AI tools available, both free and paid, we strongly recommend the use of tools endorsed by the University such as Microsoft Copilot, Cogniti and Adobe Firefly. For a list of AI tools and their uses, see the Different Generative AI Tools page on the AI in Education Canvas site.','while there are many ai tools available, both free and paid, we strongly recommend the use of tools endorsed by the university such as microsoft copilot, cogniti and adobe firefly. for a list of ai tools and their uses, see the different generative ai tools page on the ai in education canvas site.','assessment_description:AD16'),(1353,39,'AD17','assessment_description',30,'Assessment description 17','Where AI is used, you are advised to keep copies of the prompts you provided and AI outputs as evidence of your research and writing process. This allows you to produce an accurate acknowledgement of AI use when you submit your work, see guidance below. This can be requested by the unit coordinator if there is any uncertainty about the originality of your work.','where ai is used, you are advised to keep copies of the prompts you provided and ai outputs as evidence of your research and writing process. this allows you to produce an accurate acknowledgement of ai use when you submit your work, see guidance below. this can be requested by the unit coordinator if there is any uncertainty about the originality of your work.','assessment_description:AD17'),(1354,39,'AD18','assessment_description',31,'Assessment description 18','Acknowledging the use of AI','acknowledging the use of ai','assessment_description:AD18'),(1355,39,'AD19','assessment_description',32,'Assessment description 19','It is not appropriate to copy-paste AI-generated responses directly as part of your own writing since the work you submit should reflect the understanding you have acquired, your critical engagement with the material and your process of continuous revision and improvement.','it is not appropriate to copy-paste ai-generated responses directly as part of your own writing since the work you submit should reflect the understanding you have acquired, your critical engagement with the material and your process of continuous revision and improvement.','assessment_description:AD19'),(1356,39,'AD20','assessment_description',33,'Assessment description 20','Where AI is used, you are advised to keep copies of the prompts you provided and AI outputs as evidence of your research and writing process. This allows you to produce an accurate acknowledgement of AI use when you submit your work, see wording below. This can be requested by the unit coordinator if there is any uncertainty about the originality of your work.','where ai is used, you are advised to keep copies of the prompts you provided and ai outputs as evidence of your research and writing process. this allows you to produce an accurate acknowledgement of ai use when you submit your work, see wording below. this can be requested by the unit coordinator if there is any uncertainty about the originality of your work.','assessment_description:AD20'),(1357,39,'AD21','assessment_description',34,'Assessment description 21','You must acknowledge any uses of AI by inserting a note at the end of your submission where you need to describe the tool(s) that you used, what prompt(s) you provided, how the output of the artificial intelligence was used or adapted by you, and how you verified sources or information if applicable. This additional description does not add to your word count. An example of such an acknowledgement that you may provide might look like:','you must acknowledge any uses of ai by inserting a note at the end of your submission where you need to describe the tool(s) that you used, what prompt(s) you provided, how the output of the artificial intelligence was used or adapted by you, and how you verified sources or information if applicable. this additional description does not add to your word count. an example of such an acknowledgement that you may provide might look like:','assessment_description:AD21'),(1358,39,'AD22','assessment_description',35,'Assessment description 22','I acknowledge the use of ChatGPT (https://chat.openai.com/) to refine the academic language of my own work. On date I submitted my entire essay (link to original document here) with the prompt to <“Improve the academic tone and accuracy of language, including grammatical structures, punctuation and vocabulary”>. The output (link here) was then modified further to better represent my own tone and style of writing. One of the limitations I noted was insert limitation and I revised my assessment to address this limitation by insert response.','i acknowledge the use of chatgpt (https://chat.openai.com/) to refine the academic language of my own work. on date i submitted my entire essay (link to original document here) with the prompt to <“improve the academic tone and accuracy of language, including grammatical structures, punctuation and vocabulary”>. the output (link here) was then modified further to better represent my own tone and style of writing. one of the limitations i noted was insert limitation and i revised my assessment to address this limitation by insert response.','assessment_description:AD22'),(1359,39,'AD23','assessment_description',36,'Assessment description 23','Please note, your project supervisor may require you to provide a written statement if you would like to use AI heavily in your work, (i.e. for multiple approved uses above or heavy use within any individual use categories), a different approach may be needed including clearly stating the percentage of work attributed to AI for each assessment. If you are unsure or have any concerns, please discuss these with your Project Supervisor in advance. In all cases, individual group members must be transparent with their group members about intended use of generative AI in groupwork.','please note, your project supervisor may require you to provide a written statement if you would like to use ai heavily in your work, (i.e. for multiple approved uses above or heavy use within any individual use categories), a different approach may be needed including clearly stating the percentage of work attributed to ai for each assessment. if you are unsure or have any concerns, please discuss these with your project supervisor in advance. in all cases, individual group members must be transparent with their group members about intended use of generative ai in groupwork.','assessment_description:AD23'),(1360,39,'WK01','weekly_schedule',37,'Weekly: See Canvas site for detailed project schedule','See Canvas site for detailed project schedule. Learning activity: Lecture (1 hr)','see canvas site for detailed project schedule. learning activity: lecture (1 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK01'),(1361,39,'WK02','weekly_schedule',38,'Weekly: See Canvas site for detailed project schedule','See Canvas site for detailed project schedule. Learning activity: Tutorial (2 hr)','see canvas site for detailed project schedule. learning activity: tutorial (2 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK02'),(1362,40,'OV01','overview',1,'Overview paragraph 1','This unit provides students with the opportunity to address complex problems identified by industry, community, and government organisations. With mentorship from a major industry partner and an academic lead, students integrate their academic skills and knowledge by working in diverse teams across disciplinary boundaries. Students research, analyse and present solutions to a real-world problem, and build on their interpersonal and transferable skills by engaging with and learning from experts in the field. See the ICPU website for further information here: https://www.sydney.edu.au/students/industry-and-community-projects.html.','this unit provides students with the opportunity to address complex problems identified by industry, community, and government organisations. with mentorship from a major industry partner and an academic lead, students integrate their academic skills and knowledge by working in diverse teams across disciplinary boundaries. students research, analyse and present solutions to a real-world problem, and build on their interpersonal and transferable skills by engaging with and learning from experts in the field. see the icpu website for further information here: https://www.sydney.edu.au/students/industry-and-community-projects.html.','overview:OV01'),(1363,40,'LO01','learning_outcome',2,'Learning outcome 1','LO1. Demonstrate critical awareness of, and apply, disciplinary knowledge, skills and personal attributes to address complex real-world problems','lo1. demonstrate critical awareness of, and apply, disciplinary knowledge, skills and personal attributes to address complex real-world problems','learning_outcome:LO01'),(1364,40,'LO02','learning_outcome',3,'Learning outcome 2','LO2. Assess and integrate diverse stakeholder perspectives to generate innovative insights into complex problems','lo2. assess and integrate diverse stakeholder perspectives to generate innovative insights into complex problems','learning_outcome:LO02'),(1365,40,'LO03','learning_outcome',4,'Learning outcome 3','LO3. Purposefully select and apply complex problem-solving approaches and methods','lo3. purposefully select and apply complex problem-solving approaches and methods','learning_outcome:LO03'),(1366,40,'LO04','learning_outcome',5,'Learning outcome 4','LO4. Communicate novel ideas effectively and persuasively in professional settings using relevant media','lo4. communicate novel ideas effectively and persuasively in professional settings using relevant media','learning_outcome:LO04'),(1367,40,'LO05','learning_outcome',6,'Learning outcome 5','LO5. Demonstrate professionalism (proficiency, adaptivity, and proactivity) in collaborative project work','lo5. demonstrate professionalism (proficiency, adaptivity, and proactivity) in collaborative project work','learning_outcome:LO05'),(1368,40,'AS01','assessment',7,'Participation Compulsory 90% class participation','Type: Contribution. Description: Participation Compulsory 90% class participation','type: contribution. description: participation compulsory 90% class participation','assessment:AS01'),(1369,40,'AS02','assessment',8,'Individual Statement Instalment 1 Written task','Type: Portfolio or journal. Description: Individual Statement Instalment 1 Written task','type: portfolio or journal. description: individual statement instalment 1 written task','assessment:AS02'),(1370,40,'AS03','assessment',9,'Group Plan Research plan','Type: Written work. Description: Group Plan Research plan','type: written work. description: group plan research plan','assessment:AS03'),(1371,40,'AS04','assessment',10,'Group Presentation Oral presentation inclusive of 300-word or equivalent Executive summary','Type: Presentation. Description: Group Presentation Oral presentation inclusive of 300-word or equivalent Executive summary','type: presentation. description: group presentation oral presentation inclusive of 300-word or equivalent executive summary','assessment:AS04'),(1372,40,'AS05','assessment',11,'Individual Statement Instalment 2 Written task','Type: Portfolio or journal. Description: Individual Statement Instalment 2 Written task','type: portfolio or journal. description: individual statement instalment 2 written task','assessment:AS05'),(1373,40,'AS06','assessment',12,'Group Project Report Report','Type: Written work. Description: Group Project Report Report','type: written work. description: group project report report','assessment:AS06'),(1374,40,'AS07','assessment',13,'Group Work Survey Questionnaire','Type: Evaluation. Description: Group Work Survey Questionnaire','type: evaluation. description: group work survey questionnaire','assessment:AS07'),(1375,40,'AD01','assessment_description',14,'Assessment description 1','Group plan aims to articulate the issues the group will address and develop a project plan.','group plan aims to articulate the issues the group will address and develop a project plan.','assessment_description:AD01'),(1376,40,'AD02','assessment_description',15,'Assessment description 2','Individual statement aims to analyse and reflect on students’ own and other members’ ways of contributing to their work on this project.','individual statement aims to analyse and reflect on students\' own and other members\' ways of contributing to their work on this project.','assessment_description:AD02'),(1377,40,'AD03','assessment_description',16,'Assessment description 3','Group report aims to conduct in depth analysis/es and research, discuss the results, and provide recommendations or solutions to the issues outlined in the group plan.','group report aims to conduct in depth analysis/es and research, discuss the results, and provide recommendations or solutions to the issues outlined in the group plan.','assessment_description:AD03'),(1378,40,'AD04','assessment_description',17,'Assessment description 4','Group presentation including Executive Summary aims to present students’ work and findings to the project partner.','group presentation including executive summary aims to present students\' work and findings to the project partner.','assessment_description:AD04'),(1379,40,'AD05','assessment_description',18,'Assessment description 5','Group work survey aims to evaluate student’s contributions relative to the contributions of other team members.','group work survey aims to evaluate student\'s contributions relative to the contributions of other team members.','assessment_description:AD05'),(1380,40,'AD06','assessment_description',19,'Assessment description 6','Attendance aims to ensure active participation by all team members for the project work.','attendance aims to ensure active participation by all team members for the project work.','assessment_description:AD06'),(1381,40,'AD07','assessment_description',20,'Assessment description 7','Detailed information for each assessment can be found on Canvas.','detailed information for each assessment can be found on canvas.','assessment_description:AD07'),(1382,40,'AD08','assessment_description',21,'Assessment description 8','Individual contributions to group assessments may adjust the final grade that a student receives, through what is known as a Relative Performance Factor. Please see Canvas Assignment page for more details.','individual contributions to group assessments may adjust the final grade that a student receives, through what is known as a relative performance factor. please see canvas assignment page for more details.','assessment_description:AD08'),(1383,40,'AD09','assessment_description',22,'Assessment description 9','Using AI in ICPU','using ai in icpu','assessment_description:AD09'),(1384,40,'AD10','assessment_description',23,'Assessment description 10','The Use of Generative AI across multiple sectors of work is increasing exponentially. While use of these tools brings new opportunities such as increased productivity, there are also many potential limitations such as inhibiting the development of analytical and creative thinking skills. Importantly, in ICPU where 80% of assessments are group-based, your use of AI tools must also be negotiated collegially and adhere to the Student Charter 2020, including upholding honesty, ethics, professionalism, and academic integrity (please ensure you are familiar with the updated Academic Integrity 2022 policy).','the use of generative ai across multiple sectors of work is increasing exponentially. while use of these tools brings new opportunities such as increased productivity, there are also many potential limitations such as inhibiting the development of analytical and creative thinking skills. importantly, in icpu where 80% of assessments are group-based, your use of ai tools must also be negotiated collegially and adhere to the student charter 2020, including upholding honesty, ethics, professionalism, and academic integrity (please ensure you are familiar with the updated academic integrity 2022 policy).','assessment_description:AD10'),(1385,40,'AD11','assessment_description',24,'Assessment description 11','AI tools permitted','ai tools permitted','assessment_description:AD11'),(1386,40,'AD12','assessment_description',25,'Assessment description 12','You are permitted to use automated writing tools and generative artificial intelligence (AI) to facilitate your learning and completion of this assignment in individual and group project work. Please adhere to the following guidelines:','you are permitted to use automated writing tools and generative artificial intelligence (ai) to facilitate your learning and completion of this assignment in individual and group project work. please adhere to the following guidelines:','assessment_description:AD12'),(1387,40,'AD13','assessment_description',26,'Assessment description 13','Do not enter confidential, personal, copyrighted or otherwise sensitive information into any AI tool, including but not limited to materials shared by industry and/or community partners (noting also the confidentiality clauses that apply in the Student Deed Poll)','do not enter confidential, personal, copyrighted or otherwise sensitive information into any ai tool, including but not limited to materials shared by industry and/or community partners (noting also the confidentiality clauses that apply in the student deed poll)','assessment_description:AD13'),(1388,40,'