owledgement of AI use when you submit your work, see wording below. This can be requested by the unit coordinator if there is any uncertainty about the originality of your work.','where ai is used, you are advised to keep copies of the prompts you provided and ai outputs as evidence of your research and writing process. this allows you to produce an accurate acknowledgement of ai use when you submit your work, see wording below. this can be requested by the unit coordinator if there is any uncertainty about the originality of your work.','assessment_description:AD20'),(1470,42,'AD21','assessment_description',34,'Assessment description 21','You must acknowledge any uses of AI by inserting a note at the end of your submission where you need to describe the tool(s) that you used, what prompt(s) you provided, how the output of the artificial intelligence was used or adapted by you, and how you verified sources or information if applicable. This additional description does not add to your word count. An example of such an acknowledgement that you may provide might look like:','you must acknowledge any uses of ai by inserting a note at the end of your submission where you need to describe the tool(s) that you used, what prompt(s) you provided, how the output of the artificial intelligence was used or adapted by you, and how you verified sources or information if applicable. this additional description does not add to your word count. an example of such an acknowledgement that you may provide might look like:','assessment_description:AD21'),(1471,42,'AD22','assessment_description',35,'Assessment description 22','I acknowledge the use of ChatGPT (https://chat.openai.com/) to refine the academic language of my own work. On date I submitted my entire essay (link to original document here) with the prompt to <“Improve the academic tone and accuracy of language, including grammatical structures, punctuation and vocabulary”>. The output (link here) was then modified further to better represent my own tone and style of writing. One of the limitations I noted was insert limitation and I revised my assessment to address this limitation by insert response.','i acknowledge the use of chatgpt (https://chat.openai.com/) to refine the academic language of my own work. on date i submitted my entire essay (link to original document here) with the prompt to <“improve the academic tone and accuracy of language, including grammatical structures, punctuation and vocabulary”>. the output (link here) was then modified further to better represent my own tone and style of writing. one of the limitations i noted was insert limitation and i revised my assessment to address this limitation by insert response.','assessment_description:AD22'),(1472,42,'AD23','assessment_description',36,'Assessment description 23','Please note, your project supervisor may require you to provide a written statement if you would like to use AI heavily in your work, (i.e. for multiple approved uses above or heavy use within any individual use categories), a different approach may be needed including clearly stating the percentage of work attributed to AI for each assessment. If you are unsure or have any concerns, please discuss these with your Project Supervisor in advance. In all cases, individual group members must be transparent with their group members about intended use of generative AI in groupwork.','please note, your project supervisor may require you to provide a written statement if you would like to use ai heavily in your work, (i.e. for multiple approved uses above or heavy use within any individual use categories), a different approach may be needed including clearly stating the percentage of work attributed to ai for each assessment. if you are unsure or have any concerns, please discuss these with your project supervisor in advance. in all cases, individual group members must be transparent with their group members about intended use of generative ai in groupwork.','assessment_description:AD23'),(1473,42,'WK01','weekly_schedule',37,'Ongoing: Delivered intensively over 3 weeks, see Canvas site for detailed project schedule','Delivered intensively over 3 weeks, see Canvas site for detailed project schedule. Learning activity: Lecture (13 hr)','delivered intensively over 3 weeks, see canvas site for detailed project schedule. learning activity: lecture (13 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK01'),(1474,42,'WK02','weekly_schedule',38,'Ongoing: Delivered intensively over 3 weeks, see Canvas site for detailed project schedule','Delivered intensively over 3 weeks, see Canvas site for detailed project schedule. Learning activity: Tutorial (26 hr)','delivered intensively over 3 weeks, see canvas site for detailed project schedule. learning activity: tutorial (26 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK02'),(1475,43,'OV01','overview',1,'Overview paragraph 1','This capstone unit bridges the gap between theory and practice by integrating knowledge and consolidating key skills developed across the Business Information Systems major. It aims to provide students with practical experience in identifying, analysing, and solving contemporary business problems. Much of this unit is dedicated to a problem-solving, experiential approach to learning. Students ensure their career-readiness by demonstrating their ability to apply concepts, theories, frameworks, methodologies, and skills to authentic problems and challenges faced in the field of information systems.','this capstone unit bridges the gap between theory and practice by integrating knowledge and consolidating key skills developed across the business information systems major. it aims to provide students with practical experience in identifying, analysing, and solving contemporary business problems. much of this unit is dedicated to a problem-solving, experiential approach to learning. students ensure their career-readiness by demonstrating their ability to apply concepts, theories, frameworks, methodologies, and skills to authentic problems and challenges faced in the field of information systems.','overview:OV01'),(1476,43,'LO01','learning_outcome',2,'Learning outcome 1','LO1. apply and relate information systems theories and concepts in the context of an actual business problem with societal relevance','lo1. apply and relate information systems theories and concepts in the context of an actual business problem with societal relevance','learning_outcome:LO01'),(1477,43,'LO02','learning_outcome',3,'Learning outcome 2','LO2. analyse open-ended business scenarios and evaluate the implications of information systems decisions','lo2. analyse open-ended business scenarios and evaluate the implications of information systems decisions','learning_outcome:LO02'),(1478,43,'LO03','learning_outcome',4,'Learning outcome 3','LO3. apply techniques for organisational and business process analyses to resolve an actual business problem','lo3. apply techniques for organisational and business process analyses to resolve an actual business problem','learning_outcome:LO03'),(1479,43,'LO04','learning_outcome',5,'Learning outcome 4','LO4. communicate in a professional and confident manner, both orally and in writing, with actual business professionals','lo4. communicate in a professional and confident manner, both orally and in writing, with actual business professionals','learning_outcome:LO04'),(1480,43,'LO05','learning_outcome',6,'Learning outcome 5','LO5. apply team management concepts and theories to effectively work in, and manage, cross-functional teams','lo5. apply team management concepts and theories to effectively work in, and manage, cross-functional teams','learning_outcome:LO05'),(1481,43,'LO06','learning_outcome',7,'Learning outcome 6','LO6. analyse and reflect critically on the ethical and social implications of information systems.','lo6. analyse and reflect critically on the ethical and social implications of information systems.','learning_outcome:LO06'),(1482,43,'AS01','assessment',8,'Individual progress report (multiple) Written report - due dates vary based on student allocation','Type: Portfolio or journal. Description: Individual progress report (multiple) Written report - due dates vary based on student allocation','type: portfolio or journal. description: individual progress report (multiple) written report - due dates vary based on student allocation','assessment:AS01'),(1483,43,'AS02','assessment',9,'Generative AI Strategy Plan and critically reflect on using GenAI and how it affects learning.','Type: Written work. Description: Generative AI Strategy Plan and critically reflect on using GenAI and how it affects learning.','type: written work. description: generative ai strategy plan and critically reflect on using genai and how it affects learning.','assessment:AS02'),(1484,43,'AS03','assessment',10,'Reflective Journal Individual, continuous, reflective learning journal, stimulated by prompts.','Type: Portfolio or journal. Description: Reflective Journal Individual, continuous, reflective learning journal, stimulated by prompts.','type: portfolio or journal. description: reflective journal individual, continuous, reflective learning journal, stimulated by prompts.','assessment:AS03'),(1485,43,'AS04','assessment',11,'Group project presentation In-class presentation of group work','Type: Presentation. Description: Group project presentation In-class presentation of group work','type: presentation. description: group project presentation in-class presentation of group work','assessment:AS04'),(1486,43,'AS05','assessment',12,'Group assignment Written report','Type: Written work. Description: Group assignment Written report','type: written work. description: group assignment written report','assessment:AS05'),(1487,43,'AD01','assessment_description',13,'Assessment description 1','Individual assignment: This assignment is in the form of an individual progress report that corresponds to a specific section of the group project. The content of this report will vary depending on the student\'s designated role within the project team. The report comprises 1500 (± 10%) words and associated discussions during the group consultation sessions.','individual assignment: this assignment is in the form of an individual progress report that corresponds to a specific section of the group project. the content of this report will vary depending on the student\'s designated role within the project team. the report comprises 1500 (± 10%) words and associated discussions during the group consultation sessions.','assessment_description:AD01'),(1488,43,'AD02','assessment_description',14,'Assessment description 2','Group assignment: This assessment item requires students to work within their project groups to analyse and provide recommendations for resolving a business problem of an actual client. Each project group will be expected to look for and acquire their own client, and design a technology-enabled solution that will improve a substantive business process of the client. The deliverables of the project include a 15 minute presentation and a project report of 6000 (± 10%) words.','group assignment: this assessment item requires students to work within their project groups to analyse and provide recommendations for resolving a business problem of an actual client. each project group will be expected to look for and acquire their own client, and design a technology-enabled solution that will improve a substantive business process of the client. the deliverables of the project include a 15 minute presentation and a project report of 6000 (± 10%) words.','assessment_description:AD02'),(1489,43,'AD03','assessment_description',15,'Assessment description 3','Reflective journal: Individual, continuous, reflective journal about the student’s authentic learning experience gleaned from the group project and the in-class activities. The student will draft the reflective journal continuously in Canvas and the teaching team will ask them 4-5 ‘provocative’ questions to prompt their critical reflection throughout the semester. The final deliverable is a written reflective journal of 1500 words (± 10%).','reflective journal: individual, continuous, reflective journal about the student\'s authentic learning experience gleaned from the group project and the in-class activities. the student will draft the reflective journal continuously in canvas and the teaching team will ask them 4-5 \'provocative\' questions to prompt their critical reflection throughout the semester. the final deliverable is a written reflective journal of 1500 words (± 10%).','assessment_description:AD03'),(1490,43,'AD04','assessment_description',16,'Assessment description 4','Generative AI Strategy: By developing a clear strategy for using GenAI tools in assignment work, students will enhance their ability to leverage GenAI for tasks such as identifying literature, structuring ideas, refining text, and fact-checking while ensuring ethical and effective practices. The goal is not just to ensure academic integrity but also to reflect on how GenAI tools shape analytical and critical thinking skills. The deliverable is a 600 word (± 10%) document.','generative ai strategy: by developing a clear strategy for using genai tools in assignment work, students will enhance their ability to leverage genai for tasks such as identifying literature, structuring ideas, refining text, and fact-checking while ensuring ethical and effective practices. the goal is not just to ensure academic integrity but also to reflect on how genai tools shape analytical and critical thinking skills. the deliverable is a 600 word (± 10%) document.','assessment_description:AD04'),(1491,43,'AD05','assessment_description',17,'Assessment description 5','Detailed information for each assessment can be found on Canvas.','detailed information for each assessment can be found on canvas.','assessment_description:AD05'),(1492,43,'WK01','weekly_schedule',18,'Week 01: Unit Introduction','Unit Introduction. Learning activity: Seminar (3 hr)','unit introduction. learning activity: seminar (3 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK01'),(1493,43,'WK02','weekly_schedule',19,'Week 02: Case Study Research Methods','Case Study Research Methods. Learning activity: Seminar (3 hr)','case study research methods. learning activity: seminar (3 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK02'),(1494,43,'WK03','weekly_schedule',20,'Week 03: Business Problem Identification','Business Problem Identification. Learning activity: Seminar (3 hr)','business problem identification. learning activity: seminar (3 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK03'),(1495,43,'WK04','weekly_schedule',21,'Week 04: Design Science Research Methods','Design Science Research Methods. Learning activity: Seminar (3 hr)','design science research methods. learning activity: seminar (3 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK04'),(1496,43,'WK05','weekly_schedule',22,'Week 05: Solution Objective','Solution Objective. Learning activity: Seminar (3 hr)','solution objective. learning activity: seminar (3 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK05'),(1497,43,'WK06','weekly_schedule',23,'Week 06: Prototyping and Storytelling','Prototyping and Storytelling. Learning activity: Seminar (3 hr)','prototyping and storytelling. learning activity: seminar (3 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK06'),(1498,43,'WK07','weekly_schedule',24,'Week 07: Outsourcing and Automation','Outsourcing and Automation. Learning activity: Seminar (3 hr)','outsourcing and automation. learning activity: seminar (3 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK07'),(1499,43,'WK08','weekly_schedule',25,'Week 08: IT Project Management','IT Project Management. Learning activity: Seminar (3 hr)','it project management. learning activity: seminar (3 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK08'),(1500,43,'WK09','weekly_schedule',26,'Week 09: Usability Engineering','Usability Engineering. Learning activity: Seminar (3 hr)','usability engineering. learning activity: seminar (3 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK09'),(1501,43,'WK10','weekly_schedule',27,'Week 10: Design Ethics','Design Ethics. Learning activity: Seminar (3 hr)','design ethics. learning activity: seminar (3 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK10'),(1502,43,'WK11','weekly_schedule',28,'Week 11: Scientific Writing','Scientific Writing. Learning activity: Seminar (3 hr)','scientific writing. learning activity: seminar (3 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK11'),(1503,43,'WK12','weekly_schedule',29,'Week 12: Unit Review and Debriefing','Unit Review and Debriefing. Learning activity: Seminar (3 hr)','unit review and debriefing. learning activity: seminar (3 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK12'),(1504,43,'WK13','weekly_schedule',30,'Week 13: Project presentations','Project presentations. Learning activity: Seminar (3 hr)','project presentations. learning activity: seminar (3 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK13'),(1505,44,'OV01','overview',1,'Overview paragraph 1','This capstone unit bridges the gap between theory and practice by integrating knowledge and consolidating key skills developed across the Business Information Systems major. It aims to provide students with practical experience in identifying, analysing, and solving contemporary business problems. Much of this unit is dedicated to a problem-solving, experiential approach to learning. Students ensure their career-readiness by demonstrating their ability to apply concepts, theories, frameworks, methodologies, and skills to authentic problems and challenges faced in the field of information systems.','this capstone unit bridges the gap between theory and practice by integrating knowledge and consolidating key skills developed across the business information systems major. it aims to provide students with practical experience in identifying, analysing, and solving contemporary business problems. much of this unit is dedicated to a problem-solving, experiential approach to learning. students ensure their career-readiness by demonstrating their ability to apply concepts, theories, frameworks, methodologies, and skills to authentic problems and challenges faced in the field of information systems.','overview:OV01'),(1506,44,'LO01','learning_outcome',2,'Learning outcome 1','LO1. apply and relate information systems theories and concepts in the context of an actual business problem with societal relevance','lo1. apply and relate information systems theories and concepts in the context of an actual business problem with societal relevance','learning_outcome:LO01'),(1507,44,'LO02','learning_outcome',3,'Learning outcome 2','LO2. analyse open-ended business scenarios and evaluate the implications of information systems decisions','lo2. analyse open-ended business scenarios and evaluate the implications of information systems decisions','learning_outcome:LO02'),(1508,44,'LO03','learning_outcome',4,'Learning outcome 3','LO3. apply techniques for organisational and business process analyses to resolve an actual business problem','lo3. apply techniques for organisational and business process analyses to resolve an actual business problem','learning_outcome:LO03'),(1509,44,'LO04','learning_outcome',5,'Learning outcome 4','LO4. communicate in a professional and confident manner, both orally and in writing, with actual business professionals','lo4. communicate in a professional and confident manner, both orally and in writing, with actual business professionals','learning_outcome:LO04'),(1510,44,'LO05','learning_outcome',6,'Learning outcome 5','LO5. apply team management concepts and theories to effectively work in, and manage, cross-functional teams','lo5. apply team management concepts and theories to effectively work in, and manage, cross-functional teams','learning_outcome:LO05'),(1511,44,'LO06','learning_outcome',7,'Learning outcome 6','LO6. analyse and reflect critically on the ethical and social implications of information systems.','lo6. analyse and reflect critically on the ethical and social implications of information systems.','learning_outcome:LO06'),(1512,44,'AS01','assessment',8,'Generative AI Strategy Plan and cr