ss rather than technology perspective, this unit covers the enterprise ecosystem in the context of strategic and operational analytics and decision making. Topics include innovation through advanced analytics, data driven performance management, strategic business improvement and management of complex BI projects. The unit offers hands-on experience in using a commercial platform, combined with in-depth analytical skills, and enables students completing the unit to help any organization to derive more value from data and information and compete on analytics.','business analytics and the ability to interpret and respond to related outputs, is a major source of competitive advantage in the information age and is therefore a leading business priority globally. in recent times, this field has evolved from a technology topic to a management priority, creating an unprecedented demand for new competencies in managing with data. taking a business rather than technology perspective, this unit covers the enterprise ecosystem in the context of strategic and operational analytics and decision making. topics include innovation through advanced analytics, data driven performance management, strategic business improvement and management of complex bi projects. the unit offers hands-on experience in using a commercial platform, combined with in-depth analytical skills, and enables students completing the unit to help any organization to derive more value from data and information and compete on analytics.','overview:OV01'),(1753,52,'LO01','learning_outcome',2,'Learning outcome 1','LO1. Apply the fundamental concepts and practice of managing through data challenges in differentiated organisational settings.','lo1. apply the fundamental concepts and practice of managing through data challenges in differentiated organisational settings.','learning_outcome:LO01'),(1754,52,'LO02','learning_outcome',3,'Learning outcome 2','LO2. Identify and analyse issues, challenges and solutions in managing through data/business analytics systems from the business rather thantechnical perspective.','lo2. identify and analyse issues, challenges and solutions in managing through data/business analytics systems from the business rather thantechnical perspective.','learning_outcome:LO02'),(1755,52,'LO03','learning_outcome',4,'Learning outcome 3','LO3. Critically examine the intra and inter organisational and societal issues involved in implementing various types of analytical systems.','lo3. critically examine the intra and inter organisational and societal issues involved in implementing various types of analytical systems.','learning_outcome:LO03'),(1756,52,'LO04','learning_outcome',5,'Learning outcome 4','LO4. Design and implement a small-scale data analysis project in an organisational setting.','lo4. design and implement a small-scale data analysis project in an organisational setting.','learning_outcome:LO04'),(1757,52,'LO05','learning_outcome',6,'Learning outcome 5','LO5. Evaluate different analytical outputs and their ethical impacts.','lo5. evaluate different analytical outputs and their ethical impacts.','learning_outcome:LO05'),(1758,52,'LO06','learning_outcome',7,'Learning outcome 6','LO6. Apply advanced principles and techniques related to strategy, organizational change and information governance to help organisations effectively maximise value from their data, information assets and technology investments.','lo6. apply advanced principles and techniques related to strategy, organizational change and information governance to help organisations effectively maximise value from their data, information assets and technology investments.','learning_outcome:LO06'),(1759,52,'AS01','assessment',8,'Reflective Essay Written essay on core learnings','Type: Portfolio or journal. Description: Reflective Essay Written essay on core learnings','type: portfolio or journal. description: reflective essay written essay on core learnings','assessment:AS01'),(1760,52,'AS02