 principles and dv lifecycle. learning activity: seminar (3 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK10'),(1808,53,'WK11','weekly_schedule',30,'Week 11: Guided Project Work','Guided Project Work. Learning activity: Seminar (3 hr)','guided project work. learning activity: seminar (3 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK11'),(1809,53,'WK12','weekly_schedule',31,'Week 12: Group Presentations','Group Presentations. Learning activity: Seminar (3 hr)','group presentations. learning activity: seminar (3 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK12'),(1810,53,'WK13','weekly_schedule',32,'Week 13: Group Presentations','Group Presentations. Learning activity: Seminar (3 hr)','group presentations. learning activity: seminar (3 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK13'),(1811,54,'OV01','overview',1,'Overview paragraph 1','As the amount of data generated continues to grow dramatically, managing data at scale presents a set of challenges for which organizations have to be uniquely prepared. This unit provides students with what they need to know about generating, collecting, processing, storing, managing, analysing and interpreting data. The unit provides an understanding of the importance of data strategies, data governance and data quality, challenges associated with data protection, privacy and security, data management practices, and modern platforms and architecture to streamline data operations within an organisation. Students learn the importance of confidentiality, integrity, and availability of data in mitigating information risks and emergent issues around data ethics.','as the amount of data generated continues to grow dramatically, managing data at scale presents a set of challenges for which organizations have to be uniquely prepared. this unit provides students with what they need to know about generating, collecting, processing, storing, managing, analysing and interpreting data. the unit provides an understanding of the importance of data strategies, data governance and data quality, challenges associated with data protection, privacy and security, data management practices, and modern platforms and architecture to streamline data operations within an organisation. students learn the importance of confidentiality, integrity, and availability of data in mitigating information risks and emergent issues around data ethics.','overview:OV01'),(1812,54,'LO01','learning_outcome',2,'Learning outcome 1','LO1. Analyse, identify, and define organisational data management challenges based on theory and practice','lo1. analyse, identify, and define organisational data management challenges based on theory and practice','learning_outcome:LO01'),(1813,54,'LO02','learning_outcome',3,'Learning outcome 2','LO2. Propose and justify data management strategies for real-world organisational scenarios','lo2. propose and justify data management strategies for real-world organisational scenarios','learning_outcome:LO02'),(1814,54,'LO03','learning_outcome',4,'Learning outcome 3','LO3. Evaluate data-related systems, processes, components, and outcomes by applying theoretical concepts and knowledge of best practices','lo3. evaluate data-related systems, processes, components, and outcomes by applying theoretical concepts and knowledge of best practices','learning_outcome:LO03'),(1815,54,'LO04','learning_outcome',5,'Learning outcome 4','LO4. Explain principles of data protection, privacy, security and data ethics','lo4. explain principles of data protection, privacy, security and data ethics','learning_outcome:LO04'),(1816,54,'LO05','learning_outcome',6,'Learning outcome 5','LO5. Function effectively in a team to accomplish a common goal','lo5. function effectively in a team to accomplish a common goal','learning_outcome:LO05'),(1817,54,'LO06','learning_outcome',7,'Learning outcome 6','LO6. Communicate and engage orally and verbally in a professional manner','lo6. communicate and engage orally and verbally in a professional manner','learning_outcome:LO06'),(1818,54,'AS01','assessment',8,'Skills-based assessment Sk