 Data: Part 1. Learning activity: Seminar (3 hr)','enabling and maintaining data: part 1. learning activity: seminar (3 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK03'),(1833,54,'WK04','weekly_schedule',23,'Week 04: Enabling and Maintaining Data: Part 2','Enabling and Maintaining Data: Part 2. Learning activity: Seminar (3 hr)','enabling and maintaining data: part 2. learning activity: seminar (3 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK04'),(1834,54,'WK05','weekly_schedule',24,'Week 05: Using and Enhancing Data','Using and Enhancing Data. Learning activity: Seminar (3 hr)','using and enhancing data. learning activity: seminar (3 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK05'),(1835,54,'WK06','weekly_schedule',25,'Week 06: Workshop','Workshop. Learning activity: Seminar (3 hr)','workshop. learning activity: seminar (3 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK06'),(1836,54,'WK07','weekly_schedule',26,'Week 07: Data Quality Management','Data Quality Management. Learning activity: Seminar (3 hr)','data quality management. learning activity: seminar (3 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK07'),(1837,54,'WK08','weekly_schedule',27,'Week 08: Data Ethics','Data Ethics. Learning activity: Seminar (3 hr)','data ethics. learning activity: seminar (3 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK08'),(1838,54,'WK09','weekly_schedule',28,'Week 09: Data Protection, Privacy, Security and Risks','Data Protection, Privacy, Security and Risks. Learning activity: Seminar (3 hr)','data protection, privacy, security and risks. learning activity: seminar (3 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK09'),(1839,54,'WK10','weekly_schedule',29,'Week 10: Data Governance and Maturity Assessment','Data Governance and Maturity Assessment. Learning activity: Seminar (3 hr)','data governance and maturity assessment. learning activity: seminar (3 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK10'),(1840,54,'WK11','weekly_schedule',30,'Week 11: Group Project Workshop','Group Project Workshop. Learning activity: Seminar (3 hr)','group project workshop. learning activity: seminar (3 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK11'),(1841,54,'WK12','weekly_schedule',31,'Week 12: Group Presentations','Group Presentations. Learning activity: Seminar (3 hr)','group presentations. learning activity: seminar (3 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK12'),(1842,54,'WK13','weekly_schedule',32,'Week 13: Group Presentations','Group Presentations. Learning activity: Seminar (3 hr)','group presentations. learning activity: seminar (3 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK13'),(1843,55,'OV01','overview',1,'Overview paragraph 1','This unit provides an in-depth understanding of cybersecurity management, essential to organisations in protecting their data and information assets against threats and attacks. Students are exposed to concepts, methodologies, and strategies that will equip them with key skills needed to prevent, detect, and mitigate security risks, while addressing ethical and privacy concerns. This unit covers a range of topics of cybersecurity risk management, including awareness of emerging technologies, information security policy, governance frameworks, and incident response planning in response to social engineering and ransomware attacks. Students also learn how to respond to and mitigate incidents and manage employees, while developing security education with focus on effective training and awareness programs.','this unit provides an in-depth understanding of cybersecurity management, essential to organisations in protecting their data and information assets against threats and attacks. students are exposed to concepts, methodologies, and strategies that will equip them with key skills needed to prevent, detect, and mitigate security risks, while addressing ethical and privacy concerns. this unit covers a range of topics of cybersecurity risk management, including awareness of emerging technologies, information security policy, governance frameworks, and incident response planning in response to social engineering and ransomware attacks. students also learn how to respond to and mitigate incidents and manage employees, while developing security education with focus on effective training and awareness programs.','overview:OV01'),(1844,55,'LO01','learning_outcome',2,'Learning outcome 1','LO1. Discuss the role of information assets and governance management frameworks in protecting such assets in organisations','lo1. discuss the role of information assets and governance management frameworks in protecting such assets in organisations','learning_outcome:LO01'),(1845,55,'LO02','learning_outcome',3,'Learning outcome 2','LO2. Evaluate the risks associated with information assets and their impact on organisation','lo2. evaluate the risks associated with information assets and their impact on organisation','learning_outcome:LO02'),(1846,55,'LO03','learning_outcome',4,'Learning outcome 3','LO3. Apply cybersecurity concepts and methodologies to design and implement effective security management strategies and practices','lo3. apply cybersecurity concepts and methodologies to design and implement effective security management strategies and practices','learning_outcome:LO03'),(1847,55,'LO04','learning_outcome',5,'Learning outcome 4','LO4. Evaluate managerial approaches for addressing cybersecurity threats and attacks using real-world scenarios','lo4. evaluate managerial approaches for addressing cybersecurity threats and attacks using real-world scenarios','learning_outcome:LO04'),(1848,55,'LO05','learning_outcome',6,'Learning outcome 5','LO5. Address the impact of employee behaviours in mitigating security risks and ensuring a secure work environment','lo5. address the impact of employee behaviours in mitigating security risks and ensuring a secure work environment','learning_outcome:LO05'),(1849,55,'LO06','learning_outcome',7,'Learning outcome 6','LO6. Communicate cybersecurity issues, and collaborate towards solutions in a professional manner with people from diverse backgrounds','lo6. communicate cybersecurity issues, and collaborate towards solutions in a professional manner with people from diverse backgrounds','learning_outcome:LO06'),(1850,55,'AS01','assessment',8,'Class contribution Weekly workshop contribution','Type: Contribution. Description: Class contribution Weekly workshop contribution','type: contribution. description: class contribution weekly workshop contribution','assessment:AS01'),(1851,55,'AS02','assessment',9,'Early-Feedback Task Multiple-Choice Quiz','Type: Out-of-class quiz. Description: Early-Feedback Task Multiple-Choice Quiz','type: out-of-class quiz. description: early-feedback task multiple-choice quiz','assessment:AS02'),(1852,55,'AS03','assessment',10,'Reflective Report Reflective Report','Type: Portfolio or journal. Description: Reflective Report Reflective Report','type: portfolio or journal. description: reflective report reflective report','assessment:AS03'),(1853,55,'AS04','assessment',11,'Video briefing Video briefing','Type: Portfolio or journal. Description: Video briefing Video briefing','type: portfolio or journal. description: video briefing video briefing','assessment:AS04'),(1854,55,'AS05','assessment',12,'Individual Report Individual Report','Type: Case studies. Description: Individual Report Individual Report','type: case studies. description: individual report individual report','assessment:AS05'),(1855,55,'AS06','assessment',13,'Group project report Group Assignment','Type: Written work. Description: Group project report Group Assignment','type: written work. description: group project report group assignment','assessment:AS06'),(1856,55,'AS07','assessment',14,'Group presentation Group presentation','Type: Presentation. Description: Group presentation Group presentation','type: presentation. description: group presentation group presentation','assessment:AS07'),(1857,55,'AD01','assessment_description',15,'Assessment description 1','Detailed information for each assessment can be found on Canvas.','detailed information for each assessment can be found on canvas.','assessment_description:AD01'),(1858,55,'WK01','weekly_schedule',16,'Week 01: Cybersecurity Foundations','Cybersecurity Foundations. Learning activity: Seminar (3 hr)','cybersecurity foundations. learning activity: seminar (3 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK01'),(1859,55,'WK02','weekly_schedule',17,'Week 02: Cybersecurity Architecture (A)','Cybersecurity Architecture (A). Learning activity: Seminar (3 hr)','cybersecurity architecture (a). learning activity: seminar (3 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK02'),(1860,55,'WK03','weekly_schedule',18,'Week 03: Cybersecurity Architecture (B)','Cybersecurity Architecture (B). Learning activity: Seminar (3 hr)','cybersecurity architecture (b). learning activity: seminar (3 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK03'),(1861,55,'WK04','weekly_schedule',19,'Week 04: Incident Response','Incident Response. Learning activity: Seminar (3 hr)','incident response. learning activity: seminar (3 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK04'),(1862,55,'WK05','weekly_schedule',20,'Week 05: Risk Management','Risk Management. Learning activity: Seminar (3 hr)','risk management. learning activity: seminar (3 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK05'),(1863,55,'WK06','weekly_schedule',21,'Week 06: Assurance','Assurance. Learning activity: Seminar (3 hr)','assurance. learning activity: seminar (3 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK06'),(1864,55,'WK07','weekly_schedule',22,'Week 07: Governance, Strategy, and Privacy','Governance, Strategy, and Privacy. Learning activity: Seminar (3 hr)','governance, strategy, and privacy. learning activity: seminar (3 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK07'),(1865,55,'WK08','weekly_schedule',23,'Week 08: AI in Cyber Attacks and Defense','AI in Cyber Attacks and Defense. Learning activity: Seminar (3 hr)','ai in cyber attacks and defense. learning activity: seminar (3 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK08'),(1866,55,'WK09','weekly_schedule',24,'Week 09: Group Project','Group Project. Learning activity: Seminar (3 hr)','group project. learning activity: seminar (3 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK09'),(1867,55,'WK10','weekly_schedule',25,'Week 10: Group Project','Group Project. Learning activity: Seminar (3 hr)','group project. learning activity: seminar (3 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK10'),(1868,55,'WK11','weekly_schedule',26,'Week 11: Industry Clinics for Group Project','Industry Clinics for Group Project. Learning activity: Seminar (3 hr)','industry clinics for group project. learning activity: seminar (3 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK11'),(1869,55,'WK12','weekly_schedule',27,'Week 12: Incident Response (Advanced) and the Aftermath of Attacks','Incident Response (Advanced) and the Aftermath of Attacks. Learning activity: Seminar (3 hr)','incident response (advanced) and the aftermath of attacks. learning activity: seminar (3 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK12'),(1870,55,'WK13','weekly_schedule',28,'Week 13: Final Group Project Presentations','Final Group Project Presentations. Learning activity: Seminar (3 hr)','final group project presentations. learning activity: seminar (3 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK13'),(1871,56,'OV01','overview',1,'Overview paragraph 1','Traditional approaches to project management and design work well under stable conditions, when intended outcomes are well understood. Yet, under conditional of market disruption, in innovation projects, new product development or for start-up businesses, traditional methods are often restrictive and inflexible. Agile Project Management and Design Thinking offer alternative approaches that value continuous change, flexibility, time-to-market, interactive learning and self-organisation over rigorous planning and design processes. In this unit, students will learn the ethos, principles, and methods of agile project management and design thinking. Students will experience hands-on techniques such as design thinking, learn management and Scrum as applied in practice. Learning will revolve around practical activities, insights from experienced guest speakers and case studies representing various industries.','traditional approaches to project management and design work well under stable conditions, when intended outcomes are well understood. yet, under conditional of market disruption, in innovation projects, new product development or for start-up businesses, traditional methods are often restrictive and inflexible. agile project management and design thinking offer alternative approaches that value continuous change, flexibility, time-to-market, interactive learning and self-organisation over rigorous planning and design processes. in this unit, students will learn the ethos, principles, and methods of agile project management and design thinking. students will experience hands-on techniques such as design thinking, learn management and scrum as applied in practice. learning will revolve around practical activities, insights from experienced guest speakers and case studies representing various industries.','overview:OV01'),(1872,56,'LO01','learning_outcome',2,'Learning outcome 1','LO1. demonstrate knowledge of the key principles of agile projects and their differences to traditional project management values','lo1. demonstrate knowledge of the key principles of agile projects and their differences to traditional project management values','learning_outcome:LO01'),(1873,56,'LO02','learning_outcome',3,'Learning outcome 2','LO2. describe and apply foundational agile project management practices','lo2. describe and apply foundational agile project management practices','learning_outcome:LO02'),(1874,56,'LO03','learning_outcome',4,'Learning outcome 3','LO3. describe and apply foundational design thinking practices','lo3. describe and apply foundational design thinking practices','learning_outcome:LO03'),(1875,56,'LO04','learning_outcome',5,'Learning outcome 4','LO4. reflect critically about key issues in agile project management and design thinking and communicate your reflections effectively','lo4. reflect critically about key issues in agile project management and design thinking and communicate your reflections effectively','learning_outcome:LO04'),(1876,56,'LO05','learning_outcome',6,'Learning outcome 5','LO5. engage effectively in team-based agile project management and design thinking practices','lo5. engage effectively in team-based agile project management and design thinking practices','learning_outcome:LO05'),(1877,56,'LO06','learning_outcome',7,'Learning outcome 6','LO6. communicate effectively in group work situations in accordance with agile project management and design thinking practices','lo6. communicate effectively in group work situations in accordance with agile project management and design thinking practices','learning_outcome:LO06'),(1878,56,'LO07','learning_outcome',8,'Learning outcome 7','LO7. understand the principles of people-centric design and project work practices.','lo7. understand the principles of people-centric design and project work practices.','learning_outcome:LO07'),(1879,56,'AS01','assessment',9,'Essay Written essay','Type: Written work. Description: Essay Written essay','type: written work. description: essay written essay','assessment:AS01'),(1880,56,'AS02','assessment',10,'Learning journals Written journal','Type: Portfolio or journal. Description: Learning journals Written journal','type: portfolio or journal. description: learning journals written journal','assessment:AS02'),(1881,56,'AS03','assessment',11,'Agile activities Participation','Type: Contribution. Description: Agile activities Participation','type: contribution. description: agile activities participation','assessment:AS03'),(1882,56,'AS04','assessment',12,'Product owner meetings Discussion','Type: Conversation. Description: Product owner meetings Discussion','type: conversation. description: product owner meetings discussion','assessment:AS04'),(1883,56,'AS05','assessment',13,'Agile project delivery Project delivery','Type: Portfolio or journal. Description: Agile project delivery Project delivery','type: portfolio or journal. description: agile project delivery project delivery','assessment:AS05'),(1884,56,'AD01','assessment_description',14,'Assessment description 1','Learning journals: The purpose of the journal is to help students keep up to date with the required work and provide students and the unit coordinators with timely feedback on student learning progress. The journal is an integral part of the agile delivery of the core part of this unit. You will reflect on each week\'s topic utilising a set of brief instructions provided via Canvas for each of the learning journal submissions. Assessment of the weekly learning journal submissions will consider both grasps of the week\'s topic, but more importantly the degree of self-reflection and engagement with the topic.','learning journals: the purpose of the journal is to help students keep up to date with the required work and provide students and the unit coordinators with timely feedback on student learning progress. the journal is an integral part of the agile delivery of the core part of this unit. you will reflect on each week\'s topic utilising a set of brief instructions provided via canvas for each of the learning journal submissions. assessment of the weekly learning journal submissions will consider both grasps of the week\'s topic, but more importantly the degree of self-reflection and engagement with the topic.','assessment_description:AD01'),(1885,56,'AD02','assessment_description',15,'Assessment description 2','Agile activities: The agile learning sessions are built around hands-on activities whose learning outcomes depend on the active participation of each student. It is paramount that students pay attention to the purpose of each activity and show initiative in applying themselves to the task at hand. In-class activities involve the development of artefacts across agile sprints through iterative work, enabling multiple forms of engagement and active participation and allowing students to contribute in a variety of ways.','agile activities: the agile learning sessions are built around hands-on activities whose learning outcomes depend on the active participation of each student. it is paramount that students pay attention to the purpose of each activity and show initiative in applying themselves to the task at hand. in-class activities involve the development of artefacts across agile sprints through iterative work, enabling multiple forms of engagement and active participation and allowing students to contribute in a variety of ways.','assessment_description:AD02'),(1886,56,'AD03','assessment_description',16,'Assessment description 3','Product owner meetings: The purpose of PO meetings is for students to engage in time-boxed discussions with a designated product owner from the teaching team to review each sprint’s MVP. Teams use targeted feedback on personas, design thinking, and concept development to refine their work and guide priorities for the next sprint, with an emphasis on learning and iteration rather than polished outcomes.','product owner meetings: the purpose of po meetings is for students to engage in time-boxed discussions with a designated product owner from the teaching team to review each sprint\'s mvp. teams use targeted feedback on personas, design thinking, and concept development to refine their work and guide priorities for the next sprint, with an emphasis on learning and iteration rather than polished outcomes.','assessment_description:AD03'),(1887,56,'AD04','assessment_description',17,'Assessment description 4','Agile project delivery: The objective of the agile project is to use the knowledge and practical skills in agile projects and design thinking acquired in this unit of study to apply to a real-world problem. The focus of this project is in applying appropriate techniques and practices in creating the desired project outcome represented in diagrams, video and textual elements. While the outcome as such is not unimportant, the focus of this assignment and its assessment is on the application of the agile project management and design thinking techniques.','agile project delivery: the objective of the agile project is to use the knowledge and practical skills in agile projects and design thinking acquired in this unit of study to apply to a real-world problem. the focus of this project is in applying appropriate techniques and practices in creating the desired project outcome represented in diagrams, video and textual elements. while the outcome as such is not unimportant, the focus of this assignment and its assessment is on the application of the agile project management and design thinking techniques.','assessment_description:AD04'),(1888,56,'AD05','assessment_description',18,'Assessment description 5','Essay: The purpose of the essay is to demonstrate grasp of the agile philosophy and principles, as well as the agile project management and design thinking practices and techniques. The focus of the essay will lie in synthesising the learnings derived from the unit of study.','essay: the purpose of the essay is to demonstrate grasp of the agile philosophy and principles, as well as the agile project management and design thinking practices and techniques. the focus of the essay will lie in synthesising the learnings derived from the unit of study.','assessment_description:AD05'),(1889,56,'AD06','assessment_description',19,'Assessment description 6','Detailed information for each assessment can be found on Canvas.','detailed information for each assessment can be found on canvas.','assessment_description:AD06'),(1890,56,'WK01','weekly_schedule',20,'Week 01: Introduction and overview','Introduction and overview. Learning activity: Seminar (3 hr)','introduction and overview. learning activity: seminar (3 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK01'),(1891,56,'WK02','weekly_schedule',21,'Week 02: Practices, principles and philosophy of agile project delivery','Practices, principles and philosophy of agile project delivery. Learning activity: Seminar (3 hr)','practices, principles and philosophy of agile project delivery. learning activity: seminar (3 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK02'),(1892,56,'WK03','weekly_schedule',22,'Week 03: Practices, principles and philosophy of design thinking','Practices, principles and philosophy of design thinking. Learning activity: Seminar (3 hr)','practices, principles and philosophy of design thinking. learning activity: seminar (3 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK03'),(1893,56,'WK04','weekly_schedule',23,'Week 04: Agile learning session 1','Agile learning session 1. Learning activity: Seminar (3 hr)','agile learning session 1. learning activity: seminar (3 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK04'),(1894,56,'WK05','weekly_schedule',24,'Week 05: Agile learning session 2','Agile learning session 2. Learning activity: Seminar (3 hr)','agile learning session 2. learning activity: seminar (3 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK05'),(1895,56,'WK06','weekly_schedule',25,'Week 06: Agile learning session 3','Agile learning session 3. Learning activity: Seminar (3 hr)','agile learning session 3. learning activity: seminar (3 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK06'),(1896,56,'WK07','weekly_schedule',26,'Week 07: Agile learning session 4','Agile learning session 4. Learning activity: Seminar (3 hr)','agile learning session 4. learning activity: seminar (3 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK07'),(1897,56,'WK08','weekly_schedule',27,'Week 08: Agile learning session 5','Agile learning session 5. Learning activity: Seminar (3 hr)','agile learning session 5. learning activity: seminar (3 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK08'),(1898,56,'WK09','weekly_schedule',28,'Week 09: Agile learning session 6','Agile learning session 6. Learning activity: Seminar (3 hr)','agile learning session 6. learning activity: seminar (3 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK09'),(1899,56,'WK10','weekly_schedule',29,'Week 10: Agile learning session 7','Agile learning session 7. Learning activity: Seminar (3 hr)','agile learning session 7. learning activity: seminar (3 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK10'),(1900,56,'WK11','weekly_schedule',30,'Week 11: Case study: TBA','Case study: TBA. Learning activity: Seminar (3 hr)','case study: tba. learning activity: seminar (3 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK11'),(1901,56,'WK12','weekly_schedule',31,'Week 12: Case study: TBA','Case study: TBA. Learning activity: Seminar (3 hr)','case study: tba. learning activity: seminar (3 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK12'),(1902,56,'WK13','weekly_schedule',32,'Week 13: Synthesis and wrap-up','Synthesis and wrap-up. Learning activity: Seminar (3 hr)','synthesis and wrap-up. learning activity: seminar (3 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK13'),(1903,57,'OV01','overview',1,'Overview paragraph 1','Technology is at the heart of many of the contemporary trends and challenges facing organisations. This unit of study introduces students to balanced and critical ways of thinking about the nature and role of technology in business and society. It problematizes the hype surrounding new technological developments (gadgets), the deification of technology as a solution to problems of all kinds (gods), and the, often unintended, consequences of technology applications (godzilla). The unit utilises current technological developments as examples for discussion and examines technology and its design and application in the context of social networks, power relations, and current business trends.','technology is at the heart of many of the contemporary trends and challenges facing organisations. this unit of study introduces students to balanced and critical ways of thinking about the nature and role of technology in business and society. it problematizes the hype surrounding new technological developments (gadgets), the deification of technology as a solution to problems of all kinds (gods), and the, often unintended, consequences of technology applications (godzilla). the unit utilises current technological developments as examples for discussion and examines technology and its design and application in the context of social networks, power relations, and current business trends.','overview:OV01'),(1904,57,'LO01','learning_outcome',2,'Learning outcome 1','LO1. Make and defend evaluations of socio-technical systems.','lo1. make and defend evaluations of socio-technical systems.','learning_outcome:LO01'),(1905,57,'LO02','learning_outcome',3,'Learning outcome 2','LO2. Construct arguments regarding the benefits and consequences of technologies in organizational and societal setting.','lo2. construct arguments regarding the benefits and consequences of technologies in organizational and societal setting.','learning_outcome:LO02'),(1906,57,'LO03','learning_outcome',4,'Learning outcome 3','LO3. Categorize perspectives based on alternative ethical stances.','lo3. categorize perspectives based on alternative ethical stances.','learning_outcome:LO03'),(1907,57,'LO04','learning_outcome',5,'Learning outcome 4','LO4. Create and assess alternative scenario prototypes of socio-technical systems at individual, organizational and societal levels.','lo4. create and assess alternative scenario prototypes of socio-technical systems at individual, organizational and societal levels.','learning_outcome:LO04'),(1908,57,'AS01','assessment',6,'Reflection Journal The purpose of the reflection journal is to reflect on the weeks learning.','Type: Portfolio or journal. Description: Reflection Journal The purpose of the reflection journal is to reflect on the weeks learning.','type: portfolio or journal. description: reflection journal the purpose of the reflection journal is to reflect on the weeks learning.','assessment:AS01'),(1909,57,'AS02','assessment',7,'Reflection Journal The purpose of the reflection journal is to reflect on the weeks learning.','Type: Portfolio or journal. Description: Reflection Journal The purpose of the reflection journal is to reflect on the weeks learning.','type: portfolio or journal. description: reflection journal the purpose of the reflection journal is to reflect on the weeks learning.','assessment:AS02'),(1910,57,'AS03','assessment',8,'Reflection Journal The purpose of the reflection journal is to reflect on the weeks learning.','Type: Portfolio or journal. Description: Reflection Journal The purpose of the reflection journal is to reflect on the weeks learning.','type: portfolio or journal. description: reflection journal the purpose of the reflection journal is to reflect on the weeks learning.','assessment:AS03'),(1911,57,'AS04','assessment',9,'Group Project Students will work in groups applying methods introduced during class.','Type: Creative work. Description: Group Project Students will work in groups applying methods introduced during class.','type: creative work. description: group project students will work in groups applying methods introduced during class.','assessment:AS04'),(1912,57,'AS05','assessment',10,'Final Essay The final report/essay will provide opportunity to synthesize learning.','Type: Written work. Description: Final Essay The final report/essay will provide opportunity to synthesize learning.','type: written work. description: final essay the final report/essay will provide opportunity to synthesize learning.','assessment:AS05'),(1913,57,'AD01','assessment_description',11,'Assessment description 1','Video learning journals (working in pairs, (3 videos 2.5 minutes each; via Canvas)','video learning journals (working in pairs, (3 videos 2.5 minutes each; via canvas)','assessment_description:AD01'),(1914,57,'AD02','assessment_description',12,'Assessment description 2','Group project presentations/demonstrations in class (10 minutes exhibition including Q&A during week 8. 750 word writeup due same day.)','group project presentations/demonstrations in class (10 minutes exhibition including q&a during week 8. 750 word writeup due same day.)','assessment_description:AD02'),(1915,57,'AD03','assessment_description',13,'Assessment description 3','Final essay (1000 words) submitted via Canvas','final essay (1000 words) submitted via canvas','assessment_description:AD03'),(1916,57,'WK01','weekly_schedule',14,'Week 01: Futures, Megatrends and Metaphors','Futures, Megatrends and Metaphors. Learning activity: Lecture (5 hr)','futures, megatrends and metaphors. learning activity: lecture (5 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK01'),(1917,57,'WK02','weekly_schedule',15,'Week 02: Forecasting, Prediction; Gadgets on the Loose','Forecasting, Prediction; Gadgets on the Loose. Learning activity: Lecture (5 hr)','forecasting, prediction; gadgets on the loose. learning activity: lecture (5 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK02'),(1918,57,'WK03','weekly_schedule',16,'Week 03: Scenario thinking, scenario analysis; Modern Gods','Scenario thinking, scenario analysis; Modern Gods. Learning activity: Lecture (5 hr)','scenario thinking, scenario analysis; modern gods. learning activity: lecture (5 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK03'),(1919,57,'WK04','weekly_schedule',17,'Week 04: Foresight, speculative futures ; Monsters in the Classroom','Foresight, speculative futures ; Monsters in the Classroom. Learning activity: Lecture (5 hr)','foresight, speculative futures ; monsters in the classroom. learning activity: lecture (5 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK04'),(1920,57,'WK05','weekly_schedule',18,'Week 05: Digital Geographies; Speculation','Digital Geographies; Speculation. Learning activity: Lecture (5 hr)','digital geographies; speculation. learning activity: lecture (5 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK05'),(1921,57,'WK06','weekly_schedule',19,'Week 06: AI Fluency Sprint','AI Fluency Sprint. Learning activity: Lecture (5 hr)','ai fluency sprint. learning activity: lecture (5 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK06'),(1922,57,'WK07','weekly_schedule',20,'Week 07: Technological Imaginaries','Technological Imaginaries. Learning activity: Lecture (5 hr)','technological imaginaries. learning activity: lecture (5 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK07'),(1923,57,'WK08','weekly_schedule',21,'Week 08: In-class work and Presentations; Attendance Mandatory','In-class work and Presentations; Attendance Mandatory. Learning activity: Lecture (5 hr)','in-class work and presentations; attendance mandatory. learning activity: lecture (5 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK08'),(1924,58,'OV01','overview',1,'Overview paragraph 1','This unit introduces students to the foundations of project management in business contexts. It provides an overview and practical understanding of different project management approaches, ranging from structured frameworks such as the Project Management Body of Knowledge (PMBOK) to light-weight techniques such as Agile or Lean Management. Students learn how to select appropriate projects based on their alignment with an organisation\'s strategy and then how to manage those projects successfully from initiation through execution to completion. The unit explores both the technical and behavioural aspects of project management and students gain experience in critically analysing the application of techniques in specific business contexts. As organisations increasingly structure their activities on a project basis, the unit is of value to a range of discipline specialisations.','this unit introduces students to the foundations of project management in business contexts. it provides an overview and practical understanding of different project management approaches, ranging from structured frameworks such as the project management body of knowledge (pmbok) to light-weight techniques such as agile or lean management. students learn how to select appropriate projects based on their alignment with an organisation\'s strategy and then how to manage those projects successfully from initiation through execution to completion. the unit explores both the technical and behavioural aspects of project management and students gain experience in critically analysing the application of techniques in specific business contexts. as organisations increasingly structure their activities on a project basis, the unit is of value to a range of discipline specialisations.','overview:OV01'),(1925,58,'LO01','learning_outcome',2,'Learning outcome 1','LO1. Apply and analyse project management methodologies, frameworks and knowledge areas for planning across the project lifecycle.','lo1. apply and analyse project management methodologies, frameworks and knowledge areas for planning across the project lifecycle.','learning_outcome:LO01'),(1926,58,'LO02','learning_outcome',3,'Learning outcome 2','LO2. Evaluate formal and adaptive project management practices, considering their guiding principles and processes.','lo2. evaluate formal and adaptive project management practices, considering their guiding principles and processes.','learning_outcome:LO02'),(1927,58,'LO03','learning_outcome',4,'Learning outcome 3','LO3. Evaluate and critically analyse the factors affecting various project stakeholders and team processes.','lo3. evaluate and critically analyse the factors affecting various project stakeholders and team processes.','learning_outcome:LO03'),(1928,58,'LO04','learning_outcome',5,'Learning outcome 4','LO4. Create and critically reflect on project planning by applying relevant project management techniques.','lo4. create and critically reflect on project planning by applying relevant project management techniques.','learning_outcome:LO04'),(1929,58,'LO05','learning_outcome',6,'Learning outcome 5','LO5. Identify and critically assess project challenges, success factors and the applicability of formal project management frameworks.','lo5. identify and critically assess project challenges, success factors and the applicability of formal project management frameworks.','learning_outcome:LO05'),(1930,58,'AS01','assessment',7,'Individual assignment 2 Written task','Type: Written work. Description: Individual assignment 2 Written task','type: written work. description: individual assignment 2 written task','assessment:AS01'),(1931,58,'AS02','assessment',8,'Individual assignment 1 Written tasks completed in tutorials','Type: In-person written or creative task. Description: Individual assignment 1 Written tasks completed in tutorials','type: in-person written or creative task. description: individual assignment 1 written tasks completed in tutorials','assessment:AS02'),(1932,58,'AS03','assessment',9,'Class Quizzes Online quizzes','Type: Out-of-class quiz. Description: Class Quizzes Online quizzes','type: out-of-class quiz. description: class quizzes online quizzes','assessment:AS03'),(1933,58,'AS04','assessment',10,'Group Project Assignment Written task','Type: Written work. Description: Group Project Assignment Written task','type: written work. description: group project assignment written task','assessment:AS04'),(1934,58,'AD01','assessment_description',11,'Assessment description 1','Class Quizzes: Three (3) online quizzes in weeks 3, 9, and 12; they are due on Friday at 23:59 each week. These quizzes focus on the fundamental concepts and applied knowledge acquired in the unit (from lectures, tutorials and readings). These tasks will be Canvas Quizzes with various question types. Students will be assessed based on the correctness of their answers in the quizzes.','class quizzes: three (3) online quizzes in weeks 3, 9, and 12; they are due on friday at 23:59 each week. these quizzes focus on the fundamental concepts and applied knowledge acquired in the unit (from lectures, tutorials and readings). these tasks will be canvas quizzes with various question types. students will be assessed based on the correctness of their answers in the quizzes.','assessment_description:AD01'),(1935,58,'AD02','assessment_description',12,'Assessment description 2','Individual Assignment 1: This secure written assignment is completed during the tutorials in weeks 4, 5 and 6. Students will assume the role of a project manager and engage with a supplied business case study. Students will discuss the key lessons learned from a project regarding project management knowledge and whether a systematic approach would have helped. This assignment will initially be completed during the tutorial, and at the end of each tutorial, before students leave, images of students\' work will be captured to ensure the security of the assessment.','individual assignment 1: this secure written assignment is completed during the tutorials in weeks 4, 5 and 6. students will assume the role of a project manager and engage with a supplied business case study. students will discuss the key lessons learned from a project regarding project management knowledge and whether a systematic approach would have helped. this assignment will initially be completed during the tutorial, and at the end of each tutorial, before students leave, images of students\' work will be captured to ensure the security of the assessment.','assessment_description:AD02'),(1936,58,'AD03','assessment_description',13,'Assessment description 3','Individual Assignment 2: This assignment will require you to integrate information from lectures and tutorials. Students will be required to critically reflect on their self-regulated learning in the group project, research project management concepts and practices, and prepare a concise analytical report.','individual assignment 2: this assignment will require you to integrate information from lectures and tutorials. students will be required to critically reflect on their self-regulated learning in the group project, research project management concepts and practices, and prepare a concise analytical report.','assessment_description:AD03'),(1937,58,'AD04','assessment_description',14,'Assessment description 4','Group Project Assignment: This assignment employs an interactive simulation of a Project Management scenario. Using Team-based learning (TBL) and Project-based learning (PBL), group-based activities are designed to help students acquire higher-level learning skills in this context, including creativity, lateral and reflective thinking, problem-solving, and critical analysis. In this assignment, students are to design and develop a detailed project with supporting documentation and rationale for the business project.','group project assignment: this assignment employs an interactive simulation of a project management scenario. using team-based learning (tbl) and project-based learning (pbl), group-based activities are designed to help students acquire higher-level learning skills in this context, including creativity, lateral and reflective thinking, problem-solving, and critical analysis. in this assignment, students are to design and develop a detailed project with supporting documentation and rationale for the business project.','assessment_description:AD04'),(1938,58,'AD05','assessment_description',15,'Assessment description 5','Detailed instructions for assessments will be available on Canvas.','detailed instructions for assessments will be available on canvas.','assessment_description:AD05'),(1939,58,'WK01','weekly_schedule',16,'Week 01: Introduction to Project Management [online recorded lecture + on-campus tutorial]','Introduction to Project Management [online recorded lecture + on-campus tutorial]. Learning activity: Lecture (1.5 hr)','introduction to project management [online recorded lecture + on-campus tutorial]. learning activity: lecture (1.5 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK01'),(1940,58,'WK02','weekly_schedule',17,'Week 01: Introduction to Project Management [online recorded lecture + on-campus tutorial]','Introduction to Project Management [online recorded lecture + on-campus tutorial]. Learning activity: Tutorial (1.5 hr)','introduction to project management [online recorded lecture + on-campus tutorial]. learning activity: tutorial (1.5 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK02'),(1941,58,'WK03','weekly_schedule',18,'Week 02: The Value of Project Management [online recorded lecture + on-campus tutorial]','The Value of Project Management [online recorded lecture + on-campus tutorial]. Learning activity: Lecture (1.5 hr)','the value of project management [online recorded lecture + on-campus tutorial]. learning activity: lecture (1.5 hr)','weekly_schedule:WK03'),(19