ons.','this unit bridges the gap between theory and practice by integrating the knowledge and key skills developed across the digital business or business information systems specialisation. it provides students with a practical teamwork experience to identify, analyse, and solve contemporary problems by exploring the socio-technical ecosystem in which a digital business operates. this experiential learning opportunity enhances students\' career-readiness by consolidating their professional skills and ability to apply the business information systems knowledge in authentic situations.','overview:OV01'),(2079,62,'LO01','learning_outcome',2,'Learning outcome 1','LO1. Apply advanced principles and theories related to digital business and information systems in the context of an actual business organisation','lo1. apply advanced principles and theories related to digital business and information systems in the context of an actual business organisation','learning_outcome:LO01'),(2080,62,'LO02','learning_outcome',3,'Learning outcome 2','LO2. Analyse open-ended business scenarios and evaluate the implications of digital technologies for business','lo2. analyse open-ended business scenarios and evaluate the implications of digital technologies for business','learning_outcome:LO02'),(2081,62,'LO03','learning_outcome',4,'Learning outcome 3','LO3. Apply techniques for organisational and business process analyses to resolve an actual business problem','lo3. apply techniques for organisational and business process analyses to resolve an actual business problem','learning_outcome:LO03'),(2082,62,'LO04','learning_outcome',5,'Learning outcome 4','LO4. Communicate in a professional and confident manner, both orally and in writing, with actual business professionals','lo4. communicate in a professional and confident manner, both orally and in writing, with actual business professionals','learning_outcome:LO04'),(2083,62,'LO05','learning_outcome',6,'Learning outcome 5','LO5. Apply te