n Planning\", \"activity\": \"Seminar (3 hr)\", \"learning_outcomes\": \"LO1 LO2 LO3 LO4 LO5 LO6\"}, {\"week\": \"Week 11\", \"topic\": \"Presentation Planning\", \"activity\": \"Seminar (3 hr)\", \"learning_outcomes\": \"LO1 LO2 LO3 LO4 LO5 LO6\"}, {\"week\": \"Week 12\", \"topic\": \"Boardroom Presentation\", \"activity\": \"Seminar (3 hr)\", \"learning_outcomes\": \"LO1 LO2 LO3 LO4 LO5 LO6\"}, {\"week\": \"Week 13\", \"topic\": \"Review & Closure\", \"activity\": \"Seminar (3 hr)\", \"learning_outcomes\": \"LO1 LO2 LO3 LO4 LO5 LO6\"}], \"learning_outcomes\": [\"LO1. Apply advanced principles and theories related to digital business and information systems in the context of an actual business organisation\", \"LO2. Analyse open-ended business scenarios and evaluate the implications of digital technologies for business\", \"LO3. Apply techniques for organisational and business process analyses to resolve an actual business problem\", \"LO4. Communicate in a professional and confident manner, both orally and in writing, with actual business professionals\", \"LO5. Apply team management concepts and theories to effectively work in, and manage, cross-functional teams\", \"LO6. Analyse and reflect critically on the ethical and social implications of digital business\"]}'),(2,2,'archive-import-v1','baseline-v1','2026-09-11 04:52:39.572842','Digital Business Innovation','{\"level\": \"UG\", \"details\": {\"Academic unit\": \"Business Information Systems\", \"Credit points\": \"6\", \"Corequisites ?\": \"None\", \"Prohibitions ?\": \"ISYS1003 or INFO1000\", \"Prerequisites ?\": \"None\", \"Assumed knowledge ?\": \"None\", \"Available to study abroad and exchange students\": \"Yes\"}, \"session\": \"Semester 2, 2026 [Normal day] - Camperdown/Darlington, Sydney\", \"overview\": [\"The Digital Economy, with its focus on information as a key business resource, has changed the way Business Information Systems (BIS) is viewed in organisations. BIS are now seen as enablers of innovation in which people, supported by powerful technology, are considered to be the most important component. This is because problem-solving, innovation and critical thinking skills cannot be outsourced or easily acquired by competitors. This unit is designed to develop your understanding of how businesses operate. It shows how information systems support business operations and management through integration of people, business processes and systems. You will be provided with an introduction to state-of-the-art business analysis techniques, frameworks and models to assist in understanding the nature and contribution of BIS in a range of business contexts. With its emphasis on business rather than IT, this unit does not require prior IT-related experience. In this unit, you will learn about the increasingly important role of IT in business and acquire valuable business analysis and problem-solving skills.\"], \"unit_code\": \"INFS1000\", \"source_url\": \"https://www.sydney.edu.au/units/INFS1000/2026-S2C-ND-CC\", \"unit_title\": \"Digital Business Innovation\", \"assessments\": [{\"due\": \"Formal exam period\", \"type\": \"Written exam\", \"length\": \"2 hours\", \"weight\": \"35%\", \"description\": \"Final exam Written exam\"}, {\"due\": \"Multiple weeks\", \"type\": \"Practical skill\", \"length\": \"n/a\", \"weight\": \"10%\", \"description\": \"Weekly Homework Practical task\"}, {\"due\": \"Week 03\", \"type\": \"Out-of-class quiz\", \"length\": \"10-minutes\", \"weight\": \"10%\", \"description\": \"Early Feedback Task #EarlyFeedbackTask\"}, {\"due\": \"Week 07 Due date: 20 Sep 2026 at 12:10\", \"type\": \"Written test\", \"length\": \"1 hour\", \"weight\": \"20%\", \"description\": \"Mid-semester exam Written exam\"}, {\"due\": \"Week 12 Due date: 30 Oct 2026 at 17:00 Closing date: 06 Nov 2026\", \"type\": \"Written work\", \"length\": \"3000 words\", \"weight\": \"25%\", \"description\": \"Group project Project report\"}], \"retrieved_at\": \"2026-09-01T03:39:01.063300+00:00\", \"selection_rule\": \"Prefer Semester 2; otherwise Semester 1; otherwise first published 2026 outline.\", \"weekly_schedule\": [{\"week\": \"Week 01\", \"topic\": \"Unit overview and introduction to information systems\", \"activity\": \"Seminar (2 hr)\", \"learning_outcomes\": \"LO1\"}, {\"week\": \"Week 02\", \"topic\": \"Introduction to business processes\", \"activity\": \"Seminar (2 hr)\", \"learning_outcomes\": \"LO1 LO2\"}, {\"week\": \"Week 02\", \"topic\": \"Introduction to business processes\", \"activity\": \"Tutorial (1 hr)\", \"learning_outcomes\": \"LO1 LO2\"}, {\"week\": \"Week 03\", \"topic\": \"Strategy and competitive advantage\", \"activity\": \"Seminar (2 hr)\", \"learning_outcomes\": \"LO1 LO6 LO7\"}, {\"week\": \"Week 03\", \"topic\": \"Strategy and competitive advantage\", \"activity\": \"Tutorial (1 hr)\", \"learning_outcomes\": \"LO1 LO6 LO7\"}, {\"week\": \"Week 04\", \"topic\": \"Databases and information design\", \"activity\": \"Seminar (2 hr)\", \"learning_outcomes\": \"LO2 LO4 LO6\"}, {\"week\": \"Week 04\", \"topic\": \"Databases and information design\", \"activity\": \"Tutorial (1 hr)\", \"learning_outcomes\": \"LO2 LO4 LO6\"}, {\"week\": \"Week 05\", \"topic\": \"Data modelling\", \"activity\": \"Seminar (2 hr)\", \"learning_outcomes\": \"LO2 LO4 LO6\"}, {\"week\": \"Week 05\", \"topic\": \"Data modelling\", \"activity\": \"Tutorial (1 hr)\", \"learning_outcomes\": \"LO2 LO4 LO6\"}, {\"week\": \"Week 06\", \"topic\": \"Business information systems ethics\", \"activity\": \"Seminar (2 hr)\", \"learning_outcomes\": \"LO5 LO6 LO7\"}, {\"week\": \"Week 06\", \"topic\": \"Business information systems ethics\", \"activity\": \"Tutorial (1 hr)\", \"learning_outcomes\": \"LO5 LO6 LO7\"}, {\"week\": \"Week 07\", \"topic\": \"Business process management\", \"activity\": \"Seminar (2 hr)\", \"learning_outcomes\": \"LO1 LO2 LO3 LO6 LO7\"}, {\"week\": \"Week 07\", \"topic\": \"Business process management\", \"activity\": \"Tutorial (1 hr)\", \"learning_outcomes\": \"LO1 LO2 LO3 LO6 LO7\"}, {\"week\": \"Week 08\", \"topic\": \"Business process modelling (BPMN)\", \"activity\": \"Seminar (2 hr)\", \"learning_outcomes\": \"LO1 LO2 LO3 LO6 LO7\"}, {\"week\": \"Week 08\", \"topic\": \"Business process modelling (BPMN)\", \"activity\": \"Tutorial (1 hr)\", \"learning_outcomes\": \"LO1 LO2 LO3 LO6 LO7\"}, {\"week\": \"Week 09\", \"topic\": \"Project consultation\", \"activity\": \"Tutorial (1 hr)\", \"learning_outcomes\": \"LO1 LO6\"}, {\"week\": \"Week 10\", \"topic\": \"Business process analysis and improvement\", \"activity\": \"Seminar (2 hr)\", \"learning_outcomes\": \"LO1 LO2 LO3 LO6 LO7\"}, {\"week\": \"Week 10\", \"topic\": \"Business process analysis and improvement\", \"activity\": \"Tutorial (1 hr)\", \"learning_outcomes\": \"LO1 LO2 LO3 LO6 LO7\"}, {\"week\": \"Week 11\", \"topic\": \"Cybersecurity\", \"activity\": \"Seminar (2 hr)\", \"learning_outcomes\": \"LO1 LO6\"}, {\"week\": \"Week 11\", \"topic\": \"Cybersecurity\", \"activity\": \"Tutorial (1 hr)\", \"learning_outcomes\": \"LO1 LO6\"}, {\"week\": \"Week 12\", \"topic\": \"Business intelligence systems\", \"activity\": \"Seminar (2 hr)\", \"learning_outcomes\": \"LO1 LO6\"}, {\"week\": \"Week 12\", \"topic\": \"Business intelligence systems\", \"activity\": \"Tutorial (1 hr)\", \"learning_outcomes\": \"LO1 LO6\"}, {\"week\": \"Week 13\", \"topic\": \"Exam briefing and unit review\", \"activity\": \"Seminar (2 hr)\", \"learning_outcomes\": \"LO1 LO6\"}], \"learning_outcomes\": [\"LO1. make judgments about ways in which Information Technology can enable innovation and improvement in business\", \"LO2. demonstrate basic business analysis skills, such as strategic analysis, data modelling, and business process modelling\", \"LO3. create and understand visual representations of business processes using BPMN notation, as well as basic data models as the basis for information systems design\", \"LO4. create databases in MS Access software\", \"LO5. understand and address basic issues pertaining to information ethics\", \"LO6. work as an effective team in a problem-solving environment\", \"LO7. display an understanding of business design in an end-to-end manner from business idea to business execution.\"], \"assessment_summary\": [\"Group work: Team-based learning (TBL) is a set of group-based activities designed to help students to acquire higher-level learning skills in this context, including creativity, lateral and reflective thinking, problem-solving and critical analysis as well as the applied and experiential BIS knowledge. This assessment component will consider group homework preparation for the TBL sessions as well as their work and participation in, and outcomes of collaborative in-class activities in finalising their homework submissions. The TBL activity sheets will be uploaded on Canvas.\", \"Early Feedback Task: The objective of this task is to focus on the fundamental concepts, and applied knowledge acquired in sessions 1-3. This task will be in the form of a Canvas Quiz with multiple choice questions.\", \"Group project report: The objective of this task is to use the knowledge and practical skills acquired in this unit of study to investigate and solve a real-life business problem. Students are expected to create and describe their own business idea for a pre-defined scenario, which they will receive through Canvas.\", \"Mid-semester exam: This exam will focus on the fundamental concepts, and applied and experiential knowledge acquired in weeks 1-6 of the unit. Note: This assessment will take the form of a supervised exam. It is a closed-book exam with no materials allowed.\", \"Final exam: This exam will focus on the fundamental concepts, and applied and experiential knowledge acquired in weeks 1-12, including the practical assignment. Note: This assessment will take the form of a supervised exam. It is a closed-book exam with no materials allowed.\", \"Detailed information for each assessment can be found on Canvas.\"], \"available_2026_outlines\": [\"https://www.sydney.edu.au/units/INFS1000/2026-S1C-ND-CC\", \"https://www.sydney.edu.au/units/INFS1000/2026-S2C-ND-CC\"]}'),(3,3,'archive-import-v1','baseline-v1','2026-09-11 04:52:39.617977','Working in Digital Ecosystems','{\"level\": \"UG\", \"details\": {\"Academic unit\": \"Business Information Systems\", \"Credit points\": \"6\", \"Corequisites ?\": \"None\", \"Prohibitions ?\": \"None\", \"Prerequisites ?\": \"None\", \"Assumed knowledge ?\": \"INFS1000 or INFO1000 or INFO1003 or INFO1903\", \"Available to study abroad and exchange students\": \"Yes\"}, \"session\": \"Semester 2, 2026 [Normal day] - Camperdown/Darlington, Sydney\", \"overview\": [\"Digital ecosystems (such as social media, blockchain, technology platforms, artificial intelligence, big data, people analytics, and cybersecurity) fundamentally change the way we collect and present ideas, communicate, and work together. In this unit, students are introduced to various digital ecosystems and their implications for how work is done. Students learn about how employers recruit graduates online, what it is like to join and work in a modern, digital workplace, and the tensions that arise when traditional, structured workplaces are transformed through digital, flexible, and networked ways of working. Students engage in hands-on activities to acquire skills for how to present themselves effectively and professionally online (personal branding), how to communicate in digital channels in an organisational context (professional communication), how to effectively search for and work with digital information (data literacy), and how to digitally coordinate work in teams.\"], \"unit_code\": \"INFS1020\", \"source_url\": \"https://www.sydney.edu.au/units/INFS1020/2026-S2C-ND-CC\", \"unit_title\": \"Working in Digital Ecosystems\", \"assessments\": [{\"due\": \"Formal exam period\", \"type\": \"Written exam\", \"length\": \"2 hours\", \"weight\": \"40%\", \"description\": \"Final exam Final exam\"}, {\"due\": \"Week 03 Due date: 21 Aug 2026 at 13:00 Closing date: 21 Aug 2026\", \"type\": \"Out-of-class quiz\", \"length\": \"Maximum 10 mins\", \"weight\": \"10%\", \"description\": \"Individual Quiz Individual Quiz: Based on first three week topics\"}, {\"due\": \"Week 06 Due date: 07 Sep 2026 at 23:59 Closing date: 20 Sep 2026\", \"type\": \"Presentation\", \"length\": \"3 min. video + support documents\", \"weight\": \"25%\", \"description\": \"Individual assignment Individual Assignment: Develop a social media strategy\"}, {\"due\": \"Week 11 Due date: 19 Oct 2026 at 23:59 Closing date: 28 Oct 2026\", \"type\": \"Presentation\", \"length\": \"10 min. presentation + support documents\", \"weight\": \"25%\", \"description\": \"Group assignment Group Assignment: Develop a digital consulting strategy\"}], \"retrieved_at\": \"2026-09-01T03:39:01.055245+00:00\", \"selection_rule\": \"Prefer Semester 2; otherwise Semester 1; otherwise first published 2026 outline.\", \"weekly_schedule\": [{\"week\": \"Week 01\", \"topic\": \"Introduction and administration\", \"activity\": \"Lecture (1.5 hr)\", \"learning_outcomes\": \"LO1 LO2 LO3 LO4 LO5\"}, {\"week\": \"Week 01\", \"topic\": \"Introduction and administration\", \"activity\": \"Tutorial (1.5 hr)\", \"learning_outcomes\": \"LO1 LO2 LO3 LO4 LO5\"}, {\"week\": \"Week 02\", \"topic\": \"Digital literacy 1 - Literacy and knowledge\", \"activity\": \"Lecture (1.5 hr)\", \"learning_outcomes\": \"LO1 LO2 LO4\"}, {\"week\": \"Week 02\", \"topic\": \"Digital literacy 1 - Literacy and knowledge\", \"activity\": \"Tutorial (1.5 hr)\", \"learning_outcomes\": \"LO1 LO2 LO4\"}, {\"week\": \"Week 03\", \"topic\": \"Digital literacy 2 - Research and search\", \"activity\": \"Lecture (1.5 hr)\", \"learning_outcomes\": \"LO1 LO2 LO4\"}, {\"week\": \"Week 03\", \"topic\": \"Digital literacy 2 - Research and search\", \"activity\": \"Tutorial (1.5 hr)\", \"learning