outcomes\": \"LO1 LO2 LO5\"}, {\"week\": \"Week 10\", \"topic\": \"Digital Platforms 1 - Blockchain Foundations\", \"activity\": \"Lecture (1.5 hr)\", \"learning_outcomes\": \"LO1 LO2 LO5\"}, {\"week\": \"Week 10\", \"topic\": \"Digital Platforms 1 - Blockchain Foundations\", \"activity\": \"Tutorial (1.5 hr)\", \"learning_outcomes\": \"LO1 LO2 LO5\"}, {\"week\": \"Week 11\", \"topic\": \"Digital Platforms 2 - Blockchain Implications for Business and Society\", \"activity\": \"Lecture (1.5 hr)\", \"learning_outcomes\": \"LO1 LO2 LO5\"}, {\"week\": \"Week 11\", \"topic\": \"Digital Platforms 2 - Blockchain Implications for Business and Society\", \"activity\": \"Tutorial (1.5 hr)\", \"learning_outcomes\": \"LO1 LO2 LO5\"}, {\"week\": \"Week 12\", \"topic\": \"Digital Ecosystems\", \"activity\": \"Lecture (1.5 hr)\", \"learning_outcomes\": \"LO1 LO2 LO5\"}, {\"week\": \"Week 12\", \"topic\": \"Digital Ecosystems\", \"activity\": \"Tutorial (1.5 hr)\", \"learning_outcomes\": \"LO1 LO2 LO5\"}, {\"week\": \"Week 13\", \"topic\": \"Unit review and exam preparation\", \"activity\": \"Lecture (1.5 hr)\", \"learning_outcomes\": \"LO1 LO2 LO3 LO4 LO5\"}, {\"week\": \"Week 13\", \"topic\": \"Unit review and exam preparation\", \"activity\": \"Tutorial (1.5 hr)\", \"learning_outcomes\": \"LO1 LO2 LO3 LO4 LO5\"}], \"learning_outcomes\": [\"LO1. understand how digital technology changes work environments and how work is organised\", \"LO2. demonstrate critical discernment of popular claims about the future of work and the role of technology in this transformation process\", \"LO3. communicate ideas effectively using digital online technology and audiovisual elements\", \"LO4. make judgements about the effective use of digital technologies for purposes of self-presentation online\", \"LO5. appreciate the complexities of working with others effectively in a digital work environment.\"], \"assessment_summary\": [\"Individual Quiz: This quiz will assess your knowledge gained in the first three weeks.\", \"Individual assignment: Develop a social media strategy. More details will be provided by the lecturer and discussed in class.\", \"Group assignment: Develop a digital consulting strategy. More details will be provided by the lecturer and discussed in class.\", \"Final exam: This exam will assess your knowledge and abilities gained in all parts of the unit. Students will be assessed in a Bring Your Own Device (BYOD) exam taken on campus with supervision. Further information about the delivery of the exams will be provided closer to the test exam.\", \"None of the assignments in this unit are eligible for simple extensions. Detailed information for each assessment can be found on Canvas.\"], \"available_2026_outlines\": [\"https://www.sydney.edu.au/units/INFS1020/2026-S1C-ND-CC\", \"https://www.sydney.edu.au/units/INFS1020/2026-S2C-ND-CC\"]}'),(4,4,'archive-import-v1','baseline-v1','2026-09-11 04:52:39.660647','Digital Ethics and Compassionate Innovation','{\"level\": \"UG\", \"details\": {\"Academic unit\": \"Business Information Systems\", \"Credit points\": \"6\", \"Corequisites ?\": \"None\", \"Prohibitions ?\": \"None\", \"Prerequisites ?\": \"None\", \"Assumed knowledge ?\": \"INFS1000 or INFS1020 or INFO1000 or INFO1003 or INFO1903\", \"Available to study abroad and exchange students\": \"Yes\"}, \"session\": \"Semester 2, 2026 [Normal day] - Camperdown/Darlington, Sydney\", \"overview\": [\"The rapid evolution and widespread adoption of digital technologies are transforming societies, economies, and the environment. These transformations bring significant benefits but also pose serious risks of harm, particularly for vulnerable and marginalised stakeholders, requiring a balanced approach that genuinely serves the common good. This unit unpacks the ethical dilemmas of sociotechnical change, exploring how digital technologies like artificial intelligence, blockchain, and social media impact privacy, equity, democracy, dignity, business, the environment, and more. Guided by compassion as a foundational principle, students will critically examine the ambiguous and pluralistic nature of digital innovations, developing the skills to manage ethical dilemmas and promote responsible digital innovation for the common good. The course integrates ethical theories with recent practical case studies, equipping students to address contemporary ethical dilemmas in today\'s digital world.\"], \"unit_code\": \"INFS2010\", \"source_url\": \"https://www.sydney.edu.au/units/INFS2010/2026-S2C-ND-CC\", \"unit_title\": \"Digital Ethics and Compassionate Innovation\", \"assessments\": [{\"due\": \"Week 03 Due date: 19 Aug 2026 at 23:59 Closing date: 13 Sep 2026\", \"type\": \"Written work\", \"length\": \"600 words\", \"weight\": \"5%\", \"description\": \"GenAI Strategy Plan and critically reflect on using GenAI and how it affects learning.\"}, {\"due\": \"Week 06 Due date: 09 Sep 2026 at 23:59 Closing date: 30 Sep 2026\", \"type\": \"Written work\", \"length\": \"1500 words\", \"weight\": \"30%\", \"description\": \"Individual assignment Written report\"}, {\"due\": \"Week 12 Due date: 30 Oct 2026 at 23:59 Closing date: 30 Nov 2026\", \"type\": \"Interactive oral\", \"length\": \"3 slides / 5 minutes\", \"weight\": \"5%\", \"description\": \"Group Assignment / Business Presentation Slides and Oral presentation\"}, {\"due\": \"Week 13 Due date: 06 Nov 2026 at 23:59 Closing date: 30 Nov 2026\", \"type\": \"Portfolio or journal\", \"length\": \"1500 words\", \"weight\": \"30%\", \"description\": \"Reflective Journal Individual reflective learning journal, stimulated by prompts.\"}, {\"due\": \"Week 13 Due date: 06 Nov 2026 at 23:59 Closing date: 30 Nov 2026\", \"type\": \"Written work\", \"length\": \"3000 words\", \"weight\": \"30%\", \"description\": \"Group Assignment / Business Report Written report\"}], \"retrieved_at\": \"2026-09-01T03:39:01.025779+00:00\", \"selection_rule\": \"Prefer Semester 2; otherwise Semester 1; otherwise first published 2026 outline.\", \"weekly_schedule\": [{\"week\": \"Week 01\", \"topic\": \"Unit introduction\", \"activity\": \"Lecture (1.5 hr)\", \"learning_outcomes\": \"LO1 LO2 LO3 LO4 LO5\"}, {\"week\": \"Week 01\", \"topic\": \"Warm-Up & Individual Assignment Prep\", \"activity\": \"Tutorial (1.5 hr)\", \"learning_outcomes\": \"LO1 LO2 LO3 LO4 LO5\"}, {\"week\": \"Week 02\", \"topic\": \"The Big Picture: Compassionate Digital Innovation\", \"activity\": \"Lecture (1.5 hr)\", \"learning_outcomes\": \"LO1 LO2\"}, {\"week\": \"Week 02\", \"topic\": \"Selecting Evidence\", \"activity\": \"Tutorial (1.5 hr)\", \"learning_outcomes\": \"LO1 LO2\"}, {\"week\": \"Week 03\", \"topic\": \"Digital Harm Analysis\", \"activity\": \"Lecture (1.5 hr)\", \"learning_outcomes\": \"LO1 LO2\"}, {\"week\": \"Week 03\", \"topic\": \"Analysing Evidence\", \"activity\": \"Tutorial (1.5 hr)\", \"learning_outcomes\": \"LO1 LO2\"}, {\"week\": \"Week 04\", \"topic\": \"Ambivalent Affordances of Digital Technologies\", \"activity\": \"Lecture (1.5 hr)\", \"learning_outcomes\": \"LO1 LO2\"}, {\"week\": \"Week 04\", \"topic\": \"Privacy vs Security\", \"activity\": \"Tutorial (1.5 hr)\", \"learning_outcomes\": \"LO1 LO2 LO3\"}, {\"week\": \"Week 05\", \"topic\": \"Ethical Paradoxes of Sociotechnical Change\", \"activity\": \"Lecture (1.5 hr)\", \"learning_outcomes\": \"LO1 LO2 LO3\"}, {\"week\": \"Week 05\", \"topic\": \"Group Assignment Prep\", \"activity\": \"Tutorial (1.5 hr)\", \"learning_outcomes\": \"LO1 LO2 LO4\"}, {\"week\": \"Week 06\", \"topic\": \"Compassion: A Timely and Timeless Moral Guide\", \"activity\": \"Lecture (1.5 hr)\", \"learning_outcomes\": \"LO3 LO4 LO5\"}, {\"week\": \"Week 06\", \"topic\": \"Bust Your Own Bias\", \"activity\": \"Tutorial (1.5 hr)\", \"learning_outcomes\": \"LO3 LO4 LO5\"}, {\"week\": \"Week 07\", \"topic\": \"Case Study: Responsible Social Media Use\", \"activity\": \"Lecture (1.5 hr)\", \"learning_outcomes\": \"LO1 LO2 LO3 LO5\"}, {\"week\": \"Week 07\", \"topic\": \"Designing Responsibility Nudges\", \"activity\": \"Tutorial (1.5 hr)\", \"learning_outcomes\": \"LO1 LO2 LO3 LO5\"}, {\"week\": \"Week 08\", \"topic\": \"Case Study: Compassionate Web3 Governance\", \"activity\": \"Lecture (1.5 hr)\", \"learning_outcomes\": \"LO1 LO2 LO3 LO4 LO5\"}, {\"week\": \"Week 08\", \"topic\": \"Presenting Evidence\", \"activity\": \"Tutorial (1.5 hr)\", \"learning_outcomes\": \"LO1 LO2 LO3 LO4 LO5\"}, {\"week\": \"Week 09\", \"topic\": \"Case Study: Human-AI Companionship\", \"activity\": \"Lecture (1.5 hr)\", \"learning_outcomes\": \"LO1 LO2 LO5\"}, {\"week\": \"Week 09\", \"topic\": \"Sensitive Issues in Sociotechnical Systems\", \"activity\": \"Tutorial (1.5 hr)\", \"learning_outcomes\": \"LO1 LO2 LO5\"}, {\"week\": \"Week 10\", \"topic\": \"Developing Employability\", \"activity\": \"Lecture (1.5 hr)\", \"learning_outcomes\": \"LO1 LO2 LO5\"}, {\"week\": \"Week 10\", \"topic\": \"Developing Your Employability\", \"activity\": \"Tutorial (1.5 hr)\", \"learning_outcomes\": \"LO1 LO2 LO5\"}, {\"week\": \"Week 11\", \"topic\": \"Open Topic / Guest Lecture\", \"activity\": \"Lecture (1.5 hr)\", \"learning_outcomes\": \"LO1 LO2 LO3\"}, {\"week\": \"Week 11\", \"topic\": \"Reflection on common issues in assignments\", \"activity\": \"Tutorial (1.5 hr)\", \"learning_outcomes\": \"LO1 LO2 LO5\"}, {\"week\": \"Week 12\", \"topic\": \"Unit Review and Debrief\", \"activity\": \"Lecture (1.5 hr)\", \"learning_outcomes\": \"LO1 LO2 LO3 LO4 LO5\"}, {\"week\": \"Week 12\", \"topic\": \"Group Project Presentations\", \"activity\": \"Tutorial (1.5 hr)\", \"learning_outcomes\": \"LO1 LO2 LO3 LO4 LO5\"}, {\"week\": \"Week 13\", \"topic\": \"Open Topic / Guest Lecture\", \"activity\": \"Lecture (1.5 hr)\", \"learning_outcomes\": \"LO1 LO2 LO3 LO4 LO5\"}, {\"week\": \"Week 13\", \"topic\": \"Reflection Workshop\", \"activity\": \"Tutorial (1.5 hr)\", \"learning_outcomes\": \"LO1 LO2 LO3 LO4 LO5\"}], \"learning_outcomes\": [\"LO1. Analyse the ethical challenges and paradoxes associated with digital innovations.\", \"LO2. Critically evaluate the societal, economic, and environmental impacts of digital technologies, considering both benefits and harms.\", \"LO3. Apply ethical frameworks and theories to navigate and resolve ethical dilemmas in digital innovation.\", \"LO4. Communicate and collaborate effectively on ethical issues in diverse professional contexts.\", \"LO5. Make informed decisions that balance technological progress with societal well-being and ethical integrity.\"], \"assessment_summary\": [\"Individual assignment: This assignment aims to assist students’ development as an independent learner of the knowledge and skills acquired in this unit. Students are to select, analyse and submit a brief business report on a news item for a specific company relevant to this unit.\", \"Group project report: The group project is an applied project aimed at assessing the knowledge acquired in this unit of study. Students will be required to demonstrate their critical thinking and analytical skills to analyse and recommend improvements to real-world businesses.\", \"Group project presentation: The group project presentations are aimed at assessing the level of knowledge acquired in this unit of study. All group members must actively participate in the presentation.\", \"Reflective journal: Individual continuous, reflective journal about the student’s authentic learning experience gleaned from the group project and the in-class activities. While the submission is due in W13, students are encouraged to reflect on weekly prompts by the teaching team, and can discuss their reflections in the weekly consultations. The final deliverable is a written reflective journal of 1500 words (± 10%).\", \"Generative AI Strategy: By developing a clear strategy for using GenAI tools in assignment work, students will enhance their ability to leverage GenAI for tasks such as identifying literature, structuring ideas, refining text, and fact-checking while ensuring ethical and effective practices. The goal is not just to ensure academic integrity but also to reflect on how GenAI tools shape analytical and critical thinking skills. The deliverable is a 600 word (± 10%) document.\", \"Detailed information for each assessment can be found on Canvas.\"], \"available_2026_outlines\": [\"https://www.sydney.edu.au/units/INFS2010/2026-S2C-ND-CC\"]}'),(5,5,'archive-import-v1','baseline-v1','2026-09-11 04:52:39.705881','Digital Business Management','{\"level\": \"UG\", \"details\": {\"Academic unit\": \"Business Information Systems\", \"Credit points\": \"6\", \"Corequisites ?\": \"None\", \"Prohibitions ?\": \"None\", \"Prerequisites ?\": \"None\", \"Assumed knowledge ?\": \"INFS1000 or INFO1000 or INFO1003 or INFO1903\", \"Available to study abroad and exchange students\": \"Yes\"}, \"session\": \"Semester 1, 2026 [Normal day] - Camperdown/Darlington, Sydney\", \"overview\": [\"This unit will provide you with a detailed overview of the concepts and models used in doing business digitally via the Internet. These concepts and models will enable you to evaluate, synthesise and implement Internet-enabled business models. The unit will provide the critical link between the firm\'s performance and modern Internet technologies, such as e-Commerce platforms, Social Media and Social Networking. Emphasis will be put on the utilisation of Internet technologies to enable new forms of digital business, rather than on the technologies themselves. Assumed knowledge for this unit is INFS1000 or equivalent.\"], \"unit_code\": \"INFS2030\", \"source_url\": \"https://www.sydney.edu.au/units/INFS2030/2026-S1C-ND-CC\", \"unit_title\": \"Digital Business Management\", \"assessments\": [{\"due\": \"Formal exam period\", \"type\": \"Written exam\", \"length\": \"2 hours\", \"weight\": \"50%\", \"description\": \"Final exam Written exam with MCQ\"}, {\"due\": \"Week 03 Due date: 10 Mar 2026 at 14:00 Clo