 \"Week 06\", \"topic\": \"Prototyping and Storytelling\", \"activity\": \"Seminar (3 hr)\", \"learning_outcomes\": \"LO1 LO2 LO3 LO4 LO5 LO6\"}, {\"week\": \"Week 07\", \"topic\": \"Outsourcing and Automation\", \"activity\": \"Seminar (3 hr)\", \"learning_outcomes\": \"LO1 LO2 LO3\"}, {\"week\": \"Week 08\", \"topic\": \"IT Project Management\", \"activity\": \"Seminar (3 hr)\", \"learning_outcomes\": \"LO1 LO2 LO3 LO4\"}, {\"week\": \"Week 09\", \"topic\": \"Usability Engineering\", \"activity\": \"Seminar (3 hr)\", \"learning_outcomes\": \"LO1 LO2 LO3 LO4\"}, {\"week\": \"Week 10\", \"topic\": \"Design Ethics\", \"activity\": \"Seminar (3 hr)\", \"learning_outcomes\": \"LO1 LO2 LO4 LO5 LO6\"}, {\"week\": \"Week 11\", \"topic\": \"Scientific Writing\", \"activity\": \"Seminar (3 hr)\", \"learning_outcomes\": \"LO1 LO2 LO4 LO5 LO6\"}, {\"week\": \"Week 12\", \"topic\": \"Unit Review and Debriefing\", \"activity\": \"Seminar (3 hr)\", \"learning_outcomes\": \"LO1 LO2 LO3 LO4 LO5 LO6\"}, {\"week\": \"Week 13\", \"topic\": \"Project presentations\", \"activity\": \"Seminar (3 hr)\", \"learning_outcomes\": \"LO4\"}], \"learning_outcomes\": [\"LO1. apply and relate information systems theories and concepts in the context of an actual business problem with societal relevance\", \"LO2. analyse open-ended business scenarios and evaluate the implications of information systems decisions\", \"LO3. apply techniques for organisational and business process analyses to resolve an actual business problem\", \"LO4. communicate in a professional and confident manner, both orally and in writing, with actual business professionals\", \"LO5. apply team management concepts and theories to effectively work in, and manage, cross-functional teams\", \"LO6. analyse and reflect critically on the ethical and social implications of information systems.\"], \"assessment_summary\": [\"Individual assignment: This assignment is in the form of an individual progress report that corresponds to a specific section of the group project. The content of this report will vary depending on the student\'s designated role within the project team. The report comprises 1500 (± 10%) words and associated discussions during the group consultation sessions.\", \"Group assignment: This assessment item requires students to work within their project groups to analyse and provide recommendations for resolving a business problem of an actual client. Each project group will be expected to look for and acquire their own client, and design a technology-enabled solution that will improve a substantive business process of the client. The deliverables of the project include a 15 minute presentation and a project report of 6000 (± 10%) words.\", \"Reflective journal: Individual, continuous, reflective journal about the student’s authentic learning experience gleaned from the group project and the in-class activities. The student will draft the reflective journal continuously in Canvas and the teaching team will ask them 4-5 ‘provocative’ questions to prompt their critical reflection throughout the semester. The final deliverable is a written reflective journal of 1500 words (± 10%).\", \"Generative AI Strategy: By developing a clear strategy for using GenAI tools in assignment work, students will enhance their ability to leverage GenAI for tasks such as identifying literature, structuring ideas, refining text, and fact-checking while ensuring ethical and effective practices. The goal is not just to ensure academic integrity but also to reflect on how GenAI tools shape analytical and critical thinking skills. The deliverable is a 600 word (± 10%) document.\", \"Detailed information for each assessment can be found on Canvas.\"]}'),(44,44,'outline-v1','baseline-v1','2026-09-11 04:52:51.999789','Business Information Systems in Practice','{\"details\": {\"Academic unit\": \"Business Information Systems\", \"Credit points\": \"6\", \"Corequisites ?\": \"None\", \"Prohibitions ?\": \"None\"