al assignment: This assignment is in the form of an individual progress report that corresponds to a specific section of the group project. The content of this report will vary depending on the student\'s designated role within the project team. The report comprises 1500 (± 10%) words and associated discussions during the group consultation sessions.\", \"Group assignment: This assessment item requires students to work within their project groups to analyse and provide recommendations for resolving a business problem of an actual client. Each project group will be expected to look for and acquire their own client, and design a technology-enabled solution that will improve a substantive business process of the client. The deliverables of the project include a 15 minute presentation and a project report of 6000 (± 10%) words.\", \"Reflective journal: Individual, continuous, reflective journal about the student’s authentic learning experience gleaned from the group project and the in-class activities. The student will draft the reflective journal continuously in Canvas and the teaching team will ask them 4-5 ‘provocative’ questions to prompt their critical reflection throughout the semester. The final deliverable is a written reflective journal of 1500 words (± 10%).\", \"Generative AI Strategy: By developing a clear strategy for using GenAI tools in assignment work, students will enhance their ability to leverage GenAI for tasks such as identifying literature, structuring ideas, refining text, and fact-checking while ensuring ethical and effective practices. The goal is not just to ensure academic integrity but also to reflect on how GenAI tools shape analytical and critical thinking skills. The deliverable is a 600 word (± 10%) document.\", \"Detailed information for each assessment can be found on Canvas.\"]}'),(45,45,'outline-v1','baseline-v1','2026-09-11 04:52:52.513998','Foundation in Business Information Systems','{\"details\": {\"Academic unit\": \"Business Information Systems\", \"Credit points\": \"6\", \"Corequisites ?\": \"None\", \"Prohibitions ?\": \"INFS6001\", \"Prerequisites ?\": \"None\", \"Assumed knowledge ?\": \"None\", \"Available to study abroad and exchange students\": \"Yes\"}, \"session\": \"Semester 1, 2026 [Normal day] - Camperdown/Darlington, Sydney\", \"overview\": [\"This unit introduces students to the foundations of business information systems and the emerging strategic role of information and communication technologies (ICT) in transforming organisations. Students develop an understanding of how ICT come to matter to organisations as they disrupt, change and transform organisations and organisational processes. The unit covers systems issues, information literacy and use, and how various digital technologies work together to create an infrastructure for digital business and how technologies (such as social media) are disrupting \'business as usual\'. The role of information systems in capturing and distributing organisational knowledge and in enhancing decision-making is explored. Students gain an understanding of socio-technical networks, how information systems function, and how processes in organisations can be leveraged to create digital innovation and business transformation.\"], \"unit_code\": \"INFS5002\", \"source_url\": \"https://www.sydney.edu.au/units/INFS5002/2026-S1C-ND-CC\", \"unit_title\": \"Foundation in Business Information Systems\", \"assessments\": [{\"due\": \"Formal exam period Due date: 09 Jun 2026 at 23:59 Closing date: 19 Jun 2026\", \"type\": \"Written work\", \"length\": \"-\", \"weight\": \"30%\", \"description\": \"End of Semester Reflective Essay An end of semester reflection on the unit learning. For details see Canvas.\"}, {\"due\": \"Ongoing\", \"type\": \"Contribution\", \"length\": \"-\", \"weight\": \"10%\", \"description\": \"Participation Individual, see canvas for details\"}, {\"due\": \"Week 10 Due date: 04 May 2026 at 23:59 Closing date: 14 May 2026\", \"type\": \"Evaluation\", \"length\": \"-\", \"weight\": \"20%\", \"description\": \"Reflection on Group Work Provide and respond to feedback on the performance of team members.\"}, {\"due\": \"Week 13 Due date: 27 May 2026 at 23:59 Closing date: 06 Jun 2026\", \"type\": \"Portfolio or journal\", \"length\": \"-\", \"weight\": \"35%\", \"description\": \"Group Project Design proposal for system, with weekly formative submissions, see Canvas.\"}, {\"due\": \"Week 13 Due date: 29 May 2026 at 07:00 Closing date: 29 May 2026\", \"type\": \"Presentation\", \"length\": \"-\", \"weight\": \"5%\", \"description\": \"Group project Design proposal for system, with weekly formative submissions, see Canvas.\"}], \"retrieved_at\": \"2026-09-11T04:52:52.512355+00:00\", \"weekly_schedule\": [{\"week\": \"Week 01\", \"topic\": \"Introduction to Foundation in Digital Business; BIS as Technology\", \"activity\": \"Seminar (3 hr)\", \"learning_outcomes\": \"LO1 LO2 LO3 LO4 LO5 LO6\"}, {\"week\": \"Week 02\", \"topic\": \"BIS as Disruption; BIS as Transformation; BIS as Project\", \"activity\": \"Seminar (3 hr)\", \"learning_outcomes\": \"LO1 LO2 LO3 LO4 LO5 LO6\"}, {\"week\": \"Week 03\", \"topic\": \"BIS as Tool; BIS as Information; Workshop - Information Searching\", \"activity\": \"Seminar (3 hr)\", \"learning_outcomes\": \"LO1 LO2 LO3 LO4 LO5 LO6\"}, {\"week\": \"Week 04\", \"topic\": \"Workshop - Design Thinking\", \"activity\": \"Seminar (3 hr)\", \"learning_outcomes\": \"LO1 LO2 LO3 LO4 LO5 LO6\"}, {\"week\": \"Week 05\", \"topic\": \"BIS as System; BIS as System Dynamic\", \"activity\": \"Seminar (3 hr)\", \"learning_outcomes\": \"LO1 LO2 LO3 LO4 LO5 LO6\"}, {\"week\": \"Week 06\", \"topic\": \"BIS as System Thinking; BIS as Designed\", \"activity\": \"Seminar (3 hr)\", \"learning_outcomes\": \"LO1 LO2 LO3 LO4 LO5 LO6\"}, {\"week\": \"Week 07\", \"topic\": \"BIS and IT; BIS as Data; Workshop - Data Flow Diagrams\", \"activity\": \"Seminar (3 hr)\", \"learning_outcomes\": \"LO1 LO2 LO3 LO4 LO5 LO6\"}, {\"week\": \"Week 08\", \"topic\": \"Self-directed study and consultation\", \"activity\": \"Seminar (3 hr)\", \"learning_outcomes\": \"LO1 LO2 LO3 LO4 LO5 LO6\"}, {\"week\": \"Week 09\", \"topic\": \"BIS as Workflow; Workshop - Introduction to BPMN; BIS as tool for efficiency\", \"activity\": \"Seminar (3 hr)\", \"learning_outcomes\": \"LO1 LO2 LO3 LO4 LO5 LO6\"}, {\"week\": \"Week 10\", \"topic\": \"BIS as Decision; BIS as Insight\", \"activity\": \"Seminar (3 hr)\", \"learning_outcomes\": \"LO1 LO2 LO3 LO4 LO5 LO6\"}, {\"week\": \"Week 11\", \"topic\": \"BIS and Ethics; BIS as Developed\", \"activity\": \"Seminar (3 hr)\", \"learning_outcomes\": \"LO1 LO2 LO3 LO4 LO5 LO6\"}, {\"week\": \"Week 12\", \"topic\": \"BIS and Sustainability; Summary and Farewell\", \"activity\": \"Seminar (3 hr)\", \"learning_outcomes\": \"LO1 LO2 LO3 LO4 LO5 LO6\"}, {\"week\": \"Week 13\", \"topic\": \"Group Project pitch/presentation to clients.\", \"activity\": \"Seminar (3 hr)\", \"learning_outcomes\": \"LO1 LO2 LO3 LO4 LO5 LO6\"}], \"learning_outcomes\": [\"LO1. Interpret, analyze, model and visualize representations of business processes, organisational structures and data.\", \"LO2. Appraise and critically assess the use of digital technology in business, society and individual workplace contexts.\", \"LO3. Effectively communicate and collaborate with different personalities, individually and in group settings, incomplex digital work environments to achieve positive and sustainable change outcomes.\", \"LO4. Evaluate the operations of a business and suggest and design solutions and improvements enabled by digital technology.\", \"LO5. Identify current trends in business information systems and ability to assess their implications for managers, organisations, employees and other stakeholders.\", \"LO6. Appraise and Examine the problem space within which technology is used with the aim to argue for the design of a specific solution\"], \"assessment_summary\": [\"For details on assessments please see the assessment section and details provided on the Unit’s Canvas site.\"]}'),(46,46,'outline-v1','baseline-v1','2026-09-11 04:52:53.201670','Foundation in Business Information Systems','{\"details\": {\"Academic unit\": \"Business Information Systems\", \"Credit points\": \"6\", \"Corequisites ?\": \"None\", \"Prohibitions ?\": \"INFS6001\", \"Prerequisites ?\": \"None\", \"Assumed knowledge ?\": \"None\", \"Available to study abroad and exchange students\": \"Yes\"}, \"session\": \"Semester 2, 2026 [Normal day] - Camperdown/Darlington, Sydney\", \"overview\": [\"This unit introduces students to the foundations of business information systems and the emerging strategic role of information and communication technologies (ICT) in transforming organisations. Students develop an understanding of how ICT come to matter to organisations as they disrupt, change and transform organisations and organisational processes. The unit covers systems issues, information literacy and use, and how various digital technologies work together to create an infrastructure for digital business and how technologies (such as social media) are disrupting \'business as usual\'. The role of information systems in capturing and distributing organisational knowledge and in enhancing decision-making is explored. Students gain an understanding of socio-technical networks, how information systems function, and how processes in organisations can be leveraged to create digital innovation and business transformation.\"], \"unit_code\": \"INFS5002\", \"source_url\": \"https://www.sydney.edu.au/units/INFS5002/2026-S2C-ND-CC\", \"unit_title\": \"Foundation in Business Information Systems\", \"assessments\": [{\"due\": \"Formal exam period Due date: 16 Nov 2026 at 23:59 Closing date: 25 Nov 2026\", \"type\": \"Written work\", \"length\": \"2,100 words\", \"weight\": \"30%\", \"description\": \"End of Semester Reflective Essay An end of semester reflection on the un