bled by digital technology.\", \"LO5. Identify current trends in business information systems and ability to assess their implications for managers, organisations, employees and other stakeholders.\", \"LO6. Appraise and Examine the problem space within which technology is used with the aim to argue for the design of a specific solution\"], \"assessment_summary\": [\"For details on assessments please see the assessment section and details provided on the Unit’s Canvas site.\"]}'),(47,47,'outline-v1','baseline-v1','2026-09-11 04:52:53.885847','Strategic Information Systems Sourcing','{\"details\": {\"Academic unit\": \"Business Information Systems\", \"Credit points\": \"6\", \"Corequisites ?\": \"None\", \"Prohibitions ?\": \"None\", \"Prerequisites ?\": \"None\", \"Assumed knowledge ?\": \"Basic business information systems knowledge\", \"Available to study abroad and exchange students\": \"Yes\"}, \"session\": \"Semester 2, 2026 [Normal day] - Camperdown/Darlington, Sydney\", \"overview\": [\"Strategic Information Systems Sourcing has at its core the cost-effective sourcing and delivery of IS solutions with the aim of supporting and enabling business strategy. It covers the procurement of in-house systems, outsourcing strategies and third-party IS sourcing (for example from \'the cloud\'). The focus of this unit is on managerial decisions in relation to the design, implementation and delivery of an IS sourcing strategy, and the governance of IS sourcing solutions. Students develop knowledge of the concepts, tools and methodologies used in the negotiation and development of an IS sourcing strategy.\"], \"unit_code\": \"INFS6002\", \"source_url\": \"https://www.sydney.edu.au/units/INFS6002/2026-S2C-ND-CC\", \"unit_title\": \"Strategic Information Systems Sourcing\", \"assessments\": [{\"due\": \"Formal exam period Due date: 16 Nov 2026 at 23:59 Closing date: 26 Nov 2026\", \"type\": \"Written work\", \"length\": \"3000 words\", \"weight\": \"30%\", \"description\": \"Individual assignment II Reflective essay on in-class activities\"}, {\"due\": \"Multiple weeks\", \"type\": \"Presentation\", \"length\": \"5 mins\", \"weight\": \"5%\", \"description\": \"Case Study Presentation on a chosen case article\"}, {\"due\": \"Week 07 Due date: 15 Sep 2026 at 16:00\", \"type\": \"Case studies\", \"length\": \"2 hours\", \"weight\": \"10%\", \"description\": \"Case study on IT Sourcing Decision Worksheet Presentation Complete in class\"}, {\"due\": \"Week 08 Due date: 25 Sep 2026 at 23:59 Closing date: 05 Oct 2026\", \"type\": \"Written work\", \"length\": \"2000 words\", \"weight\": \"20%\", \"description\": \"Individual assignment I Develop an information systems sourcing plan\"}, {\"due\": \"Week 13 Due date: 02 Nov 2026 at 23:59 Closing date: 12 Nov 2026\", \"type\": \"Written work\", \"length\": \"3000 words\", \"weight\": \"25%\", \"description\": \"Group Report IS pitching plan as a vendor\"}, {\"due\": \"Week 13 Due date: 02 Nov 2026 at 23:59 Closing date: 06 Nov 2026\", \"type\": \"Creative work\", \"length\": \"2 mins 30 seconds\", \"weight\": \"10%\", \"description\": \"Video creation Marketing video for a chosen information system\"}], \"retrieved_at\": \"2026-09-11T04:52:53.883704+00:00\", \"weekly_schedule\": [{\"week\": \"Week 01\", \"topic\": \"Introduction to IS sourcing\", \"activity\": \"Seminar (3 hr)\", \"learning_outcomes\": \"LO2 LO3\"}, {\"week\": \"Week 02\", \"topic\": \"Strategic Management and Information Systems\", \"activity\": \"Seminar (3 hr)\", \"learning_outcomes\": \"LO1 LO2 LO3 LO4\"}, {\"week\": \"Week 03\", \"topic\": \"IS Outsourcing Foundations\", \"activity\": \"Seminar (3 hr)\", \"learning_outcomes\": \"LO1 LO2 LO3 LO4 LO5\"}, {\"week\": \"Week 04\", \"topic\": \"Business Process Analysis in IS Sourcing: BAM and CATWOE\", \"activity\": \"Seminar (3 hr)\", \"learning_outcomes\": \"LO1 LO4\"}, {\"week\": \"Week 05\", \"topic\": \"Going to Market\", \"activity\": \"Seminar (3 hr)\", \"learning_outcomes\": \"LO2 LO3 LO5\"}, {\"week\": \"Week 06\", \"topic\": \"Evaluating Sourcing Options and Vendors\", \"activity\": \"Seminar (3 hr)\", \"learning_outcomes\": \"LO1 LO4 LO5\"}, {\"week\": \"Week 07\", \"topic\": \"Integrated Discussion of Sourcing Decision Making\", \"activity\": \"Seminar (3 hr)\", \"learning_outcomes\": \"LO1 LO2 LO3 LO4 LO5\"}, {\"week\": \"Week 08\", \"topic\": \"Vendors\' perspectives\", \"activity\": \"Seminar (3 hr)\", \"learning_outcomes\": \"LO6\"}, {\"week\": \"Week 09\", \"topic\": \"Vendors\' perspectives\", \"activity\": \"Seminar (3 hr)\", \"learning_outcomes\": \"LO6\"}, {\"week\": \"Week 10\", \"topic\": \"FinOps: Financial Operations for Cloud Cost Optimization\", \"activity\": \"Seminar (3 hr)\", \"learning_outcomes\": \"LO4 LO5\"}, {\"week\": \"Week 11\", \"topic\": \"Sourcing Risks and Control Strategies\", \"activity\": \"Seminar (3 hr)\", \"learning_outcomes\": \"LO3 LO4 LO5\"}, {\"week\": \"Week 12\", \"topic\": \"Managing Transition and Post-Sourcing Operations\", \"activity\": \"Seminar (3 hr)\", \"learning_outcomes\": \"LO2 LO3 LO4 LO5\"}, {\"week\": \"Week 13\", \"topic\": \"Revision\", \"activity\": \"Seminar (3 hr)\", \"learning_outcomes\": \"LO1 LO2 LO3 LO4 LO5 LO6\"}], \"learning_outcomes\": [\"LO1. Evaluate opportunities for outsourcing IT services within a range of business settings.\", \"LO2. Demonstrate your understanding of the range of available outsourced IT services by selecting suitable services for a set of provided business scenarios.\", \"LO3. Demonstrate understanding of the theories related to outsourcing by applying them to evaluate various outsourcing scenarios.\", \"LO4. Evaluate strategic information systems sourcing decisions in a business setting.\", \"LO5. Identify risks associated with outsourcing and describe the risk mitigation strategies that are commonly applied and suggest recommendations on suitable controls.\", \"LO6. Demonstrate understanding of the sourcing process from a vendor perspective.\"], \"assessment_summary\": [\"Individual Assessments\", \"Individual Assignment I: Develop an information systems sourcing plan\", \"Individual Assignment II: An reflective essay on in-class activities; consist of multiple components.\", \"Group Assessments:\", \"Case Study Discussion: Every group presents one case study in class. The order is to be determined in class.\", \"In-class Assessment: Work as a group to solve a sourcing decision making case study in class. Including worksheet and presentation.\", \"Group Project Report: Develop an IS pitching proposal as a vendor\", \"Group Project Video: Marketing/Pitching video for a chosen information systems.\", \"Detailed information for each assessment can be found on Canvas.\"]}'),(48,48,'outline-v1','baseline-v1','2026-09-11 04:52:54.447908','Digital Business Transformation','{\"details\": {\"Academic unit\": \"Business Information Systems\", \"Credit points\": \"6\", \"Corequisites ?\": \"INFS5002 or COMP5206\", \"Prohibitions ?\": \"None\", \"Prerequisites ?\": \"None\", \"Assumed knowledge ?\": \"Understanding the major functions of a business and how those business functions interact internally and externally so the company can be competitive in a changing market. How digital technologies can be used and managed in a business. How to critically analyse a business and determine its options for digital transformation. Desirable Assumed Knowledge: Experience as a member of a project team\", \"Available to study abroad and exchange students\": \"Yes\"}, \"session\": \"Semester 1, 2026 [Normal evening] - Camperdown/Darlington, Sydney\", \"overview\": [\"The disruptive forces of digital technologies require businesses to be in a constant state of change to stay competitive in turbulent markets. However, as companies need to maintain their current revenue streams, they need to progress through a series of digital transformation projects. In this unit students learn how to analyse an organisation within a local and global context and develop knowledge of techniques required for managing digital business transformation initiatives. Topics covered include: the drivers of digital business transformation, managing digital transformation as a process, understand the power of disruptive technologies, technological impacts on new forms of organizational arrangements.\"], \"unit_code\": \"INFS6004\", \"source_url\": \"https://www.sydney.edu.au/units/INFS6004/2026-S1C-NE-CC\", \"unit_title\": \"Digital Business Transformation\", \"assessments\": [{\"due\": \"Formal exam period\", \"type\": \"Written exam\", \"length\": \"2 hours\", \"weight\": \"40%\", \"description\": \"Final Exam Written Exam\"}, {\"due\": \"Multiple weeks Due date: 20 Mar 2026 at 23:59 Closing date: 27 Mar 2026\", \"type\": \"Presentation\", \"length\": \"90-second executive pitch with Q&A\", \"weight\": \"15%\", \"description\": \"Assignment 1 Individual in-class presentation in week 5/6. This is a 90-second pitch accompanied by a one-page poster.\"}, {\"due\": \"Multiple weeks\", \"type\": \"Presentation\", \"length\": \"-\", \"weight\": \"5%\", \"description\": \"Assignment 2c Group presentation (In-class presentation Week 12/13)\"}, {\"due\": \"Week 07 Due date: 17 Apr 2026 at 23:59 Closing date: 01 May 2026\", \"type\": \"Case studies\", \"length\": \"1000 words\", \"weight\": \"10%\", \"description\": \"Assignment 2a Group report outline\"}, {\"due\": \"Week 12 Due date: 18 May 2026 at 23:59 Closing date: 25 May 2026\", \"type\": \"Case studies\", \"length\": \"3000 words\", \"weight\": \"30%\", \"description\": \"Assignment 2b Business report and presentation slides\"}], \"retrieved_at\": \"2026-09-11T04:52:54.446276+00:00\", \"weekly_schedule\": [{\"week\": \"Week 01\", \"topic\": \"Introduction and Overview\", \"activity\": \"Lecture (2 hr)\", \"learning_outcomes\": \"LO1\"}, {\"week\": \"Week 02\", \"topic\": \"Understanding Disruption\", \"activity\": \"Lecture (2 hr)\", \"learning_outcomes\": \"LO1 LO2\"}, {\"week\": \"Week 02\", \"topic\": \"Understanding Disruption\", \"activity\": \"Tutorial (1 hr)\", \"learning_outcomes\": \"LO1 LO2\"}, {\"week\": \"Week 03\", \"topic\": \"The Drivers and Enablers of Digital Transformation\", \"activity\": \"Lecture (2 hr)\", \"learning_outcomes\": \"LO1 LO2\"}, {\"week\": \"Week 03\", \"topic\": \"The Drivers and Enablers of Digital Transformation\", \"activity\": \"Tutorial (1 hr)\", \"learning_outcomes\": \"LO1 LO2\"}, {\"week\": \"Week 04\", \"topic\": \"Manage Change and Transformation-1\", \"activity\": \"Lecture (2 hr)\", \"learning_outcomes\": \"LO1 LO2 LO3 LO6\"}, {\"week\": \"Week 04\", \"topic\": \"Manage Change and Transformation-1\", \"activity\": \"Tutorial (1 hr)\", \"learning_outcomes\": \"LO1 LO2 LO3 LO6\"}, {\"week\": \"Week 05\", \"topic\": \"Manage Change and Transformation-2\", \"activity\": \"Lecture (2 hr)\", \"learning_outcomes\": \"LO1 LO2 LO3 LO6\"}, {\"week\": \"Week 05\", \"topic\": \"Manage Change and Transformation-2\", \"activity\": \"Tutorial (1 hr)\", \"learning_outcomes\": \"LO1 LO2 LO3 LO6\"}, {\"week\": \"Week 06\", \"topic\": \"Overcome Challenges of Digital Transformation\", \"activity\": \"Lecture (2 hr)\", \"learning_outcomes\": \"LO4 LO5\"}, {\"week\": \"Week 06\", \"topic\": \"Overcome Challenges of Digital Transformation\", \"activity\": \"Tutorial (1 hr)\", \"learning_outcomes\": \"LO4 LO5\"}, {\"week\": \"Week 07\", \"topic\": \"Digital Transformation of Consumption\", \"activity\": \"Lecture (2 hr)\", \"learning_outcomes\": \"LO1 LO2 LO3 LO6\"}, {\"week\": \"Week 07\", \"topic\": \"Digital Transformation of Consumption\", \"activity\": \"Tutorial (1 hr)\", \"learning_outcomes\": \"LO1 LO2 LO3 LO6\"}, {\"week\": \"Week 08\", \"topic\": \"Digital Transformation of Communication\", \"activity\": \"Lecture (2 hr)\", \"learning_outcomes\": \"LO1 LO2 LO3 LO6\"}, {\"week\": \"Week 08\", \"topic\": \"Digital Transformation of Communication\", \"activity\": \"Tutorial (1 hr)\", \"learning_outcomes\": \"LO1 LO2 LO3 LO6\"}, {\"week\": \"Week 09\", \"topic\": \"Digital Transformation of Traditional Industries\", \"activity\": \"Lecture (2 hr)\", \"learning_outcomes\": \"LO1 LO2 LO3 LO6\"}, {\"week\": \"Week 09\", \"topic\": \"Digital Transformation of Traditional Industries\", \"activity\": \"Tutorial (1 hr)\", \"learning_outcomes\": \"LO1 LO2 LO3 LO6\"}, {\"week\": \"Week 10\", \"topic\": \"Group assignment consultation and self-directed learning\", \"activity\": \"Lecture (2 hr)\", \"learning_outcomes\": \"LO2 LO3 LO6 LO7 LO8\"}, {\"week\": \"Week 10\", \"topic\": \"Group assignment consultation and self-directed learning\", \"activity\": \"Tutorial (1 hr)\", \"learning_outcomes\": \"LO2 LO3 LO6 LO7 LO8\"}, {\"week\": \"Week 11\", \"topic\": \"Review and Synthesis\", \"activity\": \"Lecture (2 hr)\", \"learning_outcomes\": \"LO1 LO6 LO4 LO5\"}, {\"week\": \"Week 12\", \"topic\": \"Group Presentations\", \"activity\": \"Lecture (2 hr)\", \"learning_outcomes\": \"LO1 LO2 LO3 LO6 LO7 LO8\"}, {\"week\": \"Week 13\", \"topic\": \"Group Presentations\", \"activity\": \"Lecture (3 hr)\", \"learning_outcomes\": \"LO1 LO2 LO3 LO6 LO7 LO8\"}], \"learning_outcomes\": [\"LO1. Identify and describe the drivers and enablers of digital transformation in business settings.\", \"LO2. Critically analyse business problems that necessitate digital transformation and change in an organisation.\", \"LO3. Critically and creatively analyse and propose business innovations to address identified business problems.\", \"LO4. Critically analyse the challenges for businesses in the face of innovation and technological advancements.\", \"LO5. Critically and creatively analyse various strategies to overcome challenges in digital transformation.\", \"LO6. Critically synthesise and apply methods, models and frameworks with business analysis, communication and research skills in digital transformation projects.\", \"LO7. Collaborate and communicate in a professional manner with people from diverse backgrounds.\", \"LO8. Contribute effectively as a responsible member of a diverse team for group assessments.\"], \"assessment_summary\": [\"• Assignment 1 (Executive Pitch and Q&A): Students will select a company that has undergone digital transformation and analyse recent news articles about the company. They will synthesise the key insights and evaluate the likely transformative impact of these developments, and communicate their analysis through a one-page poster and a 90-second executive pitch. Students will be encouraged to focus on an industry and company aligned with their future career interests. • Assignment 2a (Group Report Outline): Students will work in groups as a team of consultants to submit a structured outline for their Digital Transformation Management Plan for a selected company. The outline will present the company background and context, diagnose the need for digital transformation, and propose and briefly evaluate potential digital solutions. This submission is designed to support formative feedback from the teaching team, which groups should use to strengthen their final report and presentation.\", \"• Assignment 2b (Group Report & Presentation Slides): Students will work in groups to develop a professional business report that proposes a digital transformation solution for a selected organisation. Building on feedback from the proposal outline, the report should describe the solution in sufficient detail to show how it addresses the organisation’s challenges, and apply current change management frameworks to analyse the organisation and develop a transformative change management plan aligned with the solution and project requirements.\", \"• Assignment 2c (In-class presentation): All students in each team to design, develop, and present the critical details from Assignment 2b (group report).\", \"• Final Exam: This exam will focus on the fundamental concepts and applied and experiential knowledge acquired across the semester. Note: This assessment will take the form of a supervised exam. It is a closed- book exam; no materials are allowed.\", \"Detailed information for each assessment can be found on Canvas.\"]}'),(49,49,'outline-v1','baseline-v1','2026-09-11 04:52:54.956513','Digital Information Infrastructures','{\"details\": {\"Academic unit\": \"Business Information Systems\", \"Credit points\": \"6\", \"Corequisites ?\": \"INFS5002 or COMP5206\", \"Prohibitions ?\": \"None\", \"Prerequisites ?\": \"None\", \"Assumed knowledge ?\": \"None\", \"Available to study abroad and exchange students\": \"Yes\"}, \"session\": \"Semester 1, 2026 [Normal day] - Camperdown/Darlington, Sydney\", \"overview\": [\"The unit provides an overall introduction to the different components of digital information infrastructures in organisational contexts. This includes organisational enterprise systems architecture, legacy systems, enterprise systems, cloud infrastructure and enabling technologies such as blockchain, internet of things, or web services. Strategic managerial issues that arise from the implementation, use, and security management of information infrastructures and enterprise systems are also covered. The unit utilises a combination of practical sessions with Enterprise Systems, such as SAP, and case study analyses to build a deep understanding of relevant topics.\"], \"unit_code\": \"INFS6012\", \"source_url\": \"https://www.sydney.edu.au/units/INFS6012/2026-S1C-ND-CC\", \"unit_title\": \"Digital Information Infrastructures\", \"assessments\": [{\"due\": \"Formal exam period\", \"type\": \"Written exam\", \"length\": \"2 hours\", \"weight\": \"50%\", \"description\": \"Final Exam Closed book exam\"}, {\"due\": \"Multiple weeks\", \"type\": \"Presentation\", \"length\": \"-\", \"weight\": \"5%\", \"description\": \"Case Presentation Presentation on Case Study Articles\"}, {\"due\": \"Week 08 Due date: 24 Apr 2026 at 23:59 Closing date: 01 May 2026\", \"type\": \"Practical skill\", \"length\": \"-\", \"weight\": \"25%\", \"description\": \"Individual Assignment Written report with specified questions\"}, {\"due\": \"Week 12 Due date: 22 May 2026 at 23:59 Closing date: 01 Jun 2026\", \"type\": \"Written work\", \"length\": \"-\", \"weight\": \"17%\", \"description\": \"Group project report Report\"}, {\"due\": \"Week 12 Due date: 22 May 2026 at 23:59 Closing date: 01 Jun 2026\", \"type\": \"Presentation\", \"length\": \"-\", \"weight\": \"3%\", \"description\": \"Group project presentation Report\"}], \"retrieved_at\": \"2026-09-11T04:52:54.955310+00:00\", \"weekly_schedule\": [{\"week\": \"Week 01\", \"topic\": \"Introduction\", \"activity\": \"Seminar (3 hr)\", \"learning_outcomes\": \"LO1 LO3\"}, {\"week\": \"Week 02\", \"topic\": \"Business Process and Enterprise Systems\", \"activity\": \"Seminar (3 hr)\", \"learning_outcomes\": \"LO1 LO2 LO3\"}, {\"week\": \"Week 03\", \"topic\": \"Enterprise Systems and Accounting Process I\", \"activity\": \"Seminar (3 hr)\", \"learning_outcomes\": \"LO2 LO3 LO4\"}, {\"week\": \"Week 04\", \"topic\": \"Enterprise Systems and Procurement Process I\", \"activity\": \"Seminar (3 hr)\", \"learning_outcomes\": \"LO2 LO3 LO4\"}, {\"week\": \"Week 05\", \"topic\": \"Enterprise Systems and Procurement Process II\", \"activity\": \"Seminar (3 hr)\", \"learning_outcomes\": \"LO2 LO3 LO4\"}, {\"week\": \"Week 06\", \"topic\": \"Enterprise Systems and Lead to Cash Process\", \"activity\": \"Seminar (3 hr)\", \"learning_outcomes\": \"LO2 LO3 LO4\"}, {\"week\": \"Week 07\", \"topic\": \"Integrated Discussion on Enterprise Systems\", \"activity\": \"Seminar (3 hr)\", \"learning_outcomes\": \"LO2 LO3 LO4\"}, {\"week\": \"Week 08\", \"topic\": \"Guest Lecture (TBC)\", \"activity\": \"Seminar (3 hr)\", \"learning_outcomes\": \"LO1 LO2 LO3 LO6\"}, {\"week\": \"Week 09\", \"topic\": \"Cloud Computing and Enterprise Systems\", \"activity\": \"Seminar (3 hr)\", \"learning_outcomes\": \"LO1 LO3 LO4 LO5\"}, {\"week\": \"Week 10\", \"topic\": \"Blockchain and IoT\", \"activity\": \"Seminar (3 hr)\", \"learning_outcomes\": \"LO3 LO4 LO5\"}, {\"week\": \"Week 11\", \"topic\": \"Managing Digital Information Infrastructure I\", \"activity\": \"Seminar (3 hr)\", \"learning_outcomes\": \"LO1 LO3 LO4 LO5\"}, {\"week\": \"Week 12\", \"topic\": \"Managing Digital Information Infrastructure II\", \"activity\": \"Seminar (3 hr)\", \"learning_outcomes\": \"LO1 LO3 LO4 LO5\"}, {\"week\": \"Week 13\", \"topic\": \"Course Revision\", \"activity\": \"Seminar (3 hr)\", \"learning_outcomes\": \"LO1 LO2 LO3 LO4 LO6\"}], \"learning_outcomes\": [\"LO1. explore the strategic managerial issues that arise from the implementation and use of enterprise systems as a means of integrating data and standardising processes\", \"LO2. use an example enterprise system to gain hands-on competency in supporting key business processes\", \"LO3. provide an overview of an enterprise system implementation solution which addresses key processes, data and organisational structures, and explain the reasons behind the solution\", \"LO4. evaluate the place of enterprise systems in broader digital information infrastructure.\", \"LO5. evaluate in a critical manner the technical trends which may impact on future enterprise systems use\", \"LO6. present ideas and arguments effectively, deliver a comprehensive and integrated enterprise information infrastructure that reflects a collective effort from a professional project team\", \"LO7. apply the principles of IT resources management to effectively solve real-world problems.\"], \"assessment_summary\": [\"Individual assignment: The individual assignment consists of multiple components that may include the completion of tasks with SAP and a written report.\", \"Group project: You must demonstrate an information infrastructure which explains the role of enterprise systems within that infrastructure, discusses organisational and change management issues, and examines the effect of new technological trends.\", \"Case presentation: Each group is scheduled for a 10-minute case presentation during different weeks. The goal of these presentations is to help the class better understand the case background.\", \"Final exam: This is a closed-book exam and will assess your ability to demonstrate your understanding of all material covered in the unit of study.\", \"Detailed information for each assessment can be found on Canvas.\"]}'),(50,50,'outline-v1','baseline-v1','2026-09-11 04:52:55.479898','Business Process Management','{\"details\": {\"Academic unit\": \"Business Information Systems\", \"Credit points\": \"6\", \"Corequisites ?\": \"INFS5002 or COMP5206\", \"Prohibitions ?\": \"None\", \"Prerequisites ?\": \"None\", \"Assumed knowledge ?\": \"None\", \"Available to study abroad and exchange students\": \"Yes\"}, \"session\": \"Semester 2, 2026 [Normal evening] - Camperdown/Darlington, Sydney\", \"overview\": [\"This unit highlights the key concepts of business process management (BPM) and their importance to organisations in supporting the business operations and providing opportunities for competitive advantage and innovation. It provides a detailed understanding of the concepts, strategies, tools and technologies required throughout the BPM lifecycle. This unit takes both the strategic and change management perspectives in designing process architecture and governance, as well as analysing, designing, and measuring performance of processes across value chains and aligned to industry standards. The unit also develops practical skills in modelling and simulating processes using business process management tools.\"], \"unit_code\": \"INFS6015\", \"source_url\": \"https://www.sydney.edu.au/units/INFS6015/2026-S2C-NE-CC\", \"unit_title\": \"Business Process Management\", \"assessments\": [{\"due\": \"Formal exam period\", \"type\": \"Written exam\", \"length\": \"2 hours\", \"weight\": \"40%\", \"description\": \"Final exam Written exam\"}, {\"due\": \"Week 06 Due date: 11 Sep 2026 at 23:59 Closing date: 21 Sep 2026\", \"type\": \"Case studies\", \"length\": \"Up to 1750 words\", \"weight\": \"25%\", \"description\": \"Individual assignment Written submission\"}, {\"due\": \"Week 09 Due date: 06 Oct 2026 at 23:59 Closing date: 16 Oct 2026\", \"type\": \"Creative work\", \"length\": \"500 words (6 PPT slides)\", \"weight\": \"10%\", \"description\": \"Business Proposal Business idea and execution plan proposal\"}, {\"due\": \"Week 13 Due date: 08 Nov 2026 at 23:59 Closing date: 09 Nov 2026\", \"type\": \"Case studies\", \"length\": \"Up to 2750 words\", \"weight\": \"25%\", \"description\": \"Business Report Group Report Submission\"}], \"retrieved_at\": \"2026-09-11T04:52:55.478564+00:00\", \"weekly_schedule\": [{\"week\": \"Week 01\", \"topic\": \"Overview of Business Process Management (BPM)\", \"activity\": \"Seminar (3 hr)\", \"learning_outcomes\": \"LO1 LO6\"}, {\"week\": \"Week 02\", \"topic\": \"Process identification\", \"activity\": \"Seminar (3 hr)\", \"learning_outcomes\": \"LO2 LO5 LO6 LO7\"}, {\"week\": \"Week 03\", \"topic\": \"Process governance and discovery\", \"activity\": \"Seminar (3 hr)\", \"learning_outcomes\": \"LO2 LO4 LO5 LO7\"}, {\"week\": \"Week 04\", \"topic\": \"Process modelling 1: BPMN Notation\", \"activity\": \"Seminar (3 hr)\", \"learning_outcomes\": \"LO2 LO5 LO6 LO7\"}, {\"week\": \"Week 05\", \"topic\": \"Process modelling 2: Modelling As-Is processes using Signavio\", \"activity\": \"Seminar (3 hr)\", \"learning_outcomes\": \"LO2 LO5 LO6 LO7\"}, {\"week\": \"Week 06\", \"topic\": \"Process analysis 1 (qualitative)\", \"activity\": \"Seminar (3 hr)\", \"learning_outcomes\": \"LO2 LO6 LO7\"}, {\"week\": \"Week 07\", \"topic\": \"Process analysis 2 (quantitative): Simulating As-Is processes using Signavio\", \"activity\": \"Seminar (3 hr)\", \"learning_outcomes\": \"LO2 LO3 LO4 LO5 LO6 LO7\"}, {\"week\": \"Week 08\", \"topic\": \"Process redesign 1: Redesign heuristics\", \"activity\": \"Seminar (3 hr)\", \"learning_outcomes\": \"LO2 LO3 LO4 LO5 LO6 LO7\"}, {\"week\": \"Week 09\", \"topic\": \"Public Holiday (Mon) - No class; Business Proposal due for Feedback collection\", \"activity\": \"Seminar (3 hr)\", \"learning_outcomes\": \"LO2 LO3 LO4 LO7\"}, {\"week\": \"Week 10\", \"topic\": \"Process redesign 2: Simulating To-Be processes using Signavio\", \"activity\": \"Seminar (3 hr)\", \"learning_outcomes\": \"LO2 LO3 LO4 LO6 LO7\"}, {\"week\": \"Week 11\", \"topic\": \"Process implementation, monitoring, and mining\", \"activity\": \"Seminar (3 hr)\", \"learning_outcomes\": \"LO2 LO3 LO4 LO5 LO7\"}, {\"week\": \"Week 12\", \"topic\": \"BPM emerging topics; Group project consultation\", \"activity\": \"Seminar (3 hr)\", \"learning_outcomes\": \"LO1 LO2 LO3 LO4 LO5 LO6 LO7\"}, {\"week\": \"Week 13\", \"topic\": \"Unit Review and Final Exam Preparation\", \"activity\": \"Seminar (3 hr)\", \"learning_outcomes\": \"LO1 LO2 LO3 LO4 LO5 LO6 LO7\"}], \"learning_outcomes\": [\"LO1. Discuss the holistic role of Business Process Management (BPM) in a business environment to improve performance and align to overall strategy.\", \"LO2. Apply BPM methodologies, concepts, and principles to business problems and practice following the BPM lifecycle.\", \"LO3. Address the issues and challenges associated with process change initiatives in organisations.\", \"LO4. Evaluate the impact of process change projects on stakeholders and the role of change management in mitigating risks in such projects.\", \"LO5. Use BPM tools to model, document, and analyse processes during the BPM lifecycle.\", \"LO6. Work independently in a professional and ethical manner\", \"LO7. Work as a responsible member of a diverse team, collaborate and communicate in a professional manner with people from diverse backgrounds.\"], \"assessment_summary\": [\"Individual assignment: In this assignment students will take the role of the process analyst and engage in process discovery and analysis within a given business case context.\", \"Business Proposal assignment: In this asignment students will analyse the market and identify new services for a business case seeking to expand. Students will propose a new service and a plan to guide the execution of the project.\", \"Business Report assignment: In this assignment students will desing new processes following the service proposed in their Business Proposal pitch. Students will assess the feasibility of new processes, the resources required, and the challenges encountered during process implementation. Students will use Signavio (BPM tool) to document, simulate and analyse the new business processes.\", \"Final exam: A supervised exam that will test students’ theoretical understanding, critical thinking, and ability to apply and evaluate BPM concepts and principles in practice.\", \"Detailed information for each assessment can be found on Canvas.\"]}'),(51,51,'outline-v1','baseline-v1','2026-09-11 04:52:55.986848','Digital Business Models','{\"details\": {\"Academic unit\": \"Business Information Systems\", \"Credit points\": \"6\", \"Corequisites ?\": \"INFS5002 or COMP5206\", \"Prohibitions ?\": \"None\", \"Prerequisites ?\": \"None\", \"Assumed knowledge ?\": \"Understanding the major functions of a business and how those business functions interact internally and externally so the company can be competitive in the market is essential in order to critically analyse how and where a business can be innovative. Some knowledge of how technology can be applied in a business is also essential. Experience as a member of a project team is desirable\", \"Available to study abroad and exchange students\": \"Yes\"}, \"session\": \"Semester 1, 2026 [Normal day] - Camperdown/Darlington, Sydney\", \"overview\": [\"This unit develops knowledge and skills in innovative, digital business models and strategies from a management perspective. The unit facilitates a better understanding and application of the concepts, strategies, tools and technologies necessary for undertaking digital innovation of business models. From basic knowledge of digital business models and business processes, this unit increases awareness and understanding of stakeholders, their capabilities and their limitations in the strategic convergence of technology and business. It provides insights into the digital technologies required to support business in the 21st Century and supports development of student capabilities to analyse, develop and evaluate innovative digital business strategies and models.\"], \"unit_code\": \"INFS6016\", \"source_url\": \"https://www.sydney.edu.au/units/INFS6016/2026-S1C-ND-CC\", \"unit_title\": \"Digital Business Models\", \"assessments\": [{\"due\": \"Multiple weeks\", \"type\": \"Portfolio or journal\", \"length\": \"600 words each\", \"weight\": \"24%\", \"description\": \"Individual reflective reports Individual reflective reports\"}, {\"due\": \"Week 09 Due date: 01 May 2026 at 23:59 Closing date: 15 May 2026\", \"type\": \"Written work\", \"length\": \"2500 words\", \"weight\": \"26%\", \"description\": \"Individual project Written report\"}, {\"due\": \"Week 12 Due date: 22 May 2026 at 23:59 Closing date: 29 May 2026\", \"type\": \"Written work\", \"length\": \"5000 words\", \"weight\": \"40%\", \"description\": \"Group project report Written report\"}, {\"due\": \"Week 13 Due date: 26 May 2026 at 23:59 Closing date: 29 May 2026\", \"type\": \"Presentation\", \"length\": \"15 minutes\", \"weight\": \"10%\", \"description\": \"Group project presentation Group project presentation\"}], \"retrieved_at\": \"2026-09-11T04:52:55.985806+00:00\", \"weekly_schedule\": [{\"week\": \"Week 01\", \"topic\": \"Introduction and overview\", \"activity\": \"Seminar (3 hr)\", \"learning_outcomes\": \"\"}, {\"week\": \"Week 02\", \"topic\": \"Perspectives on digital innovation\", \"activity\": \"Seminar (3 hr)\", \"learning_outcomes\": \"\"}, {\"week\": \"Week 03\", \"topic\": \"Digital platform- 1\", \"activity\": \"Seminar (3 hr)\", \"learning_outcomes\": \"\"}, {\"week\": \"Week 04\", \"topic\": \"Digital platform- 2\", \"activity\": \"Seminar (3 hr)\", \"learning_outcomes\": \"\"}, {\"week\": \"Week 05\", \"topic\": \"Business model in the digital era-1\", \"activity\": \"Seminar (3 hr)\", \"learning_outcomes\": \"\"}, {\"week\": \"Week 06\", \"topic\": \"Business model in the digital era-2\", \"activity\": \"Seminar (3 hr)\", \"learning_outcomes\": \"\"}, {\"week\": \"Week 07\", \"topic\": \"Group project activity\", \"activity\": \"Seminar (3 hr)\", \"learning_outcomes\": \"\"}, {\"week\": \"Week 08\", \"topic\": \"Group project activity\", \"activity\": \"Seminar (3 hr)\", \"learning_outcomes\": \"\"}, {\"week\": \"Week 09\", \"topic\": \"Self-directed learning & Group assignment consultation\", \"activity\": \"Seminar (3 hr)\", \"learning_outcomes\": \"\"}, {\"week\": \"Week 10\", \"topic\": \"Digital business model- industry-specific development\", \"activity\": \"Seminar (3 hr)\", \"learning_outcomes\": \"\"}, {\"week\": \"Week 11\", \"topic\": \"Digital business model- industry-specific development\", \"activity\": \"Seminar (3 hr)\", \"learning_outcomes\": \"\"}, {\"week\": \"Week 12\", \"topic\": \"Review and synthesis\", \"activity\": \"Seminar (3 hr)\", \"learning_outcomes\": \"\"}, {\"week\": \"Week 13\", \"topic\": \"Group Presentation\", \"activity\": \"Seminar (3 hr)\", \"learning_outcomes\": \"\"}], \"learning_outcomes\": [\"LO1. Demonstrate knowledge and understanding of characteristics of digital business\", \"LO2. Effectively analyze and evaluate the strategy and business model of digital platforms\", \"LO3. Demonstrate capabilities for critical analysis and creative design of practical digital business innovations\", \"LO4. Critically assess the value and opportunities of emerging technologies for business innovations in different industries\", \"LO5. Collaborate and communicate in a professional manner with people from diverse backgrounds\"], \"assessment_summary\": [\"Individual report: Students will select, analyse, and submit a written report of a recent digital platform business relevant to the learning objectives for this unit.\", \"Group project report: The group project report is an applied assignment that requires the team\'s original development of an innovative digital business plan.\", \"Group project presentation: All students in each team will design, develop, and present the critical details from the group assignment report.\", \"Individual reflective reports: Students will write several reflective reports on the unit learning.\", \"Detailed information for each assessment can be found on Canvas.\"]}'),(52,52,'outline-v1','baseline-v1','2026-09-11 04:52:56.641923','Managing with Information and Data','{\"details\": {\"Academic unit\": \"Business Information Systems\", \"Credit points\": \"6\", \"Corequisites ?\": \"INFS5002 or COMP5206 or QBUS5001\", \"Prohibitions ?\": \"None\", \"Prerequisites ?\": \"None\", \"Assumed knowledge ?\": \"Understanding the major functions of a business and how those business functions interact Semester 1 internally and externally so the company can be competitive in a changing market. How information systems can be used and managed in a business. How to critically analyse a business and determine its options for transformation. Desirable Experience as a member of a project team\", \"Available to study abroad and exchange students\": \"Yes\"}, \"session\": \"Semester 1, 2026 [Normal day] - Camperdown/Darlington, Sydney\", \"overview\": [\"Business analytics and the ability to interpret and respond to related outputs, is a major source of competitive advantage in the information age and is therefore a leading business priority globally. In recent times, this field has evolved from a technology topic to a management priority, creating an unprecedented demand for new competencies in managing with data. Taking a business rather than technology perspective, this unit covers the enterprise ecosystem in the context of strategic and operational analytics and decision making. Topics include innovation through advanced analytics, data driven performance management, strategic business improvement and management of complex BI projects. The unit offers hands-on experience in using a commercial platform, combined with in-depth analytical skills, and enables students completing the unit to help any organization to derive more value from data and information and compete on analytics.\"], \"unit_code\": \"INFS6018\", \"source_url\": \"https://www.sydney.edu.au/units/INFS6018/2026-S1C-ND-CC\", \"unit_title\": \"Managing with Information and Data\", \"assessments\": [{\"due\": \"Multiple weeks Due date: 31 May 2026 at 23:59 Closing date: 10 Jun 2026\", \"type\": \"Portfolio or journal\", \"length\": \"2500 words\", \"weight\": \"25%\", \"description\": \"Reflective Essay Written essay on core learnings\"}, {\"due\": \"Week 07 Due date: 19 Apr 2026 at 15:10\", \"type\": \"Written test\", \"length\": \"2 hours\", \"weight\": \"35%\", \"description\": \"Mid-semester test Mid-semester test will assess core learnings from weeks 1-5\"}, {\"due\": \"Week 12 Due date: 18 May 2026 at 23:59 Closing date: 28 May 2026\", \"type\": \"Data analysis\", \"length\": \"4000 words\", \"weight\": \"30%\", \"description\": \"Project report Written report\"}, {\"due\": \"Week 13\", \"type\": \"Presentation\", \"length\": \"Poster + 5 min Presentation + 15 min Q&A\", \"weight\": \"10%\", \"description\": \"Group project presentation Group presentation of written report and related analysis\"}], \"retrieved_at\": \"2026-09-11T04:52:56.640631+00:00\", \"weekly_schedule\": [{\"week\": \"Week 01\", \"topic\": \"Foundational and historical concepts\", \"activity\": \"Seminar (3 hr)\", \"learning_outcomes\": \"\"}, {\"week\": \"Week 02\", \"topic\": \"Decision making for managers\", \"activity\": \"Seminar (3 hr)\", \"learning_outcomes\": \"\"}, {\"week\": \"Week 03\", \"topic\": \"Data quality\", \"activity\": \"Seminar (3 hr)\", \"learning_outcomes\": \"\"}, {\"week\": \"Week 04\", \"topic\": \"Strategies & business models for valuecreation\", \"activity\": \"Seminar (3 hr)\", \"learning_outcomes\": \"\"}, {\"week\": \"Week 05\", \"topic\": \"Strategic alignment and IT governance\", \"activity\": \"Seminar (3 hr)\", \"learning_outcomes\": \"\"}, {\"week\": \"Week 06\", \"topic\": \"Exam preparation\", \"activity\": \"Seminar (3 hr)\", \"learning_outcomes\": \"\"}, {\"week\": \"Week 07\", \"topic\": \"Mid-semester Test\", \"activity\": \"Seminar (3 hr)\", \"learning_outcomes\": \"LO1 LO2 LO3 LO4 LO5 LO6\"}, {\"week\": \"Week 08\", \"topic\": \"Analytics, people and culture\", \"activity\": \"Seminar (3 hr)\", \"learning_outcomes\": \"\"}, {\"week\": \"Week 09\", \"topic\": \"Ethics for business intelligence\", \"activity\": \"Seminar (3 hr)\", \"learning_outcomes\": \"\"}, {\"week\": \"Week 10\", \"topic\": \"Managing the change process and stakeholders\", \"activity\": \"Seminar (3 hr)\", \"learning_outcomes\": \"\"}, {\"week\": \"Week 11\", \"topic\": \"Guest Lecture\", \"activity\": \"Seminar (3 hr)\", \"learning_outcomes\": \"\"}, {\"week\": \"Week 12\", \"topic\": \"Managing emerging technologies: Blockchain and AI\", \"activity\": \"Seminar (3 hr)\", \"learning_outcomes\": \"\"}, {\"week\": \"Week 13\", \"topic\": \"Managing the cloud\", \"activity\": \"Seminar (3 hr)\", \"learning_outcomes\": \"\"}], \"learning_outcomes\": [\"LO1. Apply the fundamental concepts and practice of managing through data challenges in differentiated organisational settings.\", \"LO2. Identify and analyse issues, challenges and solutions in managing through data/business analytics systems from the business rather thantechnical perspective.\", \"LO3. Critically examine the intra and inter organisational and societal issues involved in implementing various types of analytical systems.\", \"LO4. Design and implement a small-scale data analysis project in an organisational setting.\", \"LO5. Evaluate different analytical outputs and their ethical impacts.\", \"LO6. Apply advanced principles and techniques related to strategy, organizational change and information governance to help organisations effectively maximise value from their data, information assets and technology investments.\"], \"assessment_summary\": [\"Mid-semester test to be held in Week 7 on core concepts delivered in weeks 1-5.\", \"Group project and report: In groups, students will use Tableau to explore a real-world data set and consider the implications for distinct personas. Students will prepare a report outlining this analysis. Students will be orally examined in groups on the contents of this report.\", \"Reflective essay: Students will utilise a reflective framework to critically evaluate managerial practices\"]}'),(53,53,'outline-v1','baseline-v1','2026-09-11 04:52:57.267634','Data Visualisation for Managers','{\"details\": {\"Academic unit\": \"Business Information Systems\", \"Credit points\": \"6\", \"Corequisites ?\": \"None\", \"Prohibitions ?\": \"None\", \"Prerequisites ?\": \"None\", \"Assumed knowledge ?\": \"None\", \"Available to study abroad and exchange students\": \"Yes\"}, \"session\": \"Semester 2, 2026 [Normal day] - Camperdown/Darlington, Sydney\", \"overview\": [\"Data visualisation, storytelling, and scenario development are prominent analytical practices that are increasingly used by professionals seeking to use data for decision making. This unit aims to equip students with necessary knowledge and data visualisation skills, acquired through real-world projects and applications inspired by leading industry practices. Students develop a holistic view of data visualisation and acquire knowledge of related tools to deal with organisational and societal challenges. This unit focuses on business/organisational decision makers and their use of data visualisation. As such this unit does not require any prior IT, computer science or data science experience.\"], \"unit_code\": \"INFS6023\", \"source_url\": \"https://www.sydney.edu.au/units/INFS6023/2026-S2C-ND-CC\", \"unit_title\": \"Data Visualisation for Managers\", \"assessments\": [{\"due\": \"Multiple weeks\", \"type\": \"Practical skill\", \"length\": \"5 hours\", \"weight\": \"5%\", \"description\": \"Skills-based assessment Self-paced workshop\"}, {\"due\": \"Multiple weeks\", \"type\": \"Case studies\", \"length\": \"10 minutes\", \"weight\": \"20%\", \"description\": \"Case study discussion Presentation\"}, {\"due\": \"Multiple weeks\", \"type\": \"Conversation\", \"length\": \"10 minutes\", \"weight\": \"20%\", \"description\": \"In-class assessment Case study discussion\"}, {\"due\": \"Week 06 Due date: 11 Sep 2026 at 23:59 Closing date: 21 Sep 2026\", \"type\": \"Written work\", \"length\": \"1500 words\", \"weight\": \"15%\", \"description\": \"Individual assignment Written report\"}, {\"due\": \"Week 11 Due date: 23 Oct 2026 at 23:59 Closing date: 02 Nov 2026\", \"type\": \"Written work\", \"length\": \"3000 words\", \"weight\": \"25%\", \"description\": \"Group project report Written report\"}, {\"due\": \"Week 11 Due date: 23 Oct 2026 at 23:59 Closing date: 02 Nov 2026\", \"type\": \"Presentation\", \"length\": \"10 minutes\", \"weight\": \"15%\", \"description\": \"Group project presentation Presentation\"}], \"retrieved_at\": \"2026-09-11T04:52:57.265283+00:00\", \"weekly_schedule\": [{\"week\": \"Week 01\", \"topic\": \"Introduction to Data Visualisation\", \"activity\": \"Seminar (3 hr)\", \"learning_outcomes\": \"LO1 LO2 LO3\"}, {\"week\": \"Week 02\", \"topic\": \"Conceptual Foundations of Data Visualisation\", \"activity\": \"Seminar (3 hr)\", \"learning_outcomes\": \"LO1 LO3 LO4\"}, {\"week\": \"Week 03\", \"topic\": \"Designing Effective Visualisations\", \"activity\": \"Seminar (3 hr)\", \"learning_outcomes\": \"LO1 LO3 LO4 LO5\"}, {\"week\": \"Week 04\", \"topic\": \"Knowledge Discovery via Data Analytics\", \"activity\": \"Seminar (3 hr)\", \"learning_outcomes\": \"LO1 LO3 LO4 LO5\"}, {\"week\": \"Week 05\", \"topic\": \"Data Quality\", \"activity\": \"Seminar (3 hr)\", \"learning_outcomes\": \"LO1 LO2 LO3 LO4\"}, {\"week\": \"Week 06\", \"topic\": \"Comprehensive Case Discussion\", \"activity\": \"Seminar (3 hr)\", \"learning_outcomes\": \"LO1 LO2 LO3 LO4 LO5\"}, {\"week\": \"Week 07\", \"topic\": \"Ethics of Data Visualisation\", \"activity\": \"Seminar (3 hr)\", \"learning_outcomes\": \"LO1 LO2 LO3 LO5\"}, {\"week\": \"Week 08\", \"topic\": \"Infographics\", \"activity\": \"Seminar (3 hr)\", \"learning_outcomes\": \"LO1 LO3 LO4 LO5\"}, {\"week\": \"Week 09\", \"topic\": \"Visual Storytelling\", \"activity\": \"Seminar (3 hr)\", \"learning_outcomes\": \"LO1 LO2 LO3 LO4 LO5\"}, {\"week\": \"Week 10\", \"topic\": \"Visualisation Principles and DV Lifecycle\", \"activity\": \"Seminar (3 hr)\", \"learning_outcomes\": \"LO1 LO3 LO4\"}, {\"week\": \"Week 11\", \"topic\": \"Guided Project Work\", \"activity\": \"Seminar (3 hr)\", \"learning_outcomes\": \"LO2 LO3 LO4 LO5\"}, {\"week\": \"Week 12\", \"topic\": \"Group Presentations\", \"activity\": \"Seminar (3 hr)\", \"learning_outcomes\": \"LO3 LO4 LO5\"}, {\"week\": \"Week 13\", \"topic\": \"Group Presentations\", \"activity\": \"Seminar (3 hr)\", \"learning_outcomes\": \"LO3 LO4 LO5\"}], \"learning_outcomes\": [\"LO1. Apply fundamental concepts of data visualisation to analyse and present data-related challenges in organisational and societal settings.\", \"LO2. Identify and analyse multi-disciplinary issues and ethical challenges associated with the use of data visualisation techniques.\", \"LO3. Explain principles and best practices of data visualisation as it applies to current and emerging industry trends.\", \"LO4. Design and develop data visualisations based on real world datasets.\", \"LO5. Recommend and evaluate data visualisation solutions and present outcomes orally and verbally.\"], \"assessment_summary\": [\"Case Study Discussion: The purpose of this assignment is for students to apply data visualisation concepts to real-world business cases and datasets. Case studies will be assigned on a weekly basis and discussed in class.\", \"In-class Assessment: The purpose of this assignment is for students to evaluate and discuss data visualsation solutions as they are being applied to real-world business cases and datasets. Case studies will be assigned on a weekly basis and discussed in class.\", \"Individual Assignment: The purpose of this assignment is for students to use data visualisation techniques to address a business problem within a particular business case context.\", \"Group Project Report: The purpose of this assignment is to enable students to explain principles and best practices of data visualisation as it applies to a business or societal context, conduct research, stimulate broader thinking through collaborative teamwork and present their findings in written format.\", \"Group Project Presentation: The purpose of this assignment is for students to evaluate and recommend data visualisation solutions in a manner relevant to decision makers. The assignment will assess students on their ability to utilize essential business communication skills and correspond with an audience in oral and interactive forms.\", \"Skills-based Assessment: The purpose of this assignment is for students to develop the skills to design and develop data visualisation solutions. This are self-paced skill development exercises that have to be completed throughout the semester.\", \"Detailed information for each assessment can be found on Canvas.\"]}'),(54,54,'outline-v1','baseline-v1','2026-09-11 04:52:58.377053','Managing Data at Scale','{\"details\": {\"Academic unit\": \"Business Information Systems\", \"Credit points\": \"6\", \"Corequisites ?\": \"None\", \"Prohibitions ?\": \"None\", \"Prerequisites ?\": \"None\", \"Assumed knowledge ?\": \"None\", \"Available to study abroad and exchange students\": \"Yes\"}, \"session\": \"Semester 1, 2026 [Normal evening] - Camperdown/Darlington, Sydney\", \"overview\": [\"As the amount of data generated continues to grow dramatically, managing data at scale presents a set of challenges for which organizations have to be uniquely prepared. This unit provides students with what they need to know about generating, collecting, processing, storing, managing, analysing and interpreting data. The unit provides an understanding of the importance of data strategies, data governance and data quality, challenges associated with data protection, privacy and security, data management practices, and modern platforms and architecture to streamline data operations within an organisation. Students learn the importance of confidentiality, integrity, and availability of data in mitigating information risks and emergent issues around data ethics.\"], \"unit_code\": \"INFS6024\", \"source_url\": \"https://www.sydney.edu.au/units/INFS6024/2026-S1C-NE-CC\", \"unit_title\": \"Managing Data at Scale\", \"assessments\": [{\"due\": \"Multiple weeks Closing date: 08 Jun 2026\", \"type\": \"Practical skill\", \"length\": \"5 hours\", \"weight\": \"5%\", \"description\": \"Skills-based assessment Skills-based evaluation\"}, {\"due\": \"Multiple weeks Closing date: 08 Jun 2026\", \"type\": \"Presentation\", \"length\": \"10 minutes\", \"weight\": \"20%\", \"description\": \"Case study discussion Presentation\"}, {\"due\": \"Multiple weeks Closing date: 08 Jun 2026\", \"type\": \"Contribution\", \"length\": \"10 minutes\", \"weight\": \"20%\", \"description\": \"In-class assessment Case study discussion\"}, {\"due\": \"Week 06 Due date: 02 Apr 2026 at 23:59 Closing date: 12 Apr 2026\", \"type\": \"Case studies\", \"length\": \"1500 words\", \"weight\": \"15%\", \"description\": \"Individual assignment Written report\"}, {\"due\": \"Week 12 Due date: 18 May 2026 at 23:59 Closing date: 28 May 2026\", \"type\": \"Case studies\